hadiths[2434]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24511","He said: My father narrated to me, I heard him alone, he said: Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing the snakes of houses except the short-tailed and the one with two stripes, for they snatch, or he said: efface, eyesight and cause pregnancy to be cast from the bellies of women, and whoever leaves them is not of us."
"24512","Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Aishah who said: The day of Ashura was a day Quraysh used to fast in pre-Islamic times, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast it. Then when he came to Madinah he fasted it and commanded its fasting. Then when the obligation of the month of Ramadan was revealed, Ramadan was what he fasted, and he left the day of Ashura, so whoever wished fasted it and whoever wished broke it."
"24513","Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say to her: I know your anger when you are angry and your pleasure when you are pleased. She said: And how do you know that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: When you are angry you say: O Muhammad, and when you are pleased you say: O Messenger of Allah."
"24514","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us from his father from Aishah who said: When my exoneration came down from heaven, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me and informed me of that, so I said: We praise Allah, Exalted and Majestic, we do not praise you."
"24515","Hushaym narrated to us from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from Abu Salamah from Aishah who said: I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bathe from one vessel from janabah."
"24516","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only permitted Sawdah bint Zamah to pour forth before dawn from Jam because she was a slow woman."
"24517","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us from Amrah from Aishah who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in my chamber, and the people followed him in prayer from behind the chamber, praying with his prayer."
"24518","Hushaym narrated to us from Abu Hurrah from al-Hasan from Sad ibn Hisham from Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at night to pray, he would open his prayer with two light rakahs."
"24519","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted a household of the Ansar to use ruqyah for every venomous sting."
"24520","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq who said: I asked Aishah about the voluntary prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so she said: He would pray before Zuhr four in my house, then go out and pray with the people, then return to my house and pray two rakahs. And he would lead the people in Maghrib, then return to his house and pray two rakahs. And he would lead them in Isha, then enter my house and pray two rakahs. And he would pray at night nine rakahs including witr. And he would pray a long night standing and a long night sitting. When he recited standing, he bowed and prostrated standing, and when he recited sitting, he bowed and prostrated sitting. And when dawn rose he would pray two rakahs, then go out and lead the people in the Fajr prayer."
"24521","Hushaym narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us from al-Shabi from Masruq from Aishah who said: I used to twist the necklaces of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with my hands. Masruq said: And I heard her clapping her hands from behind the hijab while she narrated that, then he remains among us lawful."
"24522","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed us from Mujahid from Aishah who said: Riders would pass by us while we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in ihram, and when they came alongside us one of us would let down her jilbab from her head over her face, and when they passed beyond us we uncovered it."
"24523","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us from a man from Abu al-Aliyah from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say in the prostration of the Quran: My face prostrated to the One who created it and split its hearing and sight by His power and strength."
"24524","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughirah informed us from al-Shabi from Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, found news slow in coming, he would cite in it the verse of Tarafah: News will be brought to you by one whom you did not provision."
"24525","Mutamir narrated to us from Ishaq, meaning Ibn Suwayd, from Muadhah from Aishah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: He forbade naqir and muqayyar and dubba and hantam."
"24526","Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalid from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from Aishah who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray Duha except that he came from a journey, then he would pray two rakahs."
"24527","Mutamir narrated to us from Ayyub from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One suckling and two sucklings do not prohibit."
"24528","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal informed us, Burd narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray in the house with the door closed upon him, so I came and he walked until he opened for me, then returned to his place. And she described that the door was in the qiblah."
"24529","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal informed us from Abdullah ibn Uthman from Yusuf ibn Mahak who said: We entered upon Hafsah bint Abd al-Rahman, and she informed us that Aishah informed her that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For a boy two equivalent sheep, and for a girl one sheep."
"24530","Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to me from Yazid ibn Babanus from Aishah that Abu Bakr entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after his death, and placed his mouth between his eyes and placed his hands on his temples and said: O my Prophet, O my intimate friend, O my chosen one."
"24531","Ishaq, meaning al-Azraq, and Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Ishaq said: Husayn ibn al-Mukattab narrated to us from Budayl from Abu al-Jawza from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would open the prayer with takbir and recitation with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And when he bowed he did not raise his head, and Yahya said: He held his head up straight, and did not lower it, but between that. And when he raised his head from bowing he did not prostrate until he stood straight, and when he raised his head from prostration he did not prostrate until he sat straight. She said: And he would say the tahiyyah in every two rakahs. And he would forbid the sitting of Satan. And he would spread his left foot and erect his right foot. And he would forbid the sitting of Satan. And he would forbid that one of us spread his forearms like the dog. And he would end the prayer with taslim. Yahya said: And he disliked that one spread his forearms like the spreading of the beast."
"24532","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us from Budayl from Abu al-Jawza from Aishah that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was, and he mentioned its like, and he said: He holds his head up straight, and he said: The spreading of the beast."
"24533","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur, and Yahya from Sufyan, he said: Mansur narrated to me from Ibrahim from Umarah ibn Umayr from his paternal aunt from Aishah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The purest of what a man eats is from his earnings, and his child is from his earnings."
"24534","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us from Hilal ibn Yasaf from Farwah ibn Nawfal who said: I asked Aishah about the supplication of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: He would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what my soul has done."
"24535","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never struck a servant of his nor a wife of his, nor did he strike with his hand except that he strive in the path of Allah. And nothing was done to him that he avenged it from its doer, except that the sanctities of Allah, Exalted and Majestic, be violated, then he would avenge for Allah, Exalted and Majestic. And no two matters were presented to him, one easier than the other, except he took the easier of them, unless it was a sin; if it was a sin he was the farthest of people from it."
"24536","Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Saib narrated to us from his mother from Aishah who said: When fever took his family, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would order soup, so it was made, then he ordered them and they sipped from it, then he would say: It surely strengthens the heart of the grieved and relieves the heart of the sick, as one of you removes dirt with water from her face."
"24537","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Abu Qilabah from Muadhah who said: A woman asked Aishah: Does the menstruating woman make up prayer. So she said: Are you a Haruriyyah. We used to menstruate at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we would not make up, nor were we commanded to make up."
"24538","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Humayd ibn Hilal from Abu Burdah who said: Aishah brought out to us a patched cloak and a coarse waist-wrapper, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died in these two."
"24539","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Abu Qilabah from Abdullah ibn Yazid, a foster-child of Aishah, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No one of the Muslims dies and a nation of people amounting to a hundred pray over him and intercede for him, except they are granted intercession for him."
"24540","Ismail narrated to us from Ibn Awn from Ibrahim from al-Aswad who said: They mentioned at Aishah that Ali was a legatee, so she said: When did he bequeath to him. I had him supported against my chest, or she said: in my lap, then he called for the basin, and he became limp in my lap, and I did not feel that he died, so when did he bequeath to him."
"24541","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us from Umarah ibn Umayr from Abu Atiyyah who said: Aishah said: I know how the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say talbiyah. He said: Then I heard her saying talbiyah, saying: Here I am, O Allah, here I am, no partner have You, here I am, praise and blessing belong to You, and sovereignty, no partner have You."
"24542","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from al-Amash from Tamim ibn Salamah from Urwah from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would observe itikaf, and he would put out his head to me from the mosque, and I would wash it while I was menstruating."
"24543","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from al-Amash from Umarah ibn Umayr from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray witr with nine, then when he aged and became heavy he prayed witr with seven."
"24544","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih who said: Aishah and Umm Salamah were asked which deed was most pleasing to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They said: What is continuous, even if little."
"24545","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Amr narrated to us from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would stand and pray with one end of the quilt over him and the other end over Aishah, then he would pray."
"24546","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from his father from Aishah that she said: The sun eclipsed, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed and lengthened the standing, then bowed and lengthened the bowing, then rose before prostrating and lengthened the standing, shorter than the first standing, then bowed and lengthened shorter than the first bowing, then prostrated, then stood the second, then did like what he did in the first rakah, except that his first standing was longer than his last, and his first bowing longer than his last, then he completed his prayer with the sun already cleared."
"24547","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from al-Shaybani from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from his father from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would touch his wives above the waist-wrapper while they were menstruating."
"24548","Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us from Khusayf, and Marwan ibn Shuja narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to me from Mujahid from Aishah, and Marwan said: I heard Aishah saying, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wearing gold, we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not tie musk with something of gold. He said: Will you not tie it with silver then smear it with saffron so it becomes like gold."
"24549","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Khusayf, and Marwan narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to us from Ata from Umm Salamah the like of that."
"24550","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed us from Urwah from Aishah that Abu Bakr entered upon her with two slave girls beating two tambourines beside her, so Abu Bakr scolded them, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Leave them, for every people has a festival."
"24551","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, swore that he would not enter upon his wives for a month. She said: So he stayed twenty-nine. She said: And I was the first he began with, so I said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Did you not swear a month, and I counted the days twenty-nine. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The month is twenty-nine."
"24552","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah who said: Women would pray dawn with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then go out wrapped in their cloaks, not recognized."
"24553","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Five harmful creatures are killed in the sanctuary: The scorpion, the mouse, the kite, the vicious dog, and the crow."
"24554","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that Barirah came to her seeking her help, and she was a mukatabah, so Aishah said to her: Will your people sell you. So she came to her people and mentioned that to them, so they said: No, unless they stipulate for us your wala. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Buy her and free her, for wala belongs only to the one who frees."
"24555","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr that Aflah the brother of Abu Quays asked permission to visit Aishah, and she refused to permit him. Then when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, she said: O Messenger of Allah, Aflah the brother of Abu Quays asked permission to visit me and I refused to permit him. So he said: Permit him. She said: O Messenger of Allah, only the woman nursed me, the man did not nurse me. He said: Permit him, for he is your uncle, may your right hand be dusted."
"24556","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that a woman entered upon her with two daughters of hers, so I gave her a date, and she split it between them. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Whoever is tried with something of these daughters and treats them well, they will be for him a screen from the Fire."
"24557","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would leave a deed though he loved to do it, fearing that the people would take it as sunnah and it would be made obligatory upon them. And he loved what was lightened for them of obligations."
"24558","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray after Isha eleven rakahs, then when morning came he would pray two light rakahs, then lie on his right side until the caller for prayer came to him and informed him of the prayer."
"24559","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah who said: The wife of Rifah al-Qurazi entered, while I and Abu Bakr were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she said: Rifah divorced me irrevocably, and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr married me, and with him is only like my fringe, and she took a fringe from her jilbab. And Khalid ibn Said ibn al-As was at the door, not permitted, so he said: O Abu Bakr, will you not forbid this woman what she says aloud before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did no more than smile. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As if you want to return to Rifah. Not until you taste his little honey and he tastes your little honey."
"24560","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delayed Isha until Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, called him: The women and children have slept. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out and said: None of the people of the earth prays this prayer but you, and that day none prayed but the people of Madinah."
"24561","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Abbas and from Aishah that they said: When death descended upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he began to cast his khamisah over his face, and when distressed we lifted it from him, while he said: May Allah curse the Jews and Christians, they took the graves of their prophets as mosques. Aishah says: He warned them of the like of what they did."
"24562","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah from Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell ill in the house of Maymunah, he asked permission of his wives to be nursed in my house, so they permitted him. So the Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out leaning upon al-Abbas and upon another man, with his feet trailing on the ground. And Ubayd Allah said: So Ibn Abbas said: Do you know who that man is. He is Ali ibn Abi Talib, but Aishah has no liking for him. Al-Zuhri said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while in the house of Maymunah, said to Abdullah ibn Zamah: Order the people to pray. So he met Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: O Umar, lead the people in prayer. So he led them. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard his voice and recognized him, and he was loud-voiced. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Is this not the voice of Umar. They said: Yes. He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and the believers refuse that. Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender man who cannot hold his tears, and when he recites the Quran he weeps. He said: And you said that only out of dislike that the people take Abu Bakr as ill-omened, that he be the first to stand in the place of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he said: Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. So she repeated to him, so he said: Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. You are the companions of Yusuf."
"24563","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham who said: I and my father entered upon Aishah and Umm Salamah, and they said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would wake junub then fast."
"24564","Amr ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from Mutarrif from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say in his bowing and prostration: All-Glorious, All-Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"24565","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Said from Abu Mashar from al-Nakhai from al-Aswad from Aishah who said: I used to rub it from the garment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when you see it then wash it, otherwise sprinkle it."
"24566","Muhammad ibn Adi narrated to us from Dawud, and Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us from al-Shabi from Masruq who said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would often at the end of his affair say: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, I seek Allahs forgiveness and repent to Him. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you often saying: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, I seek Allahs forgiveness and repent to Him. He said: My Lord, Exalted and Majestic, informed me that I would see a sign in my ummah, and commanded me when I saw it to glorify Him with praise and seek His forgiveness, indeed He is ever Relenting. I have seen it: When the help of Allah and victory comes, and you see people entering Allahs religion in crowds, then glorify with the praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness, indeed He is ever Relenting."
"24567","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from Amrah from Aishah who said: When my exoneration was revealed, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood upon the pulpit and mentioned that and recited the Quran. Then when he descended he ordered two men and a woman, and they were struck their hadd."
"24568","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Nafi narrated to me, and his wife was an umm walad of Abdullah ibn Umar, she narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Umar bought a slave girl on the road of Makkah and freed her and ordered her to perform hajj with him, and he sought two sandals for her and did not find them, so he cut two khuffs for her below the ankles. Ibn Ishaq said: So I mentioned that to Ibn Shihab, so he said: Salim narrated to me that Abdullah used to do that. Then Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd narrated to him that Aishah narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to permit women to wear khuffs, so he left that."
"24569","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Dawud from Amir from Masruq from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would send sacrificial camels from Madinah to Makkah, and I would twist the necklaces of the sacrificial camels with my hands, then he does what the lawful does before the sacrificial camels reach Makkah."
"24570","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Dawud from al-Shabi from Masruq who said: Aishah said: I am the first of people who asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about this verse: On the day the earth will be changed to other than the earth, and the heavens, and they will appear before Allah, the One, the Subduer. She said: So I said: Where will people be that day, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Upon the path."
"24571","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Malik from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray at night eleven rakahs, praying witr among them with one, then when he finished his prayer he lay on his right side."
"24572","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who entered ihram for umrah circumambulated the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah, then circumambulated after they returned from Mina for their hajj, and those who combined performed one circumambulation."
"24573","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Salim Abu al-Nadr from Abu Salamah from Aishah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray at night, then when he finished his prayer he lay down; if I was awake he talked with me, and if I was asleep he slept until the caller for prayer came to him."
"24574","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Said ibn Abi Said from Abu Salamah who said: I asked Aishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Ramadan, so she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not exceed in Ramadan nor otherwise eleven rakahs: He would pray four, so do not ask about their excellence and length, then pray four, so do not ask about their excellence and length, then pray three. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you sleep before you pray witr. He said: O Aishah, my eyes sleep and my heart does not sleep."
"24575","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Sumayy and Abd Rabbih ibn Said from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Aishah and Umm Salamah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would wake junub from intercourse, not a wet dream, then fast. And she said in the hadith of Abd Rabbih: In Ramadan."
"24576","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Talhah ibn Abd al-Malik from al-Qasim from Aishah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever vows to obey Allah, Mighty and Majestic, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Allah, Mighty and Majestic, let him not disobey Him."
"24577","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Abu al-Aswad from Urwah from Aishah who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Some of us entered ihram for hajj, and some of us entered ihram for umrah, and some of us entered ihram for hajj and umrah. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram for hajj. As for whoever entered ihram for umrah, they exited ihram when they circumambulated the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah. And as for whoever entered ihram for hajj or for hajj and umrah, they did not exit ihram until the day of sacrifice."
"24578","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed hajj alone."
"24579","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard it from al-Zuhri from Amrah from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would cut in a quarter dinar and upward."
"24580","Attab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, Yunus informed us from al-Zuhri who said: Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman said from Aishah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The hand of the thief is cut for a quarter dinar and upward."
"24581","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Amrah from Aishah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I entered Paradise and heard therein a recitation. I said: Who is this. They said: Harithah ibn al-Numan. Thus is righteousness, thus is righteousness. And he said once: From Aishah, if Allah wills."
"24582","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Aishah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me while I had screened myself with a curtain in which were images. When he saw it his face changed color, and he said once: His face changed, and he tore it with his hand, and said: The severest of people in punishment with Allah, Exalted and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate Allahs creation, Mighty and Majestic, or resemble. Sufyan said: The same."
"24583","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Aishah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful."
"24584","Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed us from Abu Salamah from Aishah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he wanted to sleep while junub, would perform wudu as for prayer."
"24585","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: I used to twist the necklaces of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with my hands, then he would not avoid anything that the person in ihram avoids."
"24586","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: My uncle came after the hijab was imposed, and I refused to permit him. So I asked him, and he said: Permit him, for he is your uncle. I said: Only the woman nursed me, the man did not nurse me. He said: May your right hand be dusted, permit him, for he is only your uncle."
"24587","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: Abd ibn Zamah and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas disputed before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning the son of the slave woman of Zamah. Abd said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother, the son of my fathers slave woman, born on his bed. And Sad said: My brother enjoined me when you come to Makkah to look at the son of the slave woman of Zamah and take him, for he is my son. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a clear resemblance to Utbah. He said: He is yours, O Abd, the child belongs to the bed. And veil yourself from him, O Sawdah."
"24588","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in a khamisah of his that had marks, and when he finished his prayer he said: Its marks distracted me. Take it to Abu Jahm and bring me his anbijaniyyah."
"24589","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray his night prayer while I lay across between him and the qiblah like the lying of a funeral bier."
"24590","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bathe from one vessel, and he would bathe from the qadah, which is the faraq."
"24591","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: A group of Jews sought permission upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Death be upon you. So Aishah said: Rather death be upon you and curse. He said: O Aishah, Allah, Exalted and Majestic, loves gentleness in all matters. She said: Did you not hear what they said. He said: I said: And upon you."
"24592","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Exalted and Majestic, loves gentleness in all matters."
"24593","Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us from Urwah from Aishah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a dead person more than three, except for a husband."
"24594","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram for hajj, and people entered ihram for hajj and umrah, and people entered ihram for umrah."
"24595","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The child belongs to the bed."
"24596","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: He would pray Asr while the sun was high in my chamber, the shadow not yet appearing."
"24597","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that believing women would pray dawn with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrapped in their cloaks, then return to their families, with no one recognizing them from the darkness."
"24598","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard the recitation of Abu Musa, so he said: This one has been given of the flutes of the family of Dawud."
"24599","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: The wife of Rifah al-Qurazi came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I was with Rifah, and he divorced me and made my divorce final. Then I married Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr, and with him is only like the fringe of a garment. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled and said: Do you want to return to Rifah. Not until you taste his little honey and he tastes your little honey. And Abu Bakr was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Khalid ibn Said ibn al-As was at the door waiting to be permitted, so he heard her speech and said: O Abu Bakr, do you not hear what this woman says aloud before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And he said once: What do you think of this woman speaking explicitly before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"24600","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: Mujazziz al-Mudliji entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and saw Usamah and Zayd with a woolen cover over them, their heads covered and their feet visible, so he said: These feet are of one another. And he said once: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me rejoicing."
"24601","Sufyan narrated to us from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: The most beloved drink to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the sweet cold drink."
"24602","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her: Safiyyah menstruated after she had performed the Ifadah, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Will she detain us? I said: She menstruated after she had performed the Ifadah. He said: Then let her depart, or he said: Then no."
"24603","Sufyan narrated to us, Hisham and al-Zuhri narrated to us from Urwah from Aishah, she said: Aflah ibn Abi al-Qu'ays came to me asking permission after the veil had been imposed, and the one from whose milk Aishah had been nursed is his brother, so he came asking my permission and I refused to give him permission, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me and said: Give him permission, for he is your uncle. I said: Only the woman nursed me and the man did not nurse me. He said: May your right hand be dusty, he is your uncle."
"24604","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah from Aishah, Sufyan said: I heard a long hadith from him of which I remember only a little from its beginning: We entered upon Aishah and we said: O Mother of the Believers, inform us about the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He fell ill and began to blow, and we likened his blowing to the blowing of one eating raisins, and he used to go around his wives, then when he fell ill with his complaint he asked their permission to be in the house of Aishah and that they visit him in turn, so they gave him permission, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered between two men leaning upon them, one of them was Abbas, and his feet were dragging on the ground. Ibn Abbas said: Did she not tell you who the other was? He said: No. He said: It is Ali."
"24605","Sufyan narrated to us from Sumayy from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Aishah: That dawn would overtake the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a state of major impurity, then he would wash and fast."
"24606","Sufyan narrated to us, Uthman ibn Urwah narrated to us that he heard his father saying: I asked Aishah: With what did you perfume the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: With the best of perfume."
"24607","Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn al-Munkadir informed us, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah informed him that a man asked permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Give him permission, what an evil son of the tribe he is, or: what an evil brother of the tribe, and once he said: a man, then when he entered he softened his speech to him, then when he left, Aishah said: You said about him what you said, then you softened your speech to him. So he said: O Aishah, the worst of people in rank before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is he whom people leave or shun out of fear of his obscenity."
"24608","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: It is as if I am looking at the glistening of musk on the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he is in ihram."
"24609","From Sufyan from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from al-Qasim from Aishah: Sahlah bint Suhayl came and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I see something on the face of Abu Hudhayfah because of Salim coming in to me. So he said: Breastfeed him. She said: How can I breastfeed him when he is a grown man? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed. He said: Do I not know that he is a grown man? Then she came later and said: I have not seen on the face of Abu Hudhayfah anything I dislike."
"24610","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her when she menstruated at Sarif before entering Makkah, he said to her: Perform what the pilgrim performs except that you do not circumambulate the House. She said: Then when we were at Mina I was brought beef, I said: What is this? They said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed cattle on behalf of his wives."
"24611","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I said to Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim: Did you hear your father narrating from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her while fasting? He was silent with me for a while, then he said: Yes."
"24612","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, he heard his father saying: I heard Aishah saying: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two hands of mine for his ihram when he entered ihram and for his release from ihram before he circumambulated."
"24613","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman from al-Qasim from Aishah: We set out seeing nothing but Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24614","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah that she said: Safiyyah menstruated, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Will she detain us? I said: She had already performed the Ifadah before that. He said: Then no."
"24615","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no Muslim who is pricked by a thorn or more except that it removes some of his sin."
"24616","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr from his father: He heard Ibn Umar, when Rafi ibn Khadij died, that the weeping of the living over the dead is a punishment for the dead, so I went to Amrah and mentioned that to her, so Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said it about a Jewess: You are weeping over her while she is being punished, and she recited: And no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another."
"24617","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Abi Labid from Abu Salamah: I said to Aishah: O mother, inform me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: His prayer in Ramadan and otherwise was the same, thirteen rak'ahs including the two rak'ahs of Fajr. I said: Then inform me about his fasting. She said: He used to fast until we would say he has fasted, and break fast until we would say he has broken fast, and I never saw him fast a month more than his fasting in Sha'ban, he used to fast it except a little."
"24618","Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham from his father from Aishah: That Hind said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man and I have nothing except what comes into my house. He said: Take what suffices you and your child in a reasonable manner."
"24619","Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham from his father from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raced me and I beat him, then we remained until when flesh overtook me he raced me and beat me, then he said: This is for that."
"24620","Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Aishah informed me that she was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey while she was a young girl, so he said to his companions: Go ahead, so they went ahead, then he said to her: Come, I will race you, then he mentioned the hadith."
"24621","Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham from his father from Aishah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When supper is placed and the prayer is established, begin with supper."
"24622","Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham from his father from Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah from the upper part of Makkah and left from its lower part."
"24623","Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham from his father from Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three white Suhuli garments, and Abu Bakr said: In what was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded? I said: In three garments. He said: Shroud me in these two garments of mine and buy another garment."
"24624","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id from Abu Salamah: Abd al-Rahman performed ablution in the presence of Aishah, so she said: O Abd al-Rahman, perform ablution fully, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"24625","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Sa'id from Abu Salamah from Aishah, she said: We had a mat which we spread in the day and secluded ourselves with at night, something was unclear to me which I did not understand from Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslims pray following his prayer, then he said: Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear, for Allah Almighty does not grow weary until you grow weary, and when he prayed a prayer he kept it constant, and the most beloved deed to him was the most constant."
"24626","Sufyan narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us from the nephew of Amrah, meaning this Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amrah from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lighten the two rak'ahs until I would say: Did he recite the Opening of the Book or not."
"24627","Sufyan narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us from the nephew of Amrah, and I do not know whether this one or another, from Amrah, she said: Aishah complained of an illness and her complaint lasted long, then a man came to Madinah practicing medicine, so the sons of her brother went to ask him about her pain, so he said: By Allah, you are describing the description of a bewitched woman. He said: This is a bewitched woman, a slave girl of hers has bewitched her. She said: Yes, I intended that you die so that I would be freed. He said: And she had been granted deferred manumission. She said: Sell her to the harshest of the Arabs in ownership, and put her price into one like her."
"24628","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, the foster child of Aishah, from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no dead person over whom a community of people reaching a hundred pray and intercede for him except that they are granted intercession for him."
"24629","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Karim from Qays ibn Muslim al-Jadali from Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali from Aishah: A dried piece of gazelle meat was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram, so he returned it. Sufyan said: Al-Washiqah is what was cooked and dried."
"24630","Sufyan narrated to us from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah, she said: The most beloved drink to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the sweet cold drink."
"24631","Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah: Alqamah and his companions set out as pilgrims, then some of them mentioned the fasting person kissing and embracing, so a man among them who had stood in prayer for two years and fasted them stood up: I intended to take my bow and strike you with it. He said: So refrain until you come to Aishah, so they entered upon Aishah and asked her about that, so Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss and embrace, and he was the most in control of his desire among you. They said: O Abu Shibl, ask her. He said: I will not speak obscenely in her presence today. So they asked her and she said: He used to kiss and embrace while fasting."
"24632","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Ubayd ibn Nistas, meaning Abu Ya'fur, from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah, mentioning from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When the last ten entered, he would enliven the night and wake his family and tighten his waist-wrapper. Sufyan said: One of them from the last, and he strove."
"24633","Sufyan narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us from Aishah bint Talhah from Aishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a child of the Ansar who did not reach puberty, a sparrow among the sparrows of Paradise. He said: Or other than that, O Aishah, Allah created Paradise and created people for it, and created the Fire and created people for it, while they are in the loins of their fathers."
"24634","Sufyan narrated to us from Jami ibn Abi Rashid from Mundhir from Hasan ibn Muhammad from his wife from Aishah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When evil appears in the land, Allah sends His punishment upon the people of the land. She said: And among them are the people of obedience to Allah Almighty. He said: Yes, then they return to the mercy of Allah Almighty."
"24635","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I saw the glistening of perfume, and it was read to Sufyan: I heard Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah: On the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after three."
"24636","Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from Ammarah from a paternal aunt of his from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your children are among the best of your earnings, so eat from the earnings of your children."
"24637","Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He once gifted sheep as a sacrifice."
"24638","Sufyan narrated to us, Amr narrated to us from Ata from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until women were made lawful to him."
"24639","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah: That a thief was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered him to be cut, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, we did not think it would reach this from him. He said: Had it been Fatimah I would have cut her. Then Sufyan said: I do not know how it is."
"24640","Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu al-Duha from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I was in front of him."
"24641","Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us from al-A'mash from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any woman who removes her clothes in other than her husband's house has torn the veil between her and her Lord."
"24642","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, Malik ibn Anas informed us from Talhah ibn Abd al-Malik from al-Qasim from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever vows to obey Allah Almighty, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Allah Almighty, let him not disobey Him."
"24643","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard Hisham from his father from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: You were shown to me in a dream twice, with a man carrying you in a piece of silk, saying: This is your wife. So I say: If this is from Allah Almighty, He will carry it out."
"24644","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us from his father from Aishah, she said: Staying at al-Abtah is not a Sunnah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only stayed there because it was easier for his departure."
"24645","Abdah narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us from Miqdam ibn Shurayh from his father from Aishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he saw rain would say: O Allah, a beneficial downpour. He said: And I asked Aishah: With what would the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) begin when he entered his house? She said: With the tooth-stick."
"24646","Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Habib from Urwah from Aishah, she said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I suffer from prolonged bleeding. So he said: Leave prayer during the days of your menstruation, then wash and perform ablution for every prayer, even if it drips upon the mat."
"24647","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought food on credit from a Jew and gave him his armor as a pledge."
"24648","Abu Muawiyah and Ya'la narrated to us, they said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasting in the first ten at all."
"24649","Abu Muawiyah and Ya'la narrated to us, they said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of what a man eats is from his earnings, and his child is from his earnings."
"24650","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, my father said, and Ya'la did not raise it, about a man who divorced his wife, so she married another husband, then he entered with her and divorced her before consummating with her, is she lawful for her first husband? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is not lawful for the first until the other tastes her sweetness and she tastes his sweetness."
"24651","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The husband of Barirah was free, then when she was freed, and once he said she was freed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice, so she chose herself. She said: And her family wanted to sell her stipulating the loyalty of patronage. She said: So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Buy her and free her, for patronage belongs to the one who frees."
"24652","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate his fill for three consecutive days of wheat bread until he passed on his way."
"24653","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her when she was nine years old, and he died leaving her when she was eighteen years old."
"24654","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah: It reached her that people say prayer is interrupted by the dog, the donkey, and the woman. She said: Do I see them equating us with dogs and donkeys? I would often see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying at night while I was on the bed between him and the qiblah, then when I had a need I would slip away from the foot of the bed, disliking to face him."
"24655","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from Alqamah and al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting and embrace while fasting, but he was the most in control of his desire among you."
"24656","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once gifted sheep to the House and garlanded them."
"24657","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No thorn or more afflicts the believer except that Allah Almighty raises him a degree thereby and removes a sin from him thereby."
"24658","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no believer pricked by a thorn or more except that a degree is written for him thereby and a sin is expiated from him thereby."
"24659","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from Hammam, he said: A guest stayed with Aishah, so she ordered for him a yellow blanket of hers, so he slept in it and had a wet dream, so he was shy to send it with the trace of the wet dream in it. He said: So he dipped it in water, then sent it. So Aishah said: Why did he spoil our garment for us? It would have sufficed him to rub it with his fingers, for I would often rub it from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my fingers."
"24660","Isma'il narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from the Mother of the Believers, and from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, both narrating that from the Mother of the Believers, I do not remember the hadith of this one from the hadith of that one, he said: Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, people return with two rites and I return with one rite. He said: Wait, then when you are pure go out to al-Tan'im and enter ihram from there, then meet us, and once he said: Then join us at such and such mountain, he said: I think he said so, but it is according to your hardship or your expenditure, or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"24661","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: It reached Aishah that Abd Allah ibn Amr orders women when they wash to undo their hair, so she said: How strange of Ibn Amr, he orders women when they wash to undo their hair, why does he not order them to shave? I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash from one vessel, and I would do no more than pour three pours over my head."
"24662","Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be in a state of major impurity then sleep without touching water until he would then rise and wash."
"24663","Jarir narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah, he said: I asked Aishah: How was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: And which of you can do what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) could do? His deed was constant."
"24664","Jarir narrated to us from Mansur from Abu al-Duha from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say in his bowing and prostration: Glory be to You, O Allah, our Lord, and with Your praise, O Allah, forgive me, interpreting the Qur'an."
"24665","Jarir narrated to us from Qabus from his father, he said: My father sent a woman to Aishah asking her: Which prayer was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to persist in? She said: He used to pray four before noon, lengthening the standing in them and excelling in the bowing and prostration in them, but what he never left, neither healthy nor ill nor absent nor present, was two rak'ahs before Fajr."
"24666","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah from al-Qasim from Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed Uthman ibn Maz'un while he was dead, until I saw tears flowing upon his face."
"24667","Yahya narrated to us from Abu Hazrah, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to me, he said: I heard Aishah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Prayer is not performed in the presence of food, nor while one is resisting the two impurities."
"24668","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ata narrated to me from Ubayd ibn Umayr from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not more strict in observing any voluntary prayer than the two rak'ahs before dawn."
"24669","Yahya narrated to us from Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard al-Qasim from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan. She said: I know it was only the measure of this one descending and this one ascending."
"24670","Yahya narrated to us from Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard al-Qasim narrating from Aishah, she said: How evil is what you have equated us with, the dog and the donkey. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying while I was lying across in front of him, then when he wanted to prostrate he would nudge my foot, meaning, so I would draw it to me, then he would prostrate."
"24671","Yahya narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Urwah from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is prohibited by breastfeeding is what is prohibited by birth."
"24672","He said: And Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me from Amrah from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"24673","Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When she spends, and Ibn Numayr said: When the woman feeds from her husband's house, and Abu Muawiyah said: When the woman spends from her husband's house without causing ruin, she has her reward and he has the like thereof for what he earned, and she has for what she spent, and the storekeeper has the like thereof. Abu Muawiyah said: Without decreasing anything from their rewards."
"24674","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Zakariyya, he said: Amir narrated to me, he said: Shurayh ibn Hani narrated to me, he said: Aishah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves meeting Allah Almighty, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him, and death is before meeting Allah."
"24675","Yahya narrated to us from Jabir ibn Subh, he said: I heard Khilas, he said: I heard Aishah saying: I used to spend the night, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in one blanket while I was menstruating. She said: If anything from me touched him, he would wash it, not exceeding its place, and pray in it."
"24676","Yahya narrated to us from Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard al-Qasim narrating from Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss, or kiss me, while fasting, and which of you was more in control of his desire than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24677","Yahya narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge for some of his family, wiping him with his right hand, saying: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, for You are the Healer, there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness."
"24678","He said: So I mentioned it to Mansur, so he narrated to me from Ibrahim from Masruq from Aishah the like thereof."
"24679","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr from al-A'mash from Shaqiq from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left neither dinar nor dirham nor sheep nor camel, nor did he bequeath anything."
"24680","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash from Shaqiq from Masruq from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the woman spends from her husband's food, then he mentioned its meaning, and he said: Neither one of them decreases the other anything."
"24681","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Masruq from Aishah, she said: A Jewess entered upon her asking her for perfume as a gift, so Aishah gave her, then she said: May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave. She said: So it weighed on my mind until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came. She said: So I mentioned that to him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there punishment in the grave? He said: Yes, they are punished in their graves with a punishment heard by animals."
"24682","Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr, the meaning, narrated to us, they said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah, she said: Two men entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he was harsh with them and reviled them. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, whoever receives good from you, these two have received no good from you. She said: So he said: Did you not know what I covenanted with my Lord Almighty? He said: I said: O Allah, any believer whom I revile or flog or curse, make it for him forgiveness and healing and so and so."
"24683","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted a matter, but some people abstained from it, so that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he became angry until anger was visible on his face, then he said: What is with people who turn away from what has been permitted for me? By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of them about Allah Almighty and the most fearful of them of Him."
"24684","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice, so we chose him, and he did not count it against us as anything."
"24685","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge with these words, and Ibn Ja'far said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Abu al-Duha from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge with these words: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, heal, and You are the Healer, there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness. She said: Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became heavy in his illness in which he died, I took his hand and began wiping him with it and saying them. She said: So he pulled his hand from me, then said: O Lord, forgive me and join me with the Companion. Abu Muawiyah said: She said: So this was the last I heard of his speech. Ibn Ja'far said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he visited a sick person would wipe him with his hand and say: Remove."
"24686","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge with these words, and Ibn Ja'far said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Abu al-Duha from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge with these words: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, heal, and You are the Healer, there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness. She said: Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became heavy in his illness in which he died, I took his hand and began wiping him with it and saying them. She said: So he pulled his hand from me, then said: O Lord, forgive me and join me with the Companion. Abu Muawiyah said: She said: So this was the last I heard of his speech. Ibn Ja'far said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he visited a sick person would wipe him with his hand and say: Remove."
"24687","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Habib from Ata from Aishah, she said: A thief stole from her, so she supplicated against him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do not mitigate for him."
"24688","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Thabit ibn Ubayd from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me the prayer mat from the mosque. She said: I said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand."
"24689","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Yahya, the meaning, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Dhakwan Abu Amr, the freedman of Aishah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek the counsel of women regarding their private parts. He said: It was said: The virgin is shy to speak. He said: Her silence is her permission."
"24690","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Aishah, she said: When Abu Bakr became heavy, he said: Which day is this? We said: Monday. He said: On which day was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taken? He said: We said: He was taken on Monday. He said: Then I hope for what is between me and the night. She said: And he had upon him a garment with a trace of safflower dye, so he said: When I die, wash this garment of mine and add to it two new garments, and shroud me in three garments. So we said: Why do we not make them all new? He said: So he said: No, it is only for the discharge. She said: So he died on the night of Tuesday."
"24691","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah, she said: There were three rulings concerning Barirah: Her family wanted to sell her stipulating patronage, so I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Buy her and free her, for patronage belongs only to the one who frees. He said: And she was freed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice, so she chose herself. She said: And people used to give charity to her, so she would gift to us, so I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: It is charity for her and a gift for you, so eat it."
"24692","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah, and Ibn Ja'far: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu al-Duha from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr at every part of the night, and his witr ended at dawn."
"24693","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Aishah, she said: A woman used to visit her mentioning her striving. He said: So they mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The most beloved religion to Allah Almighty is what is done constantly even if little."
"24694","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a striped woolen garment, so he gave it to Abu Jahmah and took an Anbijani garment of his. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, the striped garment is better than the Anbijani. He said: So he said: I used to look at its markings in prayer."
"24695","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew bulky and heavy he would recite whatever Allah Almighty willed while sitting, then when thirty or forty verses of the chapter remained he would stand and recite them, then prostrate."
"24696","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be brought boys and supplicate for them, and a boy was brought to him and urinated upon him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pour water upon him pouring."
"24697","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah, she said: When the verses from the end of al-Baqarah concerning usury were revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the mosque and prohibited trade in wine."
"24698","Ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman: I heard Abu al-Duha with its meaning, meaning: When the verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah were revealed."
"24699","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Tamim ibn Salamah from Urwah from Aishah, she said: Praise be to Allah Whose hearing encompasses sounds. The disputing woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speaking to him while I was in a corner of the house not hearing what she said, so Allah Almighty revealed: Allah has heard the statement of she who disputes with you concerning her husband, to the end of the verse."
"24700","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Aishah, she said: Hamzah al-Aslami came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who fasts continuously, shall I fast while traveling? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"24701","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every people have supporters, and the supporters of Quraysh are their mawali."
"24702","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Tubalah bint Yazid al-Abshamiyyah, from Aisha, she said: We used to make nabidh for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a waterskin, so we would take a handful of raisins or a handful of dates and throw it into the waterskin, then pour water over it at night, so he would drink it in the daytime, or in the daytime, so he would drink it at night."
"24703","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became gravely ill, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Abdurrahman ibn Abi Bakr: Bring me a shoulder blade or a tablet so that I may write for Abu Bakr a document over which there will be no dispute. When Abdurrahman went to stand, he said: Allah and the believers refuse that there be any dispute over you, O Abu Bakr."
"24704","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is reckoned on the Day of Resurrection will be punished. She said: So I said: Did Allah, Mighty and Majestic, not say: He will be reckoned an easy reckoning? He said: That is not the reckoning, but that is the presentation; whoever has the reckoning scrutinized on the Day of Resurrection will be punished."
"24705","Ismail narrated to us, Ishaq, meaning Ibn Suwayd, narrated to us, from Muadhah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the dubba, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat."
"24706","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Burd ibn Sinan informed us, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, he said: I said to Aisha: Did you see whether the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wash from janabah at the beginning of the night or at the end of it? She said: Sometimes he would wash at the beginning of the night and sometimes he would wash at the end of it. I said: Allah is Greatest, praise be to Allah who has made ease in the matter. I said: Did you see whether the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform witr at the beginning of the night or at the end of it? She said: Sometimes he would perform witr at the beginning of the night and sometimes he would perform witr at the end of it. I said: Allah is Greatest, praise be to Allah who has made ease in the matter. I said: Did you see whether the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite the Quran aloud or quietly? She said: Sometimes he would recite aloud and sometimes he would recite quietly. I said: Allah is Greatest, praise be to Allah who has made ease in the matter."
"24707","Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdurrahman ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The siwak is a purification for the mouth and pleasing to the Lord."
"24708","Ismail narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character and the gentlest of them to their families."
"24709","Ismail narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If a woman is married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid, her marriage is invalid, her marriage is invalid; if he consummated with her, she gets her dowry for what he obtained from her; if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian. Ibn Jurayj said: So I met al-Zuhri and asked him about this hadith, and he did not recognize it. He said: And Sulayman ibn Musa was, and so he praised him. The ruler is the judge, because to him belongs the matter of private parts and judgments."
"24710","He said: Ismail informed us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When he sits between the four branches and then joins circumcision to circumcision, ghusl has become obligatory."
"24711","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Aisha, that she washed semen that had afflicted the garment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"24712","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave us the choice, so we chose him, and he did not count it against us as anything."
"24713","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The bed of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on which he slept at night was of leather stuffed with palm fiber."
"24714","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: He is the One who sent down upon you the Book; among it are verses precise, they are the foundation of the Book, and others unspecific. As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is unspecific of it, seeking discord and seeking its interpretation, and none knows its interpretation except Allah, and those firm in knowledge say: We believe in it, all is from our Lord, and none remembers except those of understanding. So if you see those who dispute concerning it, they are those whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, meant, so beware of them."
"24715","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The one who recites the Quran and is skilled in it is with the noble righteous scribes, and the one who recites it while it is hard upon him gets two rewards."
"24716","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu Atiyyah, he said: I and Masruq entered upon Aisha, so we said to her: O Mother of the Believers, two men from the companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one of them hastens breaking the fast and hastens the prayer, and the other delays breaking the fast and delays the prayer. He said: So she said: Which of them hastens breaking the fast and hastens the prayer? He said: We said: Abdullah ibn Masud. She said: Thus the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do. And the other is Abu Musa."
"24717","Ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Khaythamah, and he said: He hastens breaking the fast and delays the sahur."
"24718","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah, from Abu Atiyyah, he said: We said to Aisha: Two men from the companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one of them hastens the Maghrib and hastens breaking the fast, and the other delays the Maghrib and delays breaking the fast. So he mentioned it."
"24719","Ismail narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdulwahid ibn Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, she said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say in some of his prayers: O Allah, reckon me an easy reckoning. When he finished, I said: O Prophet of Allah, what is the easy reckoning? He said: That He looks into his book and overlooks him; whoever has the reckoning debated that day, O Aisha, perishes; and all that afflicts the believer, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, expiates thereby from him, even the thorn that pricks him."
"24720","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died in my house and on my day and between my chest and my throat. Abdurrahman ibn Abi Bakr entered with a moist siwak, so he looked at it, and I thought he had a need for it. She said: So I took it, chewed it, shook it, and made it pleasant, then handed it to him, so he cleaned his teeth as well as I ever saw him cleaning his teeth. Then he went to lift it to me, and it fell from his hand. So I began supplicating Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with a supplication that Jibril, peace be upon him, used to supplicate for him with, and he used to supplicate with it when he was ill, but he did not supplicate with it in that illness of his. So he raised his gaze to the sky and said: The Highest Companion, the Highest Companion, meaning, and his soul overflowed. So praise be to Allah who joined my saliva and his saliva on the last day of the days of this world."
"24721","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abdurrahman ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bowed the two rakahs of Fajr, he would lie on his right side."
"24722","Ismail narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Azrah, from Humayd ibn Abdurrahman, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aisha, she said: We had a curtain in which was the image of a bird, so when one entered, he would face it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Aisha, move this, for whenever I enter and see it, I remember the world. And he had a velvet cloth, we used to say its emblem was of silk, so we used to wear it."
"24723","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Nafi informed me, from Saibah, from Aisha: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing snakes. Muhammad ibn Ubayd said: Those that are in houses. And he ordered us to kill the abtar and the one with two stripes, he said: They seek the sight and cause what is in the wombs of women to fall, and whoever leaves them is not from me."
"24724","Yahya narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, he said: Aisha bint Talhah narrated to me, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to her while fasting, and say: Is there anything with you this morning that you can feed me? So she would say: No, there is nothing with us this morning. So he would say: I am fasting. Then he came to her after that, so she said: A gift was given to us, and we hid it for you. He said: What is it? She said: Hays. He said: I had become fasting, so he ate."
"24725","Yahya narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Ammar, he said: My father, and he was trustworthy, and he is called Ibn Ammar ibn Abi Zaynab, a Medinan, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The congregation is favored over the prayer of the lone one by twenty-five."
"24726","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, he said: Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in the illness in which he died: O Aisha, what happened to the gold? So she brought between five and seven, or eight, or nine. So he began turning it with his hand and saying: What would Muhammad think of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, if he met Him while this was with him? Spend it."
"24727","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Mansur narrated to me, from Abi al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aisha, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to often say in his bowing: Glory be to You, O Allah, our Lord, and with Your praise, my Lord, forgive me, interpreting the Quran."
"24728","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Makhlad ibn Khufaf ibn Ima narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The yield is by the guarantee."
"24729","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, from Muhammad ibn Abdurrahman ibn Asad ibn Zurarah, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: When dawn rose, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not pray except two rakahs, so I would say: Did he recite the Opening of the Book in them?"
"24730","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: al-Hakam narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: I said to Aisha: What did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do with his family? She said: He was in the service of his family, and when prayer came, he went out to the prayer."
"24731","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Amr narrated to us, he said: Masruq came to Aisha and said: O Mother of the Believers, did Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, see his Lord? She said: Glory be to Allah, my hair has stood on end at what you said. Where are you with regard to three matters: whoever narrates them to you has lied. Whoever narrates to you that Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw his Lord has lied. Then she recited: Visions perceive Him not, while He perceives visions. And: It is not for a human being that Allah should speak to him except by revelation or from behind a veil. And whoever tells you of what is tomorrow has lied. Then she recited: Indeed Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs, this verse. And whoever tells you that Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concealed has lied. Then she recited: O Messenger, convey what was sent down to you from your Lord. But he saw Jibril in his form twice."
"24732","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Fever, or the severity of fever, is from the boiling of Hell, so cool it with water."
"24733","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fever, or the severity of fever, is from the boiling of Hell, so cool it with water."
"24734","Ibn Numayr and Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, from Aisha, she said: The day of Ashura was a day Quraysh fasted in the Jahiliyyah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast it. When he came to Medina, he fasted it and ordered its fasting. When the fast of Ramadan was sent down, Ramadan was the obligation, and Ashura was left; whoever willed fasted it and whoever willed did not fast it."
"24735","Yahya and Waki narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, Yahya said, he said: My father informed me, from Aisha, that Hind bint Utbah said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a miserly man, and he does not give me and my child what suffices us except what I take from his wealth without his knowledge. He said: Take what suffices you and your child with fairness."
"24736","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Aisha, she said: A month would pass over the family of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in which they would kindle no fire; there was only dates and water, except that meat was brought to us."
"24737","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seclude himself in the last ten, and say: Seek it in the last ten, meaning Laylat al-Qadr."
"24738","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father narrated to me, from Aisha, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform ruqyah, saying: Wipe away the harm, Lord of the people; in Your hand is the healing; none removes distress except You."
"24739","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, he said: Aisha said to me: O son of my sister, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never left the two prostrations after Asr with me at all."
"24740","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father narrated to me, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray at night while I lay across between him and the qiblah on the bed; when he wanted to perform witr, he would wake me."
"24741","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was bewitched, so it would seem to him that he had done something while he had not done it."
"24742","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to remain in the mosque, so he would incline his head to me, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I would comb it while I was menstruating."
"24743","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father narrated to me, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray thirteen rakahs at night, performing witr with five, not sitting except in the fifth, then giving the taslim."
"24744","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, from Aisha: They slaughtered a sheep. I said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains except its shoulder. He said: All of it has remained except its shoulder."
"24745","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Taymi and Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the two rakahs before the Fajr prayer, he said: They are dearer to me than the whole world."
"24746","Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, he said: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Urwah, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Forbidden by suckling is what is forbidden by birth."
"24747","And from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the same. Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the same."
"24748","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: None of you should say: My soul has become wicked, but let him say: My soul has become sluggish."
"24749","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: He entered upon her while with her was so-and-so, a woman, and she mentioned her prayer. So he said: Stop, upon you is what you can bear; by Allah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not tire until you tire; the most beloved religion to Allah is what its companion persists in."
"24750","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Aisha say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When supper is placed and prayer is established, begin with supper."
"24751","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, he said: Yahya ibn Abdurrahman narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The month is twenty-nine. So they mentioned that to Aisha, so she said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abdurrahman; he only said: The month can be twenty-nine."
"24752","Yahya narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, he said: They brought an uss in Ramadan, so I estimated it as eight or nine or ten ratls. So Mujahid said: Aisha narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wash with the like of this."
"24753","Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Amrah, from Aisha, she said: A crowd of desert folk came at the time of Adha. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat and store for three. When it was after that, they said: O Messenger of Allah, people used to benefit from their sacrifices, carrying from them the fat and taking from them the waterskins. He said: And what is that? They said: That which you forbade of keeping the meats of the sacrifices. He said: I only forbade it because of the crowd that came; so eat, give charity, and store."
"24754","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, he said: My father informed me, Aisha informed me, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the people entered upon him in his illness visiting him, so he prayed with them sitting, so they began praying standing, so he gestured to them to sit. When he finished, he said: The imam is only made to be followed; when he bows, bow, and when he rises, rise, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting."
"24755","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, he said: My father informed me, he said: Aisha informed me, that a man said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: My mother died suddenly, and I think if she had spoken she would have given charity; does she have reward if I give charity for her? He said: Yes."
"24756","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father, and Waki, Hisham narrated to us, the meaning, he said: My father narrated to me, from Aisha, that Umm Habibah and Umm Salamah mentioned a church they saw in Abyssinia in which were images. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Those, when there was among them a righteous man and he died, they built over his grave a mosque and pictured in it those images; those are the worst of creation with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection. My father said, he said: And Waki said: They discussed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his illness, so Umm Salamah and Umm Habibah mentioned a church they saw in the land of Abyssinia."
"24757","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Sahlah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Call for me some of my companions. I said: Abu Bakr? He said: No. I said: Umar? He said: No. I said: Your cousin Ali? He said: No. She said: I said: Uthman? He said: Yes. When he came, he said: Step aside. He began confiding with him, while the color of Uthman changed. When it was the day of the house and he was besieged in it, we said: O Commander of the Believers, will you not fight? He said: No, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, covenanted to me a covenant, and I am holding myself patient upon it."
"24758","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Qays narrated to us, he said: When Aisha advanced and reached the waters of Bani Amir at night, the dogs barked. She said: What water is this? They said: The water of al-Hawab. She said: I think I am but returning. So some of those with her said: Rather advance, so the Muslims will see you, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will reconcile between them. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us one day: How will it be with one of you at whom the dogs of al-Hawab bark?"
"24759","Yahya and Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Aisha, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order the killing of the one with two stripes, saying: It afflicts the pregnancy and seeks the sight."
"24760","Yahya and Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Aisha, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a boy to chew for him, so he sat him in his lap, and he urinated upon him, so he called for water and followed it with it. Waki said: So it was followed with it, and he did not wash it."
"24761","Yahya and Waki narrated to us, from Hisham, the meaning, Yahya said: My father informed me, he said: Aisha informed me about the washing of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from janabah. She said: He would begin with his hands and wash them, Waki said: He would wash his palms three times, then perform his ablution for prayer, then run his fingers through the roots of the hair of his head, until when he thought he had reached the skin, he would scoop three scoops and pour them upon his head, then pour over the rest of his body. Ibn Numayr said: He scooped with his hands a fill of his palms three times."
"24762","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, from Aisha, she said: I never saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in any of the night prayer sitting, until when he aged, he recited sitting, until when there remained of the surah thirty or forty verses, he stood and recited them, then bowed."
"24763","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to me, from Dhakwan, the freedman of Aisha, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me with a prisoner, so I was distracted from him, and he went. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and said: What happened to the prisoner? She said: I was distracted from him with the women, so he went out. He said: What is with you, may Allah cut your hand, or your hands. So he went out and announced to the people, so they sought him and brought him. So he entered upon me while I was turning my hands. So he said: What is with you, have you gone mad? I said: You supplicated against me, so I am turning my hands, looking which of them will be cut. So he praised Allah and extolled Him, and raised his hands extended, and said: O Allah, I am a human being, I anger as a human being anger; so whichever believing man or believing woman I supplicate against, make it for him a purification and a cleansing."
"24764","Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya, from a man, from Amrah, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, kept enjoining me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir. Yahya said: I think he named Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad for me, but I forgot his name."
"24765","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, and Abdussamad, from Harb, from Yahya, from Imran ibn Hittan, that Aisha narrated to him, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not leave in his house a garment in which was a cross except that he tore it."
"24766","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, he said: Aisha narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray the two rakahs between the call and the Subh prayer."
"24767","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Musa ibn Abi Aisha narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Aisha: We forced medicine into the mouth of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his illness, so he gestured not to force medicine into me. I said: The dislike of the patient for medicine. When he recovered, he said: Did I not forbid you not to force medicine into me? He said: None of you remains except he will be forced, except al-Abbas, for he did not witness you."
"24768","Yahya narrated to us, from Abdulhamid ibn Jafar, from his father, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whatever afflicts the Muslim of anything is for him a reward and an expiation."
"24769","Yahya narrated to us, from Hatim, meaning Ibn Abi Saghirah, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad informed him, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, uncircumcised. Aisha said: O Messenger of Allah, men and women, will some of them look at others? He said: O Aisha, the matter is more severe than that it concerns them."
"24770","Rawh narrated to us, Hatim ibn Abi Saghirah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, so he mentioned the same."
"24771","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Dawud, from Azrah, from Humayd ibn Abdurrahman, from Said ibn Hisham, he said: Aisha said: We had a curtain in which was the image of a bird. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Move it, for when I see it, I remember the world. And we had a velvet cloth we used to wear; he says its emblem was silk."
"24772","Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, he said: Amrah narrated to me, she said: I heard Aisha say: A Jewish woman came to me begging me, so she said: May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, I said: O Messenger of Allah, are we punished in the graves? He said: Seeking refuge with Allah. Then he rode a mount, and the sun eclipsed. So I went out, and I was between the chambers with the women. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came from his mount, came to his prayer place, and the people prayed behind him. So he stood and prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then raised his head and prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then raised his head and prolonged the standing, then prostrated and prolonged the prostration. Then he stood shorter than his first standing, then bowed shorter than his first bowing, then stood shorter than his first standing, then bowed shorter than his first bowing, then prostrated shorter than his first prostration. So it was four bowings and four prostrations. Then the sun cleared. So he said: You are tried in the graves like the trial of the Dajjal. She said: So I heard him after that seeking refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave."
"24773","Yahya narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, that he divorced his wife, then departed to Medina to sell a property of his there and make it into weapons and horses, then fight the Romans until he dies. So he met a group of his people, and they told him that a group of his people, six, wanted that in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Do you not have in me a good example? So he forbade them that. So he made them witness his return to her. Then he returned to us and informed us that he came to Ibn Abbas and asked him about the witr. So he said: Shall I not tell you of the most knowledgeable of the people of the earth of the witr of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes. He said: Go to Aisha and ask her, then return to me and inform me of her reply to you. He said: So I came to Hakim ibn Aflah and sought him to join me to her. So he said: I am not close to her; I forbade her to say anything concerning these two parties, but she refused but to go on in them. So I swore upon him, and he came with me. So we entered upon her, so she said: Hakim? And she recognized him. He said: Yes, or rather yes. She said: Who is this with you? He said: Sad ibn Hisham. She said: Which Hisham? He said: Ibn Amir. He said: So she asked mercy for him and said: What an excellent man Amir was. I said: O Mother of the Believers, tell me of the character of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: Do you not read the Quran? I said: Yes. She said: The character of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was the Quran. So I intended to stand, then the standing of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, occurred to me. I said: O Mother of the Believers, tell me of the standing of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So she said: Do you not read this surah: O you enwrapped? I said: Yes. She said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, obligated the standing of the night at the beginning of this surah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions stood a year until their feet swelled, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, held its ending in the sky twelve months, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down the lightening at the end of this surah, so the standing of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became voluntary after its obligation. So I intended to stand, then the witr of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, occurred to me. I said: O Mother of the Believers, tell me of the witr of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: We used to prepare for him his siwak and his purification, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would send him for what He willed to send him of the night. So he would use the siwak, then perform ablution, then pray eight rakahs, not sitting in them except at the eighth. So he would sit and mention his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and supplicate and seek forgiveness, then rise and not give the taslim. Then he would pray the ninth, so he would sit and praise his Lord and mention Him and supplicate, then give the taslim, making us hear it. Then he would pray two rakahs while sitting after he gives the taslim; so that is eleven rakahs, O my son. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, aged and took flesh, he performed witr with seven, then prayed two rakahs while sitting after he gives the taslim; so that is nine, O my son. And the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prayed a prayer, loved to persist in it. And when sleep or pain or illness kept him from the standing of the night, he would pray twelve rakahs in the daytime. And I do not know the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited the whole Quran in a night, nor stood a night until morning, nor fasted a month complete other than Ramadan. So I came to Ibn Abbas and narrated to him her hadith. So he said: She told the truth; if I entered upon her, I would come to her until she speaks to me mouth to mouth."
"24774","Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Hazrah, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to me, he said: I heard Aisha say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No prayer in the presence of food, nor while repelling the two filths."
"24775","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ata narrated to me, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was not stricter in keeping to anything of the supererogatory acts than the two rakahs before the dawn."
"24776","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, he said: Abdullah ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married me in Shawwal, and I was brought to him in Shawwal; so which of his wives was more favored with him than me? And she used to like to bring her women in Shawwal."
"24777","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: I heard al-Qasim, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls. He said: And I know it only as the measure of this descending and this ascending."
"24778","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim narrating from Aisha, she said: Evil is what you have equated us with the dog and the donkey. I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying while I lay across before him; when he wanted to prostrate, he pinched my feet, meaning, so I gathered them to me, then he prostrated."
"24779","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, he said: I said to Aisha: O mother, how was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after the latter Isha? She said: Nine standing, and two sitting, and two after the two calls."
"24780","Yahya narrated to us, from Mujalid, he said: Amr narrated to me, from Masruq, he said: I said to Aisha: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say anything when he entered the house? She said: When he entered the house, he would recite: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third valley, and nothing fills his mouth but dust; and We made wealth only to establish prayer and give zakat; and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"24781","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The most hated of men is the fierce disputant."
"24782","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Musa ibn Abi Aisha, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Aisha and Ibn Abbas, that Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was dead."
"24783","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ata say: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, he said: I and Ibn Umar were leaning to the chamber of Aisha; we heard her using the siwak. I said: O Abu Abdurrahman, did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform umrah in Rajab? He said: Yes. I said: O mother, do you hear what Abu Abdurrahman says? She said: What does he say? I said: He says the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed umrah in Rajab. She said: May Allah forgive Abu Abdurrahman; he forgot; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never performed umrah in Rajab. He said: And Ibn Umar was hearing, and he said neither no nor yes; he was silent."
"24784","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: He would order me, so I would wrap my waist while menstruating, then he would touch me directly; and I would wash his head while he was secluded and I was menstruating."
"24785","Yahya narrated to us, from Zakariya, from Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril, peace be upon him, greets you with peace. She said: And upon him, and the mercy of Allah."
"24786","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Mansur narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, specify anything of the days? She said: No, his deed was continuous; and which of you can bear what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bear?"
"24787","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, and Ibn Jafar, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi, Ibn Jafar said: From a man, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The grave has a pressure; if anyone were saved from it, Sad ibn Muadh would have been saved from it."
"24788","Yahya narrated to us, from Zakariya, he said: Amr narrated to me, he said: Shurayh ibn Hani narrated to me, he said: Aisha narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him; and death is before meeting Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"24789","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim informed me, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There were among the nations muhaddathun; if there is from my nation, it is Umar."
"24790","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kissed Uthman ibn Mazun while dead, until I saw tears flowing upon his face."
"24791","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you drowses, let him sleep until sleep goes from him; for when he prays while drowsing, perhaps he goes to seek forgiveness but reviles himself."
"24792","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Medina while it was the most epidemic land of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; so Abu Bakr complained. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, make Medina beloved to us as our love of Mecca, or stronger; and make it healthy, bless for us in its mudd and its sa, and transfer its fever and make it in al-Juhfah."
"24793","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he ordered them with what they could bear of deed, they would say: O Messenger of Allah, we are not like you; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed. She said: So he would anger until anger was known in his face."
"24794","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: Sawdah went out for her need at night after the hijab had been imposed upon them. She said: And she was a woman overtopping the women, corpulent. So Umar met her and saw her, so he called her: O Sawdah, by Allah, you are not hidden from us when you go out; so see how you go out, or how you do. So she turned back and returned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was dining, and told him what Umar said to her, while in his hand was a bone with meat. So revelation came to him, then it was lifted from him, while the bone was in his hand. So he said: Permission has been given for you to go out for your needs."
"24795","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: A bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you kiss the boys? By Allah, we do not kiss them. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What do I own if Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has removed mercy from your heart?"
"24796","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten of Ramadan."
"24797","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The bed of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was of leather, its stuffing of palm fiber."
"24798","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: Sad was wounded on the day of al-Khandaq; a man of Quraysh called Hibban ibn al-Ariqah shot him in the akhal. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pitched a tent for him in the mosque to visit him from near."
"24799","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned from al-Khandaq and put down the weapons and washed, Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him with dust upon his head. He said: You have put down the weapons, but by Allah, I have not put them; go out to them. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Where? He said: Here, and pointed to Bani Qurayzah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to them. Hisham said: So my father informed me that they came down upon the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he returned the judgment concerning them to Sad. He said: I judge that the fighters be killed, the women and offspring be taken captive, and their wealth be divided. Hisham said: My father said: So I was told that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have judged among them with the judgment of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"24800","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that the Abyssinians were playing with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a day of Eid. She said: So I looked from over his shoulder, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, lowered his shoulders for me. So I kept looking at them from over his shoulder until I was satisfied, then I left."
"24801","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Abu Usamah said: Hisham informed us, the meaning, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that your people have recently abandoned disbelief, I would have demolished the Kaabah, then built it upon the foundation of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, for Quraysh, when they built it, shortened it, and I would have made a back door for it. Abu Usamah said: Khilfan."
"24802","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: I used to play with dolls, and my friends would come and play with me, and when they saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they would withdraw from him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would bring them in to me, and they would play with me."
"24803","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she borrowed a necklace from Asma, and it was lost, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent men to seek it, and they found it, and the prayer overtook them while they had no water with them, so they prayed without ablution, and they complained of that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down tayammum, and Usayd ibn Hudayr said to Aishah: May Allah reward you with good, for by Allah, no matter befell you that you dislike but Allah made for you and for the Muslims therein good."
"24804","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: A Jew from the Jews of Banu Zurayq called Labid ibn al-Asam cast a spell on the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would imagine that he did a thing while he had not done it. She said: Until, one day or one night, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated, then supplicated, then said: O Aishah, I feel that Allah, mighty and majestic, has given me a verdict concerning what I sought His verdict about. Two men came to me, and one of them sat at my head and the other at my feet, and the one at my head said to the one at my feet, or the one at my feet to the one at my head: What ails the man? He said: He is bewitched. He said: Who bewitched him? He said: Labid ibn al-Asam. He said: In what? He said: In a comb and combings and the sheath of a male spathe. He said: And where is it? He said: In the well of Arwan. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to it with some of his companions, then he came and said: O Aishah, it is as if its water is the infusion of henna, and as if its palm trees are the heads of devils. I said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you not burn it? He said: No; as for me, Allah, mighty and majestic, has cured me, and I disliked to stir up evil therefrom against the people. She said: So he commanded that it be buried."
"24805","Ibn Numayr narrated from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these supplications: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Fire and the punishment of the Fire, and the trial of the grave and the punishment of the grave, and from the evil of the trial of wealth and from the evil of the trial of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Masih, the Dajjal. O Allah, wash away my sins with the water of snow and hail, and purify my heart of sins as You purified the white garment of filth, and distance me from my sins as You distanced between the east and the west. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness and old age and sin and debt."
"24806","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: It was said to her that Ibn Umar raises to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the dead is punished by the weeping of the living. She said: Abu Abd al-Rahman blundered; he only said that the family of the dead weep over him while he is punished for his own offense."
"24807","Ibn Numayr narrated from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in his illness while sitting, and he prayed with people standing behind him, so he beckoned to them to sit, and when he finished his prayer he said: The imam is only to be followed, so when he bows then bow, and when he rises then rise, and when he prays sitting then pray sitting."
"24808","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Ghalib who said: I came to Aishah, I and Ammar and al-Ashtar, and Ammar said: Peace be upon you, O my mother. She said: Peace be upon whoever followed the guidance, until he repeated it to her two or three times, then he said: By Allah, you are indeed my mother, even if you dislike it. She said: Who is this with you? He said: This is al-Ashtar. She said: Are you the one who wanted to kill my nephew? He said: Yes, I wanted that, and he wanted it. She said: Had you done it, you would not have prospered. As for you, O Ammar, I have heard, or she said I heard, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except for one of three: except one who commits adultery after having been married, or disbelieves after having believed, or kills a soul and so is killed for it."
"24809","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, narrated to us, from Muqatil ibn Bashir, from Shurayh ibn Hani who said: I asked Aishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: There was no prayer more deserving to be delayed, when he was occupied with discourse, than the last night prayer, and he never prayed it and then came in to me but he prayed after it four or six, and I never saw him guarding himself from the ground with anything, except that I remember that on a rainy day we placed beneath him a batt, and it is as if I see a hole in it from which water was springing."
"24810","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, and he mentioned the like of it. He said: A batt, meaning a leather mat, so he prayed upon it; I indeed saw, and he mentioned its meaning."
"24811","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh al-Harithi, from his father who said: I said to Aishah: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) go out to the countryside? She said: Yes, he used to go out to these watercourses, and he once wanted the nomadic life, so he sent for some camels of charity and gave me from them a hobbled she-camel, then he said to me: O Aishah, upon you is fear of Allah, mighty and majestic, and gentleness, for gentleness was never in a thing but it adorned it, and was never removed from a thing but it disgraced it."
"24812","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sad ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Amrah informed me, she said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Breaking the bone of the believer dead is like breaking it alive."
"24813","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah who said: Revelation would descend upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a cold morning, then his forehead would pour forth with sweat."
"24814","Abu Usamah narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: I was never jealous of any woman as I was jealous of Khadijah, and she had perished three years before he married me, because of what I used to hear him mention her, and his Lord, mighty and majestic, had commanded him to give her glad tidings of a house of reed in Paradise, and he would slaughter a sheep then distribute some of it among her friends."
"24815","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the Conquest from Kada, from upper Makkah, and he entered for the Umrah from Kuda."
"24816","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Aishah who said: I was startled one night and missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I stretched my hand and it fell upon the feet of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while they were upright and he was prostrating, saying: I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; I do not reckon praise of You; You are as You praised Yourself."
"24817","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: When the news came of Jafar ibn Abi Talib and Zayd ibn Harithah and Abdullah ibn Rawahah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat with grief recognized in his face. Aishah said: And I was peeping through the crack of the door, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the women of Jafar, and he mentioned some of their weeping, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to forbid them, and the man went, then came and said: I forbade them but they did not obey him, until on the third time she claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Throw dust in their faces. Aishah said: I said: May Allah disgrace your nose; by Allah, you neither do what he told you nor leave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alone."
"24818","Ibn Numayr narrated from Talhah ibn Yahya, he said: Aishah bint Talhah narrated to me, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fondle while fasting, then place between himself and her a garment, meaning the private part."
"24819","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Nubayh, he said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire."
"24820","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love sweets and love honey, and when he prayed Asr he would visit his wives and draw near to them, and he entered upon Hafsah and stayed with her longer than he used to stay, so I asked about that, and it was said to me: A woman of her people gave her a skin of honey, and she gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) some of it to drink. I said: By Allah, we shall indeed contrive against him. I mentioned that to Sawdah and said: When he comes to you, he will draw near to you, so say to him: O Messenger of Allah, have you eaten maghafir? He will say to you: No. Say to him: What is this smell? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it hard that any odor be found from him. He will say to you: Hafsah gave me a drink of honey to drink. Say to him: Its bees grazed on urfut. And I shall say that to him, and you say it to him, O Safiyyah. When he entered upon Sawdah, Sawdah said: By Him besides whom there is no god, I was about to begin him with what you told me, while he was at the door, out of fear of you. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near, I said: O Messenger of Allah, have you eaten maghafir? He said: No. I said: Then what is this smell? He said: Hafsah gave me a drink of honey to drink. I said: Its bees grazed on urfut. When he entered upon me I said the like of that to him, then he entered upon Safiyyah and she said the like of that to him. When he entered upon Hafsah she said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not give you some of it to drink? He said: I have no need of it. Sawdah says: Glory be to Allah, by Allah we have deprived him. I said to her: Be silent."
"24821","Abu Usamah narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: When what was said about my affair was said, and I did not know of it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood concerning me as a preacher, and I did not know of it, and he testified then praised Allah, mighty and majestic, and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: To proceed, advise me concerning people who accused my family; by Allah, I never knew any evil of my family at all, and they accused them along with one of whom, by Allah, I never knew any evil at all, and he never entered my house except while I was present, and I never absented myself on a journey but he absented himself with me. Sad ibn Muadh stood and said: We deem, O Messenger of Allah, that you strike their necks. A man of the Khazraj stood, and the mother of Hassan ibn Thabit was of the kin of that man, and said: You lie; by Allah, had they been of the Aws you would not have loved that you strike their necks, until there was nearly evil between the Aws and the Khazraj in the mosque, and I did not know of it. In the evening of that day I went out for some need, with me Umm Mistah, and she stumbled and said: May Mistah perish. I said: Why do you curse your son? She was silent. She stumbled a second time and said: May Mistah perish. I said: Why do you curse your son? Then she stumbled a third time and said: May Mistah perish, so I rebuked her and said: Why do you curse your son? She said: By Allah, I only curse him on your account. I said: On account of what affair of mine? So she mentioned the report to me. I said: And has this happened? She said: Yes, by Allah. So I returned to my house, and what I had gone out for, it was as if I had not gone out for it; I found in it neither little nor much, and I fell ill, and I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Send me to the house of my father. So he sent the boy with me, and I entered the house, and there was Umm Ruman, and she said: What brought you, O my daughter? I told her, and she said: Take the matter lightly, for by Allah, seldom is there a beautiful woman with a man who loves her, and she has co-wives, but they envied her and spoke about her. I said: And my father knew of it? She said: Yes. I said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I wept with sobs. Abu Bakr heard my voice while he was above the house reciting, and he came down and said to my mother: What is her affair? She said: The mention of her matter reached her, so his eyes overflowed, and he said: I adjure you, O my daughter, but return to your house. So I returned, and my parents remained with me in the morning until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me after Asr, with my parents surrounding me on my right and on my left, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) testified and praised Allah and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: To proceed, O Aishah, if you committed evil and wronged, repent to Allah, mighty and majestic, for Allah, mighty and majestic, accepts repentance from His servants. And a woman of the Ansar had come and was sitting at the door, so I said: Are you not ashamed before this woman to say anything? I said to my father: Answer him. He said: What shall I say? I said to my mother: Answer him. She said: What shall I say? When neither answered, I testified and praised Allah, mighty and majestic, and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: To proceed, by Allah, if I say to you that I did not do it, while Allah, majestic His majesty, witnesses that I am truthful, that will not benefit me with you; you have spoken of it and your hearts have absorbed it. And if I say to you that I did it, while Allah, mighty and majestic, knows that I did not do it, you will surely say: She has confessed it against herself. By Allah, I find no likeness for me and for you except the father of Yusuf, and I do not remember his name: Beautiful patience, and Allah is sought for help against what you describe. Then revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at that hour, and it was lifted from him, and I could discern joy in his face while he wiped his forehead, saying: Rejoice, O Aishah, for Allah, mighty and majestic, has sent down your innocence. I was at my angriest as I ever was, and my parents said to me: Stand to him. I said: By Allah, I shall not stand to him, nor praise him, nor praise you; you heard it and neither denied it nor changed it, but I praise Allah who sent down my innocence. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had come to my house and asked the slave-girl about me, and she said: No, by Allah, I know no fault in her except that she would sleep until the sheep would come in and eat her leaven or her dough, Hisham doubted. One of his companions rebuked her and said: Tell the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the truth, until they prompted her with it. Urwah said: That was held against whoever said it. She said: No, by Allah, I know of her only what the goldsmith knows of pure red gold ore. That reached the man about whom it was said, and he said: Glory be to Allah, by Allah I never uncovered the covering of any female at all, and he was killed a martyr in the path of Allah. Aishah said: As for Zaynab bint Jahsh, Allah, mighty and majestic, protected her by her religion, and she said only good; as for her sister Hamnah, she perished among those who perished. Those who spoke about it were the hypocrite Abdullah ibn Ubayy, who used to spread it and gather it, and he is the one who undertook the greatest part of it, and Mistah and Hassan ibn Thabit. Abu Bakr swore never to benefit Mistah with any benefit again, so Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: And let not those of bounty and abundance among you swear, meaning Abu Bakr, to give to kin and the poor, meaning Mistah: Do you not love that Allah forgive you, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. Abu Bakr said: Yes indeed, by Allah, we love to be forgiven, and Abu Bakr resumed for Mistah what he used to do for him."
"24822","Abu Usamah narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry with me. She said: I said: From where do you know that? He said: When you are pleased with me you say: No, by the Lord of Muhammad, and when you are angry with me you say: No, by the Lord of Ibrahim, peace be upon him. I said: Yes indeed, by Allah, I abandon nothing but your name."
"24823","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command them with what they could bear, and they would say: We are not like your state; Allah, mighty and majestic, has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed. So he would become angry until that was seen in his face. He said: Then he would say: By Allah, I am indeed the most knowledgeable of you about Allah, mighty and majestic, and the most God-fearing of you of heart."
"24824","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah who said: The day of Buath was a day which Allah, mighty and majestic, brought forward for His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while their chiefs had split and their leaders had been killed, and they softened toward Allah, mighty and majestic, and toward His Messenger in their entering Islam."
"24825","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: When my innocence was sent down, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon the minbar and called them and carried out the prescribed punishment upon them."
"24826","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad and Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah who said: We had a mat which we spread by day and curtained ourselves with by night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one night, and the people of the mosque heard his prayer, and in the morning they mentioned that to the people, and the people were many on the second night, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked out at them and said: Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear, for Allah, mighty and majestic, does not tire until you tire. And Aishah said: The most beloved of deeds to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most constant of them, even if little, and when he prayed a prayer he established it firmly. And Yazid said: A mat which we spread by day and curtain by night."
"24827","Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Harith, from Abu Salamah who said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hands and showed me the moon when it rose, and said: Seek refuge in Allah from the evil of this darkness when it settles."
"24828","Yala narrated to us, Qudamah, meaning Ibn Abdullah al-Amiri, narrated to us, from Jasrah who said: Aishah narrated to me, she said: A Jewish woman came in to me and said: The torment of the grave is from urine. I said: You lie. She said: Indeed, we cut off because of it the garment and the skin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the prayer while our voices had risen, and he said: What is this? I told him what she had said, and he said: She spoke the truth. She said: After that day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never prayed a prayer but said at the end of the prayer: O Allah, Lord of Jibril and Mikail and Israfil, protect me from the heat of the Fire and the torment of the grave."
"24829","Asbat narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from the guide of al-Saib ibn Abdullah, from al-Saib who said: I entered upon Aishah, and she narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is upon half of the prayer of one standing."
"24830","Asbat narrated from al-Shaybani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted incantation for every venomous sting."
"24831","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is upon half of the prayer of one standing."
"24832","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would indeed be brought the vessel, and I would drink from it while menstruating, then he would take it and place his mouth upon the place of mine, and I would take the bone and eat from it, then he would take it and place his mouth upon the place of mine."
"24833","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Zaynab al-Sahmiyyah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution, then kiss, and pray, and not perform ablution again."
"24834","Marwan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Sayyar informed us, he said: I heard Aishah bint Talhah mentioning, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with his thigh uncovered, and Abu Bakr asked permission and he permitted him while upon his state, then Umar asked permission and he permitted him while upon his state, then Uthman asked permission and he let down his garments over himself. When they stood, I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr and Umar asked permission of you and you permitted them while upon your state, and when Uthman asked permission you let down your garments over yourself. He said: O Aishah, shall I not be shy before a man before whom, by Allah, the angels are shy?"
"24835","Marwan narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Malik al-Makki informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The little sweetness is intercourse."
"24836","Abdah ibn Sulayman al-Kilabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad who said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The tooth-stick is a purifier for the mouth, pleasing to the Lord, mighty and majestic. Abdullah ibn Muhammad said: He is called Abu Atiq."
"24837","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Fatimah bint Muhammad, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: We did not know of the burial of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until I heard the sound of the spades at the end of the night, the night of Wednesday. Muhammad said: Al-masahi are the passages."
"24838","Waki narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq who said: I asked Aishah about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I never knew him to fast a month until he broke part of it, nor to break it until he fasted part of it, until he passed on his way."
"24839","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man reciting a verse, and said: May Allah have mercy on him; he reminded me of a verse I had been made to forget."
"24840","Waki narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Abi Muzarrid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The womb-tie: whoever joins it, Allah joins him, and whoever cuts it, Allah cuts him."
"24841","Waki narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Abdullah al-Bahi, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, whoever is gentle with my nation, be gentle with him, and whoever is harsh upon them, be harsh upon him."
"24842","Waki narrated from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he gave the salutation: O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace; blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"24843","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: The people were workers of themselves, and they would come in the evening in their state, so it was said to them: If only you would wash."
"24844","He said: Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father who said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left four before Zuhr and two before Fajr in any state."
"24845","Waki narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who has an hour of the night he stands in, then sleeps through it, but there is written for him the reward of his prayer, and his sleep is a charity given in charity upon him."
"24846","Waki narrated to us, he said: Israil and my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad who said: I asked Aishah about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night, and she said: He sleeps its beginning and stands its end."
"24847","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most hateful of men to Allah is the fiercely disputatious."
"24848","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Musa ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, from a freedman of Aishah, from Aishah who said: I never looked at the private part of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at all, or: I never saw the private part of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at all."
"24849","Waki narrated to us, from Misar and Sufyan, from Maabad ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to seek an incantation against the evil eye."
"24850","Waki narrated to us, Abu al-Umays narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died without appointing anyone as successor, and had he appointed anyone as successor he would have appointed Abu Bakr or Umar."
"24851","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Rabah, from Mamar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained six months seeing that he approaches though he does not approach, then two angels came to him, and one of them sat at his head and the other at his feet, and one of them said to the other: What ails him? He said: He is bewitched. He said: Who bewitched him? He said: Labid ibn al-Asam. He said: In what? He said: In a comb and combings, in the sheath of a male spathe, in the well of Dharwan, beneath a rock. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke from his sleep and said: O Aishah, have you not seen that Allah gave me a verdict concerning what I sought His verdict about? He went to the well and commanded that it be brought out, and said: This is the well which I was shown; by Allah, it is as if its water is the infusion of henna, and as if the tops of its palm trees are the heads of devils. Aishah said: If only you, as if she meant that it be spread. He said: By Allah, Allah has cured me, and I dislike to stir up evil therefrom against the people."
"24852","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bewitched until he would imagine that he did a thing while he had not done it, until, one day while he was with her, he supplicated to Allah, mighty and majestic, and supplicated, then said: Have you felt that Allah gave me a verdict concerning what I sought His verdict about? I said: And what is that, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men came to me, and one of them sat at my head and the other at my feet, then one of them said to his companion: What ails the man? He said: He is bewitched. He said: Who bewitched him? He said: Labid ibn al-Asam, the Jew. He said: In what? He said: In a comb and combings and the sheath of a male spathe. He said: And where is it? He said: In the well of Dharwan. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the well and looked at it, with palm trees over it, then returned to Aishah and said: By Allah, it is as if its water is the infusion of henna, and as if its palm trees are the heads of devils. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then burn it? He said: No; as for me, Allah, mighty and majestic, has cured me, and I feared to stir up evil therefrom against the people."
"24853","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me alone, he read it to me while I listened, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Aishah who said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe from one vessel, of major impurity."
"24854","Sufyan narrated to us, from Misar, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give me the bone and I would gnaw it, then he would take it and place his mouth upon the place of mine, and he would give me the vessel and I would drink, then he would take it and place his mouth upon the place of mine."
"24855","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad who said: I heard al-Qasim, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Circumambulation of the House and of Safa and Marwah and the stoning of the pillars were only made for the establishment of the remembrance of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"24856","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Harun narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aishah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting: Fa-rawhun wa rayhan, raising the ra."
"24857","Yunus narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he entered upon Aishah while disputing over land, and Aishah said: O Abu Salamah, avoid land, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wrongs a span of land will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."
"24858","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while between my throat and my chin, so I never dislike the severity of death for anyone ever after what I saw of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24859","Yunus and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib, from Aishah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The believer reaches by his good character the ranks of one who stands the night and fasts the day."
"24860","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, from Musa ibn Sarjis, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while dying, with a cup in which was water, and he would put his hand into the cup then wipe his face with the water, then say: O Allah, help me against the agonies of death."
"24861","Yunus narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Hisham, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform witr with five prostrations, not sitting between them until he sat in the fifth, then gave the salutation."
"24862","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi al-Furat, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she told him that she asked the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the plague, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told her that it was a torment which Allah, mighty and majestic, sends upon whom He wills, then Allah, mighty and majestic, made it a mercy for the believers; there is no servant in whom the plague occurs and he remains in his land, patient, expecting reward, knowing that nothing befalls him but what Allah, mighty and majestic, wrote for him, but he will have like the reward of the martyr."
"24863","Yunus narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi al-Furat, narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maymun al-Saigh, from Ata, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed while she lay across before him, and said: Are they not your mothers and your sisters and your paternal aunts?"
"24864","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, his companions fell ill, and Abu Bakr and Amir ibn Fuhayrah, freedman of Abu Bakr, and Bilal fell ill, so Aishah asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to visit them, and he permitted her. She said to Abu Bakr: How do you find yourself? He said: Every man is greeted in the morning among his family, while death is nearer than the strap of his sandal. She asked Amir, and he said: I found death before tasting it; the coward, his death is from above him. She asked Bilal, and he said: Would that I knew whether I shall spend a night in Fajj with idhkhir and jalil around me. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of their speech, and he looked to the heaven and said: O Allah, make Madinah beloved to us as You made Makkah beloved to us, and more strongly; O Allah, bless for us its sa and its mudd, and transfer its fever to Mahyaah, which is al-Juhfah, as they claimed."
"24865","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Umarah ibn Abi Farwah, that Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to him, that Urwah narrated to him, that Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, that Aishah narrated to her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave-girl commits adultery, flog her, and if she commits adultery, flog her, and if she commits adultery, flog her, then sell her even for a rope, and the rope is the dafir."
"24866","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say takbir in the two Eids seven and five before the recitation."
"24867","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Sulayman narrated to me, that Muhammad ibn Abi Salih narrated to him, from his father, that he heard Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor, and the caller to prayer is entrusted; so may Allah guide the imam and pardon the caller to prayer."
"24868","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Musa ibn Said ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Khubayb ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Menstruation came upon me at night while I was beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I withdrew. He said: What is with you, have you begun to menstruate? She said: No, but I menstruated. He said: Tie your waist-wrapper over yourself, then return."
"24869","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud therein, meaning in the eclipse."
"24870","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Make part of your prayers in your houses, and do not make them graves upon yourselves."
"24871","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Khadijah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Waraqah ibn Nawfal, and he said: I saw him in a dream, and I saw white garments upon him, so I reckon that had he been of the people of the Fire, white garments would not have been upon him."
"24872","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr informed me, that Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to him, that Yazid ibn Abi Yazid narrated to him, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man recited this verse: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it. He said: We are indeed recompensed for all our deeds; we perish then. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Yes, the believers are recompensed thereby in this world: a calamity in his body, in what harms him."
"24873","Harun ibn Maruf and Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr informed us, that Abu al-Nadr narrated to him, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughing heartily at all. Muawiyah said: Laughter, until I see his uvula from him; he only used to smile. And she said: When he saw a cloud or wind, that was recognized in his face. She said: O Messenger of Allah, the people, when they see a cloud, rejoice, hoping that rain be in it, and I see you, when you see it, I recognize dislike in your face. She said: He said: O Aishah, what secures me that torment be in it? A people were tormented by wind, and a people saw the torment and said: This is a cloud bringing us rain."
"24874","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Huyayy ibn Abdullah narrated to us, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that menstruation came upon her at night while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, so she signaled to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a garment in which was blood, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) signaled to her while in prayer: Wash it. So she washed the place of blood, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took that garment and prayed in it."
"24875","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forbidden by suckling is what is forbidden by birth."
"24876","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void; if he has intercourse with her, she has her dowry for what was attained of her private part, and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"24877","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A disbeliever of the disbelievers of Quraysh would die, and his family would weep for him, saying: The feeder of bowls, the fighter who, and Allah increases him in torment by what they say."
"24878","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, that he heard Urwah narrating, from Aishah who said: A man was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with good, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you not seen him learning the Quran?"
"24879","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, that he heard Urwah narrating, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: My soul is wicked, but let him say: My soul is languid."
"24880","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad informing, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no good in the congregation of women except in a mosque or a funeral."
"24881","Surayj narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: When ten of Ramadan remained, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would tighten his waist-wrapper and seclude himself from his family."
"24882","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, keeper of the pomegranates, from Abu Mijlaz, from al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Aishah, that she was asked about major impurity. She said: I used to rub major impurity from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24883","Hasan and Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abi Imran narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Do you know who are the foremost to the shade of Allah, mighty and majestic, on the Day of Resurrection? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Those who, when given the truth, accept it, and when asked for it, give it, and judge for people as they judge for themselves."
"24884","Abu Muawiyah, Abdullah ibn Muawiyah al-Zubayri, who came to us in Makkah, narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, he said: Urwah used to say to Aishah: O my mother, I am not amazed at your understanding; I say: Wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and daughter of Abu Bakr. And I am not amazed at your knowledge of poetry and the days of the people; I say: Daughter of Abu Bakr, and he was the most knowledgeable of people, or among the most knowledgeable of people. But I am amazed at your knowledge of medicine: how is it, and from where is it? He said: So she struck his shoulder and said: O little Urayyah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fall ill at the end of his life, or in the last of his life, and delegations of the Arabs would come to him from every direction and prescribe remedies for him, and I would treat him with them; so from there."
"24885","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Usamah, from Abdullah ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, and His angels, upon them be peace, bless those who join the rows."
"24886","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray with a cloak over him, and part of it over me."
"24887","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, who said: We asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for jihad, and he said: Your jihad, or: sufficient for you, is the Hajj."
"24888","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Aishah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, all your family entered the House except me. He said: Send to Shaybah that he open the door for you. She sent to him, and Shaybah said: We could not open it at night, in ignorance nor in Islam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in the Hijr, for your people fell short of building the House when they built it."
"24889","Abu al-Mundhir, Ismail ibn Umar, narrated to us, he said: Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar, from Abu Yunus, freedman of Aishah, from Aishah, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the prayer overtakes me while I am in major impurity, while I want to fast. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And the prayer overtakes me while I am in major impurity, while I want to fast, so I wash then fast. The man said: We are not like you, for Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said: By Allah, I hope to be the most fearful of you of Allah, mighty and majestic, and the most knowledgeable of you of what I guard against."
"24890","Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Fudayl ibn Abi Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Niyar al-Aslami, from Urwah, from Aishah, that a man followed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I follow you to gain with you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you believe in Allah and His Messenger? He said: No. He said: We do not seek the help of a polytheist. He said: Then he said to him the second time: Do you believe in Allah and His Messenger? He said: Yes. So he went along and followed him."
"24891","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Simak, from Abdullah ibn Umayrah, from Durrah bint Abi Lahab who said: I was with Aishah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: Bring me ablution water. I asked, and I and Aishah raced to the jug. She said: I outstripped her and took it myself, and he performed ablution, then raised the corner of his eye, or his eye, or his sight, to me and said: You are from me and I am from you. She said: A man was brought, and he said: I did not do it, but it was said to me. She said: And he had asked him upon the minbar: Who are the best of people? He said: The most understanding of them in the religion of Allah, mighty and majestic, and the most joining of them to his kin. And Sharik mentioned therein two other things which I did not memorize."
"24892","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Abu Lubabah al-Uqayli who said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until we said: He does not intend to break, and break until we said: He does not intend to fast, and he would recite every night Bani Israil and al-Zumar."
"24893","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not perform ablution after the bath."
"24894","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Yazid ibn Murrah, from Lamīs, from Aishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would mix, in the first twenty, sleep and prayer; when the last ten entered, he exerted himself and tightened the waist-wrapper."
"24895","Aswad narrated to us, Hasan narrated to us, from Ashath, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Umm Kulthum, from Aishah who said: We did it once and washed, meaning one who has intercourse and does not ejaculate."
"24896","Aswad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: O Allah, You made good my form, so make good my character."
"24897","Aswad narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Upon you is the House, for it is your jihad."
"24898","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This world is green and sweet; whoever We give something of it with generosity from us and wholesome food and without craving, it is blessed for him therein, and whoever We give something of it without generosity from us and unwholesome food and with craving from him, it is not blessed for him therein."
"24899","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah who said: When Sawdah grew old, she gave her day to me, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would apportion for me on her day along with his wives. She said: And she was the first woman he married after her."
"24900","Aswad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, his companions came in to visit him, and they stood, so he beckoned to them to sit. When he finished his prayer he said: The imam is to be followed; when he says takbir, say takbir, and when he bows, bow, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting, and when he prays standing, pray standing."
"24901","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia narrated to me, and Yahya ibn Ishaq said: Ibn Lahia informed us, from Khalid, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place his head in my lap while I was menstruating, and he would recite the Quran."
"24902","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Ishaq said: Ibn Lahia informed us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who are the foremost to the shade of Allah, mighty and majestic, on the Day of Resurrection. They said: Allah, mighty and majestic, and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) know best. He said: Those who, when given the truth, accept it, and when asked for it, give it, and they judge for people as they judge for themselves."
"24903","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia informed us, and Qutayba ibn Said said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: Bilal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so woman has died and found rest. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said: Only one who enters Paradise finds rest. Qutayba said: One who is forgiven."
"24904","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: Nothing of this world amazed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no one ever amazed him except one possessed of piety."
"24905","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia informed us, and Musa ibn Dawud said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwa, from Aisha, that she asked the Messenger of Allah, and Musa said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies owing fasts. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: His guardian fasts on his behalf."
"24906","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Haywa informed me, Salim, that he presented this hadith to Yazid and he recognized it, that Urwa ibn al-Zubayr said: Aisha informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any deceased who dies owing fasts, his guardian shall fast on his behalf."
"24907","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia informed us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa and al-Qasim, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not delighted by anything, nor did anything of this world delight him, except that there be in it one possessed of piety."
"24908","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, he said: Abdullah said: And I heard it from al-Hakam, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, he said: My father said, and he mentioned it from his mother Amra, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest."
"24909","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, he said: My father mentions it from his mother, from Aisha, she said: A woman entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, I and my son bought the fruit of the property of so-and-so, and we counted it and gathered it. No, by Him who honored you with what He honored you with, we obtained nothing from it except something we eat in our stomachs or feed to a poor person hoping for blessing, yet we fell short to him. So we came to ask him to remit what we fell short. And he swore by Allah he would remit nothing for us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He swore he would not do good, three times. He said: That reached the owner of the dates, so he came to him and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, if you wish I remit what they fell short, and if you wish, from the capital whatever you wish. So he remitted what they fell short. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from al-Hakam."
"24910","Al-Hakam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, and my father said: He mentions it from his mother, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out without adornment. Aisha said: Had he seen their condition today, he would have prevented them."
"24911","Al-Hakam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, from his father, from Amra, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not sell your fruits until their soundness appears and they are safe from blight."
"24912","Aswad said: Huraym ibn Sufyan al-Bajali narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha, she said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Do you kiss children. He said: By Allah, we do not kiss them. He said: I cannot help if Allah, mighty and majestic, has removed mercy from you."
"24913","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia informed us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say the takbir in the two Eids seven times in the first raka and five times in the last, besides the two takbirs of bowing."
"24914","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from his father, from Khalid ibn Salama al-Makhzumi, from al-Bahi, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to remember Allah, mighty and majestic, in all his states."
"24915","Husayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Qays ibn Wahb, from an old man of Banu Suwata, he said: I asked Aisha, I said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was junub and washed his head with a washing, would he suffice with that, or would he pour water over his head. She said: Rather, he would pour water over his head."
"24916","Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaida narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Masruq, from Aisha, she said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about turning glances in prayer, and he said: It is a snatching which Satan snatches from the prayer of the servant."
"24917","Muawiya narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with a garment on, part of it over me."
"24918","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muslim, meaning Ibn Khalid, narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, he said: Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad informed me, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah, mighty and majestic, puts in charge of anything of the affairs of the Muslims, and He intends good for him, He appoints for him a truthful minister; if he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him."
"24919","Al-Khuzai and Abu Said said: Said ibn Muslim ibn Banak narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Awf ibn al-Harith, al-Khuzai said: The son of the brother of Aisha by her mother, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aisha, beware of belittled sins, for they have a seeker from Allah, mighty and majestic."
"24920","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Layth informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Musa ibn Sarjis, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was dying, and with him was a cup in which was water, and he would put his hand in it and wipe his face with it and say: O Allah, help me against the agonies of death."
"24921","Al-Khuzai narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The makers of these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"24922","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Ibn Abi Shayba, he said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Urwa, from Aisha, that a beggar asked, she said: So I ordered the servant and he brought out something for him, she said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O Aisha, do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Ibn Abi Shayba."
"24923","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Duwayd narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zura, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is the home of one who has no home, and the wealth of one who has no wealth, and for it gathers one who has no sense."
"24924","Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, that he heard Aisha say: A crescent and a crescent would pass us, and no fire would be kindled in any house of the houses of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: O aunt, upon what then did you live. She said: Upon the two black ones, dates and water."
"24925","Husayn narrated to us, Duwayd narrated to us, from Abu Sahl, from Sulayman ibn Ruman, freedman of Urwa, from Urwa, from Aisha, that she said: By Him who sent Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the truth, he never saw a sieve, nor did he eat sifted bread, from when Allah, mighty and majestic, sent him until he was taken. I said: How did you eat barley. She said: We would say: Uff."
"24926","Husayn narrated to us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Ata, narrated to us, from Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Amra, from Aisha bint Talha, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, she said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not go out and strive with you. He said: No, your striving is the accepted Hajj, and it is striving for you."
"24927","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Ansari, he said, and he praised him well, he said: Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, that Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever a farq of it intoxicates when you drink it, a handful of it is unlawful."
"24928","Abu Tumayla Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: I saw Abu Uthman Amr ibn Sulaym judging at his door. My father said: And he is the one from whom Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated, and Mutarrif ibn Tarif, Rabi ibn Sabih, and Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated from him."
"24929","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabia, from Aisha, she said: I missed him in the night, and behold he was at al-Baqi, and he said: Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people, and you precede us, and we shall join you. O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward, nor test us after them, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24930","He said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, from al-Saib, from Aisha, she raised it, she said: He said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing, other than cross-legged."
"24931","Haytham ibn Kharija narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Maysara narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, mighty and majestic, intends good for the people of a house, He brings gentleness into them."
"24932","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Husayn narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, he said: And he informed me that Umm Bakr informed him that Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the woman who sees what causes her doubt after purity: It is only a vein, or he said: veins."
"24933","He said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Safar narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Aisha, she said: He, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would wake junub, then wash, then go out to prayer, and I would hear his recitation, and he would fast."
"24934","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Salama say: I and the foster brother of Aisha entered upon Aisha, and her brother asked her about the washing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she called for a vessel of about a sa, and washed, and poured over her head three times, with the veil between us and her."
"24935","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Sukhayr, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Declare unlawful by suckling what you declare unlawful by birth."
"24936","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun informed me, Abu Uthman al-Ansari narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever a farq of it intoxicates, a handful of it is unlawful."
"24937","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Kaysan informed me, from Amina al-Qaysiyya, she said: I heard Aisha say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not drink except from what has been tied shut."
"24938","Arim narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Malik, from Abu al-Jawza, from Aisha, that she was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and she cursed a camel of hers. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that it be sent back, and said: Nothing cursed shall accompany me."
"24939","Musa ibn Dawud and al-Ashyab said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, and Ishaq ibn Isa said: Ibn Lahia narrated to me, al-Ashyab said: Khalid ibn Abi Imran narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place his head in her lap while she was menstruating, and recite the Quran."
"24940","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Yazid ibn Babanus, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning a man who is intimate with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: For him is what is above the waist-wrapper."
"24941","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwa, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set up a pulpit for Hassan in the mosque, with which he would defend him with poetry. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: Allah, mighty and majestic, supports Hassan with Ruh al-Qudus, defending His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24942","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, the like of it."
"24943","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Qasim, meaning Ibn al-Fadl, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Aisha used to take debts, and it was said to her: What is with you and debt. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no servant who has an intention to repay his debt except that he has help from Allah, mighty and majestic. So I seek that help."
"24944","Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from a man who narrated to him, from Aisha, she said: Three things of this world appealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): food, women, and perfume. So he obtained two and did not obtain one: he obtained women and perfume, and did not obtain food."
"24945","Husayn narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no person who has a prayer at night, then sleep overcomes him, except that Allah, mighty and majestic, writes for him the reward of his prayer, and that sleep of his is charity."
"24946","Husayn said: Abu Uways narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Amra, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and heard the voice of a boy crying, and said: What is with this boy of yours crying; why do you not seek ruqya for him against the evil eye."
"24947","Sulayman ibn Dawud and Husayn said: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Amr informed me, from Habib ibn Hind al-Aslami, from Urwa, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes the first seven, he is a scholar."
"24948","Husayn said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And this, I see that in it is: from his father, from al-Araj, but thus it was in the book, and I do not know whether my father omitted it or it is thus mursal."
"24949","Sulayman said: Ismail informed us, he said: Abu Suhayl informed me, from his father, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the odd nights of the last ten."
"24950","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, that Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, he said: I asked Aisha: How was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan. She said: He would not exceed in Ramadan nor in other than it eleven rakas. He would pray four, so do not ask about their length and their beauty. Then he would pray four, so do not ask about their beauty and their length. Then he would pray three. Aisha said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you sleep before you pray witr. He said: O Aisha, my eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep."
"24951","Ishaq said: Malik informed me, from Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn Qusayt, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from his mother, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the skins of dead animals be used when tanned."
"24952","Ishaq said: Malik informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Yunus, freedman of Aisha, he said: Aisha ordered me to write a mushaf for her. She said: When you reach this verse: Guard the prayers and the middle prayer, then inform me. When I reached it, I informed her, and she dictated to me: Guard the prayers and the middle prayer and the Asr prayer, and stand for Allah devoutly. She said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24953","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abu Hazrata al-Qass narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Abi Atiq, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall pray in the presence of food, nor while repelling the two filths."
"24954","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Jafar al-Zuhri, of the family of al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, narrated to me, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does a matter not of our command, it is rejected."
"24955","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abi al-Zinad, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The bedding of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leather, and its stuffing was palm fiber."
"24956","Ishaq narrated to us, Dawud, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when we had eaten our fill of the two black ones, water and dates."
"24957","Ishaq said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to me, he said: Muawiya ibn Salih al-Hadrami narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Qays, he said: I asked Aisha: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray witr at the beginning of the night or at its end. She said: He would do all of that; sometimes he would pray witr at the beginning of the night, and sometimes he would pray witr at its end. I said: Praise be to Allah who made latitude in the matter. I said: How was his recitation; would he recite softly or aloud. She said: He would do all of that; sometimes he would recite softly, and sometimes he would recite aloud. He said: I said: Praise be to Allah who made latitude in the matter. He said: I said: How would he act in janaba; would he wash before sleeping, or sleep before washing. She said: He would do all of that; sometimes he would wash and sleep, and sometimes he would perform ablution and sleep. He said: I said: Praise be to Allah who made latitude in the matter."
"24958","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdillah, he said: Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: There is no prophet except that his soul is taken, then he sees the reward, then it is returned to him, and he is given choice between being returned to him until he joins. I had memorized that from him. When I was supporting him against my chest, I looked at him until his neck leaned, and I said: He has passed away. She said: Then I recognized what he had said, and I looked at him until he raised himself and looked. She said: I said: Then, by Allah, he will not choose us. And he said: With the Highest Companion in Paradise, with those upon whom Allah bestowed favor among the prophets and the truthful, to the end of the verse."
"24959","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salama, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my community bears a debt, then strives to repay it, then dies without repaying it, I am his guardian."
"24960","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak narrated to me, from his mother, from Muadha, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed four rakas of Duha in my house."
"24961","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Muammil narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aisha, the first of people to perish are your people. She said: I said: May Allah make me ransom for you, the sons of Taym. He said: No, but this tribe of Quraysh; deaths deem them sweet, and the first of people to perish are relieved from them. I said: What remains of people after them. He said: They are the core of people; when they perish, people perish."
"24962","Musa said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: Jabir informed me that Umm Kulthum informed him that Aisha informed her that she and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that, then they washed from it one day."
"24963","Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed us, from Jabir, that Umm Kulthum informed him that Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned its meaning."
"24964","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer from when the sun rises until it is high, and from when it declines until it sets."
"24965","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, and Abu al-Nadr, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray between the last Isha prayer and Fajr eleven rakas, giving salams in each two, and praying witr with one, and he would prostrate in his supererogatory prayer as long as one of you recites fifty verses before raising his head. When the muadhdhin fell silent after the first of his adhan, he would stand and pray two light rakas, then lie on his right side until the muadhdhin would come to him and go out with him."
"24966","Sufyan narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Abu Salama, from Aisha, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his hands on the mane of a horse, talking to a man. I said: I saw you placing your hands on the mane of the horse of Dihya al-Kalbi, talking to him. He said: And did you see. She said: Yes. He said: That was Jibril, peace be upon him, and he sends you greetings of peace. She said: And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; may Allah reward him well, a companion and a guest; what an excellent companion and what an excellent guest. Sufyan said: Al-dakhil is the guest."
"24967","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Hittan al-Sadusi, from Aisha, that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there striving upon women. He said: Hajj and Umra is the striving of women."
"24968","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Ala al-Shanni, of Abd al-Qays, narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Sarj narrated to me, Imran ibn Hittan narrated to me, he said: I entered upon Aisha and discussed with her until we mentioned the judge. Aisha said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will come upon the just judge on the Day of Resurrection an hour in which he will wish he had never judged between two, even concerning a date."
"24969","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran informed us, from Qatada, from Zurara, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying to a man: What is your name. He said: Shihab. He said: You are Hisham."
"24970","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fadala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Aisha, if only we had someone to talk to us. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not send for Abu Bakr. Then he was silent. Then he said: If only we had someone to talk to us. I said: Shall I not send for Umar. Then he was silent. She said: Then he called a servant before him and confided to him, and he went. She said: Then Uthman sought permission, and he permitted him, and he entered, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conversed with him privately at length. Then he said: O Uthman, Allah, mighty and majestic, will clothe you with a shirt; if the hypocrites want you to remove it, do not remove it for them, nor any dignity. He said it to him two or three times."
"24971","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq narrated to me that Dhakwan Abu Salih informed him that Aisha informed him, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was crying. He said to me: What makes you cry. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I remembered the Dajjal and wept. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Dajjal emerges while I am alive, I will suffice you against him. And if the Dajjal emerges after me, then your Lord, mighty and majestic, is not one-eyed. He will emerge in the Jewry of Isfahan until he comes to Medina and alights at its outskirts, and on that day it has seven gates, upon each pass of them two angels. The worst of its people will go out to him, until Sham, a city in Palestine, at the gate of Ludd. Abu Dawud once said: Until he comes to Palestine, the gate of Ludd. Then Isa, peace be upon him, will descend and kill him. Then Isa, peace be upon him, will remain on earth forty years, a just leader and an equitable judge."
"24972","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, he said: Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Circumambulation of the Kaba, and between al-Safa and al-Marwa, and stoning the pillars were only instituted to establish the remembrance of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"24973","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Habib al-Muallim narrated to us, from Yazid Abu al-Muhazzim, from Abu Hurayra, from Aisha, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning the hems of women, he said: A span. She said: I said: Then their shins will show. He said: Then a cubit."
"24974","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a hardship that will be before the Dajjal. They said: What wealth is best that day. He said: A strong youth who gives his family water to drink. As for food, there is none. They said: What is the food of the believers that day. He said: Glorification, sanctification, praise, and proclaiming oneness. Aisha said: Where are the Arabs that day. He said: The Arabs that day are few."
"24975","Abd al-Samad and Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, Affan said: al-Mana informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among a group of the Emigrants and the Helpers, and a camel came and prostrated to him. His companions said: O Messenger of Allah, beasts and trees prostrate to you, so we are more entitled to prostrate to you. He said: Worship your Lord and honor your brother. Had I been one to order anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have ordered the woman to prostrate to her husband. Had he ordered her to carry from a yellow mountain to a black mountain, and from a black mountain to a white mountain, it would befit her to do it."
"24976","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Qatada narrated to us, from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand in the inaba prayer and bow three bowings, then prostrate, then bow three bowings, then prostrate."
"24977","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwa, from Aisha, that she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the prayer place and said the takbir, and the people said the takbir. Then he recited and recited aloud and lengthened the standing. Then he bowed and lengthened the bowing. Then he raised his head and said: Allah hears him who praises Him. Then he stood and recited and lengthened the recitation. Then he bowed and lengthened the bowing. Then he raised his head. Then he prostrated. Then he stood and did in the second the like of that. Then he said: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah, mighty and majestic; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life. When they do that, hasten to prayer."
"24978","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Hawdha al-Qurayi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Umm Hilal narrated to him that she heard Aisha say: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) see clouds except that I saw agitation in his face; when it rained, he calmed."
"24979","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night, and I thought he would go to one of his women, so I followed him, and he went to the graves. Then he said: Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people, and we shall join you. O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward, nor test us after them. She said: Then he turned and saw me, and said: Woe to her, had she been able, she would not have done."
"24980","He said: Sharik mentioned it another time, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"24981","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Asim, and Ali ibn Ishaq said: Abdillah informed us, he said: Asim informed us, from Muadha, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek permission when it was the day of the woman among us, after this verse was revealed: You defer whom you will of them and take to yourself whom you will, and whomever you seek of those you set aside, there is no blame upon you. She said: I said to her: What would you say to him. She said: I would say to him: If that is up to me, I do not wish, O Messenger of Allah, to prefer anyone over you."
"24982","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, and Ali ibn Ishaq said: Abdillah informed us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aisha, that Sawda said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given my day to Aisha. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would divide her day for her."
"24983","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Usama ibn Zayd, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Urwa, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of the blessing of a woman is the ease of her proposal, the ease of her dowry, and the ease of her womb."
"24984","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abdillah narrated to me, from Musa ibn Sarjis, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever eats with his left, Satan eats with him, and whoever drinks with his left, Satan drinks with him."
"24985","Mansur ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Amr, from al-Muttalib ibn Hantab, that Abdillah ibn Amir sent to Aisha maintenance and clothing. She said to the messenger: I, my son, do not accept anything from anyone. When he went out, she said: Bring him back to me. So they brought him back, and she said: I remembered something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me. He said: O Aisha, whoever gives you a gift unasked, accept it, for it is provision Allah offers you."
"24986","Mansur ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Layth informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Musa ibn Sarjis, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was dying, and with him was a cup in which was water, and he would put his hand in it and wipe his face with it and say: O Allah, help me against the agonies of death."
"24987","Mansur ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Layth informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, or was taken, or died, while he was between my chest and my chin. So I never dislike the severity of death for anyone ever after what I saw of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24988","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from his father, that Urwa ibn al-Zubayr narrates to him, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Fatima, his daughter, and confided to her, and she wept. Then he confided to her, and she laughed. Aisha said: I said to Fatima: What is this that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confided to you, so you wept, then he confided to you and you laughed. She said: He confided to me and informed me of his death, so I wept. Then he confided to me and informed me that I am the first of his family to follow him, so I laughed."
"24989","Mansur ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, informed us, from Sharik ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Namir, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the dates of al-Aliya is healing, or he said: an antidote, first thing in the morning on an empty stomach."
"24990","Abu Salama narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, he said: Sakhr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmala narrated to us, he said: Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to them: Your affair is among what concerns me after me, and none will persevere with you except the persevering. Qutayba said: Sakhr ibn Abdillah."
"24991","Abu Salama narrated to us, Khalid ibn Sulayman al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Urwa, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sat in a gathering or prayed, would speak words. Aisha asked him about the words, and he said: If he speaks good, they are a seal upon them until the Day of Resurrection, and if he speaks other than that, they are expiation: Glory be to You and with Your praise, there is no god but You, I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him."
"24992","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Aisha, she said: When the verse of choice was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: O Aisha, I want to mention a matter to you, so decide nothing in it without your parents. She said: What is it. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and recited to me this verse: O Prophet, say to your wives: If you desire Allah and His Messenger and the Last Abode, the whole verse. She said: I said: I have chosen Allah, mighty and majestic, and His Messenger. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoiced at that."
"24993","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Aisha, she said: I would sleep with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one bed, while I was menstruating, with a garment on me."
"24994","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa narrated to me, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a prostration of Asr before the sun sets, and of Fajr before the sun rises, has caught it."
"24995","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr informed us, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to enter ihram, he would wash with khitmi and shinan, and oil with something of oil, not much. She said: And we performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Hajj, and he gave Umra to his women and left me, and I felt in myself that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Umra to his women and left me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave Umra to your women and left me. He said to Abd al-Rahman: Go out with your sister, let her perform Umra; circumambulate her around the House and al-Safa and al-Marwa, then let her finish, then bring her to me before I depart on the night of al-Hasba. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed at al-Hasba only for my sake."
"24996","Harun narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: And Haywa said: Abu Sakhr informed me, from Ibn Qusayt, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a horned ram that steps in blackness, looks in blackness, and kneels in blackness. It was brought for him to sacrifice with it. Then he said: O Aisha, bring the knife. Then he said: Sharpen it with a stone. She did so. Then he took it and took the ram and laid it down, then slaughtered it, and said: In the name of Allah; O Allah, accept from Muhammad and the family of Muhammad and from the community of Muhammad. Then he sacrificed with it (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24997","Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Aflah narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: I twisted the necklaces of the sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he collared them and marked them, then directed them to the House, and stayed in Medina, and nothing that was lawful for him became unlawful for him."
"24998","Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out swiftly from al-Batha on the night of departure."
"24999","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utba narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salama, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to marry one of his daughters, he would sit at her curtain and say: So-and-so mentions so-and-so, naming her and naming the man who mentions her. If she remained silent, he would marry her, and if she disliked, she would knock the curtain; when she knocked it, he would not marry her."
"25000","Abdullah said: I found this hadith in the book of my father in his handwriting: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Taymi, and he is al-Ayshi, narrated to us, he said: Hammad informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, they weep over him, yet he is punished in his grave for his sin."
"25001","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: A man sneezed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What should I say, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say: Praise be to Allah. The people said: What should we say to him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say to him: May Allah have mercy on you. He said: What should I say to them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say to them: May Allah guide you and set right your affairs."
"25002","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, he said: Aishah bint Talhah narrated to us that Aishah, Mother of the Believers, said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, shall we not strive in jihad with you? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: For you is the best and most beautiful jihad: Hajj, an accepted Hajj. So Aishah said: I will never abandon Hajj after I heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25003","Yunus narrated to us: Fulayh narrated to us, from Salih ibn Ajlan, from Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: When Sa'd died and his funeral was brought, Aishah ordered that he be passed by her, so he was taken through the mosque, and she supplicated for him. That was disapproved to her, so she said: How quick people are to speak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over Ibn Bayda except in the mosque."
"25004","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah and Salih ibn Ajlan, from Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that she ordered that the funeral of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas be passed by her, so it was passed by her. It reached her that something was said about that, so she said: How quick people are to speak. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over Suhayl ibn Bayda except in the mosque."
"25005","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to us, from Umm Kulthum, from Aishah, she said: When it was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that so-and-so is sick and does not eat food, he said: You should take talbinah, so give it to him to sip. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it washes the belly of one of you just as one of you washes his face with water from dirt."
"25006","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O Aishah, shield yourself from the Fire even with half a date, for it fills the need of the hungry as it does that of the full."
"25007","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Suwayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Aishah bint Talhah mention, and the muhrim wearing perfume was mentioned in her presence, so she mentioned from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, that they used to go out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with bandages of perfume upon them, having applied the bandage before entering ihram, then they would bathe while it was upon them, sweating and bathing, and he did not forbid them from it."
"25008","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Hawdhah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his paternal aunt, that Aishah narrated to her, she said: I never saw agitation in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he would see clouds. Then when those clouds rained, that agitation would go away."
"25009","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, he said, and Yahya said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me that Abu Salamah narrated to him, and there was between him and some people a dispute over land, and that he entered upon Aishah and mentioned that to her. So she said: O Abu Salamah, avoid the land, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wrongs even a handspan of land will be collared with it from seven earths."
"25010","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Masruq, from Aishah, that a man was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: What an evil servant of Allah, the brother of the clan. Then he entered upon him, and he began speaking to him. Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn to him with his face until I thought he had a standing with him."
"25011","Hasan narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Yuhannas, that Aishah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer, they would come to them even crawling."
"25012","Hashim narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath, he said: Abdullah ibn Ma'qil al-Muharibi narrated to me, he said: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that nabidh be made in gourds, green jars, and pitch-coated vessels."
"25013","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Thawr, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Aishah, that she was asked about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He used to fast Sha'ban and aim to fast Monday and Thursday."
"25014","Abdullah said: I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting: Muhammad ibn Humayd Abu Sufyan narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to aim to fast Sha'ban and to fast Monday and Thursday."
"25015","Hashim narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The makers of these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"25016","Hashim narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, the like of that."
"25017","Hashim narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: When one of her family was afflicted and the women of the company dispersed from her and there remained the women of her close family, she would order a pot of talbinah, so it was cooked, then she would order tharid, so it was crumbled, and she would pour the talbinah over the tharid. Then she said: Eat from it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Talbinah comforts the heart of the sick and removes some of the grief."
"25018","Hashim narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Abi Humayd al-Ansari, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his illness from which he did not recover: May Allah curse the Jews and the Christians, for they took the graves of their prophets as mosques. She said: Had it not been for that, his grave would have been made prominent, except that it was feared it would be taken as a mosque."
"25019","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Muslim narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that a man bought a slave boy, profited from him, then found or saw a defect in him, so he returned him on account of the defect. The seller said: The profit of my slave. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Profit belongs to the guarantor."
"25020","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yahya al-Ghassani, he said: I came to Medina and met Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, and he was governor over Medina. He said: A thief was brought to me, so my maternal aunt Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman sent to me: Do not hasten in the matter of this man until I come to you and inform you what I heard from Aishah concerning the thief. He said: So she came to me and informed me that she heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cut off for a quarter of a dinar, and do not cut off for what is less than that. And a quarter of a dinar at that time was three dirhams, and the dinar was twelve dirhams. He said: And his theft was less than a quarter of a dinar, so I did not cut him."
"25021","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Yahya, from Salim, the freedman of Daws, that he heard Aishah say to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr: Perform ablution fully, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"25022","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'ahs between the call and the iqama of the Fajr prayer."
"25023","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from his father, he said: It was said to Aishah: O Mother of the Believers, this month was sighted at twenty-nine. She said: What amazes you of that? I never fasted with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty-nine more than I fasted thirty."
"25024","Hashim narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me saying: O Aishah, your people are the quickest of my nation to join me. She said: When he sat, I said: O Messenger of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom, you entered saying words that frightened me. He said: What is it? She said: You claim that my people are the quickest of your nation to join you. He said: Yes. She said: And why is that? He said: Deaths deem them sweet, and their nation envies them. She said: So I said: How will people be after that, or at that time? He said: Locusts, whose strong eat their weak, until the Hour rises over them. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: A man explained it: they are the locusts whose wings have not grown."
"25025","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Aishah, that a Jewish woman used to serve her, and whenever Aishah did her any kindness, the Jewish woman would say to her: May Allah shield you from the torment of the grave. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there torment of the grave before the Day of Resurrection? He said: No, and why is that? She said: This Jewish woman, whenever we do her any kindness, says: May Allah shield you from the torment of the grave. He said: The Jews have lied, and they lie against Allah, Mighty and Majestic; there is no torment before the Day of Resurrection. She said: Then he remained after that as long as Allah willed to remain. Then one day at midday he came out wrapped in his garment with reddened eyes, calling out at the top of his voice: O people, trials have shaded you like pieces of the dark night. O people, if you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little. O people, seek refuge in Allah from the torment of the grave, for the torment of the grave is true."
"25026","Hashim and Yunus narrated to us, they said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: I would enter the house for some need while the sick person was in it, and I would not ask about him except in passing. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would put his head into my room while he was in the mosque, and I would comb it. And he would not enter the house except for some need. Yunus said: When he was in retreat."
"25027","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Barirah came to Aishah seeking her help in her contract of manumission, and she had not paid any of her contract. So Aishah said to her: Go back to your family; if they like that I pay your contract on your behalf and your loyalty belongs to me, I will do so. So Barirah mentioned that to her family, but they refused and said: If she wishes to count it as charity upon you, let her do so, but your loyalty belongs to us. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Buy her and free her, for loyalty belongs only to the one who frees. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: What is with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, it is not his, even if he stipulates a hundred times. The condition of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is truer and more binding."
"25028","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that she said: Umm Habibah bint Jahsh sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I suffer non-menstrual bleeding. He said: That is only a vein, so wash and then pray. So she used to wash at every prayer. Ibn Shihab said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not order her to wash at every prayer; she only did it herself."
"25029","Hashim narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send sacrificial animals from Medina, and I would twist the garlands of his sacrificial camels, then he would not avoid anything that the muhrim avoids."
"25030","Hashim narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: Safiyyah bint Huyayy menstruated after she had performed the Ifadah. Aishah said: So I mentioned her menstruation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will she detain us? She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, she already performed the Ifadah and circumambulated the House, then menstruated after the Ifadah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then let her depart."
"25031","Hashim narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me joyful with the lines of his face shining. He said: Have you not seen that Mujazziz just looked at Zayd ibn Harithah and Usamah and said: Some feet are indeed from others."
"25032","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Kaysan narrated to us, he said: Amrah bint Qays al-Adawiyyah narrated to me, she said: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who flees from the plague is like the one who flees from the battlefield."
"25033","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us: Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to strive in the last ten nights as he did not strive in others."
"25034","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Tufayl ibn Sakhbarah informed me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The greatest marriage in blessing is the easiest of them in cost."
"25035","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hafsah bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from her paternal aunt Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us regarding the fara'ah: from a flock of sheep, from five, one."
"25036","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to us, from Habib ibn Hind, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes the first seven of the Quran is a scholar."
"25037","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, Abu Bakr and Bilal took fever. Abu Bakr, when the fever seized him, would say: Every man is greeted morning in his family, while death is nearer than the strap of his sandal. And Bilal, when it left him, would chant, saying: Would that I knew whether I will spend a night in a valley with idhkhir and jalil around me, and whether I will one day come to the waters of Majannah, and whether Shama and Tafil will appear to me. O Allah, disgrace Utbah ibn Rabi'ah and Umayyah ibn Khalaf as they expelled us from Mecca."
"25038","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: The Abyssinians played before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque, so I came to look, and he kept lowering his shoulder for me so I could look at them."
"25039","Affan narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us: Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Sa'ibah, a freedwoman of al-Fakih ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to me, she said: I entered upon Aishah and saw in her house a spear set down. I said: O Mother of the Believers, what do you do with this spear? She said: This is for these geckos; we kill them with it. For the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that when Ibrahim, prayer and peace be upon him, was thrown into the Fire, there was no creature on earth but that it extinguished the Fire from him except the gecko, which blew upon him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to kill it."
"25040","Affan narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us: Nafi' narrated to me, he said: A freedwoman of al-Fakih ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi narrated to me, she said: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from killing the house snakes except the double-striped and the tail-less, for they erase sights and kill the children of pregnant women in their bellies. Whoever does not kill them is not of us."
"25041","My father said: Hasan narrated both of them to us together, from Jarir, the meaning and the chain, from from."
"25042","My father said: Hasan narrated both of them to us together, from Jarir, the meaning and the chain, from from."
"25043","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from his father al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The severest of people in punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate."
"25044","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray, between the last Isha until the dawn splits, eleven rak'ahs, giving salam in every two rak'ahs and praying witr with one. And he would remain in his prostration as long as one of you recites fifty verses. Then when the caller fell silent, he would stand and pray two light rak'ahs, then lie on his right side until the caller came to him."
"25045","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Zurarah, that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: Umm Habibah bint Jahsh, while she was under Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, suffered non-menstrual bleeding for seven years, so she complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is not menstruation; it is only a vein. So when menstruation comes, leave the prayer, and when it goes, wash and then pray. Aishah said: So she used to wash for every prayer, then pray. And she used to sit in the tub of her sister Zaynab bint Jahsh until the redness of the blood would rise over the water."
"25046","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: Zabban ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in the chamber while I was in the house, and he would separate the even from the odd with a taslim we could hear."
"25047","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take of deeds what you can bear, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not tire until you tire. Aishah said: And the most beloved prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed a prayer, was that he persisted in it. Abu Salamah said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: And those who are constant in their prayers."
"25048","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that Abu Bakr entered upon her while with her were two slave girls in the days of Mina beating two tambourines, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was covered over with his garment. So he scolded them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered his face and said: Leave them, O Abu Bakr, for these are days of festival. And Aishah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shielding me with his cloak while I looked at the Abyssinians playing in the mosque, until I was the one who tired, then I sat. So estimate the young girl, fresh in age, keen on amusement."
"25049","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, he said: Aishah narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not fast any month of the year more than his fasting of Sha'ban; he would fast it all."
"25050","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: My father said, and Buhlul ibn Hakim narrated to me, from al-Awza'i, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, he said: Salim al-Dawsi narrated to me, he said: I heard Aishah say to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr: O Abd al-Rahman, perform ablution fully, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"25051","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to me, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, he said: Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned observing retreat in the last ten of Ramadan, so Aishah asked his permission, and he permitted her. So she ordered her tent, and it was pitched. And Hafsah asked Aishah to seek permission for her from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she did. So she ordered her tent, and it was pitched. When Zaynab saw that, she ordered her tent, and it was pitched. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed, would leave, then he saw the tents. So he said: What are these? They said: The tents of Aishah, Hafsah, and Zaynab. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you intend righteousness by this? I am not in retreat. So he returned. Then when he broke fast, he observed retreat in ten of Shawwal."
"25052","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Utbah, meaning Ibn Damrah, meaning Ibn Habib, narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Qays, the freedman of Ghutayf, narrated to me that he came to Aishah, Mother of the Believers, and greeted her. So she said: Who is the man? He said: I am Abdullah, the freedman of Ghutayf ibn Azib. So she said: Ibn Ufayf? So he said: Yes, O Mother of the Believers. So he asked her about the two rak'ahs after the Asr prayer: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray them? She said to him: Yes. And he asked her about the offspring of the disbelievers, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are with their fathers. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, without deeds? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knows best what they would have done."
"25053","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Rashid ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing cuts the prayer of the Muslim except the donkey, the disbeliever, the dog, and the woman. So Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, we have indeed been likened to evil beasts."
"25054","Abu al-Yaman and Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ill omen is bad character."
"25055","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, that a mukatab of hers entered upon her with the remainder of his contract, so she said to him: You will not enter upon me after this time of yours. So take to striving in the path of Allah, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Dust in the path of Allah never mixes with the heart of a Muslim man but Allah forbids him the Fire."
"25056","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given choice between two matters in Islam but he chose the easier of them."
"25057","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: When the caller pronounced the iqama, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two light rak'ahs, then lie on his right side until the caller came to him to inform him of the prayer."
"25058","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never offered the Duha voluntary prayer in travel nor in residence."
"25059","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my chamber shielding me with his cloak while I looked at the Abyssinians, how they play, until I was the one who tired. And estimate the young girl, fresh in age, keen on amusement."
"25060","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves gentleness in all matters."
"25061","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr while the sun was still high in my chamber."
"25062","Buhlul ibn Hakim al-Qarqasani narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to sleep, he would perform ablution, his ablution for prayer."
"25063","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: I took a durnuk with images in it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and tore it, and said: The severest of people in torment on the Day of Resurrection are those who liken to the creation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"25064","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hands, then he would not withdraw from anything nor leave it. Indeed we do not know what makes the sacred lawful except circumambulation of the House."
"25065","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the Ifadah, he wanted from Safiyyah something a man wants from his wife, so it was said to him: She is menstruating. So he said: Barren, will she detain us? They said: She already circumambulated on the Day of Sacrifice. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed with her. Ibn Mus'ab said: I never heard him mention, meaning al-Awza'i, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim except once."
"25066","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said, and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never offered the Duha voluntary prayer at all, yet I offer it. And she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to leave a deed while loving to do it, fearing that people would take it as a practice and it would be made obligatory upon them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved what was light upon people of the obligations."
"25067","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to give in charity gold that was with us during his illness. She said: Then he recovered, so he said: What did you do? She said: What I saw of you distracted me. He said: So bring it. She said: So she brought it to him, seven or nine - Abu Hazim doubts - dinars. So he said when she brought them to him: What would Muhammad think if he met Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while this was with him? And what would this spare Muhammad if he met Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while this was with him?"
"25068","Ali ibn Ayyash and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to us, Husayn said: from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: Crescent and crescent and crescent would pass over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no fire was kindled in any of his houses. I said: O aunt, upon what did you live? She said: Upon the two black ones: dates and water. Husayn said: He heard Aishah say: Crescent and crescent would pass us, and no fire was kindled in any of the houses of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said: O aunt, the like of it."
"25069","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri and Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to me, they said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night while I lay across between him and the qibla."
"25070","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while I was screened with a qiram with an image in it, so he tore it. Then he said: The severest of people in torment on the Day of Resurrection are those who liken to the creation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"25071","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to me while he was in retreat in the mosque until he leaned upon the door of my chamber, so I would wash his head while I was in my chamber and the rest of his body was in the mosque."
"25072","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubayd narrated to me, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me at Sarif, and I had menstruated, while I was cast down. So he said to me: Have you menstruated? So I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and I do not think women were created except for evil. So he said: No, but it is something the women of the sons of Adam were tried with."
"25073","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Rabi'ah ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Uthman ibn Affan, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him. When we saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of us turned to the other. And among the last speech he spoke to him was that he struck his shoulder and said: O Uthman, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, may clothe you a shirt. If the hypocrites want you to take it off, do not take it off until you meet me. O Uthman, Allah may clothe you a shirt. If the hypocrites want you to take it off, do not take it off until you meet me. Three times. So I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, where was this from you? She said: I forgot it, by Allah, I did not remember it. He said: So I informed Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan of it, but he was not satisfied with what I informed him until he wrote to the Mother of the Believers to write it to him, so she wrote it to him in a letter."
"25074","Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from one who heard Makhul narrate, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda', from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank standing and sitting, walked barefoot and shod, and turned from his right and from his left."
"25075","Bishr ibn Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, he said, and my father informed me, he said: Muhammad said: Urwah informed me that Aishah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of the gecko: A little wicked creature. And I did not hear him order killing it."
"25076","Bishr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, concerning what the muhrim kills of animals. Al-Zuhri said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five of the animals, all of them wicked, are killed in the sanctuary: the vicious dog, the scorpion, the kite, the crow, and the mouse."
"25077","Bishr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said, then my father narrated to me, he said, Muhammad said, and Yahya ibn Urwah informed me that he heard Urwah say: Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: People asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the soothsayers, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: They are nothing. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, they sometimes tell of a thing that turns out true. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That word of truth the jinn snatches and casts it into the ear of his ally like the cackle of the hen, then they mix into it more than a hundred lies."
"25078","Bishr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The sun eclipsed in the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the mosque, stood, said takbir, and the people lined behind him. So he said takbir and recited a long recitation, then said takbir and bowed a long bowing, then said: Allah hears whoever praises Him. So he stood and did not prostrate, and recited a long recitation shorter than the first recitation, then said takbir and bowed a long bowing shorter than the first bowing, then said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, our Lord, to You is praise. Then he prostrated. Then he did in the other rak'ah the like of that, completing four bowings and four prostrations. And the sun cleared before he left. Then he stood, praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with what He deserves, then said: They are only two signs of the signs of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life. So when you see them, rush to prayer. And Kathir ibn Abbas used to narrate that Abdullah ibn Abbas used to narrate of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day the sun eclipsed the like of what Urwah narrated from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said to Urwah: Your brother, on the day the sun eclipsed in Medina, did not add over two rak'ahs like the Fajr prayer. So he said: Yes, he missed the Sunnah."
"25079","Bishr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm narrated to me that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: A woman came with two daughters of hers asking me, but she found with me nothing but one date, so I gave it to her. So she took it and split it in two between her daughters, and ate nothing of it. Then she stood and left, she and her daughters. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, so I narrated her story to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is tried with daughters by anything and treats them well, they will be a shield for him from the Fire."
"25080","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No affliction befalls the Muslim but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, expiates by it from him, even the thorn he is pricked with."
"25081","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, this is Jibril, peace be upon him, and he sends you peace. So she said: And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah. She said: And he sees what we do not see."
"25082","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Fatimah, daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she sought permission while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with Aishah in her cloak, so he permitted her. So she entered upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, your wives sent me to you asking you for justice concerning the daughter of Abu Quhafah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O my little daughter, do you not love what I love? So she said: Yes. So he said: Then love this one, for Aishah. She said: So Fatimah stood and went out, came to the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and narrated to them what she said and what he said to her. So they said to her: You have availed us nothing. So return to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Fatimah, peace be upon her, said: By Allah, I will never speak to him about her again. So the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Zaynab bint Jahsh, so she sought permission, and he permitted her. So she entered and said: O Messenger of Allah, your wives sent me to you asking you for justice concerning the daughter of Abu Quhafah. Aishah said: Then Zaynab fell upon me. Aishah said: So I kept looking at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he would permit me against her. I did not cease until I knew that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not dislike that I defend myself. She said: So I fell upon Zaynab, and I did not delay in silencing her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled. Then he said: She is the daughter of Abu Bakr."
"25083","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me that Aishah said: The wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Fatimah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned its meaning."
"25084","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eleven rak'ahs at night. That was his prayer: he would prostrate a prostration of that as long as one of you recites fifty verses before he raised his head, and he would pray two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer, then lie on his right side until the caller came to him for prayer."
"25085","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said, and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate in prayer: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and the trial of death. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from sin and debt. She said: So someone said to him: How often you seek refuge from debt, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: When a man falls into debt, he speaks and lies, and promises and breaks."
"25086","Yunus narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate in prayer, then he mentioned the like of it."
"25087","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Sa'id ibn Khalid ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan informed me, while I was narrating to him these hadiths, that he asked Urwah ibn al-Zubayr about what fire touched. So Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said: I heard Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire touched."
"25088","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he died, was covered with a Hibarah garment."
"25089","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while with me was a Jewish woman, and she was saying to me: Have you felt that you are tried in the graves? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trembled and said: Only the Jews are tried. So Aishah said: Then we remained nights. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you felt that it was revealed to me that you are tried in the graves? Aishah said: So I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after that seek refuge from the torment of the grave."
"25090","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said that Aishah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while healthy, used to say: No prophet was ever taken until he sees his seat in Paradise, then he is given life. When he fell ill and death came to him, with his head on the thigh of Aishah, he fainted. When he recovered, he fixed his gaze toward the ceiling of the house, then said: O Allah, the Highest Companion. Aishah said: So I said: It is his speech he used to tell us while healthy."
"25091","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that a man asked Aishah about fasting. So she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Sha'ban, and he used to aim to fast Thursday and Monday."
"25092","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Ziyad Khiyar ibn Salamah, that he asked Aishah about onions. So she said: The last food the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate was food with onions in it."
"25093","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Qays say: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting in fasting."
"25094","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His angels, peace be upon them, bless those who join the rows. And whoever fills a gap, Allah raises him by it a degree."
"25095","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: al-Zubaydi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will raise people on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, uncircumcised. He said: So Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, then how about private parts? He said: For every man among them on that Day a matter to occupy him."
"25096","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Nafi', from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he saw rain, would say: O Allah, make it a wholesome downpour."
"25097","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he saw rain, would say: O Allah, make it a wholesome downpour."
"25098","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to accept the gift and reward for it."
"25099","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from the last of his day when he prayed Zuhr, then returned to Mina, so he stayed in it the nights of the days of Tashriq, stoning the pillar when the sun declined, each pillar with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble, and standing at the first and at the second, prolonging the standing and supplicating humbly, and stoning the third without standing at it."
"25100","Sakan ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given a favor, let him repay it. And whoever cannot, let him mention it. For whoever mentions it has thanked it. And whoever adorns himself with what he did not attain is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"25101","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: When I oiled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I parted a parting from above his crown and left a forelock for him."
"25102","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usamah, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the believer attains by his good character the ranks of one who stands at night in prayer and fasts by day."
"25103","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Said, meaning Ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As, narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me saying: O Aishah, your people are the quickest of my ummah to join me. She said: When he sat, I said: O Messenger of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom, you entered saying words that frightened me. He said: What is it? She said: You claim that my people are the quickest of your ummah to join you. He said: Yes. She said: For what is that? He said: Deaths find them sweet, so their ummah envies them. She said: I said: How will the people be after that, or at that time? He said: Young locusts whose strong eat their weak, until the Hour comes upon them. And al-daba are the locusts whose wings have not yet grown."
"25104","Hashim narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, he said: It was said to Aishah: O Mother of the Believers, this month is twenty-nine days. She said: What amazes you of that? I never fasted with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty-nine days more often than I fasted thirty."
"25105","He said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water. Ibrahim said: I heard nothing from Hisham except this one hadith."
"25106","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: My mother narrated to me, from Muadhah al-Adawiyyah, from Aishah, that she informed her, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel, and I would say to him: Leave some for me, leave some for me."
"25107","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Talhah, narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, kept enjoining me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"25108","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sad ibn Hisham ibn Amir, he said: I came to Aishah and said: O Mother of the Believers, inform me of the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: His character was the Quran. Do you not read the Quran, the word of Allah, mighty and majestic: And indeed you are upon a great character. I said: I want to devote myself unmarried to worship. She said: Do not do it. Do you not read: You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married, and children were born to him."
"25109","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Yahya, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: Had the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seen of women what we have seen, he would have prevented them from the mosques, as the Children of Israel prevented their women. I said to Amrah: Did the Children of Israel prevent their women? She said: Yes."
"25110","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: As if I am looking at myself twisting the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of sheep, then he does not refrain from anything."
"25111","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from al-Mualla ibn Ziyad and Hisham and Yunus, from al-Hasan, that Aishah said: Supplications the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate often: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you supplicate often with this supplication. He said: The heart of the son of Adam is between two fingers of the fingers of Allah, mighty and majestic; if He wills He makes it deviate, and if He wills He makes it steadfast."
"25112","Yunus narrated to us: Nafi, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is reckoned on that day will be punished. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah, mighty and majestic, says: He will be reckoned an easy reckoning. He said: That is the presentation; whoever has his reckoning scrutinized on that day will be punished."
"25113","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Ibn Qurayzah al-Sadafi, he said: I said to Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lie with you while you were menstruating? She said: Yes, when I had tied my waist-wrapper tightly upon me, and we had then only one bed. When Allah, mighty and majestic, provided me with another bed, I kept apart from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25114","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blessedness of a woman is the ease of her engagement and the ease of her dowry."
"25115","He said: Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in major impurity and wanted to sleep while impure, he performed his ablution for prayer before sleeping, and he used to say: Whoever wants to sleep while impure, let him perform his ablution for prayer."
"25116","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym, from Muslim ibn Mikhraq, from Aishah, he said: It was mentioned to her that people recite the Quran once or twice in a night, so she said: Those recited and did not recite. I used to stand with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the full moon, and he would recite Surah al-Baqarah and Al Imran and al-Nisa; he would not pass a verse of fear except he supplicated Allah, mighty and majestic, and sought refuge, nor pass a verse of glad tidings except he supplicated Allah, mighty and majestic, and desired unto Him."
"25117","Qutaybah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from his father, from Musab ibn Shaybah, from Musafi ibn Abd Allah al-Hajabi, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that a woman said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does a woman bathe when she has a wet dream and sees water? He said: Yes. Aishah said to her: May your hands be dusty. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave her; whence does resemblance come except from that? If her water overcomes the water of the man, the child resembles his maternal uncles, and if the water of the man overcomes her water, it resembles him."
"25118","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ibn al-Had, that Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, the freedman of Ibn Ayyash, narrated to him, from Irak ibn Malik, he said: I heard him narrate to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Aishah, that she said: A poor woman carrying her two daughters came to me, so I fed her three dates; she gave each one of them a date and raised a date to her mouth to eat it, then her two daughters asked her for it, so she split the date she wanted to eat between them. She said: Her affair amazed me, so I mentioned what she did to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has made Paradise obligatory for her thereby and freed her thereby from the Fire."
"25119","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, from his mother, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one night, so I sent Barirah after him to see where he went. She said: He went toward Baqi al-Gharqad, stood at the lowest part of al-Baqi, then raised his hands, then left. Barirah returned to me and informed me. In the morning I asked him: O Messenger of Allah, where did you go in the night? He said: I was sent to the people of al-Baqi to pray for them."
"25120","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to observe retreat in the mosque during the last ten of Ramadan until Allah took him, then his wives observed retreat after him."
"25121","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Ishaq ibn Umar, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never prayed a prayer at its last time twice until Allah, mighty and majestic, took him."
"25122","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, from his mother, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the people in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: Whoever of you likes to begin with an umrah before the hajj, let him do so. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed hajj alone and did not perform umrah."
"25123","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, from his mother, from Aishah, that she said: I loved to enter the House and pray in it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and admitted me into al-Hijr and said to me: Pray in al-Hijr if you want to enter the House, for it is but a part of the House, but your people shortened it when they built the Kabah and excluded it from the House."
"25124","Ali ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd Rabbihi ibn Said narrated to me, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say for the sick: In the name of Allah, with the soil of our land, with the saliva of some of us, that our sick be healed by the permission of our Lord."
"25125","Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd Allah said, and I heard it myself from Uthman, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya al-Ansari narrated to me, from Yunus al-Ayli, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died at sixty-three years of age."
"25126","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abd Allah said, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, he said: Hafs narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abbad ibn Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: I brought Ibn al-Zubayr to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he rubbed his palate with a date and said: This is Abd Allah, and you are Umm Abd Allah."
"25127","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abd Allah said, and I heard it myself from him, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from Khalid ibn Salamah, from al-Bahiyy, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Aishah said: I did not know until Zaynab entered upon me without permission while angry, then she said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I think when the little daughter of Abu Bakr turns her forearms to you. Then she turned to me, so I turned away from her until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Defend yourself. So I faced her until I saw her saliva had dried in her mouth, saying nothing back to me, and I saw the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beaming."
"25128","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abd Allah said, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, he said: Hafs narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Ibn Judan in the pre-Islamic period used to join kinship and feed the poor; will that benefit him? He said: No, O Aishah, he never said a day: My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment."
"25129","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Harmalah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah, he said: I came to Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), asking her about something. She said: I inform you of what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in this house of mine: O Allah, whoever is entrusted with any affair of my ummah and is hard upon them, be hard upon him; and whoever is entrusted with any affair of my ummah and is gentle with them, be gentle with him."
"25130","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah informed us, he said: al-Awzai informed us, he said: Shaddad Abu Ammar narrated to me, from Aishah, that women of Basra entered upon her, so she ordered them to cleanse with water, and said: Command your husbands to do that, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it, and it is a cure for piles. Aishah says it, or Abu Ammar."
"25131","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani: He heard Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays say: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting in fasting."
"25132","Muhammad ibn Idris, meaning al-Shafii, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, that he said: I asked Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): In how many garments was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded? She said: In three white Sahuli garments."
"25133","Muhammad ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I asked Aishah: How much was the dowry of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: His dowry to his wives was twelve uqiyah and a nashsh. She said: Do you know what a nashsh is? I said: No. She said: Half an uqiyah; that is five hundred dirhams. This is the dowry of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his wives."
"25134","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Sulaym informed me, he said: He heard his father narrate from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved beginning with the right in all his affair as much as he could, in his purification and his combing and his putting on sandals. He said: When Ashath came to Kufah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved beginning with the right as much as he could."
"25135","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Ashath ibn Sulaym, from his father, from Masruq, he said: I said to Aishah: Which deed was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: The continuous one. I said: At what hour did he stand for prayer? She said: When he heard the cry."
"25136","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, he said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrate from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I was between him and the qiblah."
"25137","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing and his prostration: All-Glorious, All-Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"25138","Bahz narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd, he said: Aishah said: The family of Abu Bakr sent us a leg of a sheep at night; so I held and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut, or she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held and I cut. She says to the one she was narrating to: This was without a lamp. Aishah said: A month would come upon the family of Muhammad without baking bread or cooking a pot. Humayd said: I mentioned it to Safwan ibn Muhriz, and he said: No, rather every two months."
"25139","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Sulaym narrated to us that he heard his father narrate from Masruq, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while a man was with her. The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed as if it distressed him. She said: O Messenger of Allah, he is my brother. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look to who your brothers are, for suckling is only from hunger in infancy."
"25140","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muadhah, that a woman asked Aishah: One of us menstruates; does her prayer suffice her without making up? She said: Are you a Haruriyyah? We used to menstruate at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not do that."
"25141","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who recites the Quran, skilled in it, is with the noble righteous scribes, and the one who recites it with difficulty upon him gets two rewards."
"25142","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim informed us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Sawdah was a slow heavy woman, so she asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pour forth from Jam before the standing, and he permitted her. Aishah said: I wished I had asked his permission and he had permitted me. Al-Qasim used to dislike pouring forth before the standing."
"25143","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, that Sad ibn Hisham narrated to him, he said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, narrate to me about the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Do you not read the Quran? He said: I said: Yes. Then he mentioned the hadith. She said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer, he persisted in it, and when the night standing escaped him, his eyes overcome by sleep or pain, he prayed twelve rakahs by day. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never stood a night completing it until morning, nor recited the Quran in a night completing it, nor fasted a month completing it other than Ramadan, until he died."
"25144","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me that Aishah said to him: O son of my sister, Abu Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Umar, his hearing erred. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a man punished in his grave for his own deed while his family weep over him; and by Allah, no bearer of burdens bears the burden of another."
"25145","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muadhah, she said: I asked Aishah: How many rakahs did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray of Duha? She said: Four rakahs, and he adds what Allah, mighty and majestic, wills."
"25146","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Muadhah, from Aishah, she said: Command your husbands to wash from themselves the trace of relieving themselves and urine, for we are shy to forbid them that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"25147","He said: Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Layth and Thabit informed us, from Sumayyah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was displeased with Safiyyah bint Huyayy over something. Safiyyah said: O Aishah, make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pleased with me, and your day is mine. She said: Yes. So she took a veil of hers dyed with saffron, sprinkled it with water so its scent would spread, and sat beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Away from me, O Aishah, it is not your day. She said: That is the bounty of Allah, He gives it to whom He wills. She informed him of the matter, and he became pleased with her."
"25148","Affan narrated to us: Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, he said: Ismail al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalaf, the freedman of Bani Jumah, narrated to me that he entered with Ubayd ibn Umayr upon Aishah, the Mother of the Believers, in the portico of Zamzam, there being no shade in the mosque but it. She said: Welcome to Abu Asim, meaning Ubayd ibn Umayr. What prevents you from visiting us? He said: I fear to bore you. She said what she said. He said: I came to ask you about a verse in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite it? She said: Which verse? He said: Those who give what they give, or: Those who do what they do. She said: Which of them is dearer to you? He said: I said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, one of them is dearer to me than the whole world, or: the world and what is in it. She said: Which of them? I said: Those who do what they do. She said: I testify that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it thus, and thus it was revealed, or she said: I testify thus it was revealed, and thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it; but orthography is a letter."
"25149","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Ata, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while she lay across to his right and to his left."
"25150","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yahya al-Dabbi narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, from his mother, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated, so Umar stood behind him with a jug. He said: What is this, O Umar? He said: Water to perform ablution with, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I was not commanded every time I urinate to perform ablution; had I done that, it would have become a sunnah."
"25151","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling nor two sucklings prohibit marriage."
"25152","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left the two rakahs after Asr with me at all."
"25153","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, that Aishah stayed with Safiyyah Umm Talhah al-Talahat, and saw daughters of hers praying without headcovers though they had menstruated. He said: Aishah said: No girl among them shall pray except in a headcover. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, and in my lap was a girl, so he threw to me his waist-wrapper and said: Split it between this one and the girl in the lap of Umm Salamah, for I do not see her but she has menstruated, or: I do not see them but they have menstruated."
"25154","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his illness: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Aishah said to Hafsah: Abu Bakr is a tender man; when he stands in your place, the people will not hear from weeping. He said: Command him to lead the people in prayer. She said: She repeated to him several times, each time he saying: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. On the third he said: Leave me; you are the companions of Yusuf. Let Abu Bakr lead the people."
"25155","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Aishah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to bathe from major impurity, he washed his hands three times, then took with his right to pour upon his left, and washed his private part until he cleaned it, then washed his hand well, then rinsed his mouth three times and inhaled three times, and washed his face three times and his arms three times, then poured water upon his head three times, then bathed; when he came out, he washed his feet."
"25156","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: Five women narrated to me from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the earthen jar."
"25157","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was affected by magic, so it seemed to him that he did something though he had not done it, until one day I saw him supplicating. He said: Do you feel that Allah, mighty and majestic, has given me a ruling in what I asked Him about? Two men came to me; one sat at my head and the other at my feet. One said: What ails the man? The other said: Bewitched. Who bewitched him? Labid ibn al-Asam. In what? In a comb and combings and the sheath of a male palm spathe. Where is it? In Dhi Arwan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went, and when he returned he informed Aishah. He said: As if its palm trees are the heads of devils, and as if its water is the infusion of henna. I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you take it out for the people? He said: As for Allah, mighty and majestic, He has healed me, and I feared to stir up evil therefrom upon the people."
"25158","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Umm Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning a man who divorced his wife three times, then another married her, then divorced her before touching her: The first may not marry her until she tastes of his honey and he tastes of hers."
"25159","Affan narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about bit, and bit is honey wine which the people of Yemen used to drink. He said: Every drink that intoxicates is forbidden."
"25160","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, he said: I heard al-Shabi narrate from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his wives a choice; was it divorce?"
"25161","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, that Aishah said: When she came to al-Hawab and heard the barking of dogs, she said: I think I am but returning. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Which of you will be barked at by the dogs of al-Hawab? Al-Zubayr said to her: Go on; perhaps Allah, mighty and majestic, will reconcile between people through you."
"25162","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, that Abu Musa said to Aishah: I want to ask you about something, and I am shy of you. She said: Ask and do not be shy, for I am but your mother. So he asked her about a man who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. She said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When circumcision touches circumcision, ghusl has become obligatory."
"25163","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Imran, meaning al-Quraii, from Abd Allah ibn Shammas, that he heard Aishah narrate, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us the hantam, which is the earthen jar, and the dubba, the naqir, and the muzaffat."
"25164","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalid narrate from Abu Qilabah, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, the foster-son of Aishah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: No Muslim man over whom a community of people pray, all of them interceding for him, except they are granted intercession for him."
"25165","Abu Said, the freedman of Bani Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Nafi al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: My father Husayn, this one is sound in hadith, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Sad ibn Hisham, that he entered upon the Mother of the Believers Aishah and asked her about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He used to pray eight rakahs at night and make witr with the ninth, and pray two rakahs sitting. And she mentioned ablution: He would rise to his prayer and order his purification water and his siwak. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew bulky, he prayed six rakahs and made witr with the seventh, and prayed two rakahs sitting. She said: He remained thus until he died. I said: I want to ask you about devoting oneself unmarried to worship; what do you think of it? She said: Do not do it. Have you not heard Allah, mighty and majestic, say: We sent messengers before you and made for them wives and offspring. So do not practice celibacy. So he went out understanding, came to Basra, stayed but a little until he went out to the land of Mukran and was killed there upon his best deed."
"25166","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Abu Mashar, from al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, that she said: I used to scrape it from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hand; if you see it, wash it, and if it is hidden to you, sprinkle it."
"25167","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: He was asked about a woman making up prayers during the days of her menstruation. He said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muadhah, that a woman asked Aishah about that. She said: Are you a Haruriyyah? We used to menstruate at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and would not make up any prayer."
"25168","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrate from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Five harmful creatures are killed in the sacred and non-sacred: the snake, the pied crow, the mouse, the vicious dog, and the kite."
"25169","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi, from the wife of Ibn Umar, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said concerning one who drinks in a silver vessel: As if he is gurgling fire in his belly."
"25170","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi, from a person, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grave has a squeeze; had anyone been saved from it, Sad ibn Muadh would have been saved."
"25171","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah informed us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Urwah narrate from Aishah, she said: I saw myself in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), between him and the qiblah, while he prayed. Sad said: I think he said: While she was menstruating. Hajjaj said: Shubah said: Sad is the one who doubts."
"25172","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid narrate from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that she said: The family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate to satiety barley bread two consecutive days until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died."
"25173","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Awfa ibn Dalham, from Muadhah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to attain something of our faces while fasting."
"25174","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Said narrated to us from dictation, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The skilled in the Quran is with the noble righteous scribes, and the one who recites it while it is hard upon him, stammering in it, gets two rewards."
"25175","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting; and which of you is more master of his desire than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"25176","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I asked the Mother of the Believers about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He would pray a long night standing and a long night sitting; when he recited standing he bowed standing, and when he recited sitting he bowed sitting."
"25177","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Hafsah, the freedman of Aishah, that Aishah informed him that when the sun eclipsed at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he performed ablution and ordered, and it was announced: Prayer is congregational. So he stood and prolonged the standing in his prayer. She said: I think he recited Surah al-Baqarah, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then said: Allah hears whoever praises Him. Then he stood like his standing and did not prostrate, then bowed, then prostrated, then stood and did like what he had done, then bowed two bowings in a prostration, then sat, and the sun cleared."
"25178","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from al-Ashath, he said: Abd Allah ibn Miqal al-Muharibi narrated to me, he said: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making nabidh in the dubba, the hantam, and the muzaffat."
"25179","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his ihram when he entered ihram, and for his release when he released at Mina before pouring forth for tawaf."
"25180","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: I wished I had asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Sawdah asked his permission, to pray Fajr at Mina and arrive before the people come. They said to Aishah: Did Sawdah ask his permission? She said: She was a heavy slow woman, so he permitted her."
"25181","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that Safiyyah menstruated at Mina though she had poured forth. Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, I see Safiyyah but detaining us. He said: Why? I said: She menstruated. He said: Had she not poured forth? I said, Muhammad ibn Ubayd doubted, she said: Yes. He said: No detention upon you, so depart."
"25182","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray wearing a cloak of these striped ones, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with part of it upon him and part upon me; and the mirt is of black garments."
"25183","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, he said: Umaynah narrated to me, from Aishah, that she was asked about nabidh of the earthen jar. She said: Is one of you unable to take a skin from her sacrifice? Then she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, or: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prevented, nabidh of the earthen jar, and such-and-such; Sulayman forgot it."
"25184","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of believers in faith are the best of them in character and the gentlest of them to their families."
"25185","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Salim, the freedman of Daws, that he heard Aishah say to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr: Perform ablution fully, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"25186","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali Abu Jafar, from Aishah, that she used to take debt. It was said to her: What is with you and debt? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant intending to repay his debt except Allah, mighty and majestic, gives him help. So I seek that help."
"25187","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Wail narrate from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a woman gives charity from her husband's house, she gets a reward for it, and the husband the like of that, and the storekeeper the like of that, and neither of them decreases anything from the reward of his companion: For the husband for what he earned, and for her for what she spent."
"25188","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, that he said: I entered upon Aishah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in major impurity, then bathe, then go to the mosque with his head dripping, then fast that day. So I informed Marwan ibn al-Hakam of her saying. He said to me: Inform Abu Hurayrah of Aishah's saying. I said: He is my friend, and I would like you to excuse me. He said: I insist upon you to go to him. So I and he went to Abu Hurayrah, and I informed him of her saying. He said: Aishah then knows better about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25189","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Abu Bakr entered upon her while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with her on the day of Fitr or Adha, and with her were two girls beating two tambourines. Abu Bakr rebuked them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave us, O Abu Bakr; every people have a festival, and our festival is this day."
"25190","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was in retreat in the mosque, so Aishah would come and he would stick out his head, and she would comb it while menstruating."
"25191","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, he said: I said to Aishah: Inform me of a supplication the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate. She said: He often said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I did and from the evil of what I did not do."
"25192","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) often said in his bowing and his prostration: Glory be to You, O Allah, our Lord, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me."
"25193","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, he said: Amrah said to me: Give me a piece of your land to be buried in, for I heard Aishah say: Breaking the bone of the dead is like breaking the bone of the living. Muhammad said: A freedman of Medina used to narrate it from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25194","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his aunt Amrah, from Aishah, that she said: When dawn rose, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs, or prayed only two rakahs. I say: He recites in them the Opening of the Book."
"25195","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Budayl, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I was ill in Faris, praying sitting, so I asked Aishah about that. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray a long night standing and a long night sitting; when he recited standing he bowed standing, and when he recited sitting he bowed sitting."
"25196","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Marthad, or Mazyad, narrate from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray nine rakahs at night."
"25197","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Khaythamah narrate from Abu Atiyyah, from Aishah, that she said: I know how the talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was. Then I heard her after that chant: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk; labbayk, no partner have You, labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours."
"25198","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu al-Duha narrate from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made witr in every part of the night, and his witr settled toward dawn."
"25199","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu al-Duha narrate from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: When the last verses of Surah al-Baqarah were revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and recited them in the mosque, and forbade trading in wine."
"25200","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have sweet water fetched for him from the houses of al-Suqya."
"25201","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the child until he reaches puberty, and from the insane until he regains reason. And Hammad said: and from the mentally impaired until he regains reason."
"25202","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Amash informed me, from Thabit, he said: I heard al-Qasim, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me the khumrah (small prayer mat). She said: I am menstruating. He said: It is not in your hand."
"25203","Affan narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan said: Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, will you remember your families on the Day of Resurrection? He said: As for three stations, then no: the Book, the Scale, and the Sirat."
"25204","Affan narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan said: Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, on the day the earth is changed to other than the earth and the heavens, where will the people be? He said: This is something none of my ummah asked me about before you. The people will be upon the Sirat."
"25205","Affan narrated to us, he said: Bishr, meaning Ibn Mufaddal, narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah did not pray in our shuur (inner garments). Bishr said: it is the garment that is worn beneath the outer covering."
"25206","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif narrated to us, from Amir, from Masruq, he said: Aishah said, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would remain fasting, then he would kiss whatever part of my face he wished, until he broke his fast."
"25207","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform wudu as his wudu for prayer when he intended to perform ghusl from janabah, then he would insert his hand into the vessel and trace the roots of his hair, and when he thought he had fully cleared the skin, he would pour over his head three times, then he would wash. And Urwah said, except that he begins by washing his hand, then his private part."
"25208","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Amir al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would indeed spend the night in a state of janabah, then Bilal would come to him for the morning prayer, so he would stand and perform ghusl, and I would look at the water dripping down his skin and hair, then I would hear his recitation for the morning prayer, then he would remain fasting. Mutarrif said: I said to Amir: In Ramadan? He said: It is the same for you."
"25209","Affan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Wasil al-Ahdab narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, he said: Aishah, Mother of the Believers, saw me washing a trace of janabah that had soiled my garment, so she said: What is this? I said: Janabah soiled my garment. She said: I indeed saw us, when it would soil the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would do no more than say with it like this. And Mahdi described it: rubbing one hand against the other."
"25210","Hasan ibn Musa and Affan and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The pen has been lifted from three: from the child until he reaches puberty, from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the mentally impaired until he regains reason. Affan said: and from the insane until he regains reason. And Hammad said: and from the mentally impaired until he regains reason. And Rawh said: and from the insane until he regains reason."
"25211","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umm Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given a gift containing a necklace of onyx, so he said: I shall surely give it to the dearest of my family to me. The women said: It has gone to the daughter of Abu Quhafah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Umamah bint Zaynab and hung it around her neck."
"25212","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) going out to prayer with his head dripping; he had been in janabah, so he performed ghusl, while intending to fast."
"25213","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I asked al-Aswad ibn Yazid about what Aishah narrated to him concerning the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He would sleep the first part of the night and enliven the last of it, then if he had a need with his family he would fulfill his need, then he would rise before touching water, and when it was at the first call (to prayer), she said: he would leap up - and by Allah, she did not say: he stood - and pour water over himself - and by Allah, she did not say: he performed ghusl, and I know what you intend - and if he was not in janabah he would perform wudu as a man performs wudu for prayer, then pray two rakahs."
"25214","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abis ibn Rabiah, he said: I said to Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the meat of sacrifices after three days? She said: No, but only a few of them used to sacrifice, so he did that so that whoever sacrificed would feed whoever had not sacrificed. And I saw us storing the trotter from our sacrifices, then eating it after ten days."
"25215","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I came to al-Aswad ibn Yazid, and he was a brother and friend to me, so I said: O Abu Amr, narrate to me what the Mother of the Believers narrated to you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: She said: He would sleep the first part of the night and enliven the last of it, and perhaps he had a need with his family, then he would sleep before touching water, and when it was at the first call he would leap up - and she did not say: he stood - and pour water over himself - and she did not say: he performed ghusl, and I know what you intend - and if he was not in janabah he would perform wudu as a man performs wudu for prayer."
"25216","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Aswad, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr said to me: Narrate to me some of what the Mother of the Believers would confide to you, for perhaps there is something she narrated to you that you conceal from people. He said: I said: She indeed narrated to me a hadith, I memorized its beginning. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that your people are recent in their time of jahiliyyah - or he said: of disbelief, Ibn al-Zubayr says - I would have demolished the Kabah and made for it two doors in the ground, a door to enter by and a door to exit by. Abu Ishaq said: And I saw it like that."
"25217","Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would not refrain from any need he had with a woman until the pilgrims returned."
"25218","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us with it, he said: And he would not refrain from a need, if he had one, with a woman until the pilgrims returned."
"25219","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban informed me that Aishah, Mother of the Believers, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is prohibited by suckling is what is prohibited by lineage, whether maternal uncle or paternal uncle or son of a brother."
"25220","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so woman has died and found rest. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said: Only one who is forgiven finds rest."
"25221","Sakan ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended to sleep while in janabah, would perform wudu as his wudu for prayer, and when he intended to eat or drink, he would wash his hands, then eat or drink if he wished."
"25222","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray thirteen prostrations (units) of the night, and most of his prayer was standing; then when he grew old and heavy, most of his prayer was sitting. And he would pray his prayer while I lay across in front of him on the bedding he slept upon, until he intended to perform witr, when he would nudge me and I would stand, then he would perform witr, then lie down until he heard the call to prayer, then stand and prostrate two light prostrations, then lay his side on the ground, then go out to prayer."
"25223","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one is reckoned on the Day of Resurrection and then forgiven. The Muslim sees his deed in his grave, and Allah, Exalted and Glorious, says: Then on that day no man nor jinn shall be asked about his sin. The criminals shall be known by their marks."
"25224","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sleep while in janabah when he had performed wudu as his wudu for prayer."
"25225","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: I placed upon the door of my house a curtain containing images, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to enter, he looked at it and tore it down. She said: So I took it and cut from it two cushions, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recline upon them."
"25226","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Umar narrated to us, from his father, he said: I said to Aishah: Did you used to perform ghusl with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Yes, I would perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a single vessel."
"25227","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Umar narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I was accused of what I was accused of while I was unaware, and afterward some of that reached me. And while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with me, revelation was sent down to him - and when revelation was sent down to him he would be seized by something like slumber - and while he was sitting with me, the revelation descended upon him, then he raised his head while wiping from his forehead, and said: Be glad, O Aishah. I said: By the praise of Allah, Exalted and Glorious, not by your praise. Then he recited: Those who accuse chaste women, until he reached: acquitted of what they say."
"25228","Abu Said narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar, from his father, from Aishah, she said: When the verse of choice was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I wish to mention to you a matter; do not decide anything in it until you consult your parents. I said: What is it? Then he recited the verse of choice. I said: Rather I choose Allah, Exalted and Glorious, and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoiced at that."
"25229","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clientage (wala) belongs to the one who emancipates."
"25230","Abu Said and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to us, from Muadhah, Abu Said said: Aishah narrated to her, she said: I would perform ghusl, I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a single vessel, and I would race him and say: Leave some for me, leave some for me."
"25231","Abu Said narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, and al-Khuzai said: Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Umm Bakr bint al-Miswar narrated to us - al-Khuzai said: from Umm Bakr bint al-Miswar - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf sold a land of his to Uthman ibn Affan for forty thousand dinars, then distributed it among the poor of Banu Zuhrah and among the Muhajirun and the Mothers of the Believers. Al-Miswar said: So I came to Aishah with her share, and she said: Who sent this? I said: Abd al-Rahman. She said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say - and al-Khuzai said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall show kindness to you after me except the patient ones. May Allah give Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf to drink from Salsabil of Paradise."
"25232","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is not cut except for a quarter dinar and upward. Abu Said narrated to us: Ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned the same alike."
"25233","He narrated to us. [Source text truncated in index; only this fragment preserved.]"
"25234","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, he said: Urwah informed me, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while raising his voice in talbiyah for Hajj."
"25235","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite upon himself the Muawwidhat (chapters of refuge) and blow. Aishah said: So when he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, I began to recite upon him and wipe him with his hand, hoping for the blessing of his hand."
"25236","Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone (ifrad)."
"25237","Abu Salamah narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from his mother, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that benefit be taken from the skins of dead animals when tanned."
"25238","Abu Salamah narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: I used to comb the hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in itikaf, and he would not enter the house except for a human need."
"25239","Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I asked Aishah, saying: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in Ramadan? She said: His prayer in Ramadan and other than Ramadan was one: he would pray eleven rakahs; he would pray four, so ask not of their excellence and length, then he would pray four rakahs, so ask not of their excellence and length, then he would pray three rakahs. I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you sleep before you perform witr? He said: My eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep."
"25240","Abu Salamah narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, he said: Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, he said: I and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr entered one day upon Aishah, and she said: Had you seen the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day during an illness he suffered. She said: And he had with me six dinars - Musa said: or seven. She said: Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to distribute them. She said: The pain of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distracted me until Allah restored him. She said: Then he asked me about them, saying: What happened to the six - he said: or the seven. I said: No, by Allah, your pain had distracted me. She said: So he called for them, then arranged them in his palm, then said: What would the Prophet of Allah think if he met Allah, Exalted and Glorious, while these were with him."
"25241","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, narrated to us, from Sharik, meaning Ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O Aishah, be gentle, for when Allah intends good for the people of a household, He guides them to the door of gentleness."
"25242","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the ajwah dates of al-Aliyah, first thing in the morning on an empty stomach: a cure for every magic or poison."
"25243","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a lizard (dabb), but he did not eat it nor forbid it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not feed it to the poor? He said: Do not feed them what you do not eat."
"25244","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Atiq, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the ajwah of al-Aliyah: a cure, or it is an antidote, first thing in the morning."
"25245","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Huddani narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr say: Aishah, Mother of the Believers, narrated to me, she said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asleep, he laughed in his sleep, then woke. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what did you laugh at? He said: People of my ummah heading toward this House for the sake of a man of Quraysh who has sought refuge in the Sanctuary; when they reach al-Bayda, they will be swallowed up, their destinations diverse; Allah will raise them according to their intentions. I said: And how will Allah, Exalted and Glorious, raise them according to their intentions while their destinations are diverse? He said: The road gathered them; among them are the discerning, the wayfarer, and the coerced; they perish in one destruction and proceed to diverse destinations."
"25246","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal of Banu al-Najjar narrated to us, he said: I heard Aba al-Rijal narrate, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Breaking the bone of the dead is like breaking it while alive."
"25247","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A house in which there are no dates is as if there is no food in it."
"25248","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the infusion of unripe dates, which is al-zahw (reddening dates)."
"25249","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, I and my son bought from so-and-so the fruit of his land, then we came to him asking him to reduce (the price), and by Allah, we obtained nothing of its fruit except something we ate in our stomachs or fed to a poor person hoping for blessing, yet he swore he would not do so. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He swore he would not do good, he swore he would not do good, he swore he would not do good. That reached the man, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you wish, all the fruit, and if you wish, what they waived. So he waived for them what they waived."
"25250","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore he would not enter upon his wives for a month, then when it was twenty-nine days of the month, he came to enter. I said to him: Did you not swear for a month? He said: The month is twenty-nine days."
"25251","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until their soundness appears and they are safe from blight."
"25252","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Malik Abu Qudamah al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Aishah bint Sad narrated to us, from Umm Dharrah, she said: I saw Aishah praying al-Duha, saying: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray except four rakahs."
"25253","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha al-Muharibi narrated to us, from his father, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about turning in prayer. He said: A snatching that Satan snatches from the prayer of the servant."
"25254","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, he said: al-Suddi narrated to us, from Abd Allah al-Bahiy, he said: Aishah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque and said to the slave girl: Hand me the khumrah. She said: He intended to spread it and pray upon it. She said: She is menstruating. He said: Her menstruation is not in her hand."
"25255","Muammal narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Thawr, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek to fast Mondays and Thursdays."
"25256","Muammal narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, he said: It was said to Aishah: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do in his house? She said: As one of you does: he would mend his sandal and patch his garment."
"25257","Muammal narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Salim said: Aishah said: I would perfume the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had stoned the jamrah, before he performed tawaf of the House. Salim said: The sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more deserving to be followed than the saying of Umar."
"25258","Muammal narrated to us, he said: Nafi, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us: Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, from Aishah, she said: When it was the illness of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he passed away, he said: Call for me Abu Bakr and his son, so let him write, lest one greedy aspire to the affair of Abu Bakr, nor one wishing wish. Then he said: Allah and the Muslims refuse, twice - and Muammal said once: and the believers. Aishah said: So Allah and the Muslims refused - and Muammal said once: and the believers - except that it be my father. So it was my father."
"25259","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from his maternal uncle, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: They complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what they found of whispering (waswasah), saying: O Messenger of Allah, we indeed find something, that if one of us fell from heaven would be dearer to him than to speak of it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is pure faith."
"25260","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Aishah, she said: The wife of Uthman ibn Mazun used to dye herself and perfume herself, then she abandoned it, then entered upon me. I said to her: Is your husband present or absent? She said: Present as absent. I said to her: What is wrong with you? She said: Uthman desires neither world nor women. Aishah said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, so I informed him of that. Then he met Uthman and said: O Uthman, do you believe in what we believe in? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then what example have you in us."
"25261","Muammal narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Abu Fakhita, from Aishah, with the like of it, and he added in it that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Uthman: Do you believe in what we believe in? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then do as we do."
"25262","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Sufyan - and he mentioned another man, from Sufyan - from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be with his family at the beginning of the night, then sleep without touching water, and when he woke at the end of the night he would return to his family and perform ghusl."
"25263","Muammal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, all your women have a kunyah except me. He said: Then take kunyah by your son Abd Allah."
"25264","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until we said: he does not break fast, and break fast until we said: he does not fast. And he never completed fasting a month at all except Ramadan, and I never saw him in any month fasting more than in Shaban."
"25265","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Amrah, that she informed him she heard Aishah - and it was mentioned to her that Abd Allah ibn Umar says: The dead is indeed punished by the weeping of the living - so Aishah said: May Allah forgive Aba Abd al-Rahman; indeed he did not lie, but he forgot or erred. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only passed by a Jewess being wept over, and said: They weep over her while she is punished in her grave."
"25266","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: From every part of the night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr: from its beginning, its middle, and its end; then his witr ended at dawn."
"25267","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone (ifrad)."
"25268","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Amr, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina before he visited the House."
"25269","Surayj and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man indeed acts with the deeds of the people of Paradise, while he is written in the Book among the people of Hell; then before his death he turns and acts with the deeds of the people of Hell, dies, and enters Hell. And a man indeed acts with the deeds of the people of Hell, while he is written in the Book among the people of Paradise; then before his death he turns and acts with the deeds of the people of Paradise, dies, and enters it."
"25270","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Aishah, and from Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, from his mother, from Aishah, and from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone (ifrad)."
"25271","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Aishah, and from Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, from his mother, from Aishah, and from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone (ifrad)."
"25272","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Aishah, and from Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, from his mother, from Aishah, and from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone (ifrad)."
"25273","Surayj narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Aishah said: The reinforcements of the Arabs crowded upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they distressed him, and the Muhajirun stood to clear a way before him, until he stood upon the threshold of Aishah, when they pressed him, so he surrendered his cloak into their hands and leapt over the threshold and entered, saying: O Allah, curse them. Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, the people are ruined. He said: No, by Allah, O daughter of Abu Bakr, I have stipulated upon my Lord, Exalted and Glorious, a condition that has no breach. I said: I am only a human, I am angered by what humans are angered by, so whichever believer a sudden outburst from me reaches, make it for him an expiation."
"25274","Surayj narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), there was no day but he would go around to all of us, woman by woman, drawing near and touching without intimacy, until he reached the one whose day it was, then spent the night with her."
"25275","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: O son of my sister, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Aishah, do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you."
"25276","Surayj narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: O son of my sister, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, a man indeed acts for a long time with the deeds of the people of Hell, while with Allah, Exalted and Glorious, he is written among the people of Paradise. And a man indeed acts for a long time with the deeds of the people of Paradise, while with Allah, Exalted and Glorious, he is written among the people of Hell."
"25277","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: O son of my sister, the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was above wafrah and below jummah. And by Allah, O son of my sister, a month would pass over the household of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with no fire kindled in the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except for a little meat. And it was but the two black things: water and dates, except that around us were neighboring households of the Ansar - may Allah reward them with good in present and past - each day sending to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) some of the milk of their sheep, meaning: so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would partake of that milk. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while in my shelf there was no food a living creature could eat except near half of barley; so I ate from it until it lasted long without perishing, then I measured it and it perished, so would that I had not measured it. And by Allah, his bedding was of leather stuffed with fiber. And al-Hashimi said: with some of the milk of their sheep, and mentioned the like, except his bedding."
"25278","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is closely questioned in reckoning will not be forgiven. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, then where is His saying: he shall be reckoned an easy reckoning? He said: That is the presentation."
"25279","Surayj and Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated to us - Musa said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad - from Hisham - Surayj said in his hadith, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from his father, from Aishah, that water would be drawn for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the houses of al-Suqya."
"25280","Surayj narrated to us: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Muslim ibn Qurt, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to relieve himself, let him clean himself with three stones, for they suffice him."
"25281","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is reckoned is punished."
"25282","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, that Aishah gave charity of something, then ordered Barirah to come to her and look at it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you."
"25283","Surayj narrated to us: Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, so I placed my hand upon his chest and said: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, You are the Physician and You are the Healer. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: Join me with the Highest Companion, join me with the Highest Companion."
"25284","Surayj narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when his eye overcame him or he ached and did not pray at night, would pray in the day twelve rakahs."
"25285","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he visited a sick person, would say: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, indeed You are the Healer, there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no illness."
"25286","al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, she said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he fell ill or slept, would pray in the day twelve rakahs. She said: And I never saw him stand a night until morning, nor fast a complete consecutive month except Ramadan. And she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would do a deed and establish it firmly."
"25287","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he had a need with his family, would come to them, then return without touching water."
"25288","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sleep the first part of the night and stand the last of it."
"25289","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Nafi, from Saibah, a freedwoman of al-Fakih ibn al-Mughirah, that she entered upon Aishah and saw in her house a spear laid down, so she said: O Mother of the Believers, what do you do with this spear? She said: We kill with it the geckos, for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us that when Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was cast into the Fire, there was no creature but it extinguished the fire from him except the gecko, for it would blow upon it. So he (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded killing it."
"25290","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, and from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: As if I look at the glisten of perfume in his partings while he raises his voice in talbiyah. It was said to Sulayman: Concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"25291","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, and from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: As if I look at the glisten of perfume in his partings while he raises his voice in talbiyah. It was said to Sulayman: Concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"25292","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: As if I look at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25293","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Umm Musa, she said: I asked Aishah about the two rakahs after Asr. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never came to me in a day but he prayed two rakahs after Asr."
"25294","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ubayd ibn Rifaah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is the worst of the three when he acts with the deeds of his parents, meaning the child of adultery."
"25295","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing wholly black dogs."
"25296","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, he said: I said to Aishah: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do before he went out? She said: He would pray two rakahs, then go out."
"25297","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash Sulayman, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent sheep as a gift to the House (Kabah)."
"25298","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Zurarah ibn Awfa narrate, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The example of one who recites the Quran and maintains it while it is hard upon him, he has two rewards. He said: And the example of one who recites the Quran while memorizing it is like the noble righteous scribes (angels)."
"25299","Aswad narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ashath, from his father, from Masruq, he said: I asked Aishah about the night prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: When he heard the caller (rooster), he would stand and pray."
"25300","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Huraym informed us, he said: Ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away on Monday and was buried on Wednesday night."
"25301","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abu al-Jawza, from Aishah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to begin recitation with All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"25302","Aswad narrated to us, he said: Hasan narrated to us, from Ashath, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Umm Kulthum, from Aishah, she said: We did it once and we performed ghusl in the case of one who has intercourse and does not ejaculate."
"25303","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will the beloved remember his beloved on the Day of Resurrection. He said: O Aishah, as for at three then no: as for at the Scale until it weighs heavy or light then no, and as for at the scattering of the books, whether he is given in his right or given in his left then no, and when a neck emerges from the Fire and folds over them and rages against them and that neck says: I have been entrusted with three, I have been entrusted with three, I have been entrusted with one who claimed another god with Allah, and I have been entrusted with one who does not believe in the Day of Reckoning, and I have been entrusted with every obstinate tyrant. He said: So it folds over them and casts them into the depths, and for Hell there is a bridge finer than hair and sharper than the sword, upon it are hooks and thorns seizing whomever Allah wills, and the people upon it are like the blink of an eye and like lightning and like wind and like excellent horses and riding camels, and the angels say: Lord grant safety, Lord grant safety; so one saved secure, and one scratched secure, and one rolled up in the Fire upon his face."
"25304","Aswad ibn Amir and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh, from al-Bahiyy, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Hand me the khumrah. She said: I am menstruating. He said: It is not in your hand."
"25305","My father said: And Waki had already narrated it to us."
"25306","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The first thing he would begin with when he entered his house was the siwak, and the last of it when he left his house was the two rakahs before Fajr."
"25307","Aswad and Hajjaj, the meaning, said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, he said: I asked Aishah about wiping over the khuffs, so she said: Go to Ali and ask him. He said: So I went to him and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us when we traveled to wipe over our khuffs. Aswad said in his hadith: And perhaps Sharik said: When we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey we would wipe over our khuffs."
"25308","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Khusayf, he said: A man narrated to me sixty years ago, from Aishah, she said: I fumigated my head with intense fumigation, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, do you not know that upon every hair is janabah."
"25309","Aswad narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Aishah, that a man entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he brought him near and drew his sitting close, then when he left Aishah said to him: O Messenger of Allah, did you not complain of this man. He said: Yes, but indeed among the worst of people, or the worst of people, are those who are honored only out of fear of their evil."
"25310","Aswad narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would become junub then sleep, then wake, then sleep, and not touch water."
"25311","Aswad narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Qays ibn Wahb, from a man of Banu Suwah, he said: I asked Aishah about the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so she said: Do you not read the Quran: Indeed you are upon a great character. He said: I said: Narrate to me about that. She said: I made food for him and Hafsah made food for him, so I said to my slave-girl: Go, and if she comes with the food and places it before, then overturn the food. She said: So she came with the food. She said: So the slave-girl threw it and the bowl fell and broke, and it was leather. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered it and said: Replace, or: Take retaliation, Aswad doubted, a vessel in place of your vessel, and he said nothing."
"25312","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rose from his bed in part of the night and I thought he wanted one of his wives, so I followed him until he stood upon the graves and said: Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people, and indeed we shall join you. Then he said: O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward and do not trial us after them. She said: Then he turned and saw me, so he said: Woe to her, if she could, what she did."
"25313","He said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bahiyy, from Aishah, or from Ibn Umar, Sharik doubted, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated upon the khumrah."
"25314","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that a woman came to her and said: My daughter is a bride, she fell ill and her hair fell out in tufts, shall I add to it. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who adds hair and the woman who has it added, or she said: the woman who adds hair."
"25315","He said: Aswad narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Hisham, from his wife Fatimah, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have a daughter who is a bride, and she fell ill and her hair fell out, shall I add to it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the woman who adds hair and the woman who has it added."
"25316","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj al-Ataki narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq narrating from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, that a slave-girl from the Ansar was married and she fell ill and her hair fell out, so they wanted to join to it, and they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about adding hair, so he cursed the woman who adds hair and the woman who has it added."
"25317","Husayn and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ghusl from janabah then come to the mosque with his head dripping, while he intended fasting that day."
"25318","Husayn and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bahiyy, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Hand me the khumrah from the mosque. She said: I said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand. Abu Ahmad said: Your menstruation is not from your hand."
"25319","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the desert to the charity camels and gave his wives a camel each, except me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave them a camel each except me, so he gave me a strong difficult camel that had not been ridden upon. He said: O Aishah, be gentle with it, for gentleness does not mix with a thing except it adorns it, nor depart a thing except it disgraces it."
"25320","Husayn narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed standing would bow standing, and when he prayed sitting would bow sitting."
"25321","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sad ibn Hisham, he said: I came to Aishah and said: O Mother of the Believers, I want to devote myself to worship. She said: Do not do it. Have you not read: There has certainly been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married and children were born to him."
"25322","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his mother Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The surplus of water is not to be withheld, nor the hollow of a well."
"25323","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she bought a patterned cloth with images and wanted to make it a canopy, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her and she showed it to him and informed him that she wanted to make it a canopy, so he said to her: Cut it into two cushions. She said: So I did, and I used to recline upon them and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recline upon them."
"25324","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Imran ibn Bashir, from Salim Sablan, he said: We went out with Aishah to Makkah. He said: And she would go out with Abu Yahya al-Taymi leading her in prayer. He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq caught up with us, and Abd al-Rahman performed wudu badly, so Aishah said: O Abd al-Rahman, perform wudu fully, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels on the Day of Resurrection from the Fire."
"25325","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from al-Ashath, meaning Ibn Sulaym, from Habbah, he said: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to make nabidh in gourd, hantam, and muzaffat."
"25326","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir say: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Aishah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Indeed Jibril, peace be upon him, conveys salam to you. She said: And upon him be salam and the mercy of Allah."
"25327","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Bilal would come to him and announce to him the prayer while he was junub, so he would stand and perform ghusl, then come to the mosque and pray, and I would hear his recitation with his head dripping, then he would fast that day."
"25328","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he sits between the four branches then joins circumcision to circumcision, ghusl has become obligatory."
"25329","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from Mujahid, he said: Aishah said: The family of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a wild animal, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out it played and ran and came and went, and when it sensed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had entered it crouched and did not move as long as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the house, out of dislike to harm him."
"25330","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, he said: I said to Aishah: Narrate to me of the most beloved deed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) She said: The most beloved deed to him was that which a man persists upon, even if little."
"25331","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Habib narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ata ibn Yasar, he said: A man came and spoke ill of Ali and Ammar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both, in the presence of Aishah. She said: As for Ali, I am not saying anything to you about him, and as for Ammar, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He is not given choice between two matters except he chooses the more guided of them."
"25332","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Safiyyah, from his mother, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast for one of his wives with two mudds of barley."
"25333","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri, freedman of Banu Asad, narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray at night long standing and long sitting. I said: How did he do. She said: When he recited standing he bowed standing, and when he recited sitting he bowed sitting."
"25334","He said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Masruq, from Aishah, she said: I bear witness that he never came in my day ever except he prayed two rakahs after Asr."
"25335","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch me intimately while I was menstruating and enter with me under my blanket while I was menstruating, but he was the most controlling of you of his desire."
"25336","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Bajali al-Sulami narrated to us, from his mother, she said: I asked Aishah about Umrah after Hajj. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent my brother with me, so I went out from the Haram and performed Umrah."
"25337","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Aban narrated to us, from Qatadah and Yazid al-Rishk, from Muadhah, from Aishah, that she said: Command your husbands to wash from themselves the trace of stool and urine, for we are shy from them, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"25338","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, that Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq informed Abdullah ibn Umar, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you not seen that your people, when they built the Kabah, fell short of the foundations of Ibrahim, peace be upon him. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not return it upon the foundations of Ibrahim. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that your people are recent in disbelief. Abdullah ibn Umar said: By Allah, if Aishah heard that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I do not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left touching the two corners adjacent to the Hijr except that the House was not completed upon the foundations of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, intending that the people encompass the whole House in tawaf from beyond the foundations of Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
"25339","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri said: Urwah narrated to me, from Aishah, she used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No calamity befalls a Muslim except it is expiated by it for him, even the thorn he is pricked with."
"25340","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that Aishah, Mother of the Believers, narrated to him about the pledge of women: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never touched with his hand the hand of a woman ever, except to take pledge upon her; when he took upon her and she gave him, he said: Go, for I have pledged you."
"25341","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that Aishah narrated to him, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was never given choice between two matters ever except he chose the easier of them, unless it were sin; if it were sin he was the farthest of people from it. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never took revenge for himself for anything violated of him, except a sanctity belonging to Allah Almighty be violated, then he takes revenge for Allah Almighty thereby."
"25342","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him that Aishah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he complained would recite upon himself with the Muawwidhat and blow. He said: Aishah said: When the pain of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intensified I would recite upon him and wipe from him with his hand, hoping for its blessing."
"25343","I think Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Humayd ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Hand me the khumrah from the mosque. I said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand."
"25344","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray much of his prayer sitting."
"25345","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went out would cast lots among his wives."
"25346","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zahiriyyah informed me, from Aishah, that she said: A woman gifted her dates in a tray, so she ate some and some remained, and she said: I adjure you except you eat the rest. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fulfill her oath, for the sin is upon the one who causes violation."
"25347","Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Aban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muadhah, from Aishah, she said: Command your husbands to wash from themselves the trace of stool and urine, for we are shy from them, and indeed the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"25348","Muhammad ibn Kunasah al-Asadi Abu Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, he said: It reached me that Aishah said: I never eavesdropped upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except once, for Uthman came to him in midday heat and I thought he came to him about the matter of women, so jealousy carried me to listen to him, and I heard him say: Indeed Allah Almighty will clothe you with a shirt; your nation will want you to take it off, so do not take it off. When I saw Uthman giving them all they asked except taking it off, I knew it was from the covenant of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he covenanted to him."
"25349","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Masruq and Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a sick person was brought to him would say: Remove the harm, Lord of the people, heal, You are the Healer, there is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness."
"25350","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, that she bought Barirah from people of the Ansar and they stipulated the wala, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wala is for one who confers the favor. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her choice, and her husband was a slave, and she gifted meat to Aishah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you would make for us from this meat. Aishah said: It was given as charity to Barirah. He said: It is upon her charity and for us a gift."
"25351","Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: I said to al-Aswad: Did you ask the Mother of the Believers Aishah about what it is disliked to make nabidh in. He said: Yes. I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, what is disliked to make nabidh in. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the household from gourd and muzaffat."
"25352","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: Aishah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he performed ghusl from janabah would rinse his mouth and sniff water."
"25353","Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Umarah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: While Aishah was in her house she heard a sound in Madinah and said: What is this. They said: A caravan of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf arrived from Sham carrying everything. He said: It was seven hundred camels. He said: Madinah shook with the sound. Aishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I have seen Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf entering Paradise crawling. That reached Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, so he said: If I can, I shall surely enter it standing. So he made it with its saddles and loads in the path of Allah Almighty."
"25354","Sulayman ibn Harb and Affan said: Shubah narrated to us, Affan said: Qatadah informed me, from Mutarrif, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing: Subbuh Quddus, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"25355","Shubah said: Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Aishah, that she said: In his bowing and his prostration. Affan said: Shubah said: So I mentioned that to Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah, and he said: In his bowing and his prostration."
"25356","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abu Sakhr narrated to me, from Ibn Qusayyt, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed would stand until his feet cracked. Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do you do this though there has been forgiven for you what preceded of your sin and what remained. He said: O Aishah, shall I not be a thankful slave."
"25357","He said: Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abu Sakhr informed me, from Abu Qusayyt, he narrated to him, that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from her at night. She said: So I was jealous over him. She said: So he came and saw what I do, so he said: What is with you, O Aishah, are you jealous. She said: So I said: What is with me that one like me would not be jealous over one like you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Has your devil taken hold of you. She said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is there a devil with me. He said: Yes. I said: And with every human. He said: Yes. I said: And with you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes, but my Lord Almighty aided me against him until he submitted."
"25358","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was never given choice between two matters except he chose the easier of them, as long as it was not sin; if it was sin he was the farthest of people from it. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never took revenge for himself in a matter violated of him, except a sanctity for Allah Almighty be violated, then he takes revenge for Allah Almighty."
"25359","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Revenue is with liability."
"25360","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spread it out."
"25361","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: So we made them two cushions, meaning the curtain."
"25362","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Khawwat ibn Salih, from his paternal aunt Umm Amr bint Khawwat, that a woman said to Aishah: My daughter was struck by illness and her hair fell, and it is full, I cannot comb it, and she is a bride, shall I add to her hair. Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who adds hair and the woman who has it added."
"25363","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from Aishah, she said: People from the Jews entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Al-sam be upon you. He said: And upon you. Aishah said: Upon you be the curse of Allah and the curse of the cursers. They said: Your father was not foul-mouthed. When they left, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What carried you to what you did. She said: Did you not hear what they said. He said: Did you not see me say: And upon you. What I say to them befalls them, and what they said to me does not befall me."
"25364","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Nafi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, that a woman from the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my daughter complained and the hair of her head fell, and her husband has pressed me, do you see that I add to her head. He said: No, for the joined have been cursed."
"25365","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid al-Ayli narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came to his bed every night would join his palms then blow into them and recite into them: Say He is Allah One, and Say I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and Say I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, then wipe with them what he could of his body, beginning with them upon his head and face and what faces of his body, doing that three times."
"25366","He said: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abi al-Zinad, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed my chin upon his shoulder so I could look at the play of the Abyssinians, until I was the one who tired and turned away from them."
"25367","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, he said: Urwah said to me: Indeed Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day: So the Jews know that in our religion there is latitude. Indeed I was sent with a lenient monotheism."
"25368","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talqani narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, and Ali ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah informed us, from Anbasah ibn Said, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Abbas said: Do you know what is the vastness of Hell. I said: No. He said: Yes indeed, by Allah, you do not know: between the lobe of one's ear and his shoulder is a journey of seventy autumns, in which run valleys of pus and blood. I said: Rivers. He said: No, rather valleys. Then he said: Do you know what is the vastness of Hell. I said: No. He said: Yes indeed, by Allah, you do not know: Aishah narrated to me that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying: And the earth entirely will be His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens folded in His right hand, where will the people be that day, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They will be upon the bridge of Hell."
"25369","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Aishah, this is Jibril, peace be upon him, and he conveys salam to you. I said: Upon you and upon him be salam and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. You see what we do not see, O Messenger of Allah."
"25370","Ibrahim and Ali ibn Ishaq said: Ibn Mubarak, from Mamar and Yunus, and Ali ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Mamar and Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became heavy and his pain intensified, he sought permission of his wives to be nursed in my house, so they permitted him."
"25371","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq and Ali said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, Ali said: Ibn Mubarak informed us, from Yunus, Ali said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah informed me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended travel would cast lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out he would go out with her. And he would apportion for each woman of them her day and night, except that Sawdah bint Zamah had given her day and night to Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking thereby the pleasure of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"
"25372","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awzai and Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The caller to prayer, when he fell silent from the dawn prayer, would pray two light rakahs, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"
"25373","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihzam narrated to us, he said: Karimah bint Hammam narrated to me, she said: I entered the Sacred Mosque and they cleared it for Aishah, so a woman asked her: What do you say, O Mother of the Believers, about henna. She said: My beloved (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked its color and disliked its smell, and it is not forbidden for you between every two menstruations, or at every menstruation."
"25374","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Safiyyah, that his mother Safiyyah bint Shaybah narrated to him that Aishah narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recline in my lap while I was menstruating, then recite the Quran."
"25375","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Yunus and Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq entered upon her and headed toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was covered with a Hibarah cloak, so he uncovered his face, then bent over him and kissed him and wept, then said: By my father and mother, by Allah, Allah Almighty will never combine two deaths upon you ever; as for the death that was decreed upon you, you have died it."
"25376","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Mujalid informed us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he mentioned Khadijah would praise her and praise well. She said: So I was jealous one day and said: How much you mention her, red of gums, Allah Almighty has replaced her for you with better than her. He said: Allah Almighty has not replaced me with better than her: she believed in me when people disbelieved in me, and confirmed me when people denied me, and supported me with her wealth when people withheld from me, and Allah Almighty provided me her children when He withheld me the children of women."
"25377","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah narrated to me, from Aishah, that she said: Are you not amazed at Abu Hurayrah. He came and sat beside my chamber narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) making me hear that, while I was glorifying. He stood before I finished my glorification. Had I reached him I would have refuted him: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not narrate hadith continuously as you narrate continuously."
"25378","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Asim informed us, from Muadhah, from Aishah, she said: I used to wash, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from one vessel, he racing me and I racing him, and I say: Leave for me, leave for me."
"25379","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me when I was six years old in Makkah after the death of Khadijah, and consummated with me when I was nine years old in Madinah."
"25380","He said: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: Revelation would indeed come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon his riding camel, and it would strike with its chest-neck to the ground."
"25381","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: Abu Bakr said to her: O my daughter, on which day did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) die. I said: Monday. He said: In how many did you shroud the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I said: O my father, we shrouded him in three white Sahuli Yemeni new cloths, without shirt or turban therein; he was wrapped therein wrapping."
"25382","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, he said: My father informed me that Aishah said to him: O son of my sister, you have seen of the honoring by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of his uncle a wondrous matter, and that is that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would be seized by flank pain and it would intensify greatly, and we would say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has been seized by kidney vein; we could not bring ourselves to say: the flank. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was seized one day and it intensified greatly until he fainted and we feared for him and people rushed to him, and we thought he had pleurisy, so we administered medicine by mouth forcibly. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recovered and awoke and knew that he had been forcibly medicated and found the trace of the medicine, so he said: You thought that Allah Almighty imposed it upon me; Allah would not impose it upon me. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no one remains in the house except he is forcibly medicated except my uncle. So I saw them medicating them man by man. Aishah said: And who was in the house that day. Then she mentions their merit. So all the men were medicated, and the forced medicine reached the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so they were medicated woman by woman, until the forced medicine reached a woman of us. Ibn Abi al-Zinad said: I know her only as Maymunah. He said: And some people said: Umm Salamah. She said: Indeed, by Allah, I am fasting. We said: Evil is what you thought, that we leave you though the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has sworn. So we medicated her, by Allah, O son of my sister, though she was fasting."
"25383","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was below the jummah and above the wafrah."
"25384","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he wanted to sleep while junub would perform wudu as his wudu for prayer, and when he wanted to eat and drink, she said: he would wash his hands then eat and drink."
"25385","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like the hadith of Yunus."
"25386","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from one who narrated to him, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he wanted to sleep while junub would perform wudu as his wudu for prayer; when he wanted to eat he would wash his hands then eat."
"25387","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym al-Hadrami, from Muslim ibn Mikhraq, he said: I said to Aishah: O Mother of the Believers, some people recite the Quran in a night twice or thrice. She said: Those recited and did not recite. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand the complete night and recite Surah al-Baqarah and Surah Al Imran and Surah al-Nisa, then he would not pass a verse of glad tidings except he supplicated Allah Almighty and desired, nor pass a verse of fright except he supplicated Allah Almighty and sought refuge."
"25388","Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj; among us one who entered ihram with Hajj and among us one who entered ihram with Umrah, and he had driven sacrificial animals. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever entered ihram with Umrah and did not drive, let him exit ihram; and whoever entered ihram and drove, let him not exit ihram; and whoever entered ihram with Hajj, let him complete his Hajj. Aishah said: And I was among those who entered ihram with Umrah."
"25389","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, from Nafi, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he saw rain would say: O Allah, a wholesome abundant rain."
"25390","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ghusl and pray two rakahs; I do not see him renewing wudu after ghusl."
"25391","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Salamah bint Suhayl ibn Amr suffered istihadah, so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that, so he commanded her with ghusl at every prayer. When that burdened her, he commanded her to combine Dhuhr and Asr with one ghusl, and Maghrib and Isha with one ghusl, and Fajr with one ghusl."
"25392","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: Jewelry came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Negus, gifted to him, among it a gold ring with an Abyssinian stone. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it with a stick with part of his fingers turning away from it, then called Umamah bint Abi al-As, daughter of his daughter, and said: Adorn yourself with this, O my daughter."
"25393","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Muti narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Yazid al-Jufi, from Amir, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes a dead person and fulfills trust therein and does not disclose what he sees of him at that, exits his sins as the day his mother bore him. He said: Let the closest of you to him undertake it if he knows; if he does not know, then whom you see having a share of piety and trustworthiness."
"25394","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Abu Amr, freedman of Aishah, informed him, from Aishah, that she informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be junub and want to sleep, so he would perform wudu as his wudu for prayer, then sleep."
"25395","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cultivates a land belonging to no one, he is most entitled to it."
"25396","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No calamity befalls a Muslim except it is expiated for him, even the thorn he is pricked with."
"25397","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw Jibril, peace be upon him, descending, having filled what is between heaven and earth, and upon him garments of sundus, with pearls and rubies hanging from him."
"25398","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, that Muadhah narrated to him, she said: I said to Aishah: Does one of us make up her prayer when she becomes pure. She said: Are you a Haruriyyah. We used to menstruate while with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we would not do that, or she said: he did not command us with that."
"25399","He said: Bahz narrated it to us, and he did not say: Muadhah narrated to me, and he said: from and from."
"25400","Affan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah ibn Abi Raitah al-Mujashii narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Ishaq informed me, he said: My paternal aunt Aishah bint Talhah informed me, from her maternal aunt Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The jihad of women is the Hajj of this House."
"25401","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muadhah, she said: I asked Aishah, how many rakahs did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray for Duha? She said: Four rakahs, and he would add whatever Allah willed."
"25402","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muadhah, from Aishah, that she said: Order your husbands to wash off from themselves the trace of relieving themselves and urine, for we are shy to forbid them from that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"25403","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, I took his hand and began passing it over his chest and supplicated with these words: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind. So he pulled his hand away from my hand and said: I ask Allah for the Highest, Most Blessed Companion."
"25404","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, she said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah ibn Judan in the Jahiliyyah used to feed the guest and free the captive and uphold kinship and treat the neighbor well, so I praised him, will that benefit him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, he never said even one day: O Allah, forgive me on the Day of Judgment. And Affan once said: So I praised him."
"25405","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) showed affection to me and said: You are the most important of what I leave behind me, and by Allah none will show kindness to you except the patient ones, or the truthful ones."
"25406","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the wind had intensified, his face changed."
"25407","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his illness from which he did not rise: May Allah curse the Jews and the Christians, they took the graves of their prophets as mosques. He said: I said: Had it not been for that, his grave would have been made prominent, except that he feared it would be taken as a mosque."
"25408","Affan narrated to us, from Abu Awanah, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allegiance belongs to the one who frees."
"25409","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with about a sa."
"25410","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: Safiyyah bint Shaybah narrated to me that Aishah narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd. Affan once said: To the measure of a mudd, and bathe with a sa."
"25411","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Firas, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered with him one day and said: O Prophet of Allah, which of us will join you fastest? He said: The longest of you in hand. So they took a reed and measured it, and Sawdah bint Zamah was the longest of us in forearm. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and Sawdah was the fastest of us to join him, so we knew afterwards that the length of her hand was only from charity, and she was a woman who loved charity. And Affan once said: A reed we measure."
"25412","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Umm Muhammad narrated to me, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sleep at night or day and then wake except that he used the tooth-stick."
"25413","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am at the Pool waiting for those among you who will come to me, and men will surely be cut off before reaching me, so I will surely say: O Lord, my nation, my nation. So it will surely be said to me: You do not know what they did after you; they kept turning back on their heels."
"25414","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us that Abu Salamah narrated to him that Aishah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to sleep, would perform his ablution for prayer, then sleep."
"25415","Affan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she was asked: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do in his house? She said: He would sew his garment and patch his sandal and do what men do in their houses."
"25416","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Muammil informed me, he said: I heard al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed two rakahs before Fajr, would perhaps lie down."
"25417","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away with his head between my chest and my throat. She said: When his soul departed, I never found any scent more pleasant than it."
"25418","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn al-Mutamir narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thinking it was only Hajj. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived at Makkah and performed tawaf and did not exit ihram, and he had the sacrificial animal with him. Those with him among his women and his companions performed tawaf, and those among them who had no sacrificial animal exited ihram, and she menstruated. So we completed our rites of our Hajj, and when it was the night of al-Hasbah, the night of departure, she said: O Messenger of Allah, will your companions return with Hajj and Umrah while I return with Hajj only? He said: Did you not perform tawaf on the nights we arrived? She said: I said: No. He said: Go with your brother to al-Tanim and enter ihram for Umrah, then your appointed place is such-and-such place. She said: And Safiyyah menstruated, so he said: May she be barren or shaven, she will surely detain us. Did you not perform tawaf of the House on the Day of Sacrifice? She said: Yes. He said: No harm, then depart. She said: So I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveling at the end of the night while he was ascending upon the people of Makkah and I was descending upon them, or he was descending upon them and I was ascending."
"25419","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his mother, from Aishah, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, how do I bathe upon purity? He said: Take a musk-scented cloth and perform ablution. She said: How do I perform ablution with it? He said: Perform ablution with it. She said: How do I perform ablution with it? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) glorified Allah and turned away from her, then said: Perform ablution with it. Aishah said: So I understood what the Messenger of Allah intended, so I took it and pulled it to me and informed her of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended."
"25420","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Marwan Abu Lubabah from Banu Uqayl narrated to us, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until we would say he does not intend to break his fast, and break his fast until we would say he does not intend to fast, and he would recite every night Bani Israil and al-Zumar."
"25421","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: And Makhul narrated it to me. Both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever makes the private part of the woman lawful of dowry or waiting period belongs to her, and whatever her father or her brother or her guardian is honored with after the marriage contract belongs to him, and the most deserving of what a man is honored with are his daughter and his sister."
"25422","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: And Makhul narrated it to me. Both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever makes the private part of the woman lawful of dowry or waiting period belongs to her, and whatever her father or her brother or her guardian is honored with after the marriage contract belongs to him, and the most deserving of what a man is honored with are his daughter and his sister."
"25423","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Muti narrated to me, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, he said: Aishah said: Whoever washes a dead person and fulfills the trust in it, meaning that he does not spread what he sees of him at that time, he will be of his sins like the day his mother bore him. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the closest of his family to him take charge of him if he knows, and if he does not know, then let the one among you whom you see having a share of piety or trustworthiness take charge of him."
"25424","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five pests are killed in the lawful land and the sanctuary: the vicious dog, the mouse, the kite, the crow, and the scorpion."
"25425","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that some people used to worship with severe worship, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them and said: By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of you about Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and the most fearful of you of Him. And he used to say: Upon you are the deeds you can bear, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, does not tire until you tire."
"25426","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would strive in the last ten nights as he would not strive in other than it."
"25427","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Numan, from Aishah, she said: When the two circumcised parts met, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would bathe."
"25428","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah and Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Muadhah, from Aishah, that she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel, racing him in haste."
"25429","Affan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Sad ibn Aws, from Misda Abu Yahya al-Ansari, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her while fasting and suck her tongue. I said: Did you hear it from Sad ibn Aws? He said: Yes."
"25430","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hammad informed us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that a mastigure was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not eat it. Aishah said: So I said, O Messenger of Allah, shall I not feed it to the poor? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not feed them from what you do not eat."
"25431","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Habib al-Muallim narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhazzim, from Abu Hurayrah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the hems of women: A span. He said: So Aishah said: Then their shins would show. And Affan once said: Their shins. He said: Then a cubit."
"25432","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abdullah ibn Abi Utbah, from Aishah, that charity meat had been given in charity to Barirah, so she gifted some to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So it was said to him: It is from charity meat. He said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"25433","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, and Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard sounds and said: What are these sounds? They said: The palm trees, they are pollinating them, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Had they not done it, it would have been fine. So they did not pollinate that year, and it became poor dates. So they mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If it is something of your worldly affairs, then it is your concern, and if it is something of your religious affairs, then it is for me."
"25434","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me that Aishah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sleep, then when he woke he would use the tooth-stick, then perform ablution, then pray eight rakahs, sitting in every two and giving salutation, then pray witr with five rakahs, not sitting except in the fifth and not giving salutation except in the fifth."
"25435","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sulaym, from Abdullah ibn Maqil al-Muharibi, he said: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to make nabidh in the gourd and the tarred vessel and the green jar."
"25436","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Said al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Jumay ibn Umayr al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: I went with my paternal aunt and my maternal aunt to Aishah, so she asked her: How would one of you do for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when she menstruated? So she said: When that happened to one of us, she would wrap herself in a wide waist-wrapper, then embrace the Messenger of Allah with her hands and her chest."
"25437","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Yazid al-Rishk informed me, from Muadhah, from Aishah, that she asked her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha as four? She said: Yes, four, and he would add whatever Allah willed."
"25438","Affan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Atiq narrated to us, from his father, that he heard Aishah narrate to him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The tooth-stick is purification for the mouth and pleasing to the Lord."
"25439","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasting the days of the ten ever."
"25440","Affan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: In his illness in which he passed away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would blow upon himself (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the Muawwidhat. When he became too heavy for that, I began blowing upon him with them and wiping him with his own hand."
"25441","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Ismail al-Suddi narrated to us, from Abdullah al-Bahiyy, from Aishah, she said: I would not make up what was upon me of Ramadan except in Shaban, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away."
"25442","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me, he said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: He is the One who sent down upon you the Book, in it are decisive verses, they are the Mother of the Book, and others allegorical, as for those in whose hearts is deviation, until he finished it. He said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has named them, so if you see them, beware of them."
"25443","Quraysh ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Abd al-Malik al-Taymi, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from his paternal aunt Amrah, from Aishah, that she said: We used to make nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the morning in a skin, and we would not cover it nor make sediment for it. When evening came, he would eat supper and drink after his supper. If anything remained, I would empty it or pour it out, then we would wash the skin and make nabidh in it from the evening meal. When morning came, he would eat breakfast and drink after his breakfast. If anything extra remained, I would pour it out or empty it, then he washed the skin. So it was said to him: Is washing the skin in it twice? He said: Twice."
"25444","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: Umar erred. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade prayer intending the rising of the sun and its setting."
"25445","He said: Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she entered ihram for Umrah, then arrived and did not perform tawaf of the House until she menstruated. So she performed all the rites, though she had entered ihram for Hajj. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her on the Day of Sacrifice: Your tawaf suffices you for your Hajj and your Umrah. But she refused, so he sent her with Abd al-Rahman to al-Tanim, and she performed Umrah after Hajj."
"25446","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran narrated to me, he said: My father informed me, he said: Aishah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the caller, he would say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."
"25447","He said: Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hammad informed us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: As if I am looking at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after days while he is in ihram."
"25448","He said: Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, I took his hand and began passing it over his chest and supplicated with these words: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind. So he pulled his hand away from my hand and said: I ask Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for the Highest, Most Blessed Companion."
"25449","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I used to rub semen from the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would go and pray in it."
"25450","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, that Aishah said: You have made us in the rank of the dog and the donkey. I saw myself under my blanket between the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the qiblah, and I disliked appearing in front of him, until I would slip out from under the blanket slipping."
"25451","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Miqdam ibn Shurayh ibn Hani, he said: I heard my father narrate from Aishah, may Allah Almighty be pleased with her, that he heard her say: I was upon a difficult camel and I began beating it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Upon you is gentleness, for gentleness is never in anything except that it adorns it, and it is never removed from anything except that it disfigures it."
"25452","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, both said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam informed me, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, that he was staying with Aishah. Bahz said: A man from al-Nakha was staying with Aishah, then he had a wet dream, so a slave girl of Aishah saw him washing the trace of janabah from his garment, or washing his garment. Bahz said: Thus Shubah said. So she said: I saw myself doing no more than rubbing it from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25453","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated it to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that Hammam ibn al-Harith was staying with Aishah, then he mentioned its meaning."
"25454","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrate from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright and draw near and receive glad tidings, for none will be admitted to Paradise by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, except that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, covers me with mercy from Him. And know that the most beloved deed to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is the most constant, even if little."
"25455","He said: Affan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, kept advising me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"25456","Affan narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to me, he said: Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade celibacy."
"25457","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned severe hardship that will be before the Dajjal. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, where will the Arabs be then? He said: O Aishah, the Arabs then will be few. So I said: What will suffice the believers then of food? He said: What suffices the angels: glorification and magnification and praise and declaring unity. I said: Then which wealth then is best? He said: A strong boy who waters his family from water, and as for food, then there is no food."
"25458","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Musa, he said: Mudrik, or Ibn Mudrik, sent me to Aishah to ask her about things. He said: So I came to her and she was praying Duha. So I said: I will sit until she finishes. So they said: Far from it. So I said to her permission-announcer: How do I seek permission upon her? He said: Say: Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. Peace be upon the Mothers of the Believers, or the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Peace be upon you. He said: So I entered upon her and asked her. So she said: The brother of Azib, what a good household. So I asked her about continual fasting, so she said: When it was the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions fasted continually, and it was hard upon them. When they saw the crescent, they informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Had it increased, I would have increased. So it was said to him: You do that, or something like it. He said: I am not like you; I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink. And I asked her about the two rakahs after Asr, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man for charity. She said: So she came to him at noon, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr and was occupied in its division until he prayed Asr, then he prayed them. And she said: Upon you is night prayer, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not leave it; if he was ill, he would recite while sitting. And I knew that one of you says: It suffices me to stand what is written for me, and how would he attain that? And I asked her about the day disputed in Ramadan, so she said: For me to fast a day of Shaban is more beloved to me than to break fast a day of Ramadan. He said: So I went out and asked Ibn Umar and Abu Hurayrah, and each one of them said: The wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) know better about that than us. I heard my father say: Yazid ibn Khumayr is sound in hadith. My father said: Abdullah ibn Abi Musa is a mistake, Shubah erred in it; he is Abdullah ibn Abi Qays."
"25459","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a sick person, he would wipe him with his hand and say: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer, there is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness. When he fell ill in his illness in which he died, Aishah said: I took his hand and went to say it, so he pulled his hand away and said: O Allah, forgive me and place me in the Highest Companion."
"25460","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Aishah said: What interrupts prayer? He said: So we said: The donkey and the woman. He said: So Aishah said: The woman is then an evil animal. I saw myself in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lying across like the lying of a bier while he was praying. Shubah said: Between him and the qiblah, as I think."
"25461","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: I asked Aishah, how did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) act? So she said: He would be in the service of his family, then when prayer came, he would go out and pray."
"25462","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Ibrahim narrate from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was junub and wanted to sleep or eat, he would perform ablution."
"25463","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that Alqamah and Shurayh ibn Artah were with Aishah. So one of them said: Ask her about kissing for the fasting person. So one of them said: I will not speak obscenely before the Mother of the Believers. So she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting and embrace while fasting, and he was the most in control of you of his desire."
"25464","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from his mother, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The child of a man is from his earnings, from the purest of his earnings, so eat from their wealth wholesomely."
"25465","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Abu Bakr entered upon her while with her were two slave girls beating two tambourines. So Abu Bakr rebuked them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Leave them, for every people have a festival."
"25466","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she used to bathe, she and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel."
"25467","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh ibn Hani, from his father, he said: Aishah said: I would gnaw meat from the bone while menstruating, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take it and place his mouth where my mouth was, and I would drink from the vessel, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take it and place his mouth where my mouth was, while I was menstruating."
"25468","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked Aishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I never saw him prefer one night over another."
"25469","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail, he said: I heard al-Shabi narrate from Masruq, he said: I asked Aishah about a man who sends his sacrificial animal, does he abstain from what the one in ihram abstains from? He said: So I heard the sound of her hands from behind the veil, then she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would send them, then nothing would become forbidden of him."
"25470","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from a paternal aunt of his who asked Aishah about an orphan in her care. So Aishah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purest of what a man eats is from his earnings, and his child is from his earnings."
"25471","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Bakkar, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Sanani, informed us, then he mentioned a hadith. He said: And I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrate from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is reckoned will be punished. She said: So I said: What about His saying, the Mighty and Majestic: He will be reckoned an easy reckoning? He said: That is only the presentation, but whoever is questioned closely about the account will be punished."
"25472","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: When someone complained, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wipe him with his right hand, then say: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, and You are the Healer, there is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness."
"25473","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, he said: Aishah said: When Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, sent down the verses, the verses of usury from the end of Surah al-Baqarah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and recited them to us, then he forbade trade in wine."
"25474","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not recite in any of the night prayer sitting until he entered age. When thirty or forty verses remained upon him, he would stand and recite them, then prostrate."
"25475","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from his father Abis ibn Rabiah, from Aishah, he said: We asked her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid eating the meat of sacrifices after three? So she said: He said it only in a year in which people hungered, so he wanted the rich to feed the poor. And we would lift the trotter and eat it after fifteen days. I said: Then what compelled you to that? He said: So she laughed and said: The family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate to full of bread with condiment for three nights until he met Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"25476","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur ibn Safiyyah, from his mother, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while we had eaten to full of the two black ones: dates and water."
"25477","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Hudhayfah, a man from the companions of Abdullah, from Aishah, she said: I went to mimic a woman or a man before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not like that I mimicked anyone though I have such-and-such, the greatest."
"25478","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, he said: I said to Aishah: Does the fasting person embrace, meaning his wife? She said: No. I said: Did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embrace while fasting? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most in control of you of his desire."
"25479","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, that she said: As if I am looking at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he is in ihram."
"25480","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Aishah narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not fast in any month of the year more than his fasting in Shaban, for he would fast all of Shaban. And he used to say: Take of deeds what you can bear, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, does not tire until you tire. And the most beloved prayer to him was what was persisted upon, even if little. And when he prayed a prayer, he would persist upon it."
"25481","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, he said: Aishah narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rakahs between the call and the iqamah of the dawn prayer."
"25482","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Aishah: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleep while junub? She said: Yes, and he would perform his ablution for prayer."
"25483","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ata al-Khurasani informed us that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr entered upon Aishah on the Day of Arafah while she was fasting and water was being sprinkled upon her. So Abd al-Rahman said to her: Break your fast. So she said: Shall I break fast though I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fasting the Day of Arafah expiates the year before it."
"25484","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: I saw you in a dream twice, when a man was carrying you in a piece of silk and saying: This is your wife. So I uncover it, and it is you. So I say: If this is from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, He will carry it out."
"25485","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Abu Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah, that Umm Habibah bint Jahsh was under Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and she suffered prolonged bleeding and would not become pure. So her affair was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: It is not menstruation, but it is a kick from the womb. So let her look at the measure of her period for which she used to menstruate, let her leave prayer, then let her look at what is after that, let her bathe at every prayer and pray."
"25486","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw rain, he would say: O Allah, wholesome abundant rain."
"25487","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Asim, from Muslim, from Masruq, and Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, he said: I asked Aishah about the witr of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: From every night he prayed witr, its middle and its end and its beginning. So his witr ended at dawn until he died."
"25488","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she said: Sad ibn Abi Waqqas and Abd ibn Zamah disputed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Sad said: O Messenger of Allah, the son of my brother Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas entrusted to me that he is his son, look at his resemblance. And Abd ibn Zamah said: This is my brother, O Messenger of Allah, he was born on the bed of my father. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at his resemblance and saw a clear resemblance to Utbah. So he said: He is yours, O Abd ibn Zamah. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. And veil yourself from him, O Sawdah daughter of Zamah. She said: So he never saw Sawdah ever."
"25489","He said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send the sacrificial animal, then not do what the one in ihram does."
"25490","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing remains after me of prophethood except the bearers of glad tidings. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the bearers of glad tidings? He said: The righteous dream, a man sees it or it is seen for him. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard this hadith from Yahya ibn Ayyub more than once. Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated it to us, dictating it to us dictation. He said: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us the like of it."
"25491","Al-Hakam ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel, while we were junub, but water does not become junub."
"25492","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked prayer in the wraps of women."
"25493","Qatadah said: And either Kathir or Abd Rabbihi narrated to me, Hammam doubted, from Abu Iyad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed wearing a woolen cloak of Aishah, part of it upon her and part of it upon him."
"25494","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, make me among those who, when they do good, rejoice, and when they do bad, seek forgiveness."
"25495","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raced me, and I outran him."
"25496","Affan narrated to us, he said: al-Kirmani Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Masruq narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abi Burdah ibn Abi Musa al-Ashari, from Abu Burdah, he said: I came to Aishah and said: O my mother, narrate to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Birds move by decree, and the good omen used to please him."
"25497","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Aishah, she said: As if I am looking at its glisten, the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he is in ihram."
"25498","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: Muadhah al-Adawiyyah narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: Order your husbands to wash off from themselves the trace of relieving themselves and urine, for I am shy to order them with that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"25499","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Mamar and Numan, or one of them, narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never cursed a Muslim with a remembered curse, nor took revenge for himself for anything brought to him, except that the sanctities of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, be violated. And he never struck anything with his hand ever, except that he strike with it in the path of Allah. And he was never asked anything and withheld it, except that he be asked a sin, for he was the farthest of people from it. And he was never given choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them. And when he was freshly with Jibril, peace be upon him, studying with him, he was the most generous with good than the sent wind."
"25500","Affan narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated to me, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Umm Muhammad, wife of his father, from Aishah, she said: Umm Salamah was with us, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came at nightfall. She said: So I mentioned something he did with his hand. She said: And he did not notice Umm Salamah. She said: And I began gesturing to him until he noticed. Umm Salamah said: Is it like this now? Was there ever one of us with you except in deceit as I see? And she insulted Aishah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began forbidding her, but she refused. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Insult her back. So she insulted her until she overcame her. Then Umm Salamah went to Ali and Fatimah and said: Aishah insulted her and said to you and said to you. So Ali said to Fatimah: Go to him and say: Aishah said to us and said to us. So she came to him and mentioned that to him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: She is the beloved of your father, by the Lord of the Kabah. So she returned to Ali and mentioned to him what he said to her. So he said: Is it not enough except that Aishah said to us and said to us, until Fatimah came to you and you said to her: She is the beloved of your father, by the Lord of the Kabah."
"25501","Azhar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn informed us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed me, from Umm Muhammad, the wife of his father, she said - and she used to visit Aishah - she said: Zaynab bint Jahsh was with us, and he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Sulaym ibn Akhdar, except that Sulaym said: Umm Salamah."
"25502","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at his ihram with the best perfume I could find."
"25503","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to kiss in Ramadan while he was fasting."
"25504","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Sulaym informed me that he heard his father narrating from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, loved starting with the right side in all his affairs, in his purification, his combing of hair, and his shoes. She said: Then I asked him in Kufah, and he said: Starting with the right as much as one is able."
"25505","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she narrated to him that she used to bathe, she and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a single vessel, he scooping before her and she scooping before him."
"25506","Affan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Abu Uthman al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrating from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that she heard him saying: Every intoxicant is unlawful, and whatever intoxicates in the quantity of a farq, a handful of it is unlawful."
"25507","Affan narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to me, he said: Aishah used to take on debts, so it was said to her: What is with you and debt? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There is no servant who has an intention to repay his debt except that he will have help from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for him, so I seek that help."
"25508","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished with al-Ahzab, he entered the washroom to bathe, then Jibril, peace be upon him, came and said: Have you already laid down arms? We have not laid down our arms yet. Rise against Banu Qurayzah. Aishah said: It is as if I am looking at Jibril, peace be upon him, through the opening of the door, having bound his head due to dust."
"25509","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: I used to perform ruqyah for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, against the evil eye, placing my hand on his chest and saying: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, in Your hand is healing, none removes it but You."
"25510","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abbad, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying in his bowing in the night prayer: There is no god but You."
"25511","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Affan said: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, he said: I entered upon Aishah, and she brought out to us a coarse waist-wrapper from what is made in Yemen and a cloak of the kind they call mulabbadah - Bahz said: you call - and she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died in these two garments."
"25512","Affan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, she said: A woman among his wives who was experiencing non-menstrual bleeding observed itikaf with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she would see yellowness and redness, so sometimes we placed a basin beneath her while she was praying."
"25513","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Ismail al-Suddi, from Abdullah al-Bahiyy, from Aishah, she said: I would not make up what was due upon me from Ramadan except in Shaban, until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away."
"25514","Affan narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Thumamah ibn Hazn al-Qushayri narrated to me, he said: I asked Aishah about nabidh, and she said: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he forbade them to make nabidh in dubba, naqir, muqayyar, and hantam. And she called an Abyssinian slave girl and said to me: Ask this one, for she used to make nabidh for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a waterskin at night; I would tie its mouth and hang it, and in the morning he would drink from it."
"25515","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: When a sick person was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he would say: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer, there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no illness."
"25516","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit, from Shumaysah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a journey of his, and a camel belonging to Safiyyah fell ill, while among the camels of Zaynab there was surplus, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: A camel belonging to Safiyyah has fallen ill, so if only you would give her a camel from your camels. She said: Should I give that Jewess? He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left her for Dhu al-Hijjah and al-Muharram, two or three months, not coming to her. She said: Until I despaired of him and moved my bed. She said: Then one day at midday, I saw the shadow of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, approaching. Affan said: Hammad narrated it to me from Shumaysah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then I heard him afterwards narrating it from Shumaysah from Aishah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said afterwards: During a Hajj or Umrah - he said: And I do not think him but he said: During the Farewell Hajj."
"25517","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Aishah, that she made for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a black woolen cloak, and he mentioned its blackness and whiteness, so he wore it, and when he sweated and smelled the odor of wool, he cast it off, and he used to love pleasant scent."
"25518","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah informed us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited this verse: He it is Who sent down upon you the Book, in it are verses that are clear, they are the Mother of the Book, and others ambiguous, up to: those in whose hearts is deviation, until when he finished it, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has named them, so when you see them, beware of them."
"25519","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Abu Bakr said to her: On which day did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, die? She said: On Monday. He said: If Allah wills, I do not hope for anything between me and the night. He said: In what did you shroud him? She said: In three white Yemeni Suhuli cloths, among which was neither shirt nor turban. And Abu Bakr said: Look at this garment of mine in which there is a trace of saffron or red dye, wash it and add two other garments with it. Aishah said: O my father, it is worn out. He said: The living has more right to the new, and it is only for the discharge of fluids. And Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr had given them a Hibarah shawl, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was wrapped in it, then they took him out of it and he was shrouded in three white cloths. He said: So Abdullah took the shawl and said: I will surely shroud myself in something that touched the skin of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he said afterwards: By Allah, I will not shroud myself in something that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, prevented His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from being shrouded in. So he died on the night of Tuesday and was buried at night, and Aishah died and Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr buried her at night."
"25520","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Shaddad informed us, from Abu Udhrah, he said - and he had met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade men and women from public baths, then he permitted men to enter them wearing waist-wrappers."
"25521","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, that Aishah said: You have put us in the position of the dog and the donkey. I would see myself under my cloak between the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the qiblah, and I would dislike to appear in front of him, so I would slip out from under the quilt stealthily."
"25522","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I used to rub semen from the garment of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he would go and pray in it."
"25523","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal, meaning Ibn Fudalah, narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn al-Had narrated to me that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr used to narrate from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that she used to say: When dawn rose, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray two light rakahs, then lie down on his right side."
"25524","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah al-Aslami, from Abdullah ibn Niyar al-Aslami, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she said: Umm Sunbulah gave milk as a gift to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but did not find him, so she said to her: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has forbidden that the food of the Bedouins be eaten. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr entered, and he said: What is this with you, O Umm Sunbulah? She said: Milk I gifted to you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Pour, Umm Sunbulah. So she poured, and he said: Hand to Abu Bakr. So she did, then he said: Pour, Umm Sunbulah. So she poured, and she handed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he drank. Aishah said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was drinking milk - and how cooling it is to the liver - O Messenger of Allah, I had been told that you had forbidden the food of the Bedouins. He said: O Aishah, they are not Bedouins; they are people of our countryside and we are people of their town, and when they are invited they respond, so they are not Bedouins."
"25525","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Zubayd informed us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade dubba and muzaffat vessels."
"25526","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Muslim ibn Qurt, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you goes to relieve himself, let him take three stones with him to clean himself with them, for they suffice him."
"25527","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man attains by good character the rank of one who fasts and stands in prayer."
"25528","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Salih ibn Ajlan and Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abbad, from Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, that Aishah ordered the funeral bier of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas to be passed by her in the mosque, and it reached her that something was said about that, so she said: How quick people are to speak. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not pray over Suhayl Ibn al-Bayda except in the mosque."
"25529","al-Nadr ibn Ismail Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa."
"25530","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, that she said - Bahz said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me wearing a waist-wrapper and a cloak, faced the qiblah, spread his hands, and said: O Allah, I am only a human, so whichever servant among Your servants I strike or harm, do not punish me for it. Bahz said: In it."
"25531","He said: Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim informed us, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: Sawdah was a slow, heavy woman, so she sought permission from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to depart from Muzdalifah before standing, and I would have loved to have sought his permission and he permitted me. And al-Qasim used to dislike departing before standing."
"25532","Affan narrated to us, Jafar ibn Kaysan narrated to me, he said: Muadhah al-Adawiyyah narrated to me, she said: I entered upon Aishah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My nation perishes only by stabbing and plague."
"25533","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Jabr ibn Habib informed us, from Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught her this supplication: O Allah, I ask You for all good, its immediate and its delayed, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the best of what Your servant and Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked You, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what Your servant and Prophet sought refuge from. O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and whatever brings near to it of speech or deed, and I ask You to make every decree You decree for me good."
"25534","Affan narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, he said: Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab narrated to us, he said: I asked Aishah: Was poetry recited in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? She said: It was the most hateful speech to him."
"25535","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: When one of us menstruated, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would order her to wrap her waist-wrapper, then he would embrace her."
"25536","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Talhah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, leaned toward me to kiss me, so I said: I am fasting. He said: And I am fasting. She said: So he leaned toward me and kissed me."
"25537","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from al-Shabi, Aishah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when the earth is changed to other than the earth and the heavens, and they come forth before Allah, the One, the Irresistible, where will the people be on that day? He said: On the Sirat."
"25538","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs informed me, he said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Aishah said: What do you say interrupts prayer? He said: They say: A woman, a dog, and a donkey interrupt prayer. She said: I would see myself lying across in front of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, like the lying of a funeral bier."
"25539","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the killing of the snake with two stripes, for it seeks eyesight and causes miscarriage."
"25540","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed us, from his father, he said: Aishah said: When this verse was revealed: You may defer whom you will of them and take to yourself whom you will, he said: Aishah said: I do not see your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, but hastening for you your desire."
"25541","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Aswad ibn Yazid and Masruq saying: We bear witness upon Aishah that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was never with me on a day except that he prayed two rakahs after Asr."
"25542","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she said: Abu Bakr entered upon us on a day of Eid, and with us were two slave girls recalling the Day of Buath, a day on which the chiefs of al-Aws and al-Khazraj were killed, so Abu Bakr said: Servants of Allah, the pipe of Satan? Servants of Allah, the pipe of Satan? He said it three times. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu Bakr, every people has an Eid, and today is our Eid."
"25543","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umar ibn Qays, from Muhammad ibn al-Ashath, from Aishah, she said: While I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a Jewish man sought permission and he permitted him, and he said: Death be upon you. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And upon you. She said: I intended to speak. She said: Then he entered a second time and said the same, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And upon you. She said: Then he entered a third time and said: Death be upon you. She said: So I said: Rather death be upon you and the anger of Allah, brothers of apes and pigs, do you greet the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with what Allah did not greet him with? She said: So he looked at me and said: Gently, Allah does not love obscenity nor indulging in it. They said a word and we returned it upon them, so nothing harmed us, and it remained upon them until the Day of Resurrection. They do not envy us for anything as they envy us for Friday, which Allah guided us to and they strayed from, and for the qiblah, which Allah guided us to and they strayed from, and for our saying behind the imam: Amen."
"25544","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hajabi informed us, from his mother Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would recline upon me while I was menstruating and recite the Quran."
"25545","Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: Barirah came to me seeking my help in her contract of manumission, so I said to her: If your masters wish, I will pay them your price in one payment and free you. So she consulted her masters, and they said: No, unless you stipulate guardianship for us. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Buy her, for guardianship belongs only to the one who frees."
"25546","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, from Umm Bakr, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf sold a land of his to Uthman ibn Affan for forty thousand dinars, then distributed it among the poor of Banu Zuhrah, the needy among people, and the Mothers of the Believers. Al-Miswar said: So I entered upon Aishah with her share of that, and she said: Who sent this? I said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None will show tenderness toward you after me except the patient. May Allah give Ibn Awf to drink from Salsabil of Paradise."
"25547","Abu Said narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Umm Bakr narrated to us that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf sold a land of his, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: She said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: None will show tenderness toward you after me except the patient."
"25548","Ibn al-Ashjai narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Aishah, she said: I would see myself scraping semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"25549","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Aishah, she said: I used to rub it off."
"25550","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would sleep until he snored, then stand and pray without performing ablution."
"25551","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory."
"25552","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I never saw anyone hastening Dhuhr more than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar."
"25553","Waki narrated to us, Mughirah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ata, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to delay Dhuhr and hasten Asr, and delay Maghrib and hasten Isha while traveling."
"25554","Waki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: I heard Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He did not make my name lawful and my kunyah unlawful, nor did he make my kunyah unlawful and my name lawful."
"25555","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, that a lahd grave was dug for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"25556","Waki narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about sudden death, and he said: Rest for the believer and a seizure of wrath for the wicked."
"25557","Waki narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Aishah, she said: A young woman came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father married me to his nephew to raise his low status thereby, so he gave the matter to her. She said: I have approved what my father did, but I wanted women to know that fathers have nothing of the matter."
"25558","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: When: And warn your nearest kin was revealed, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and said: O Fatimah bint Muhammad, O Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib, O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, I own nothing for you from Allah; ask me of my wealth what you wish."
"25559","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Miqdam, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Whoever narrates to you that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, urinated standing, do not believe him; the Messenger of Allah did not urinate standing since the Quran was revealed to him."
"25560","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah or Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sacrificed two fat, large, white-black, horned, castrated rams."
"25561","Waki narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from his father, from Aishah, she said: We would set aside a trotter for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would eat it after a month."
"25562","Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Sughayra narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If we had means, I would demolish the Kabah and build it, and make for it two doors, a door people enter from and a door they exit from. She said: When Ibn al-Zubayr took charge, he demolished it and made for it two doors. She said: So it remained so, then when al-Hajjaj prevailed over him, he demolished it and restored its original building."
"25563","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Hudhayfah, that Aishah imitated a woman before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioning her shortness, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have backbitten her."
"25564","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Hudhayfah, from Aishah, that she imitated a woman, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: I would not like to imitate anyone even if I had such-and-such."
"25565","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Thabit, from Ata, from Aishah, she said: A garment of mine was stolen, so I began supplicating against him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not lighten his burden thereby."
"25566","Waki narrated to us another time, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, from Ata, from Aishah, that a garment of hers was stolen, so she supplicated against its owner, and he said: Do not lighten his burden thereby."
"25567","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left neither dinar nor dirham, nor slave man nor slave woman, nor sheep nor camel."
"25568","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Asbahani, from Mujahid ibn Wardan, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that a freed slave of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell from a palm tree and died, leaving something but no child nor close relative, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give his inheritance to a man from the people of his village."
"25569","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A menstruating woman performs all the rites except tawaf of the House."
"25570","Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left me while he was comforted and content, then returned to me while he was sad. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you left me while you were comforted and content, and returned while you were sad. He said: I entered the Kabah and wished I had not done so; I fear I have burdened my nation after me."
"25571","Waki narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Guard against the Fire even with half a date."
"25572","Waki narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Thumamah ibn Hazn narrated to me, he said: I asked Aishah about nabidh, and she said: This is the servant of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so ask her - an Abyssinian slave girl - and she said: I used to make nabidh for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a waterskin in the evening, tie its mouth, and when morning came he would drink from it."
"25573","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Habib, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A woman with non-menstrual bleeding prays even if blood drips onto the mat."
"25574","Waki narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Musab ibn Shaybah, from Talq ibn Habib, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ten are of the fitrah: trimming the mustache, leaving the beard, siwak, sniffing water, trimming nails, washing the finger joints, plucking the armpit, shaving the pubic hair, and lessening water, meaning istinja. Zakariyya said: Musab said: And I forgot the tenth, unless it is rinsing the mouth."
"25575","Waki narrated to us, Misar and Sufyan narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: I never met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at dawn except that he was sleeping with me."
"25576","Waki narrated to us, Umar ibn Suwayd al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: The wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would go out with him wearing dimad that they would bathe in and sweat in, and he would not forbid them from it, whether in ihram or not."
"25577","Waki narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt, from Irak, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: They have done it; face the qiblah with my seat."
"25578","Waki narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, he heard it from him, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed while wearing a striped cloak, part of which was upon her while she was menstruating."
"25579","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Miqdam, from his father, from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a rising cloud, his face reddened, and when it rained he would say: O Allah, a wholesome downpour."
"25580","Waki narrated to us, Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to us, from a woman of Quraysh called Umm Kulthum, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon you is the hated beneficial one, talbinah, meaning broth. She said: And when anyone of his household complained, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would keep the pot on the fire until he met one of its two ends, meaning he recovered or died."
"25581","Waki narrated to us, he said: Abu Aqil narrated to me, from Buhayyah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon you is the black seed, for in it is healing from every disease except death, meaning death; and the black seed is shuniz."
"25582","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan and Misar narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered her to seek ruqyah against the evil eye."
"25583","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard a man reciting a verse and said: May Allah have mercy on him, he reminded me of a verse I had been made to forget."
"25584","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Burd, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would sometimes perform witr before sleeping and sometimes perform witr after sleeping, and sometimes bathe before sleeping and sometimes sleep before bathing from janabah."
"25585","Waki narrated to us, from Sharik, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, he said: I said to her: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrate anything of poetry? She said: Yes, the poetry of Abdullah ibn Rawahah; he would narrate this verse: And he brings you news from one you did not provision."
"25586","Waki narrated to us, from Ali, meaning Ibn Mubarak, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray the two rakahs between the adhan and the iqamah."
"25587","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from his father, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Suckling is only from hunger."
"25588","Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shimr, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Aishah, that she rode a camel and cursed it, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Do not ride it."
"25589","Waki narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, scraped off spit in the mosque."
"25590","Waki narrated to us, from Ismail, from Musab ibn Ishaq ibn Talhah, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: It lightens upon me that I saw the whiteness of Aishah's palm in Paradise. Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Usamah, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The speech of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was distinct, understood by everyone; he did not deliver it hastily. Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq, from Aban ibn Salih, from Umm Hakim, from Aishah, she said: I prayed a prayer I used to pray in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; if my father were resurrected and forbade me from it, I would not leave it."
"25591","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, he said: It was mentioned to her that the dead is punished by the weeping of the living, so she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said it only concerning a disbelieving man: He is being punished while his family weep over him."
"25592","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Tawaf, running between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and stoning the pillars were only made for establishing the remembrance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"25593","Waki narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Sharik, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you."
"25594","And he said: Usamah, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Asma."
"25595","Waki narrated to us, from Sharik, from al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh, from al-Bahiyy, from Aishah, that Usamah stumbled at the threshold of the door and bled, he said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began sucking it and saying: If Usamah were a girl, I would adorn her and clothe her until I married her off."
"25596","Waki narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I asked Aishah about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she said: I never knew him to fast a month until he broke fast from it, nor break fast until he fasted from it, until he passed away."
"25597","Waki narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say in his supplication: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done and from the evil of what I have not done."
"25598","Waki narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Abu Udhrah, a man who had met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade public baths for men and women, then permitted them for men in waist-wrappers and did not permit them for women."
"25599","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Aishah, she said: She is only Suhaylah bint Sahl, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered her to bathe for every prayer, then when that was hard upon her, he ordered her to combine Dhuhr and Asr with one bath, and Maghrib and Isha with one bath, and to bathe for Fajr."
"25600","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother Amrah, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding that surplus well water be withheld. Yazid said: Meaning surplus water."
"25601","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Aishah, who said: While I was with her, a man who had been flogged for wine passed by her door, and she heard the noise of the people. She said: What is this? I said: A man was taken drunk from wine and flogged. She said: Glory be to Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The drinker does not drink, while he drinks, while he is a believer, meaning wine, nor does the adulterer commit adultery, while he commits it, while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal, while he steals, while he is a believer, nor does a plunderer plunder a valuable prize to which people raise their heads while he is a believer. So beware, beware."
"25602","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Dhakwan, from Aishah, who said: A Jewish woman came and begged for food at my door, and said: Feed me; may Allah protect you from the trial of the Dajjal and from the trial of the torment of the grave. She said: I kept detaining her until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this Jewish woman saying? He said: And what is she saying? I said: She says: May Allah protect you from the trial of the Dajjal and from the trial of the torment of the grave. Aishah said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and raised his hands extended, seeking refuge with Allah from the trial of the Dajjal and from the trial of the torment of the grave. Then he said: As for the trial of the Dajjal, there has been no prophet but he warned his community, and I shall warn you with a warning with which no prophet warned his community: he is one-eyed, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is not one-eyed; written between his eyes is Kafir, which every believer will read. As for the trial of the grave, concerning me you are tried and about me you are questioned. When the righteous man is seated in his grave, unafraid and not distracted, then it is said to him: In what were you? He says: In Islam. It is said: What is this man who was among you? He says: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he came to us with the clear proofs from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and we believed him. Then an opening is made for him toward the Fire, and he looks at it, parts of it crushing others, and it is said to him: Look at what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has protected you from. Then an opening is made for him toward Paradise, and he looks at its blossom and what is in it, and it is said to him: This is your seat therein. And it is said: Upon certainty you lived, upon it you died, and upon it you will be resurrected, if Allah wills. And when the evil man is seated in his grave, frightened and distracted, it is said to him: In what were you? He says: I do not know. It is said: What is this man who was among you? He says: I heard the people saying something, so I said as they said. Then an opening is made for him toward Paradise, and he looks at its blossom and what is in it, and it is said to him: Look at what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has turned away from you. Then an opening is made for him toward the Fire, and he looks at it, parts of it crushing others, and it is said to him: This is your seat therein; you lived upon doubt, upon it you died, and upon it you will be resurrected, if Allah wills. Then he is punished."
"25603","Muhammad ibn Amr said: Sa'id ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The dead person is attended by the angels. When the man is righteous, they say: Come out, O good soul that was in a good body, and come out praiseworthy, and receive glad tidings of rest and sweet scent and a Lord who is not angry. That keeps being said to it until it comes out. Then it is taken up to heaven, and permission to enter is sought for it. It is said: Who is this? It is said: So-and-so. It is said: Welcome to the good soul that was in the good body; enter praiseworthy and receive glad tidings, and it is said: of rest and sweet scent and a Lord who is not angry. That keeps being said to it until it is brought to the heaven in which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is. When the man is evil, they say: Come out, O wicked soul that was in a wicked body; come out of it blameworthy, and receive tidings of boiling water and foul discharge and other things of their kind in pairs. That keeps being said to it until it comes out. Then it is taken up to heaven and permission to enter is sought for it. It is said: Who is this? It is said: So-and-so. It is said: No welcome to the wicked soul that was in the wicked body; return blameworthy, for the gates of heaven will not be opened for you. Then it is sent down from heaven, then it goes to the grave. The righteous man is seated, and it is said to him, and he answers with the like of what is in the hadith of Aishah, exactly."
"25604","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, who said: Diqrah, the mother of Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhaynah, narrated to me, saying: We were circumambulating the House with the Mother of the Believers, and she saw on a woman a cloak with a cross figure in it. The Mother of the Believers said: Cast it off, cast it off, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he saw anything like this, tore it off."
"25605","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, that he heard Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrating that he heard Aishah narrating that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said that he was burned. He asked him what his case was, and he said: I had intercourse with my wife in Ramadan. Then a basket called al-araq containing dates was brought to him, and he said: Where is the burned one? The man stood up, and he said: Give this in charity."
"25606","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah narrating that Aishah used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed awake one night while she was beside him. She said: I said: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah? She said: He said: Would that a righteous man from among my companions would guard me tonight. She said: While I was in that state, I heard the sound of weapons. He said: Who is this? He said: I am Sa'd ibn Malik. He said: What brought you? He said: I came to guard you, O Messenger of Allah. She said: Then I heard the snoring of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his sleep."
"25607","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: A sheep was given as a gift to Hafsah while we were both fasting, and she broke my fast, for she was the daughter of her father. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to us, we mentioned that to him, and he said: Make up a day in its place."
"25608","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah and Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that Umm Habibah bint Jahsh suffered non-menstrual bleeding for seven years, and she was the wife of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. She asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is only a vein and it is not menstruation, so wash and pray. She said: So she used to wash for every prayer."
"25609","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, who said: Aishah used to say: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in three ways: some of us entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together, some of us entered ihram for Hajj alone, and some of us entered ihram for Umrah. Whoever had entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together did not become free of anything that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, had forbidden to him until he completed his Hajj. Whoever had entered ihram for Umrah, then circumambulated the House and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah and shortened his hair, became free of what had been forbidden to him until he began Hajj."
"25610","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from his father, from his grandfather Alqamah ibn Waqqas, who said: Aishah informed me, saying: I went out on the day of al-Khandaq following the tracks of the people. She said: I heard the thud of the earth behind me, meaning the sound of the earth. She said: I turned, and there was Sa'd ibn Muadh with his nephew al-Harith ibn Aws carrying his shield. She said: I sat down on the ground, and Sa'd passed by wearing an iron coat of mail from which his limbs protruded, and I feared for the limbs of Sa'd. She said: Sa'd was among the greatest and tallest of people. She said: He passed by chanting rajaz, saying: Would that a little battle could be met by a camel; how fine death is when the appointed time comes. She said: I stood up and rushed into a garden, and in it were a group of Muslims, among them Umar ibn al-Khattab, and among them a man wearing a sabghah of his, meaning a helmet. Umar said: What brought you? By my life, by Allah, you are bold, and what assures you that there will not be a calamity or a retreat? She said: He kept blaming me until I wished the earth would split open for me that moment and I would enter into it. She said: The man lifted the sabghah from his face, and it was Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, who said: O Umar, woe to you, you have said much since today; where is there any retreat or flight except to Allah, Mighty and Majestic? She said: A man from the polytheists of Quraysh called Ibn al-Ariqah shot Sa'd with an arrow of his, saying to him: Take it, and I am Ibn al-Ariqah. It struck his medial arm vein and severed it. Sa'd supplicated to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, saying: O Allah, do not cause me to die until You delight my eyes regarding Qurayzah. She said: They had been his allies and clients in the Jahiliyyah. She said: His wound healed, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent the wind against the polytheists, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sufficed the believers in fighting, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, was Strong, Mighty. Abu Sufyan and those with him joined Tihamah, Uyaynah ibn Badr and those with him joined Najd, and Banu Qurayzah returned and fortified themselves in their fortresses. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to Madinah, laid down arms, and ordered a tent of leather, which was pitched for Sa'd in the mosque. She said: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him, with the trace of dust on his front teeth, and said: Have you laid down arms? By Allah, the angels have not yet laid down arms. Go out to Banu Qurayzah and fight them. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put on his armor and announced to the people the departure, that they should go out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and passed by Banu Ghanm, who were neighbors of the mosque around it, and said: Who passed by you? They said: Dihyah al-Kalbi passed by us; and Dihyah al-Kalbi, his beard, teeth and face resembled Jibril (peace be upon him). She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them and besieged them for twenty-five nights. When the siege and hardship intensified, it was said to them: Come down to the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They consulted Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir, who signaled to them that it meant slaughter. They said: We will come down to the judgment of Sa'd ibn Muadh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come down to the judgment of Sa'd ibn Muadh. So they came down, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Sa'd ibn Muadh, who was brought on a donkey with a saddle of palm fiber upon it, having been carried on it, surrounded by his people, who said: O Abu Amr, your allies and clients and people of valor and those you know. She said: But he did not return anything to them nor turn to them, until when he drew near their homes he turned to his people and said: It is time for me not to care, for the sake of Allah, about the blame of any blamer. Abu Sa'id said: When he appeared before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Stand for your chief, and bring him down. Umar said: Our Chief is Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: Bring him down, so they brought him down. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Judge concerning them. Sa'd said: I judge concerning them that their fighters be killed, their offspring taken captive, and their wealth divided; and Yazid at Baghdad said: and distributed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have judged concerning them with the judgment of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and the judgment of His Messenger. She said: Then Sa'd supplicated, saying: O Allah, if You have left anything of the war of Quraysh for Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then keep me alive for it, and if You have ended the war between him and them, then take me to You. She said: His wound burst open, though it had healed until nothing could be seen of it except like the eye of a needle, and he returned to his tent which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had pitched for him. Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar attended him. She said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I could distinguish the weeping of Umar from the weeping of Abu Bakr while I was in my chamber; and they were as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Merciful among themselves. Alqamah said: I said: O my mother, how did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) act? She said: His eye did not shed tears for anyone, but when he felt grief, he would take hold of his beard."
"25611","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Maymun informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to us, he said: Aishah informed me that she used to wash semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would go out and pray while I looked at the spots on his garment from the effect of washing."
"25612","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Aishah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Quran, it is deficient."
"25613","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: Jibril made an appointment with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at an hour to come to him at it, but he was late in coming to him at it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and found him standing at the door. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I awaited you for your appointment. He said: In the house there is a dog, and we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a picture. Under the bed of Aishah there was a puppy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it and it was taken out. Then in the morning he ordered concerning dogs and they were killed."
"25614","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, who said: I asked Aishah how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted. She said: He used to fast until we said he would not break his fast, and break his fast until we said he would not fast. I never saw him in any month fasting more than in Sha'ban; he used to fast all of Sha'ban except a little; indeed he used to fast all of Sha'ban."
"25615","Yazid narrated to us, he said: al-Asbagh informed us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, who said: Rabi'ah al-Jurashi narrated to me, saying: I asked Aishah: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say when he stood at night, and with what did he begin? She said: He used to say Allahu Akbar ten times, and glorify Allah ten times, and say La ilaha illa Allah ten times, and seek forgiveness ten times, and say: O Allah, forgive me, guide me and provide for me, ten times, and say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from distress on the Day of Reckoning, ten times."
"25616","Yazid narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Amrah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you have stoned and shaved, then perfume, clothes and everything have become lawful for you except women."
"25617","Yazid narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to touch one of us while she was menstruating, he ordered her to wrap her waist, and when he wanted to sleep while in a state of major impurity, he performed ablution as for prayer."
"25618","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray, between finishing the Isha prayer and Fajr, eleven rak'ahs, giving salam in every two and praying witr with one. In his prostration he would prostrate for as long as one of you would recite fifty verses before raising his head. When the muezzin fell silent after the first call, he stood and prayed two light rak'ahs, then lay down on his right side until the muezzin came to him and he went out with him."
"25619","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Budayl, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eating food with six of his companions when a Bedouin came and ate it in two mouthfuls. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he mentioned the name of Allah it would have sufficed you. When one of you eats food, let him mention the name of Allah; if he forgets to mention the name of Allah at its beginning, let him say: In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end."
"25620","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: Her foster brother asked her about the washing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from major impurity, so she called for water of about a sa', washed herself, and poured over her head three times."
"25621","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Salamah, who said: I asked Aishah about the washing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from major impurity, and she said: He used to wash his hands three times, then wash his private parts, then wash his hands, then rinse his mouth and nose, then pour over his head, then pour over the rest of his body."
"25622","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Mu'adhah, that a woman said to Aishah: Should one of us make up her prayer when she was menstruating? She said: Are you a Haruriyyah? We used to menstruate in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not order us to make up the prayer."
"25623","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a spiny-tailed lizard and did not eat it. I said: Shall we not feed it to the poor? He said: Do not feed them what you do not eat."
"25624","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammad informed us, and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub - Affan said: and Ayyub narrated to us - from Abu Qilabah, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to divide among his wives and be just. Affan said: And he would say: This is my division. Then he would say: O Allah, this is my doing in what I own, so do not blame me for what You own and I do not own."
"25625","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sa'd, informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: I said: Have you considered the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj or Umrah, there is no blame upon him to circumambulate them? He said: I said: By Allah, there is no blame upon anyone not to circumambulate them. Aishah said: Evil is what you said, O son of my sister. If it were as you interpreted it, it would be: there is no blame upon him not to circumambulate them. But it was only revealed because the Ansar, before they became Muslim, used to enter ihram for Manat, the false goddess whom they worshipped at al-Mushallal, and whoever had entered ihram for her felt scrupulous about circumambulating al-Safa and al-Marwah. They asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that and said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to feel scrupulous about circumambulating al-Safa and al-Marwah in the Jahiliyyah. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, up to His saying: there is no blame upon him to circumambulate them. Aishah said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established the going between them as sunnah, so it is not proper for anyone to abandon going between them."
"25626","Yazid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me on the day in which his illness began, and I said: O my head. He said: I wish that had happened while I was alive, so I would prepare you and bury you. She said: I said, thinking otherwise, as if I see you on that day as a bridegroom with one of your wives. He said: And O my head. Call your father and your brother to me so that I may write a document for Abu Bakr, for I fear that someone will say or someone will wish: I am more entitled; but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and the believers refuse anyone except Abu Bakr."
"25627","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the afflicted until he recovers, and from the child until he understands."
"25628","Yazid narrated to us, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah informed us, from Ismail, from Abu Khalaf, that he entered with Ubayd ibn Umayr to Aishah, and Ubayd ibn Umayr asked her how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to read this verse: Those who bring what they bring, or: who give what they give? She said: Which of them is dearer to you? He said: By Allah, one of them is dearer to me than such-and-such. She said: Which of them? He said: Those who bring what they bring. She said: I testify that thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite it, and thus it was revealed, but the spelling was altered."
"25629","Affan narrated to us, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, Ismail al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Khalaf, the freedman of Banu Jumah, narrated to me, that he entered with Ubayd ibn Umayr to the Mother of the Believers Aishah, and he mentioned the same meaning."
"25630","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Aishah, who said: A black cloak of wool was made for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the whiteness of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and its blackness. When he sweated, he smelled the wool from it and threw it off. He said: And I think she said: He used to like a pleasant scent."
"25631","Yazid narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Kaysan, Yahya ibn Ishaq and Affan informed us - the meaning is one and this is the wording of the hadith of Yazid; they did not differ in chain or meaning - they said: Ja'far ibn Kaysan al-Adawi informed us, he said: Mu'adhah bint Abd Allah al-Adawiyyah narrated to us, saying: I entered upon Aishah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My community will perish only by stabbing and plague. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this stabbing we know, but what is the plague? He said: A swelling like the swelling of a camel. The one who stays through it is like a martyr, and the one who flees from it is like one fleeing from battle."
"25632","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ibn Sakhbarah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The greatest of women in blessing are those easiest in provision."
"25633","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, make me among those who, when they do good, rejoice, and when they do evil, seek forgiveness."
"25634","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, who said: Shaybah al-Khudari narrated to me, saying: We were with Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things I swear to: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share. The shares of Islam are three: prayer, fasting and zakah. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not befriend a servant in this world and then entrust him to another on the Day of Resurrection. No man loves a people but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will place him with them. And a fourth: if I swore to it, I would hope not to sin: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not cover a servant in this world but He will cover him on the Day of Resurrection. Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: When you hear the like of this hadith from the like of Urwah narrating it from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), memorize it."
"25635","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, and Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Sumayyah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was angry with Safiyyah bint Huyayy. She said to me: Is there a way for you to make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pleased with me, and I will give you my day? I said: Yes. She took a veil of hers dyed with saffron, sprinkled it with water - Affan said: so its scent would spread - then veiled herself with it. Then she entered upon him on my day and sat beside him. He said: Away from me, O Aishah, for this is not your day. I said: The bounty of Allah, He gives it to whom He wills. Then I told him my story. Affan said: So he became pleased with her."
"25636","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Mu'adhah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Duha four rak'ahs and add whatever he wished."
"25637","Yazid narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Burd informed us, he said: Umm Salim al-Rasibiyyah narrated to us, from Aishah, who said: When milk was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: How much blessing is in the house, one or two?"
"25638","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity."
"25639","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, who said: I asked Aishah about prayer after Asr, and she said: Pray. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade your people, the people of Yemen, from praying when the sun rises."
"25640","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mu'adhah, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days of every month. She said: I said: Which part of it did he fast? She said: He did not care which part of it he fasted."
"25641","Muhammad ibn Ja'far Gundar narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Makhrami narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Ibrahim informed me, that a man bequeathed a third of each of his dwellings to a person. I asked al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, and he said: Combine three in one place, for I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does a deed that is not in accordance with our command, his matter is rejected."
"25642","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us: Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"25643","And Muhammad ibn Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed people."
"25644","And al-Khaffaf said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"25645","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I lay reclining to his right and to his left."
"25646","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his hands on the forelock of a horse while talking to a man. I said: I saw you placing your hands on the forelock of the horse of Dihyah al-Kalbi while talking to him. He said: And did you see me? She said: Yes. He said: That was Jibril (peace be upon him), and he sends you greetings of peace. She said: Upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; may Allah reward him well as a companion and guest; what an excellent companion and excellent guest. Sufyan said: Al-dakhil means the guest."
"25647","Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Kathir ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Iyad, from Aishah, that she said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while part of my cloak was over him."
"25648","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk al-Dayli narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah al-Ashhali informed us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The siwak is a purifier for the mouth and pleasing to the Lord. And in the black seed there is healing from every disease except al-sam. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-sam? He said: Death."
"25649","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Aishah, who said: When news was slow in coming to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would illustrate it with the verse of Tarafah: News will be brought to you by one whom you did not provision."
"25650","Hushaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sleep while in a state of major impurity without touching water."
"25651","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabir, from Yazid ibn Murrah, from Lamis, that she said: I asked Aishah. She said: I said to her: A woman makes oil to endear herself to her husband? She said: Remove from yourself that which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not look upon. She said: And a woman said to Aishah: O my mother. Aishah said: I am not your mother, but I am your sister. Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to mix the twenty with prayer and sleep, but when the last ten came, he exerted himself, tightened his waist-wrapper, and exerted himself."
"25652","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabr ibn Habib, from Umm Kulthum, from Aishah, that Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting to speak to him while Aishah was praying. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Keep to the comprehensive ones, or another phrase. When Aishah finished, she asked him about that, and he said to her: Say: O Allah, I ask You for all good, its immediate and its delayed, what I know of it and what I do not know. I seek refuge with You from all evil, its immediate and its delayed, what I know of it and what I do not know. I ask You for Paradise and what brings near to it of word or deed. I seek refuge with You from the Fire and what brings near to it of word or deed. I ask You for the good that Your servant and Messenger Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked You for. I seek Your protection from what Your servant and Messenger Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought Your protection from. And I ask You to make the outcome of whatever matter You decree for me right guidance."
"25653","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Jabr ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr narrating from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Keep to the comprehensive, all-encompassing supplications. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"25654","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Jabr ibn Habib narrated to us, from Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr, from Aishah, and he mentioned the like of it."
"25655","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Aishah, that she said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and thought he had gone to one of his slave girls. I sought him, and there he was, prostrating, saying: My Lord, forgive me what I concealed and what I revealed."
"25656","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Umarah, meaning Ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two garments, Omani or Qatari. Aishah said to him: These two garments are coarse; you sweat in them and they become heavy on you, and so-and-so has received cloth, so send to him to sell you two garments on credit. He said: I know what Muhammad wants; he only wants to take my two garments, that is, not to give me my money. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Shu'bah said: I think he said: He has lied; they know that I am the most God-fearing of them toward Allah, Mighty and Majestic - or he said: the most truthful of them in speech and the most faithful in trust."
"25657","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd Rabb, meaning Ibn Sa'id, from Nafi', from Sa'ibah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of Dhu al-Tufyatayn and the abtar, and said: They efface the sight and cause miscarriage."
"25658","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, that he heard his father narrating from Masruq, who said: I asked Aishah which deed was dearest to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: The lasting one. Ibn Ja'far said: I said: At what time did he rise? She said: When he heard the caller."
"25659","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, from his father, from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved beginning with the right in all his affairs. Then al-Ash'ath said finally: He loved beginning with the right as much as he could in his combing, his shoes and his purification."
"25660","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, who said: I heard Safiyyah narrating from Aishah that Asma asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about washing after menstruation. He said: One of you takes her water and her lote and purifies herself and perfects the purification, then pours over her head and rubs it vigorously until it reaches the roots of her head, then pours water over herself, then takes a musk-scented cloth and purifies herself with it. Asma said: How should she purify herself with it? He said: Glory be to Allah, purify yourself with it. Aishah said, as if concealing that: Seek the trace of the blood with it. She asked him about washing from major impurity. He said: You take your water and purify yourself and perfect the purification - or: take purification to its fullest - then pour over her head and rub it until it reaches the roots of her head, then pour water over herself. Aishah said: Excellent women are the women of the Ansar; modesty did not prevent them from understanding the religion."
"25661","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing and prostration: Subbuh, Quddus, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"25662","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, narrating that he heard his father narrating that he heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not leave four rak'ahs before Zuhr and two rak'ahs before Fajr."
"25663","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, the freedman of Umar ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: I used to sleep in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my feet in his qiblah. When he prostrated, he nudged me and I drew in my feet, and when he stood, I extended them. And houses in those days had no lamps."
"25664","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in his house while ill, praying seated, and people behind him prayed standing. He signaled to them to sit. When he finished, he said: The imam is only made to be followed. When he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; and when he prays seated, pray seated."
"25665","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Shayban, from Abu Nawfal, who said: I asked Aishah whether poetry was recited in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: It was the most hateful speech to him."
"25666","And he said, from Aishah: He used to like the comprehensive supplications and leave what is besides that."
"25667","He said: And Aishah said: When the righteous are mentioned, then hail Umar."
"25668","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from his mother, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place his head in her lap and recite the Quran while she was menstruating."
"25669","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his brother, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, that Jibril (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a mule, wearing a turban with its end between his shoulders. I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did you see him? That was Jibril (peace be upon him)."
"25670","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Fulayt: Jasrah narrated to me, from Aishah, that she said: I never saw a maker of food like Safiyyah. She gave as a gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a vessel containing food, and I could not restrain myself from breaking it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is its expiation? He said: A vessel like the vessel and food like the food."
"25671","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spit, mucus or phlegm on the qiblah wall and scraped it off."
"25672","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from his mother, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah permitted benefiting from the skins of dead animals when they are tanned."
"25673","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Niyar, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Badr, and a man from the polytheists followed him and caught up with him at al-Jamrah. He said: I wanted to follow you and gain booty with you. He said: Do you believe in Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger? He said: No. He said: Go back, for we will not seek the help of a polytheist. He said: Then he caught up with him at al-Shajarah, and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoiced at that, for he had strength and endurance. He said: I came to follow you and gain booty with you. He said: Do you believe in Allah and His Messenger? He said: No. He said: Go back, for I will not seek the help of a polytheist. He said: Then he caught up with him when he appeared on al-Bayda, and he said the like of that to him. He said: Do you believe in Allah and His Messenger? He said: Yes. He said: So he went out with him."
"25674","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays, who said: I asked Aishah how many rak'ahs the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr with. She said: With four and three, six and three, eight and three, and ten and three. He never prayed witr with more than thirteen nor less than seven, and he never left two rak'ahs."
"25675","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays, who said: I asked Aishah how the sleep of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a state of major impurity: did he wash before sleeping? She said: He did all of that. Sometimes he washed and slept, and sometimes he performed ablution and slept. He said: I said to her: How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night: did he recite aloud or softly? She said: He did all of that. Sometimes he recited aloud and sometimes softly."
"25676","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays, who said: I heard Aishah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to watch for the crescent of Sha'ban as he did not watch for any other, then fast upon sighting Ramadan. If it was obscured from him, he counted thirty days, then fasted."
"25677","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Rabi'ah, meaning Ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays, that al-Nu'man ibn Bashir narrated to him, saying: Mu'awiyah wrote with me to Aishah. He said: I came to Aishah and delivered to her the letter of Mu'awiyah. She said: O my son, shall I not narrate to you something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes indeed. She said: I and Hafsah were one day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If only we had a man to converse with us. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not send for Abu Bakr for you? He fell silent. Then he said: If only we had a man to converse with us. Hafsah said: Shall I not send for Umar for you? He fell silent. Then he said: No. Then he called a man and confided something to him, and it was only a little before Uthman came. He turned to him with his face and his speech, and I heard him say to him: O Uthman, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, may clothe you with a shirt, and if they want you to take it off, do not take it off - three times. He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, where were you regarding this hadith? She said: O my son, by Allah, I had forgotten it until I did not think I had heard it."
"25678","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Dhakwan, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a khumrah."
"25679","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing: Subbuh, Quddus, Lord of the angels and the Spirit. He said: And Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah said: in his bowing and his prostration."
"25680","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The two rak'ahs of Fajr are better than the whole world. He said: Qatadah used to hear this hadith and say: They are dearer to me than red camels."
"25681","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the bells to be cut from the necks of camels on the day of Badr."
"25682","Abu Kamil and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah - Affan said: Qatadah informed us - from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Safiyyah bint al-Harith, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of an adult woman is not accepted except with a veil."
"25683","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Abu Hassan, that a man said to Aishah: Abu Hurayrah narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ill omen is in the woman, the house and the animal. She became violently angry, so that one part of her flew to the sky and a part to the earth, and said: The people of the Jahiliyyah used to take omens from that."
"25684","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Aishah, who said: The household of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a wild animal which, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, became excited, played, came forward and went back. When it sensed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had entered, it crouched and did not move, fearing to harm him."
"25685","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Utbah, from Aishah, that charity meat was given to Barirah, and it was taken to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was said that it was from charity meat. He said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"25686","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr - Affan said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr informed us - from Musa ibn Talhah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Khadijah, and I said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has replaced you with a woman - Affan said: with an old woman from the old women of Quraysh, from the women of Quraysh, red of gums - who perished long ago. She said: His face changed with a change the like of which I saw only at the descent of revelation or at a rain cloud, until it is seen whether it is mercy or punishment."
"25687","Abd al-Razzaq and Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, al-Mughirah ibn Hakim informed me, from Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr, that she informed him, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the night prayer one night until most of the night had gone and the people of the mosque had slept - and Ibn Bakr said: dozed - then he came out and prayed, and said: Indeed it is its time, were it not that it would be hard upon my community; and Ibn Bakr said: that I would burden."
"25688","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: This is Jibril (peace be upon him), and he greets you with peace. She said: Upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; you see what we do not see."
"25689","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered and sent Fatimah to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said to her: Tell him that your wives adjure you to be just regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah. She said: She entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was with Aishah in her cloak, and said to him: Your wives sent me to you, and they adjure you to be just regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do you love me? She said: Yes. He said: Then love her. She returned to them and told them what he had said to her. They said: You have done nothing; go back to him. She said: By Allah, I will never go back to him about her. Al-Zuhri said: And she was truly the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they sent Zaynab bint Jahsh. Aishah said: She was the one who rivaled me among the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Your wives sent me to you, and they adjure you to be just regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah. She said: Then she turned upon me reviling me, and I kept watching the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and looking at the edge of his eye, whether he permitted me to defend myself against her. He did not speak. She said: She reviled me until I thought he would not dislike my defending myself against her. So I faced her, and it was not long before I silenced her. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: She is the daughter of Abu Bakr. Aishah said: I never saw a woman better than her, more charitable, more joining of kinship, more giving of herself in everything by which nearness to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is sought, than Zaynab, apart from a sharpness of temper in which she was quick to return from."
"25690","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri or another, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: Fatimah bint Utbah ibn Rabi'ah came to pledge allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he took upon her: that they associate nothing with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery - the verse. She said: She placed her hand upon her head out of shyness, and what he saw of her pleased the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Aishah said: Affirm, O woman, for by Allah he only pledged allegiance to us upon this. She said: Then yes indeed. So he pledged allegiance to her upon the verse."
"25691","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usamah, from Musa ibn Sarjis, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was dying, with a cup containing water beside him. He put his hand into the cup and wiped his face with the water, saying: O Allah, help me against the agonies of death."
"25692","Abu Amir narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr say: Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl narrated to me that Aishah informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Aishah, beware of the insignificant sins, for they have a seeker from Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"25693","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me, from Aishah, who said: I missed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night and thought he had gone to one of his wives. Abd al-Razzaq said: I felt around, then I returned, and there he was, bowing or prostrating, saying: Glory be to You and with Your praise; there is no god but You. I said: By my father and mother, you are in one state and I am in another."
"25694","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah or Amrah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the illness in which he died: Pour over me water from seven skins whose bindings have not been loosened, that I may rest and enjoin the people. Aishah said: We seated him in a brass tub of Hafsah and poured that water over him until he began gesturing to us that you have done. Then he went out."
"25695","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: What do you seek by that? He said: As for: Glory be to You and with Your praise; there is no god but You - Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me, from Aishah, that she missed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night and thought."
"25696","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, that Aishah said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, all your wives have a kunyah except me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Take the kunyah Umm Abd Allah. So she was called Umm Abd Allah until she died, though she never gave birth at all."
"25697","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I slept and saw myself in Paradise, and I heard the voice of a reciter reciting. I said: Who is this? They said: This is Harithah ibn al-Nu'man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Such is righteousness, such is righteousness; and he was the most dutiful of people to his mother."
"25698","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah or another, that Aishah said: No character was more hateful to the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than lying. A man would tell a lie in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it would remain in his heart against him until he knew that he had repented from it."
"25699","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night, and when he finished, he said to me: Rise and pray witr."
"25700","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, who said: An effeminate man used to enter upon the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they counted him among those without desire. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered one day while he was with one of his wives, describing a woman, saying: When she approaches, she approaches with four, and when she turns away, she turns away with eight. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see that this one knows what is here; let him not enter upon you. So they veiled him."
"25701","Rawh narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his brother, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a mule wearing a turban with its end between his shoulders, so I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about him, and he said: Did you see him, that was Jibril, peace be upon him."
"25702","Abu Amir narrated to us, from Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, from Sharik ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: In the Ajwah dates of al-Aliyah there is healing, or an antidote, first thing in the morning on an empty stomach."
"25703","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abdul-Karim informed me, that Mujahid informed him, that a mawla of Aishah who used to lead her informed him, that she, when she heard the sound of the bell ahead of her, would say: Stop with me, so he would stop until she no longer heard it, and when she heard it behind her, she said: Hurry with me until I no longer hear it, and she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It has a follower from among the jinn."
"25704","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umm Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two snakes are sent against the disbeliever, one from the side of his head and another from the side of his feet, biting him with a bite, whenever they finish they return, until the Day of Resurrection."
"25705","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar, from Musab ibn Shaybah, from Talq ibn Habib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Ghusl is taken on account of four: Friday, janabah, cupping, and washing the dead."
"25706","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Ata, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman is married for three things: for her wealth, her beauty, and her religion, so hold to the one with religion, may your hands be dusty."
"25707","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to us, from Umm Kulthum, from Aishah, she said: When it was said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that so-and-so is in pain and does not eat food, he said: Upon you is talbinah, so give it to him to sip, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it washes the stomach of one of you as one of you washes his face with water from dirt."
"25708","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: When the verse of the choice was revealed, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me and said: O Aishah, I want to mention a matter to you, so do not decide anything in it without your parents. She said: What is it. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me and recited to me this verse: O Prophet, say to your wives, if you desire Allah and His Messenger and the Hereafter, the whole verse. She said: So I said: I have chosen Allah and His Messenger. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rejoiced at that."
"25709","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The angels were created from light, and the jinn were created from a smokeless flame of fire, and Adam, peace be upon him, was created from what was described to you."
"25710","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, Salim Abu al-Nadr, mawla of Umar ibn Ubaydullah, narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast until we would say he will not break his fast, and he would break his fast until we would say he will not fast, and I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, complete the fasting of a month at all except Ramadan, and I never saw him in any month fasting more than in Shaban."
"25711","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Ibn Thawban, from his mother, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded that benefit be taken from the skins of dead animals when they are tanned."
"25712","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Jabir, from Arfajah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me one day and said: Today I have done something I wish I had not done, I entered the House, and I fear that a man may come from a distant horizon and be unable to enter it, and go back with something in himself about it."
"25713","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to take the pledge from women by words, with this verse: that they will not associate anything with Allah. She said: And his hand never touched the hand of a woman at all, except a woman he owned."
"25714","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, and Abd al-Ala, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was shrouded in a Hibarah garment."
"25715","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from his father, from Khalid ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi, from al-Bahi, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to remember Allah, Mighty and Majestic, at all his times."
"25716","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Qays ibn Wahb, from a man of Banu Suwaah, from Aishah, concerning what flows between a man and his wife of water, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pour water upon water."
"25717","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar and Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The first of what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was begun with of revelation was the true dream, or she said: the righteous dream, Ibn al-Mubarak doubted. She said: And he would not see a dream except that it came like the break of dawn."
"25718","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Aishah, he said: I said: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raise his voice in recitation. She said: Sometimes he raised it and sometimes he lowered it."
"25719","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never touched the hand of a woman in a pledge at all."
"25720","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to take ghusl and pray two rakahs and the morning prayer, I do not see him renewing wudu after ghusl."
"25721","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to touch his wife while fasting."
"25722","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Ata, he said: I heard that the black dog and the menstruating woman cut off the prayer. Ata said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that Aishah informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed while she was lying across in front of him, and he said: Are they not your mothers and your sisters and your paternal aunts."
"25723","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to sleep, he would join his hands and blow into them, then recite: Say, He is Allah, One, and: Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and: Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, then wipe with them his face and his head and the rest of his body. Uqayl said: And I saw Ibn Shihab doing that."
"25724","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated to me, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Isha, then prayed eight rakahs standing and two rakahs sitting between the two calls to prayer, he would not leave them."
"25725","Muammal Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned Khadijah one day and spoke at length in praise of her, so there seized me what seizes women of jealousy, so I said: Allah has replaced for you, O Messenger of Allah, an old woman from the old women of Quraysh with red gums. She said: So the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed with a change I never saw him change with at anything at all, except at the descent of revelation or at a rain cloud, until it is known whether it is mercy or punishment."
"25726","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever of my ummah bears a debt, then strives to pay it, then dies before paying it, I am his guardian."
"25727","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi al-Furat, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that she informed him that she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the plague, so the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed her that it was a punishment Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends upon whom He wills, then Allah made it a mercy for the believers, so there is no servant in whose land the plague falls who remains in his land, patient and seeking reward, knowing that nothing will befall him except what Allah has written for him, except that he will have the like of the reward of a martyr."
"25728","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, he said: I heard al-Qasim reporting from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There is no good in the congregation of women except in a mosque or at the funeral of one slain."
"25729","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik informed us, and Husayn, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash Sulayman, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the skins of dead animals, and he said: Its tanning is its purification."
"25730","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Aishah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said of the gecko: A little wicked one, and I did not hear him command killing it."
"25731","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As, that Said ibn al-As informed him that Aishah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Uthman narrated to him that Abu Bakr sought permission upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was lying on his bed wearing the cloak of Aishah, so he gave permission to Abu Bakr while in that state, and he fulfilled his need to him, then left, then Umar sought permission, so he gave him permission while in that state, and he fulfilled his need to him, then left, then Uthman came, then he sought permission upon him, so he sat up and said to Aishah: Gather your clothes upon you, then he fulfilled his need to him, then he left, so Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, why did I not see you show concern for Abu Bakr and Umar as you showed concern for Uthman. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Uthman is a shy man, and I feared that if I gave him permission in that state he would not convey his need to me. Layth said: And a group of people said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Aishah: Shall I not feel shy from one whom the angels feel shy from."
"25732","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As, from his father, from Aishah, that Abu Bakr sought permission upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was wearing a cloak, then he mentioned its meaning."
"25733","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yaqub al-Ansari narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Yazid al-Ansari, from his wife, that she asked Aishah about the meat of sacrifices, so Aishah said: Ali came to us from a journey, so we offered him some of it, and he said: I will not eat it until I ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about it. She said: So Ali asked him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat it from Dhul-Hijjah to Dhul-Hijjah."
"25734","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to me, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that she, when one of her family died and the women gathered then dispersed except her family and her close ones, would order a pot of talbinah, so it was cooked, then tharid was made and the talbinah was poured over it, then she said: Eat from it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Talbinah soothes the heart of the sick and removes some grief."
"25735","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, he said: Aishah narrated to me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he came out of the place of relieving himself, would say: Your forgiveness."
"25736","Hashim and Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, they said: Israil narrated to us, from Asim, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Aishah, that she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, You have made my creation good, so make my character good."
"25737","Hashim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray while I was beside him."
"25738","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yafur, from al-Hasan, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prayed Isha, would enter the house, then pray two rakahs, then pray after them two rakahs longer than them, then pray witr with three without separating among them, then pray two rakahs while sitting, bowing while sitting and prostrating while sitting."
"25739","Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The family of Muhammad never ate their fill three times of wheat bread until he passed away, and never was a crumb lifted from his table at all until he passed away."
"25740","Qurad Abu Nuh narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I asked Aishah, Mother of the Believers, with what did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, open his prayer when he stood at night. She said: When he stood he would say takbir and say: O Allah, Lord of Jibril and Mikail and Israfil, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, You judge between Your servants in what they used to differ, guide me in what I differed in of the truth by Your permission, indeed You guide whom You will to a straight path."
"25741","Yahya said: Abu Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he stood at night, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his poetry, and his pride. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say: Seek refuge with Allah from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his pride, and his poetry. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are his madness, his pride, and his poetry. He said: As for his madness, it is this epilepsy that seizes the sons of Adam, and as for his pride, it is arrogance, and as for his poetry, it is poetry."
"25742","Abu Nuh narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar, from Abu Yunus, from Aishah, she said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was standing at the door and I was listening, he said: I wake up in janabah and I want to fast. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I wake up in janabah and I want to fast. The man said: I am not like you, Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what remained. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became angry and said: I hope to be the most fearful of you of the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and the most knowledgeable of you of what I avoid."
"25743","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Niyar al-Aslami, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a pouch of beads, so he divided it for the free woman and the slave woman, and she said: My father used to divide for the free man and the slave."
"25744","Hashim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to kiss while fasting, but he was the most in control of you of his desire."
"25745","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, he said: I said to Aishah: Did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite anything of poetry as an example. She said: He used to recite as an example from the poetry of Abdullah ibn Rawahah, saying: And news will be brought to you by one whom you did not provide."
"25746","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak, meaning Ibn Fadalah, narrated to us, my mother informed me, from Muadhah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in my house of Duha four rakahs."
"25747","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from al-Suddi, from Abdullah al-Bahi, from Aishah, she said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which people are best. He said: The generation in which I am, then the second, then the third."
"25748","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, he said: Aishah said: It is not fitting for anyone to hate Usamah after I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever loves Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger, let him love Usamah."
"25749","Hashim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from one vessel, while we were both in janabah, but water does not become junub."
"25750","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the sins of the servant increase and he has no deeds to expiate them, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, afflicts him with grief to expiate them from him."
"25751","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Abdullah ibn Shaqiq narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never fasted a complete month since he came to Madinah except Ramadan."
"25752","Abu Asim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed me, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, he said: We were leaning against the chamber and I was hearing the sound of the siwak, or her siwak, while she was brushing her teeth. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform umrah in Rajab. He said: Yes. I said: O Mother of the Believers, do you not hear what Abu Abd al-Rahman says. She said: What does Abu Abd al-Rahman say. He said: He says the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed umrah in Rajab. She said: May Allah forgive Abu Abd al-Rahman, by Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never performed an umrah, or an umrah, except that Abu Abd al-Rahman was with him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never performed umrah in Rajab."
"25753","Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade celibacy."
"25754","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, he said: Aishah said to me: Does Abu Hurayrah not amaze you, he came and sat beside my chamber narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, making me hear that, while I was glorifying Allah, then he stood before I finished my glorification, had he sat until I finished my glorification I would have answered him, indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not narrate speech in succession as you narrate."
"25755","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Kill all snakes, except the small white curtailed snake among them and the one with two stripes on its back, for they kill the child in the belly of his mother and dim the eyes, whoever leaves them is not from us."
"25756","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"25757","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The jet-black dog is a devil."
"25758","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Aqil, meaning al-Thaqafi, narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Said narrated to us, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told his wives a story one night, so a woman among them said: O Messenger of Allah, the story was the story of Khurafah. So he said: Do you know what Khurafah is, Khurafah was a man of Udhrah whom the jinn captured in the Jahiliyyah, so he remained among them a long time, then they returned him to mankind, and he used to tell people of the wonders he saw among them, so people said: The story of Khurafah. My father said: Abu Aqil, this is trustworthy, his name is Abdullah ibn Aqil al-Thaqafi."
"25759","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Dawad, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from his mother, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away when people had eaten their fill of the two black ones, dates and water."
"25760","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from his mother, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recline in my lap while I was menstruating, reciting the Quran."
"25761","Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Dawad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Mansur ibn Safiyyah narrated to us, from his mother, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"25762","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Hafsah, mawla of Aishah, that Aishah informed him, when the sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he performed wudu and commanded, so it was called that prayer is gathering, so he stood and lengthened the standing in his prayer, he said: So I think he recited Surat al-Baqarah, then he bowed and lengthened the bowing, then he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, then he stood the like of what he stood and did not prostrate, then he bowed, then prostrated, then he stood and did the like of what he did, then he bowed twice with one prostration, then he sat, and the sun was unveiled."
"25763","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her and said: Were it not that Quraysh would exult, I would have informed them of what they have with Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"25764","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman informed us, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hafsah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to slaughter for a girl one sheep and for a boy two sheep, and commanded us with the fara, from every five sheep one sheep."
"25765","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she used to reproach the women who offered themselves to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: Does a woman not feel shy to offer herself without a dowry, so there was revealed, or he said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: You may defer whom you will of them and take to you whom you will, and whoever you seek of those you set aside, there is no blame upon you. She said: I see your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, hastening for you in your desire."
"25766","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that al-Harith ibn Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: How does revelation come to you. He said: Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and it is the hardest upon me, then it leaves me and I have understood, and sometimes an angel comes to me in the likeness of a man, so I understand what he says."
"25767","Amir ibn Salih al-Zubayri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, from al-Harith ibn Hisham, that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned the like of it."
"25768","Abu Amir and Surayj, meaning Ibn al-Numan, narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar, from Abu Yunus, mawla of Aishah, from Aishah, she said: A man sought permission upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Evil is the son of the tribe. When he entered, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cheerful to him and open with him, then he left, then another man sought permission, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Good is the son of the tribe. When he entered, he was not open with him as he was open with the other, nor was he cheerful with him as he was cheerful, then when he left I said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so sought permission and you said to him what you said, then you were cheerful to him and open with him, and you said to so-and-so what you said and I did not see you do with him what you did with the other. So he said: O Aishah, among the worst of people is he who is feared for his obscenity."
"25769","Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Hani, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Uthman, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered, and I recognized in his face that something had spurred him, so he performed wudu, then went out and did not speak to anyone, so I drew near to the chambers and heard him saying: O people, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Command the good and forbid the evil before you call upon Me and I do not answer you, and you ask Me and I do not give you, and you seek My help and I do not help you."
"25770","Bakr ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: I heard Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj narrating from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Aishah, that Abu Bakr led people in prayer while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the row."
"25771","Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed behind Abu Bakr sitting in his illness in which he died."
"25772","Shababah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in his illness in which he died: Command Abu Bakr to lead people in prayer. Aishah said: Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, when he stands in your place weeping will seize him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are the companions of Yusuf, command Abu Bakr to lead people in prayer. So Abu Bakr prayed, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed behind him sitting."
"25773","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihzam narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, al-Qasim narrated to us, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Whoever is given his share of gentleness has been given his share of the good of this world and the Hereafter, and joining kinship and good character and good neighborliness populate homes and increase lifespans."
"25774","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The excellence of Aishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over food."
"25775","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Niyar al-Aslami, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a pouch in which were beads, so he divided for the free woman and the slave woman. Aishah said: And my father used to divide for the free man and the slave. My father said: Yazid ibn Harun said: So he divided between the free woman and the slave woman equally."
"25776","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Two prayers the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never left, secretly nor openly: two rakahs after Asr and two rakahs before Fajr."
"25777","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Said ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Aishah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, concerning this verse: Those who give what they give while their hearts are fearful that they will return to their Lord, O Messenger of Allah, is he the one who steals and commits adultery and drinks wine while fearing Allah. He said: No, O daughter of Abu Bakr, O daughter of al-Siddiq, but he is the one who prays and fasts and gives charity while fearing Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"25778","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Sallam, informed us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Qilabah informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah informed him that Aishah informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was struck by pain, so he began to complain and turn on his bed, so Aishah said: Had one of us done this you would have found fault with him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The righteous are burdened heavily, and no believer is struck by a mishap, from a thorn and what is above that, except that a sin is removed from him by it and a rank is raised by it."
"25779","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to raise his hands supplicating until I heard: O Allah, I am but a human, so do not punish me for insulting a man among the Muslims if I harm him."
"25780","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away in my house and on my night."
"25781","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, that she asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about something of the matter of charity, and she mentioned something small, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Give and do not withhold in a vessel, lest it be withheld from you."
"25782","Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abu al-Rijal, from his mother Amrah, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fruit is not to be sold until it is safe from blight. My father said: Kharijah is weak in hadith."
"25783","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ali narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me that Umm Bakr informed him, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said concerning a woman who sees what makes her doubt after purity, he said: It is only veins, or he said: a vein."
"25784","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Usamah, from Uthman ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His angels send blessings upon those who join the rows."
"25785","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: I heard Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, he said: Shaybah al-Khudri narrated to me that he witnessed Urwah narrating to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not make a man who has a share in Islam like one who has no share, he said: And the shares of Islam are fasting, prayer, and charity, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not take charge of a man in this world then entrust him on the Day of Resurrection to another, and no man loves a people except that he will come with them on the Day of Resurrection, he said: And the fourth: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not cover a sin for a servant in this world except that He covers it for him in the Hereafter, he said: So Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: When you hear the like of this hadith from the like of Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, memorize it."
"25786","Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Aishah: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, complained, Jibril, peace be upon him, would charm him, saying: In the name of Allah I charm you, from every disease He heals you, from the evil of an envier when he envies, and from the evil of every possessor of an eye."
"25787","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: Umm Muhammad narrated to me that Aishah narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not sleep at night nor by day then wake except that he brushed his teeth before wudu."
"25788","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash informed us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bought food from a Jew and pawned his armor to him."
"25789","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, from Aishah, she said: When I menstruated I would tighten my waist-wrapper over me, then enter with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his cover, but he was the most in control of you of his desire."
"25790","Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Makhlad ibn Khufaf, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed that produce is with liability. I heard from Qurran ibn Tammam in the year one hundred and eighty-one, and Ibn al-Mubarak was still alive, and in it Ibn al-Mubarak died."
"25791","Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Muadhah al-Adawiyyah, from Aishah, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from one vessel, and it was between us."
"25792","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Misar narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: I never found him at the last predawn except sleeping with me, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"25793","al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon a woman of the Ansar, and in the house was a hanging water-skin, so he bent its mouth and drank while standing."
"25794","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was wrapped in a Hibarah garment, then it was taken from him. al-Qasim said: Remnants of that garment are still with us."
"25795","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: When the circumcised passes the circumcised, ghusl has become obligatory, I did it, I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we bathed."
"25796","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Ikrimah and Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pass by the pot and take a bone, eat some of it, then pray, without performing wudu and without touching water."
"25797","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Ata ibn al-Saib, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in janabah, a vessel with water would be placed for him, so he would pour upon his hands and wash them before entering them into the water, then he would enter his right hand into the vessel and pour with it upon his left hand, washing his private part, then rinse his mouth and sniff water three times, and wash his face and his forearms, then scoop three scoops and pour them upon his head, then wash."
"25798","Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Rabiah, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Loyalty is for the one who frees."
"25799","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: I saw you in a dream twice, I see a man carrying you in a piece of silk, saying: This is your wife, so I uncover it and behold it is you, so I say: If this is from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He will carry it out."
"25800","Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray at night thirteen rakahs, and he would pray witr with five units, not sitting between them until sitting in the last, then giving salam."
"25801","Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Urwa, he said: I heard Urwa narrating from Aisha, she said: I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the best I could afford before he entered ihram, then he would enter ihram."
"25802","Hammad narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given a choice between two matters, one of them easier than the other, except that he chose the easier of the two, so long as it was not a sin; and if it was a sin, he was the furthest of people from it."
"25803","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, Uthman ibn Urwa narrated to me, from Urwa, from Aisha, the like of it. Sufyan said: Uthman ibn Urwa said to me: Hisham reports it from me."
"25804","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from a man of Quraysh of Banu Taym called Talha, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached for me, so I said: I am fasting. He said: And I am fasting."
"25805","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih al-Asadi, from al-Shabi, from Muhammad ibn al-Ashath ibn Qays, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not withhold himself from anything of my face while he was fasting."
"25806","Waki narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from al-Abbas ibn Dharih, from al-Shabi, from Muhammad ibn al-Ashath ibn Qays, from Aisha, the like of it."
"25807","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Aisha, that she used to wash semen from the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25808","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The day of Ashura was a day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast in the pre-Islamic period, and Quraysh used to fast it in the pre-Islamic period; then when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina he fasted it and ordered its fasting, then when Ramadan was revealed, Ramadan became the obligation and Ashura was left."
"25809","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Musab ibn Shayba, from Safiyya bint Shayba, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one morning wearing a striped cloak of black hair."
"25810","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umara, from his paternal aunt, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of what you eat is from your earnings, and your children are from your earnings."
"25811","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: There was a Makhzumi woman who used to borrow goods and deny them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her hand to be cut off. Her family came to Usama ibn Zayd and spoke to him, so Usama spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Usama, I do not see you but interceding with me regarding one of the prescribed punishments of Allah, Exalted and Majestic. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to address the people and said: Those before you were destroyed only because when the noble among them stole they let him be, and when the weak among them stole they cut him off. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, if Fatima bint Muhammad were to steal I would cut off her hand. Then he had the hand of the Makhzumi woman cut off."
"25812","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, regarding His saying, Exalted and Majestic: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the symbols of Allah, she said: There were men of the Ansar who used to enter ihram for Manat in the pre-Islamic period, and Manat was an idol between Makka and Madina. They said: O Prophet of Allah, we used to go between al-Safa and al-Marwa to venerate Manat, so is there any sin upon us if we go between them? So Allah, Exalted and Majestic, revealed: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umra, there is no blame upon him to go about between them."
"25813","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, she said: When: If you desire Allah and His Messenger, was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, beginning with me, and said: O Aisha, I will mention a matter to you, and you need not hasten in it until you consult your parents. She said: By Allah, he knew they would not order me to separate from him. She said: Then he recited to me: O Prophet, say to your wives: If you desire the life of this world and its adornment. I said: In this should I consult my parents? I desire Allah, Exalted and Majestic, and His Messenger and the abode of the Hereafter."
"25814","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to test the believing women only with the verse that Allah, Exalted and Majestic, said: When the believing women come to you pledging to you that they will not associate, and not, and not."
"25815","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, al-Zuhri said: Urwa informed me, from Aisha, she said: When twenty-nine nights had passed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me. She said: He began with me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore not to come to us for a month, yet you have come after twenty-nine, counting them. He said: The month is twenty-nine nights. Then he said: O Aisha, I will mention a matter to you, and you need not hasten in it until you consult your parents. Then he recited to me the verse: O Prophet, say to your wives, until he reached: a great reward. Aisha said: He knew that my parents would not order me to separate from him. She said: I said: In this should I consult my parents? I desire Allah and His Messenger and the abode of the Hereafter."
"25816","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from Qatada, from Zurara, from Sad ibn Hisham, he said: I asked Aisha, saying: Inform me of the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: His character was the Quran."
"25817","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, she said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How does the revelation come to you, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Sometimes it comes to me with a ringing like the ringing of a bell, then it leaves me, and I have retained it, and that is the hardest of it upon me; and sometimes it comes to me in the form of a man, or he said: the angel, and informs me, and I retain what he says."
"25818","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amra, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand of the thief is cut off for a quarter of a dinar and above."
"25819","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I was informed from Ibn Shihab, from Urwa, from Aisha, that she said, while mentioning the affair of Khaybar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send Ibn Rawaha to the Jews, and he would estimate the date-palms for them when they ripened, before any of it was eaten. Then the Jews would be given the choice whether to take it by that estimate or hand it over to them by that; the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordering of the estimation was only so that the zakat would be counted before the fruit was eaten and dispersed."
"25820","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ibn Shihab, that it reached him, from him, from Urwa, from Aisha, that she said, while mentioning the affair of Khaybar, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: when the first of the dates ripen, and he said: before the fruits are eaten."
"25821","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Farewell Hajj, and I entered ihram for Umra, and I had not driven the sacrificial animal with me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has the sacrificial animal with him, let him enter ihram for Hajj along with his Umra, then let him not come out of ihram until he comes out of both of them together. Then I menstruated, and when the night of Arafa came, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I had entered ihram for Umra, so what shall I do with my Hajj? He said: Undo your hair and comb it, and hold back from the Umra, and enter ihram for Hajj. When I had completed my Hajj, he ordered Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and he performed Umra with me from al-Tanim in place of my Umra that I had left off."
"25822","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, and Hisham, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Dubaa bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and she said: I want to perform Hajj and I am ill. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform Hajj and stipulate: My release is where You detain me."
"25823","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to depart, he was informed that Safiyya was menstruating. He said: Is she going to detain us? Then he was informed that she had already performed the farewell circumambulation, so he ordered her to depart."
"25824","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of five harmful creatures in the sacred and non-sacred territory: the kite, the scorpion, the mouse, the crow, and the vicious dog."
"25825","Yaqub narrated to us, from Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab, from his uncle, he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five of the beasts, all of them harmful, are killed in the sacred and non-sacred territory: the vicious dog, the scorpion, the crow, the kite, and the mouse."
"25826","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray, and he prolonged the standing greatly, then bowed and prolonged the bowing greatly, then raised his head and stood and prolonged the standing greatly, though less than the first standing, then prostrated, then stood and prolonged the standing, though less than the first, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, though less than the first bowing, then raised his head and stood and prolonged the standing, though less than the first standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, though less than the first bowing, then prostrated. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, and the sun had cleared. He addressed the people, praised Allah, Exalted and Majestic, and extolled Him, then said: The sun and the moon are among the signs of Allah, and they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life. When you see them, magnify Allah and supplicate to Allah, Exalted and Majestic, and pray and give charity. O nation of Muhammad, there is no one more jealous than Allah, Exalted and Majestic, that His servant should commit adultery or His maidservant should commit adultery. O nation of Muhammad, by Allah, if you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little. Have I conveyed?"
"25827","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Qasim narrating from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see Safiyya as nothing but detaining us. He said: Had she not performed the farewell circumambulation? She said: Yes, she had. He said: Then there is no detention upon you. So he departed with her."
"25828","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: I would have loved to have sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Sawda sought his permission, so that I might pray the morning prayer at Mina and stone the pillar before the people come. It was said to her: And had she sought his permission? She said: Yes, she was a heavy, slow woman, so she sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave her permission."
"25829","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amra, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the two rakas before Fajr, and he would lighten them until I would say: Has he recited in them the Mother of the Quran?"
"25830","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Aisha, she said: I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Will your wives return with a Hajj and an Umra while I return with a Hajj that has no Umra with it? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed for her at al-Batha, and ordered her, and she went out to al-Tanim, and her brother Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr went out with her, and she entered ihram for Umra, then came to the House and circumambulated it and went between al-Safa and al-Marwa, and shortened her hair; then he sacrificed a cow on her behalf."
"25831","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The most beloved deeds to Allah, Exalted and Majestic, are the most constant, even if little."
"25832","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, narrated to us, he said: Abu Salama narrated to us, from Aisha, he said: I said: O my mother, how was the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: He used to fast until we would say: He does not break fast, and he would break fast until we would say: He does not fast; and I never saw him fast in any month more than his fasting in Shaban; he would fast Shaban except a little, rather he would fast all of it."
"25833","Ibn Numayr and Rawh narrated to us, with the same meaning, they said: Hanzala narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, Rawh said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad saying: I heard Aisha saying: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night was ten rakas, he would make witr with one prostration, and he would pray the two rakas of Fajr, so that is thirteen."
"25834","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hanzala narrated to us, from Ibn Sabit, from Aisha, she said: I was late coming to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: What kept you, O Aisha? She said: O Messenger of Allah, there is a man in the mosque whose recitation I have never seen anyone better than. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went, and there was Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfa. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Praise be to Allah who has placed in my nation one like you."
"25835","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, from a man, from Masruq, from Aisha, she said: The right hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was for his food and his prayer, and his left was for other than that."
"25836","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Amra narrated to us, from Aisha bint Talha, from Aisha, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there jihad upon women? He said: Yes, upon them is a jihad in which there is no fighting: Hajj and Umra."
"25837","Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three Suhuli garments, among which there was neither a shirt nor a turban."
"25838","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: Dhakwan, the freed slave of Aisha, said: I heard Aisha saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the young girl whom her family marries off: Is her permission sought or not? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Her permission is sought. Aisha said: I said to him: She is shy and remains silent. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is her permission, when she remains silent."
"25839","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muawiya ibn Ishaq, from Aisha bint Talha, from Aisha, she said: We sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for jihad, and he said: Hajj suffices you, or: Your jihad is Hajj."
"25840","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa informed me that Ibn Shihab informed him that Urwa informed him that Aisha informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman married off without the permission of her guardians, her marriage is invalid, three times; and she shall have her dowry for what he took of her; and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"25841","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: Aisha said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hasten to anything as he hastened to the two rakas before the morning prayer, nor to any spoils he sought."
"25842","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Muawiya ibn Ishaq, from Aisha bint Talha, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, she said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about jihad, and he said: Hajj suffices you, or he said: Your jihad is Hajj."
"25843","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Ibn Sirin, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night, long while standing and long while sitting. He said: I said: How did he do? She said: When he recited standing, he bowed standing, and when he recited sitting, he bowed sitting."
"25844","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, and al-Thawri, from Ayyub, and he mentioned its meaning."
"25845","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Yahya ibn Yamar, he said: I asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleep while junub? She said to me: Sometimes he would bathe before sleeping, and sometimes he would sleep before bathing, but he would perform ablution. He said: Praise be to Allah who has placed latitude in the religion."
"25846","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, Abd al-Razzaq said: And he used to mention it from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, and so it was in his book, meaning al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Urwa, that Aisha said: A woman came, and with her were her two daughters, and she found nothing with me except one date, so I gave it to her, and she took it and split it between her two daughters, and ate nothing of it. Then she stood and went out, she and her two daughters. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me in the wake of that, and I told him her story. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is tested with any of these daughters and treats them well, they will be a veil for him from the Fire."
"25847","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: By Allah, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing at the door of my room while the Abyssinians played with spears, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) screened me with his cloak so I could watch their play from between his ear and his shoulder. Then he would remain standing for my sake until I was the one to leave. So estimate the measure of a young girl, fond of amusement."
"25848","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, she said: I used to play with dolls, and my friends would come to me; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, they would flee from him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take them and return them to me."
"25849","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to blow upon himself during the illness in which he died, with the chapters of refuge."
"25850","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw rain he would say: O Allah, a wholesome, abundant rain."
"25851","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Amra, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah said: I slept and saw myself in Paradise, and I heard the voice of a reciter reciting. I said: Who is this? They said: This is Haritha ibn al-Numan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Such is righteousness, such is righteousness; and he was the most dutiful of people to his mother."
"25852","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No illness or pain befalls the believer except that it is an expiation for his sin, even the thorn he is pricked with or the mishap he suffers."
"25853","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As, from his father, from Aisha, she said: Abu Bakr sought permission to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was with him under one cloak. She said: He gave him permission, and he conveyed his need to him while he was with me under the cloak, then he went out. Then Umar sought permission, and he gave him permission, and he conveyed his need to him in that same state, then he went out. Then Uthman sought permission, so he straightened his garments upon himself and sat, and conveyed his need to him, then he went out. Aisha said: I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr sought permission and conveyed his need to you in that state of yours, then Umar sought permission and conveyed his need to you in that state, then Uthman sought permission and it is as if you took care. He said: Uthman is a shy man, and had I given him permission in that state, I feared he would not convey his need to me."
"25854","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a husband and I have a co-wife, and I claim fullness from my husband, saying: He gave me such and clothed me with such, though it is a lie. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who claims fullness with what he was not given is like one wearing two garments of falsehood."
"25855","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, and from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, he said: A man asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do any work in his house? She said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to mend his sandal and sew his garment, and work in his house as one of you works in his house."
"25856","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a cloud portending rain, his face would change, and he would go in and out, come forward and turn back; then when it was dispelled from him and that was mentioned to him, he said: I was not sure it would not be as Allah said: Then when they saw it as a cloud approaching their valleys, to: a wind in which is a painful punishment."
"25857","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of Abu Musa al-Ashari reciting, he said: Abu Musa has been given of the flutes of the family of Dawud."
"25858","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Aisha, he said: A man asked her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his voice at night when he recited? She said: Yes, sometimes he would raise and sometimes he would lower. He said: Praise be to Allah who has placed latitude in the religion. He said: Did he pray witr at the beginning of the night? She said: Yes, sometimes he would pray witr at the beginning of the night and sometimes he would pray witr at its end. He said: Praise be to Allah who has placed latitude in the religion."
"25859","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eleven rakas at night; then when dawn broke he would pray two light rakas, then recline on his right side until the caller to prayer came to announce the prayer to him."
"25860","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, he said: Sad ibn Hisham informed me that he heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with nine rakas and two rakas while sitting; then when he grew weak he prayed witr with seven and two rakas while sitting."
"25861","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, that Sad ibn Hisham ibn Amir, who was his neighbor, informed him, and he mentioned the hadith, and that he visited Aisha, and she mentioned, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to pray nine rakas, sitting in them only at the eighth, praising Allah, Exalted and Majestic, remembering Him and supplicating, then rising without saluting, then praying the ninth, sitting, praising Allah, Exalted and Majestic, remembering Him and supplicating, then saluting with a salutation that made us hear, then praying two rakas while sitting."
"25862","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatada, from Muadha al-Adawiyya, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the Duha prayer as four rakas, and add whatever Allah willed."
"25863","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar, from Qatada, he said: Muadha al-Adawiyya narrated to me, and he mentioned it."
"25864","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never performed the supererogatory prayer of Duha. He said: And Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would leave a deed though he loved to do it, fearing the people would take it as a practice and it would be made obligatory upon them. She said: And he loved what was light upon the people."
"25865","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed with the people, prolonging the recitation, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then raised his head and prolonged the recitation, though less than his first recitation, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, though less than his first bowing, then raised his head and prostrated two prostrations, then stood and did in the second raka the like of that, then finished and said: The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah, Exalted and Majestic. When you see that, hasten to prayer."
"25866","Mamar narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa informed me, from his father, from Aisha, the like of this, and he added: He said: When you see that, give charity and pray."
"25867","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me, from Aisha, that she reported, of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and of herself, that the two of them both bathed together from one vessel while junub."
"25868","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels were created from light, the jinn were created from a smokeless flame of fire, and Adam, upon him be peace, was created from what was described to you."
"25869","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, of the one in retreat and how his practice was, from Said ibn al-Musayyab and Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she informed them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform retreat in the last ten of the month of Ramadan until Allah, Exalted and Majestic, took him."
"25870","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays informed us, from Sad ibn Said, brother of Yahya ibn Said, from Amra, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Breaking the bone of the dead is like breaking it while alive. He said: They think it is regarding sin. Abd al-Razzaq said: I think it is the saying of Dawud."
"25871","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Musa ibn Uqba informed me, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Hamza ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she and the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to the family of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas: Have him pass by us in the mosque, so that the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) might pray over him. The people disapproved of that, and that was mentioned to Aisha. She said: Do you wonder at the people when they disapprove of this? By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over Sahl ibn Bayda only in the mosque."
"25872","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Al-Zuhri informed me, of the hadith of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr and Ibn al-Musayyab, narrating from Urwa, from Aisha, and Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform retreat in the last ten of Ramadan, then he never ceased doing that until death took him, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father saying: This hadith is thus in the Book of Fasting from Abu Hurayra and Aisha, and in Retreat from Aisha alone."
"25873","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Urwa ibn al-Zubayr claiming that Urwa informed him that Aisha informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never came to her after Asr except that he prayed two rakas."
"25874","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah said, and my father narrated to me, and Ibn Bakr said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka said: I heard the household of Aisha mentioning from her that she used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exerted his body greatly in worship, except that when he advanced in age and grew heavy with flesh, most of his prayer was while sitting."
"25875","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman informed me that Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him that Aisha informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until he came to pray much of his prayer while sitting."
"25876","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, he said: Urwa said: Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one night in the middle of the night and prayed in the mosque, and men gathered and prayed with him following his prayer. In the morning the people spoke: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and prayed in the mosque in the middle of the night. The next night more of them gathered. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, having bathed, in the middle of the night, and prayed, and they prayed with him following his prayer. Then morning came and they spoke of that, and on the third night many people gathered, until the people of the mosque grew numerous. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the middle of the night and prayed, and they prayed with him. When the fourth night came, the people gathered until the mosque could hardly hold its people, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and did not go out. She said: Until I heard some of them saying: Prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go out to them. When he had prayed the Fajr prayer, he saluted, then stood among the people and testified, then said: To proceed: Your affair last night was not hidden from me, but I feared it would be made obligatory upon you and you would be unable to bear it."
"25877","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Urwa, that Aisha used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never prayed the supererogatory prayer of Duha. He said: And Aisha used to perform it, and she used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would leave a deed fearing the people would take it as a practice and it would be made obligatory upon them."
"25878","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, that he reported, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aisha, that she said: Upon none of the supererogatory prayers was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more assiduous than upon the two rakas before the morning prayer. I heard this from Ata repeatedly."
"25879","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The skilled one in the Quran is with the noble, righteous scribes, and the one who reads while it is hard upon him, stammering in it, shall have two rewards, two."
"25880","Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: I bought Barira, and her family stipulated her allegiance. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Buy her and free her, for allegiance belongs only to one who pays the price. She said: So I bought her and freed her. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her and gave her the choice regarding her husband; she chose herself, and her husband was free."
"25881","Jarir narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, the like of the hadith of Mansur, except that he said: Her husband was a slave; had he been free, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not have given her the choice."
"25882","Hushaym narrated to us, from Sayyar, from al-Shabi, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to the wash-basin and bathe from it for major impurity after morning had come, then he would remain that day of his fasting."
"25883","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Aisha, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel."
"25884","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, he said: A man of the people of Kufa narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aisha, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of his washing place where he bathed for major impurity, he would wash his feet."
"25885","Hushaym narrated to us, Mughira narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In place of cauterization is the poultice, in place of throat remedies is the snuff, and in place of blowing is the mouth-pour."
"25886","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, from Aisha, that she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, on the day of Badr, those men and they were thrown into the well, Utba and Abu Jahl and their companions, he stood over them and said: May Allah reward you with evil, O people of a prophet; never was there a worse expulsion nor a severer denial. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how do you address people who have rotted? He said: You do not understand my words better than they, or: They understand my words better than you."
"25887","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would keep his right hand free for his food and his needs, and keep his left hand free for cleansing and what is there."
"25888","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, from Aisha, that she used to wash the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was menstruating and he was in retreat, putting his head out from the mosque to the room."
"25889","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, from Aisha, she said: I would wrap my waist-wrapper while menstruating and enter with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) into his blanket."
"25890","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mughira informed us, from Ibrahim, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice, and we chose him, and he did not count that as a divorce."
"25891","Hushaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sleep while junub without touching water."
"25892","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, and Bahz, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Muadha, from Aisha, that she said: Tell your wives to wash from themselves the traces of stool and urine, for I am shy before them; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it. Bahz said: Tell your wives."
"25893","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Said, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to bathe, he would begin with his palms and wash them, then pour with his right upon his left and wash his private parts, until when he was clean he would incline his hand to the wall and wash it, then turn to the ablution water and pour it over himself."
"25894","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Said, from Qatada, from Muadha al-Adawiyya, from Aisha, that she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for major impurity from one vessel."
"25895","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Aisha, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for major impurity from one vessel."
"25896","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Budayl, from Abu al-Jawza, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to open his prayer with the takbir, open the recitation with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, and seal it with the salutation."
"25897","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Abu Mashar, from al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, that Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send the sacrificial animal, and we would twist its necklaces for it, then he would not abstain from anything that the one in ihram abstains from."
"25898","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, he said: Ibn Burayda narrated to me, he said: Aisha said: O Prophet of Allah, tell me, if I coincide with the Night of Decree, what shall I say? He said: You say: O Allah, You are Pardoning, You love pardon, so pardon me."
"25899","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, and Yazid, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri said: From Kahmas, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Shaqiq saying: I said to Aisha: Did the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray the Duha prayer? She said: No, except when he came from an absence. He said: I said: Did he pray sitting? She said: After the people had worn him down. He said: I said: Did he recite a chapter? She said: The Mufassal. He said: I said: Did he fast a whole month? She said: I never knew him to fast a whole month except Ramadan, nor do I know him to have left fasting a whole month without taking some of it, until he passed away. Yazid said: Joining. And likewise Abu Abd al-Rahman said."
"25900","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh ibn Hani narrating from his father, from Aisha, he said: Aisha rode a camel, and it was unruly, so she kept turning it back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Be gentle, for it is never in a thing except that it beautifies it, and never removed from a thing except that it disgraces it."
"25901","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Mu'adhah, from 'A'ishah, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel, and he would vie with me and I would vie with him until I would say: Leave some for me, leave some for me."
"25902","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mu'adhah, that a woman asked 'A'ishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray al-Duha? He said: She said: Yes, and he would add whatever Allah willed."
"25903","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mu'adhah, she said: I asked 'A'ishah about ghusl from janabah, so she said: Water, nothing makes it impure; I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel; he would begin and wash his hands."
"25904","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: I said to 'A'ishah: O Mother of the Believers, inform me about what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade of vessels. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-dubba', al-hantam, and al-muzaffat."
"25905","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that a woman with istihadah asked in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so it was said: It is only a rebellious vein; and she was commanded to delay al-Zuhr and hasten al-'Asr and bathe one ghusl, and to delay al-Maghrib and hasten al-'Isha' and bathe for them both one ghusl, and to bathe for the Fajr prayer one ghusl. Ibn Ja'far said: One ghusl."
"25906","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, he said: I heard al-Qasim narrating from 'A'ishah, that he said: She had a garment with images spread toward a sahwah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray toward it, so he said: Keep it away from me. She said: So I kept it away and made it into cushions."
"25907","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, he said: I heard al-Qasim narrating from 'A'ishah, that she wanted to buy Barirah for emancipation, but they stipulated her wala'; so she mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Buy her and free her, for wala' belongs only to the one who frees; and meat was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This is what was given in charity to Barirah, so he said: It is charity for her and a gift for us; and she was given the choice. 'Abd al-Rahman said: And her husband was free. Shu'bah said: Then I asked him about her husband, so he said: I do not know."
"25908","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel, from janabah."
"25909","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, that he used to enter upon 'A'ishah. He said: I said: And how did he enter upon her? He said: He would go out with his khal, al-Aswad. He said: And there was between him and 'A'ishah brotherhood and affection."
"25910","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, from his paternal aunt 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, that she said: When dawn rose, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rak'ahs, or he would not pray except two rak'ahs; I say: He recites in them al-Fatihah."
"25911","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, and Hajjaj, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Malik ibn 'Urfutah, from 'Abd Khayr, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-dubba', al-hantam, and al-muzaffat."
"25912","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, that she said: I never saw pain upon anyone more severe than it was upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25913","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Khaythamah narrating from Abu 'Atiyyah, he said: We said to 'A'ishah: Among us are two men from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one of them hastens the iftar and delays the suhur, and the other delays the iftar and hastens the suhur. He said: So 'A'ishah said: Which of them is the one who hastens the iftar and delays the suhur? He said: So I said: He is 'Abdullah. So she said: Thus would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"25914","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from his paternal aunt, from 'A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's child is from his earning, among the purest of his earning."
"25915","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu al-Duha narrating from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his wives the choice; so was it divorce?"
"25916","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, that she said: I indeed saw the glisten of perfume on the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram."
"25917","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who is pricked by a thorn or more except Allah raises him by it a degree and removes from him by it a sin."
"25918","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, and 'Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan informed us, in meaning, from al-A'mash, from Thabit ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Hand me the khumrah. She said: So I said: I am menstruating. So he said: It is not in your hand. So I handed it to him."
"25919","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed us, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, that she used to bathe, she and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel."
"25920","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maymun, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating from 'Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from 'A'ishah, that a man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or a man was mentioned in his presence, so he said: What an evil servant of Allah and brother of the clan; then he entered upon him, so he turned to him with his face until we thought he had a standing with him."
"25921","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, and Hajjaj, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu al-Malih, Hajjaj said: from a man, he said: Some women from the people of al-Sham entered upon 'A'ishah, so she said: Are you the ones who enter the bathhouses? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no woman who removes her clothes outside her house except she tears a veil between her and Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Hajjaj said: Except she tears her veil."
"25922","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu al-Malih, from 'A'ishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned its meaning."
"25923","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, he said: I heard Abu Salamah, he said: I entered upon 'A'ishah and asked her about the ghusl of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from janabah. She said: His vessel would be brought to him, so he would wash his hands three times, then pour from the vessel onto his private part and wash it, then pour with his right hand onto his left and wash it, then rinse his mouth and sniff water, then pour over his head three times, then wash the rest of his body."
"25924","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, that she said: When one of us menstruated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would command her to wrap her waist, then he would lie with her. He said: This is Ibn al-Mubarak; then he said afterwards: Then he would touch her."
"25925","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, she said: I used to twist the necklaces of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sheep, then nothing of it becomes forbidden."
"25926","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj, Shu'bah informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, she said: I would be in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and when I wanted to get up I disliked passing in front of him, so I would slip away stealthily."
"25927","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, he said: I asked 'A'ishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: It was continuous."
"25928","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch while fasting."
"25929","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, she said: Umm Salamah said to 'A'ishah: There enters upon you the adolescent boy whom I would not like to enter upon me. So 'A'ishah said: Do you not have in the Messenger of Allah a good example? She said: The wife of Abu Hudhayfah said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim enters upon me, and he is a man, and there is in the soul of Abu Hudhayfah something of it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Suckle him so that he may enter upon you."
"25930","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Umm al-Mu'minin, that she said: When one of us was menstruating, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would command us to wrap the waist, then enter with him into his blanket."
"25931","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu 'Abdullah al-Jadali, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither obscene nor deliberately obscene nor loud in the markets, nor did he repay evil with its like, but he would pardon and forgive."
"25932","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz said: Shu'bah narrated to us, Bahz said: Ash'ath ibn Sulaym narrated to us, that he heard his father narrating, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far said: from al-Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, from his father, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while there was a man with her, and it was as if he became angry, so she said: He is my brother. He said: Look at whom your brothers are, for suckling is only from hunger."
"25933","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, from his father, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, that a Jewish woman entered upon her and mentioned the torment of the grave, so she said to her: May Allah protect you from the torment of the grave. So 'A'ishah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the torment of the grave, so he said: Yes, the torment of the grave is true. 'A'ishah said: So I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray a prayer afterwards except he sought refuge from the torment of the grave."
"25934","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to us, Hajjaj and Bahz said: Shu'bah informed me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Mujahid, Bahz said: Ibn Wardan, and Hajjaj said: Mujahid ibn Wardan, from the people of Madinah, and they praised him highly, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, she said: A mawla of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought his inheritance, so he said: Is there here anyone from the people of his village? Bahz said: They said: Yes. He said: So give it to him."
"25935","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, that he asked Ibn 'Umar about a man perfuming himself at his ihram, so he said: To be smeared with tar is more beloved to me than to do it. He said: So my father asked 'A'ishah and informed her of the saying of Ibn 'Umar, so she said: May Allah have mercy on Abu 'Abd al-Rahman; I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would go around his wives, then he would wake in ihram exuding perfume."
"25936","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I asked 'A'ishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast the known days of the month? So she said: Yes."
"25937","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran, from Talhah, Ibn Ja'far said: Ibn 'Abdullah, from 'A'ishah, that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: I have two neighbors, so to which of them should I give a gift? He said: To the nearer of them to you in door."
"25938","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran, from Talhah, a man from Quraysh from Banu Taym ibn Murrah, from 'A'ishah, that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the like of it."
"25939","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Rawh said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from 'Ali ibn Husayn, Rawh said: I heard 'Ali ibn Husayn, from Dhakwan, the mawla of 'A'ishah, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived when four days of Dhu al-Hijjah had passed, so he entered upon me while angry, so I said: Who angered you, O Messenger of Allah? May Allah enter him into the Fire. So he said: Did you not feel that I commanded the people with a command, yet I see them hesitating? Al-Hakam said: As if they, I think; had I faced of my affair what I have now seen, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal with me until I bought it, then I would dissolve ihram as they dissolved. Rawh said: Hesitating about it. He said: As if they feared, I think."
"25940","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, that she wanted to buy Barirah for emancipation, but her masters wanted to stipulate her wala', so she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Buy her; wala' belongs only to the one who frees; and he gave her the choice regarding her husband, and her husband was free; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat, so it was said: This is what was given in charity to Barirah, so he said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"25941","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Ibrahim narrating from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, that she said: It is as if I am looking at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he is in ihram."
"25942","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, that she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to depart, he saw Safiyyah at the door of her tent, gloomy or sad, and she had menstruated, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Aqra or halqa; you will detain us; did you pour forth on the Day of Sacrifice? She said: Yes. He said: Then depart."
"25943","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from 'A'ishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no Muslim who is pricked by a thorn or more except Allah, Mighty and Majestic, raises him by it a degree or removes by it from him a sin."
"25944","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah informed me, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Talhah ibn 'Abdullah, Hajjaj said: Ibn 'Awf, and Ya'qub narrated it to us from his father, he said: Ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined toward me to kiss me, so I said: I am fasting. He said: And I am fasting. So he kissed me. Hajjaj said: Shu'bah said to me: Sa'd said to me: Talhah is the paternal uncle of my father Sa'd."
"25945","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz said: Shu'bah narrated to us, Bahz said: Sa'd ibn Ibrahim informed me, that he heard Abu Salamah narrating from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deed is most beloved to Allah? He said: The most constant of it, even if little. Bahz said: What is persisted in. And he said: Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear."
"25946","Bahz and Ibn Ja'far said: Shu'bah narrated to us, Bahz said: Sa'd ibn Ibrahim informed me, he said: I heard 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while I was between him and the qiblah. Ibn Ja'far said: Sa'd said: And I think he said: While she was menstruating."
"25947","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, and Rawh said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd, he said: I heard 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from 'A'ishah, that she said: I used to hear that no prophet would die until he is given choice between this world and the Hereafter. He said: So I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in his illness in which he died, and hoarseness seized him, saying: With those upon whom Allah bestowed favor, of the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, and excellent are those as companions. She said: So I thought he was given the choice then. Rawh said: He was given choice between this world and the Hereafter."
"25948","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say in his ruku': Subbuh, Quddus, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"25949","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, he said: I asked 'A'ishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night, so she said: He would sleep at the beginning of the night, then stand; and when it was the time of sahar he would pray witr, then come to his bed; and if he had a need he would go to his wife; and when he heard the adhan he jumped up; and if he was junub he would pour water over himself, otherwise he would perform wudu', then go out to prayer."
"25950","'Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I heard al-Aswad, he said: I asked 'A'ishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the like of it."
"25951","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Masruq, that they said: We testify regarding 'A'ishah that she said: There was no day of hers when he was with me except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed them both in my house, meaning the two rak'ahs after 'Asr."
"25952","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr said to al-Aswad: Narrate to me from Umm al-Mu'minin 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, for she used to confide in you. He said: She informed me that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Were it not that your people are recent in their time of jahiliyyah, I would have demolished the Ka'bah, then I would have made for it two doors; so when Ibn al-Zubayr ruled, he demolished it and made for it two doors."
"25953","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The most beloved deed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that which its doer persists in."
"25954","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn 'Abdullah, that 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq informed 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you not see that your people, when they built the Ka'bah, fell short of the foundations of Ibrahim, peace be upon him? She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not return it upon the foundations of Ibrahim, peace be upon him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the recency of your people in disbelief. He said: So 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar said: If 'A'ishah heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I do not see that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left touching the two corners that adjoin al-Hijr except that the House was not completed upon the foundations of Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
"25955","Haddathana, he said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated it to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, that she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Farewell Hajj, so we entered ihram for 'umrah, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him enter ihram for hajj with 'umrah, then let him not dissolve until he dissolves from both together. She said: So I arrived at Makkah while menstruating, and I did not circumambulate the House nor between al-Safa and al-Marwah, so I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Undo your head and comb and enter ihram for hajj and leave 'umrah. She said: So I did; and when we completed the hajj, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me with 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr to al-Tan'im, so I performed 'umrah, so he said: This is in place of your 'umrah. She said: So those who entered ihram for 'umrah circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then dissolved, then circumambulated another tawaf after returning from Mina for their hajj; as for those who combined the hajj, they circumambulated one tawaf."
"25956","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah, that she said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Safiyyah bint Huyayy has menstruated. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps she will detain us; did she not circumambulate with you at the House? They said: Yes. He said: Then go forth."
"25957","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, that she informed him that Aflah, the brother of Abu al-Qu'ays, came seeking permission to enter upon her, and he was her paternal uncle through suckling, after the hijab was revealed. She said: So I refused to permit him; and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, I informed him of what I had done, so he commanded me to permit him."
"25958","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, that she used to say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not glorify the Duha supererogatory prayer, yet I do glorify it."
"25959","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Malik, and Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from 'Alqamah ibn Abi 'Alqamah, from his mother, from 'A'ishah, that she said: Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfah gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a Shamiyyah khamisah with a mark, so he witnessed the prayer in it; and when he finished he said: Return this khamisah to Abu Jahm, for I looked at its mark in prayer and it almost tempted me."
"25960","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the mosque, so people prayed with his prayer; then he prayed the next night and people increased; then they gathered on the third or fourth night, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not come out to them; and in the morning he said: I saw what you did, and nothing prevented me from coming out to you except that I feared it would be made obligatory upon you; and that was in Ramadan."
"25961","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray at night thirteen rak'ahs, then when he heard the call to Fajr he would pray two light rak'ahs."
"25962","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she informed him that she never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying the night prayer sitting until he aged; so he would recite sitting until, when he wanted to bow, he stood and recited about thirty or forty verses, then bowed."
"25963","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid and Abu al-Nadr, mawla of 'Umar ibn 'Ubaydullah, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray sitting, reciting while sitting; and when there remained of his recitation about thirty or forty verses, he stood and recited while standing, then bowed, then prostrated, then did in the second rak'ah the like of that."
"25964","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Abu Yunus, mawla of 'A'ishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: 'A'ishah commanded me to write for her a mushaf. She said: When you reach this verse, inform me: Maintain the prayers and the middle prayer. He said: So when I reached it I informed her, so she dictated to me: Maintain the prayers and the middle prayer and the 'Asr prayer, and stand for Allah devoutly. Then she said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25965","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never prayed the Duha supererogatory prayer at all, yet I do glorify it; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would leave a deed while loving to do it, fearing that people would do it and it would be made obligatory upon them."
"25966","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, he said: And Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us: Malik informed me, from Rabi'ah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from 'A'ishah, that she said: There were in Barirah three sunnahs; one of the three sunnahs was that she was freed and given choice regarding her husband; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning her: Wala' belongs to the one who frees; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while the pot was boiling with meat, so bread and condiment from the condiment of the house were brought near to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did I not see a pot with meat in it? So they said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but that is meat given in charity to Barirah, and you do not eat charity. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"25967","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, that 'A'ishah informed her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with her, and that she heard the voice of a man seeking permission in the house of Hafsah. 'A'ishah said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a man seeking permission in your house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I think he is so-and-so, a paternal uncle of Hafsah through suckling. So 'A'ishah said: O Messenger of Allah, if so-and-so were alive, my paternal uncle through suckling, would he enter upon me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, suckling forbids what birth forbids."
"25968","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray al-Subh, then the women would leave wrapped in their murut, not recognized from the ghalas."
"25969","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'A'ishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, until when we were at al-Bayda' or Dhat al-Jaysh, a necklace of mine broke, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed to seek it, and the people stayed with him, and they were not upon water nor did they have water with them; so the people came to Abu Bakr and said: Do you not see what 'A'ishah has done? She detained the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people, and they are not upon water nor do they have water. So Abu Bakr came, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had placed his head on my thigh, so he said: You detained the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people, and they are not upon water nor do they have water. She said: So Abu Bakr reproached me and said whatever Allah willed him to say, and began striking with his hand on my flank, and nothing prevented me from moving except the place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on my thigh; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until people woke without water, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed the verse of tayammum, so they performed tayammum. So Usayd ibn al-Hudayr said: It is not your first blessing, O family of Abu Bakr. She said: So we dispatched the camel I was upon and found the necklace beneath it."
"25970","He said: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sa'd, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, from Talhah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss me while fasting, and I fasting."
"25971","He said: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Abu 'Udhrah, and he had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade men and women from bathhouses, then permitted men in waist-wrappers."
"25972","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad ibn Tahlah narrated to us, from Abu al-Rijal, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O 'A'ishah, a house with no dates in it, its people are hungry. 'Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan had narrated it to us from him."
"25973","'Abd al-Rahman and 'Affan said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, 'Affan said: al-Azraq ibn Qays informed us, from Dhakwan, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray upon the khumrah."
"25974","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from 'Abdullah al-Bahiyy, from 'A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the slave-girl while in the mosque: Hand me the khumrah. She said: He wanted to spread it and pray upon it. So she said: I am menstruating. So he said: Your menstruation is not in your hand."
"25975","'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il al-Suddi narrated to us, from 'Abdullah al-Bahiyy, he said: 'A'ishah narrated to me, then he mentioned it."
"25976","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from 'Abdullah al-Bahiyy, from 'A'ishah, she said: I would not make up what remained upon me of Ramadan during the entire life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except in Sha'ban."
"25977","He said: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Mina', he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying: My khalah 'A'ishah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Were it not that your people are recent in shirk or jahiliyyah, I would have demolished the Ka'bah and leveled it to the ground and made for it two doors, an eastern door and a western door, and added to it from al-Hijr six cubits; for Quraysh shortened it when they built the Ka'bah."
"25978","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from a man, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no person who has a night prayer which sleep overcomes him except his sleep is charity upon him and the reward of his prayer is written for him."
"25979","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah, she said: I used to twist the necklaces of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hands, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would garland them with his hand, then send them with my father, and he would not leave anything Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made lawful to him until the sacrificial animal is sacrificed."
"25980","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to me, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from his khalah 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Were it not that your people are recent in their time of shirk, I would have demolished the Ka'bah, then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Ibn Mahdi."
"25981","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until women were made lawful to him."
"25982","'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: I heard 'A'ishah, Umm al-Mu'minin, saying: Barirah was a mukatabah to some people of the Ansar, so I wanted to buy her, so I commanded her to go to them and inform them that I wanted to buy her and free her, so they said: If you grant us her wala', we will sell her to her. So I sought a fatwa from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Buy her and free her, for wala' belongs only to the one who frees; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while the pot was boiling with meat, so he said: From where is this for you? I said: Barirah gifted it to us, and it was given in charity to her. So he said: This is charity for Barirah and a gift for us. She said: And she was under a slave, so when he freed her, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Choose; if you wish to remain under this slave, and if you wish to leave him."
"25983","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, that 'A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me in my house in an izar and rida', so he faced the qiblah and spread his hands and said: O Allah, I am only a human, so whichever servant of Your servants I struck or harmed, do not punish me for it."
"25984","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from 'A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the dead, for they have proceeded to what they sent forth."
"25985","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, and Abu 'Amir narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Namir, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, that 'A'ishah said: When it was 'A'ishah's night, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out, when two-thirds of the night had gone, to al-Baqi', and say: Peace upon you, O people of the abode of believing folk; we and you and what you are promised tomorrow are deferred. Abu 'Amir said: You are deferred. And we, if Allah wills, will join you."
"25986","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, he heard al-Qasim, he said: I heard 'A'ishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does a deed upon which our command is not, it is rejected."
"25987","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic? He said: The most constant of them, even if little. He said: And I heard him, meaning Abu Salamah, narrating from 'A'ishah or from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear."
"25988","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Overlook the slips of people of good standing, except the hudud."
"25989","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us and said: By the One besides whom there is no god, the blood of a Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, is not lawful except for three persons: the one who abandons Islam and separates from the jama'ah, and the married adulterer, and a life for a life."
"25990","Al-A'mash said: So I narrated it to Ibrahim, so he narrated to me from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, the like of it."
"25991","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'A'ishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his ihram when he entered ihram, and for his release when he dissolved before circumambulating the House."
"25992","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Ghalib, that 'A'ishah said to al-Ashtar: Are you the one who wanted to kill my nephew? He said: I was keen to kill him and he was keen to kill me. She said: Did you not know what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said? The blood of a man is not lawful except a man who apostatized or abandoned Islam, or committed zina after being married, or killed a soul for other than a soul."
"25993","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Mujahid ibn Wardan, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, that a mawla of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a date-palm cluster and died, so he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Does he have any lineage or kin? They said: No. He said: Give his inheritance to some people of his village."
"25994","'Umar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn al-Asbahani, from Mujahid ibn Wardan, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed his inheritance to the people of his village."
"25995","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah, from Abu 'Atiyyah, and Ibn Ja'far, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, he said: I heard Khaythamah narrating from Abu 'Atiyyah, from 'A'ishah, she said: I indeed know how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say talbiyah: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk; labbayk, no partner have You; labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion. Ibn Ja'far said: Then I heard her afterwards saying talbiyah."
"25996","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, she said: I never saw any human at all upon whom pain was more severe than upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25997","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted something, but some men turned away from it, so he said: What is with men whom I command a command yet they turn away from it? By Allah, I am indeed the most knowledgeable of them about Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and the most intense of them in fear of Him."
"25998","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he fell ill he would recite upon himself with al-Mu'awwidhat and blow."
"25999","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in i'tikaf, he would draw his head near to me and I would comb it, and he would not enter the house except for a human need."
"26000","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given choice between two matters except he chose the easier of them, so long as there was no sin in it; and if there was sin in it, he was the farthest of people from it; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never took revenge for himself for anything done to him, except that a sanctity of Allah be violated, so he would take revenge for Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"26001","Abdulrahman narrated to us from Malik from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eleven rakahs at night, making witr one of them with a single rakah, then when he finished his prayer he would lie down on his right side."
"26002","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik informed us from al-Miqdam from his father, he said: I said to Aishah, O Mother, with what would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) begin when he entered your house, and with what would he end? She said: He would begin with the siwak and end with the two rakahs of Fajr."
"26003","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us from Ali ibn Zayd from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Aishah, she said: I raced the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I beat him."
"26004","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from Abu Salamah from Aishah, she said: I used to sleep lying across in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed, and when he wanted to pray witr he would nudge me with his foot and say: Move aside."
"26005","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed us from Abu Salamah from Aishah, he said: I said, O Mother, how was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the last Isha? She said: He used to pray thirteen rakahs, nine standing and two sitting, and two after the two calls, meaning between the adhan of Fajr and the iqamah."
"26006","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, informed us from Abu Salamah from Aishah, she said: A month would pass for the family of Muhammad with no smoke seen in any of their houses. I said, O Mother, what was their food? She said: The two black ones, dates and water, except that he had truthful neighbors from the Ansar who had milch animals, and they would send to him some of their milk."
"26007","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed us from Abu Salamah from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the illness in which he died: What happened to the gold? She said: I said, it is with me. He said: Bring it to me. So I brought it, and it was between nine or five. He placed it in his hand, then he said with it, and Yazid gestured with his hand: What would Muhammad think of Allah if he met Allah the Mighty and Majestic while this was with him? Spend it."
"26008","He said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Maysarah, he said: Umm al-Muminin Aishah said: I would tie my waist-wrapper then enter with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) under his blanket while I was menstruating."
"26009","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us from Ata from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would become junub then sleep, and when he rose he would wash and go out with his head dripping, then fast the rest of that day."
"26010","Yazid narrated to us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us from Abdullah ibn Buraydah that Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, if I coincide with Laylat al-Qadr, with what should I supplicate? He said: Say: O Allah, You are Pardoning and love pardon, so pardon me."
"26011","Yazid narrated to us: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down and prayed in the mosque one night in Ramadan, and people prayed behind him following his prayer, then he came down the second night and they were more than that, then they increased on the third night. When it was the fourth night, the mosque was crowded with its people, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not come down. They spoke about that, saying what is the matter with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he did not come down. He heard their talk, and when morning came he said: O people, I have heard your talk, and nothing prevented me from coming down to you except fear that the standing of this month would be made obligatory upon you."
"26012","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Kahmas informed us from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, he said: Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, if I coincide with Laylat al-Qadr, with what should I supplicate? He said: Say: O Allah, You are Pardoning and love pardon, so pardon me."
"26013","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us from Abdurrahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would send them, and he would not give up anything of what he used to do before that."
"26014","Abdulwahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us from Ayyub from Muhammad that Aishah was asked about the two rakahs of Fajr, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lighten them. She said: I think he used to recite something like Say O disbelievers and Say He is Allah the One."
"26015","Abdulwahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us from a man from Umar ibn Abdulaziz that he said: I have not faced the qiblah with my private part for such and such time. Then Irak ibn Malik narrated from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his privy to be faced toward the qiblah when it reached him that people disliked that."
"26016","Abdulwahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Muhammad from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in the morning junub without a wet dream, then fast."
"26017","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us from Ayyub, meaning Abu al-Ala al-Qassab, from Abu Hashim from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray sitting, and when he wanted to bow he would stand and recite about ten verses or whatever Allah willed, then bow."
"26018","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Burd narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah, she said: Our door was in the qiblah of the mosque, and I sought to open it while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, so he walked until he opened for me, then returned to the place where he had been."
"26019","Ali narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed me from al-Zuhri from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every condition not in the Book of Allah the Mighty and Majestic is rejected, even if they stipulated a hundred times."
"26020","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us from Abdullah ibn Buraydah from Aishah, she said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, tell me, if I knew Laylat al-Qadr, what would I call upon my Lord the Mighty and Majestic with, or what would I ask Him? He said: Say: O Allah, You are Pardoning and love pardon, so pardon me."
"26021","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Hanzalah al-Sadusi informed us from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, he said: Muawiyah led the people in Asr prayer, then he turned and saw people praying after Asr, so he entered, and Ibn Abbas entered upon him, and I was with him, and Muawiyah made room for him on the couch and he sat with him. He said: What is this prayer which I saw the people praying, while I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray it nor command it? He said: That is what Ibn al-Zubayr gives them fatwa about. Then Ibn al-Zubayr entered and greeted and sat. Muawiyah said: O Ibn al-Zubayr, what is this prayer which you order the people to pray? We never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray it nor command it. He said: Aishah Umm al-Muminin narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed it with her in her house. He said: So Muawiyah and another man ordered me to go to Aishah and ask her about that. He said: So I entered upon her and asked her about that, and I told her what Ibn al-Zubayr had reported from her. She said: Ibn al-Zubayr did not remember correctly. I only told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed these two rakahs after Asr with me, and I asked him, I said: You prayed two rakahs you were not praying. He said: Something came to me and I was distracted in distributing it from the two rakahs after Zuhr, and Bilal came to me and called me to prayer, and I disliked detaining the people, so I prayed them. He said: So I returned and informed Muawiyah. He said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: Did he not pray them? Then we will not leave them. Muawiyah said to him: You will never cease to be dissenting."
"26022","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us from al-Hadhdha from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Aishah Umm al-Muminin that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he gave salam from the prayer would say: O Allah, You are al-Salam and from You is peace, blessed are You O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"26023","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us: Dawud narrated to us from al-Shabi from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say often before his death: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him. She said: He used to say it often, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, you supplicate with a supplication you did not supplicate with before today. He said: My Lord the Mighty and Majestic informed me that I would see a sign in my ummah, and that when I saw that sign I should glorify Him with His praise and seek His forgiveness. I have seen that: When the help of Allah and the conquest comes, and you see the people entering the religion of Allah in crowds."
"26024","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us from Khalid from Abu Qilabah from Abdurrahman ibn Attab, he said: Abu Hurayrah used to say: Whoever wakes junub has no fast. He said: Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent me, me and another man, to Aishah and Umm Salamah to ask them about one junub waking in Ramadan before washing. He said: One of them said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub then wash and complete the fast of his day. He said: And the other said: He would wake junub without having a wet dream, then complete his fast. He said: So they returned and informed Marwan of that. He said to Abdurrahman: Inform Abu Hurayrah of what they said. Abu Hurayrah said: That is what I used to think and suppose. He said: Marwan said to him: With I think and I suppose you give people fatwa?"
"26025","Ali narrated to us from Khalid and Hisham from Ibn Sirin from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rakahs of Fajr: Say O disbelievers and Say He is Allah the One."
"26026","He said: And he narrated to us from Khalid, meaning Ali, from Ibn Sirin from Aishah, she said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite them quietly."
"26027","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed me from Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt, he said: I was with Umar ibn Abdulaziz during his caliphate, he said: And with him was Irak ibn Malik. Umar said: I have not faced the qiblah nor turned my back to it with urine or stool for such and such time. Irak said: Aishah narrated to me that when the talk of the people about that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he ordered his sitting-place and faced the qiblah with it."
"26028","Ali narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us from Abu Qilabah from Aishah, she said: Young maidens used to come out of their chambers for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the two Eids."
"26029","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Safiyyah saying: Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or Hafsah, or both of them, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah to mourn more than three days except for her husband."
"26030","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from al-Walid ibn Abdurrahman al-Qurashi from Aishah that she said: I menstruated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his bed, so I slipped away. He said to me: Did you menstruate? I said: Yes. He said: Then tighten your waist-wrapper over you, then return."
"26031","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abdulwahid ibn Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr saying: I heard Umm al-Muminin Aishah saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the easy reckoning. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the easy reckoning? He said: The man, his sins are presented to him, then he is pardoned for them. Whoever is questioned closely about the reckoning will perish. And no thorn or anything greater befalls a servant except that Allah the Mighty and Majestic expiates thereby some of his sins."
"26032","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab informed that Urwah informed him that Aishah informed him, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would send them, and he would stay, and would not refrain from anything."
"26033","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about a man who gives his wife a choice and she chooses him. He said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: I will present a matter to you, and you need not hasten in it until you consult your parents. I said: What is this matter? She said: Then he recited to me: O Prophet, say to your wives: If you desire the worldly life and its adornment, come, I will provide for you and release you with a handsome release. And if you desire Allah and His Messenger and the Hereafter, then Allah has prepared for the doers of good among you a great reward. Aishah said: So I said: In which of that do you command me to consult my parents? Rather I desire Allah and His Messenger and the Hereafter. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pleased with that and it delighted him, and he said: I will present to your companions what I presented to you. She said: So I said to him: Then do not inform them of what I chose. But he did not do that, and he would say to them as he said to Aishah, then he would say: Aishah has chosen Allah and His Messenger and the Hereafter. Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us a choice, and we did not consider that divorce."
"26034","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us from Imran from Abu Salamah from Aishah, she said: Safiyyah bint Huyayy menstruated while she was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina after having performed ifadah. She said: When it was the day of departure, that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Perhaps she will detain us. He said: So it was said, O Messenger of Allah, she had already circumambulated the House. He said: Then let her depart."
"26035","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us from Sufyan from Asim from Zirr ibn Hubaysh from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left neither a dinar nor a dirham, nor a slave-girl nor a slave, nor a sheep nor a camel."
"26036","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Yazid al-Rishk from Muadhah that a woman asked Aishah: Does a menstruating woman make up the prayer? She said: Are you a Haruri? The women of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to menstruate; did he order them to make up?"
"26037","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, he said: I said to Aishah Umm al-Muminin: At what hour do you pray witr? Perhaps he said: She said: I do not pray witr until they call the adhan, and they do not call until dawn rises. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two muadhdhins, Bilal and Amr Ibn Umm Maktum. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Amr calls, eat and drink, for he is a man blind of sight, and when Bilal calls, raise your hands, for Bilal does not call, he said thus, until morning comes."
"26038","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us from Hammad from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah that she said: It is as if I look at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after days while he is in ihram."
"26039","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us from Abdurrahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with perfume containing musk at his ihram before he entered ihram, and on the Day of Sacrifice before he circumambulated the House."
"26040","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abdurrahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Aishah that she said: I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his sacred state when he entered ihram and for his released state when he exited ihram, before he circumambulated the House."
"26041","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik and Sakhr and Hammad narrated to us from Abdurrahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah the like of it, except that they said: For his sacred state before he enters ihram."
"26042","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Yusuf ibn Mahak and Ata mentioning from Aishah that she said: I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his exiting ihram and at his entering ihram."
"26043","Rawh narrated to us: Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us from Hammad from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah that she said: It is as if I look at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he is in ihram."
"26044","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Aishah, she said: It is as if I look at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after days while he is in ihram."
"26045","Abdussamad ibn Abdulwarith narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to me, he said: The son of the brother of Amrah narrated to me from his aunt Amrah from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the two rakahs before the morning prayer and lighten them, until I would doubt whether he recited the Fatihah of the Book in them or not."
"26046","Umar ibn Hafs Abu Hafs al-Muaiti narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not take a kunyah? She said: With whom shall I take a kunyah? He said: Take kunyah by your son Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr. He said: So she was called Umm Abdullah."
"26047","Waki narrated to us from Hisham from a man of the children of al-Zubayr from Aishah that she said: O Messenger of Allah, all your women have a kunyah except me. He said: You are Umm Abdullah."
"26048","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Abu al-Duha from Masruq from Aishah, she said: When the verses of riba were revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the minbar and recited them to the people, then he forbade trade in wine."
"26049","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wala is for the one who paid the price and freed, and for the holder of the favor. And her husband was free, so she was given a choice."
"26050","Waki narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Aishah, she said: The Abyssinians were playing on a feast day, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me, and I would look over his shoulder at them. Then Abu Bakr came and said. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave her, for every people has a feast, and this is our feast."
"26051","Waki narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Aishah, she said: When And warn your nearest kin was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: O Fatimah bint Muhammad, O Safiyyah bint Abdulmuttalib, O Banu Abdulmuttalib, I do not avail you against Allah anything; ask me of my wealth whatever you wish."
"26052","Waki narrated to us from Shubah from Abu Imran al-Jawni from a Qurashi man called Talhah from Aishah: I said, O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors; to which of them should I give a gift? He said: To the nearer of them in door to you."
"26053","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Zuhayr from Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, and Mawla al-Muttalib, from al-Muttalib, meaning Ibn Hantab, from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man attains by good character the rank of one who fasts and stands in prayer."
"26054","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Asim from Zirr from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left neither a dinar nor a dirham, nor a sheep nor a camel. Sufyan said: I learned, and I doubt about the slave and the slave-girl."
"26055","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Zubayd from Mujahid from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril kept enjoining me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"26056","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Abdurrahman ibn Abis from his father, he said: I entered upon Aishah and said to her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the meat of sacrifices after three days? She said: Yes. The people were afflicted with hardship, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved that the rich feed the poor. Then I saw the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating the trotter after fifteen days. I said to her: What was that for? He said: So she laughed and said: The family of Muhammad never ate their fill of bread with condiment for three days until he met Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"26057","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Israil and Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; he said: Israil informed me, the meaning, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Yusuf ibn Mahak from his mother from Aishah, she said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, shall we not build for you at Mina a house or a structure to shade you from the sun? He said: No, it is only the resting-place of whoever gets there first."
"26058","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Hammad ibn Salamah from Abu Imran al-Jawni from Yazid ibn Babanus from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would embrace me and take from my head while I was menstruating."
"26059","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us from Layth from Abdurrahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah, she said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, and one of us would menstruate and become pure, and he would not order us to make up, nor would we make it up."
"26060","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Sad from al-Zuhri, and Abu Kamil, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us from Amrah from Aishah, she said: Umm Habibah bint Jahsh, Abu Kamil said: Umm Habib, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she had been in istihadah for seven years. She complained of that to him and sought his fatwa about it. He said: This is not menstruation, but this is a vein, so wash and pray. So she would wash for every prayer and pray, and she would sit in a tub and the redness of the blood would rise over the water, then she would pray."
"26061","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha from his father from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked beginning with the right in all his affairs, in his combing, in his purification, and in his sandal. Shubah said: Then I asked him after that, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved, or liked, beginning with the right as much as he could."
"26062","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qays, he said: I asked Aishah about the two rakahs after Asr. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs after Zuhr, but he was distracted from them until he prayed Asr. When he finished, he bowed them in my house, and he never left them until he died. Abdullah ibn Abi Qays said: So I asked Abu Hurayrah about it. He said: We used to do it, then we left it."
"26063","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah narrated to us from Abu al-Zahiriyyah from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, he said: I entered upon Aishah and she said: Do you recite Surat al-Maidah? He said: I said: Yes. She said: It is the last surah revealed, so whatever lawful you find in it, deem lawful, and whatever unlawful you find in it, deem unlawful. And I asked her about the character of the Messenger of Allah, and she said: The Quran."
"26064","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Muawiyah from Abdullah ibn Abi Qays that he heard Aishah saying: The most beloved of months to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to fast was Shaban, then he would join it with Ramadan."
"26065","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad narrated to me from Abu al-Rijal from Amrah from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, a house with no dates in it, its people are hungry."
"26066","Abdurrahman narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, make me of those who, when they do good, rejoice, and when they do evil, seek forgiveness."
"26067","Abdurrahman and Affan narrated to us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Safiyyah bint Shaybah from Aishah, she said: The women of the Ansar were mentioned, and she praised them and spoke good of them. She said: When Surat al-Nur was revealed, they went to the edges or hems of their waist-wrappers and tore them, then took veils from them. And a woman of them entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about purification from menstruation. He said: Yes, let one of you take her water and her lote-leaves and purify herself, then perfect the purification, then pour over her head, then press upon the roots of her head, then rub it, for that is purification, then pour water over herself, then take a musk-scented cloth and purify herself with it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, how do I purify myself with it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was speaking euphemistically about that. Aishah said: Follow with it the trace of blood. Affan said: Then pour over her head some water and press the roots of her head and rub it. Affan said: To the edges or hems."
"26068","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us from Sadaqah, a Kufan man, he said: Jumay ibn Umayr, one of Banu Taym Allah ibn Thalabah, narrated to us, he said: I entered with my mother and my maternal aunt upon Aishah, and one of them asked: How did you do at washing? Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution as his ablution for prayer, then pour over his head three times, and we pour over our heads five times because of the braids."
"26069","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh from his father from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered his house, he would begin with the siwak."
"26070","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn Shayban from Abu Nawfal, he said: I asked Aishah: Was poetry recited in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: The most hateful speech to him. And he said, from Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked comprehensive supplications and would leave what is between that."
"26071","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Hammad ibn Zayd from Marwan Abu Lubabah, he said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until we said he does not intend to break fast, and break fast until we said he does not intend to fast. And he would recite every night Bani Israil and al-Zumar."
"26072","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Malik from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given a choice between two matters except he chose the easier of them, unless it involved sin; if it was sin, he was the farthest of people from it."
"26073","Abdullah narrated to us: Abdulmalik ibn Amr Abu Amir narrated to me, he said: Hisham narrated to us from Yahya from Abu Salamah that Aishah narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not fast any month of the year more than his fasting of Shaban; he would fast all of Shaban. And he would say: Take of deeds what you can bear, for Allah the Mighty and Majestic does not tire until you tire. And the most beloved prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was what was done persistently, and when he prayed a prayer he kept to it."
"26074","Abdulmalik ibn Amr and Yazid narrated to us, they said: Hisham informed us from Yahya from Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Aishah about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He would pray thirteen rakahs: he would pray eight rakahs, then pray witr, then pray two rakahs while sitting; when he wanted to bow he would stand and bow, then pray the two rakahs between the call and the iqamah of the Fajr prayer."
"26075","Abdurrahman narrated to us, he said: I heard Sufyan narrating, he said: Ali ibn al-Aqmar narrated to us from Abu Hudhayfah, and he was of the companions of Abdullah, and Talhah used to narrate from him, from Aishah, she said: I imitated a man for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It would not please me to imitate a man even if I had such and such. She said: So I said, O Messenger of Allah, Safiyyah is a woman, and he gestured with his hand as if meaning short. He said: You have mixed with a word which, if mixed with the water of the sea, would taint it."
"26076","Abdullah said: I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting; Abdullah did not hear this hadith, meaning the hadith of Jabir: Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Sufyan from Jabir from Abdurrahman ibn al-Aswad from his father from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came out of the privy would perform ablution."
"26077","Abdurrahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah, he said: I asked Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah single out anything of the days? She said: No, his deed was continuous, and which of you could bear what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) could bear?"
"26078","Abdurrahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: When I menstruated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would order me, so I would tie my waist-wrapper, then he would touch me."
"26079","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I and he would wash from a single vessel while we were junub."
"26080","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would put his head out to me while he was in itikaf, and I would wash it while I was menstruating."
"26081","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah that she bought Barirah. She said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, I will buy Barirah and stipulate wala for them. He said: Buy, for wala is only for the one who holds the favor, or for the one who freed."
"26082","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur and al-Amash from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sheep, then he would not enter ihram."
"26083","Abdurrahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fast the ten. Abdurrahman said: And Abu Awanah reported it with isnad from al-Aswad."
"26084","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan, and Waki, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Abu al-Duha from Masruq from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) often said in his prostration and bowing: Glory be to You our Lord and with Your praise, O Allah forgive me, interpreting the Quran. Waki said: O Allah and with Your praise."
"26085","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur from Musa ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid from a freedman of Aishah from Aishah, she said: I never saw the private part of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at all."
"26086","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Hammad from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out to the Fajr prayer with his head dripping, then wake fasting."
"26087","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh from his father from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he saw a rising cloud on a horizon of the horizons of the sky would leave his work, even if in prayer, then say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil in it. If Allah removed it, he would praise Allah, and if it rained he would say: O Allah, a beneficial downpour."
"26088","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan, and Abu Nuaym: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Shaybani from Abdurrahman ibn al-Aswad from his father from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ruqyah for every venomous sting."
"26089","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Malik ibn Anas from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about bit, and he said: Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful."
"26090","Abdurrahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur ibn Safiyyah from his mother from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would place his head in her lap and recite the Quran while she was menstruating."
"26091","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Amir narrated to us from Masruq, he said: I asked Aishah, he said: I said: There is here a man who sends his sacrificial animal to the Kabah and orders the one driving it for him from a marked place he commanded, so he garlands it, and he remains in ihram until the people exit ihram. He said: So I heard her clapping her hands from behind the veil: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would send his sacrificial animal, and nothing forbidden for a man to one of his family would become forbidden for him until the people returned."
"26092","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwah, from his father from Aishah that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only alighted at al-Muhassab to make his departure easier, and it is not a sunnah; whoever wishes may alight there, and whoever wishes may not alight there."
"26093","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah, he said: Mansur narrated to me from Muslim from Masruq from Aishah: When the last verses of Surat al-Baqarah were revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited them to the people and forbade trade in wine."
"26094","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Zakariyya, he said: Amir narrated to us from Masruq from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would send them, and he would not enter ihram."
"26095","He said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Mansur and Sulayman narrated to me from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeing it only as Hajj."
"26096","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father informed me from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given a choice between two matters, one easier than the other, except he took the easier one."
"26097","Yahya narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father informed me from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands for the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would send them, then stay with us and not avoid anything that one in ihram avoids."
"26098","Yahya narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur and Sulayman narrated to me from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sheep, then he would send them, and he would not enter ihram."
"26099","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah from Mansur, he said: Sheep."
"26100","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wash from a single vessel while we were junub."
"26101","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'ba, he said: al-Hakam narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was junub and wanted to sleep, he performed wudu."
"26102","My father said, and Waki' and Muhammad ibn Ja'far said in this hadith: When he wanted to sleep or eat, he performed wudu. Yahya said: Shu'ba abandoned the hadith of al-Hakam about the junub person, when he wants to eat, performing wudu."
"26103","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'ba from al-Hakam from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aisha: Barira was given charity, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"26104","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'ba, he said: al-Hakam and Sulayman narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aisha, she said: I saw perfume, one of them said: in the head or hair, and the other said: in the parting of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in ihram."
"26105","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, Yahya said: Hisham dictated it to me, he said: My father informed me, he said: Aisha informed me, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, coinciding with the crescent of Dhu al-Hijja, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wishes to enter ihram for umra, let him enter ihram, and whoever wishes to enter ihram for hajj, let him enter ihram. Had I not brought the sacrificial animal, I would have entered ihram for umra. She said: Some of them entered ihram for umra and some of them entered ihram for hajj, and I was among those who entered ihram for umra, then I menstruated before entering Makka, and the day of Arafa overtook me while I was menstruating, so I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Leave your umra, undo your head and comb, and enter ihram for hajj. So I did, and when it was the night of al-Hasba, he sent Abd al-Rahman with me to al-Tan'im, and he seated her behind him, and she entered ihram for umra in place of her umra, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, fulfilled her hajj and her umra, and there was nothing in any of that, no sacrificial animal, no fasting, and no charity."
"26106","Waki' narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, similar to it. Waki' said: And wash and enter ihram for hajj. Urwa said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, fulfilled her hajj and her umra."
"26107","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me from Abu Salama, he said: Aisha saw Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr performing wudu, so she said: O Abd al-Rahman, perfect the wudu, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"26108","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Habib ibn Shahid from Ikrima from Aisha: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to kiss while fasting, and for you in the Messenger of Allah there is a good example."
"26109","Waki' narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Qatada from Zurara ibn Awfa from Sa'd ibn Hisham from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The one who recites the Qur'an while skilled in it is with the noble righteous scribes, and the one who recites it while it is hard upon him has two rewards."
"26110","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh ibn Hani' al-Harithi from his father, he said: I said to Aisha: With what did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, begin when he entered his house? She said: With the siwak."
"26111","Waki' narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from his father from Aisha, and he said: Aflah narrated to us from al-Qasim from Aisha, and he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aisha, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a single vessel. And he said in the hadith of Mansur: While we were both junub."
"26112","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan and Mis'ar narrated to us from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh from his father from Aisha, she said: I would drink while menstruating, then hand it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would place his mouth upon the place of my mouth, and I would gnaw meat from the bone while menstruating, then hand it to him, and he would place his mouth upon the place of my mouth."
"26113","Waki' narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Aswad ibn Yazid from Aisha, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not perform wudu after ghusl."
"26114","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh ibn Hani' from his father, Aisha said: Whoever narrates to you that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, urinated standing, do not believe him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not urinate standing; he did not urinate standing since the Qur'an was revealed to him."
"26115","Waki' narrated to us from Shu'ba, and Muhammad said: Shu'ba narrated to us from al-Hakam from Ibrahim, Muhammad said: I heard Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aisha: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he wanted to sleep or eat while junub, performed wudu."
"26116","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwa and Abu Salama from Aisha: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he wanted to eat while junub, washed his hands."
"26117","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us from his father from Aisha, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray at night while I lay across between him and the qibla, and when he wanted to perform witr, he woke me and I performed witr."
"26118","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Aisha informed me, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would kiss some of his wives while fasting."
"26119","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, he said: Aisha informed me, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was shrouded in three white Yemeni garments, in which there was neither shirt nor turban."
"26120","Yahya narrated to us from Abd Allah, he said: I heard al-Qasim saying: Aisha said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for his exiting ihram and his entering ihram, when he entered ihram, and for his exiting ihram when he exited ihram before circulating or circumambulating the House."
"26121","Yahya narrated to us from Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: Aisha said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I see Safiyya as nothing but detaining us. He said: What is her matter? I said: She has menstruated. He said: Had she not performed the Ifada? I said: Yes, but she menstruated afterward. He said: Then there is no detention upon you, so he departed with her."
"26122","Yahya narrated to us from Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Aisha: A man divorced his wife thrice, then another married her and divorced her before touching her, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: Is she lawful for the first? He said: No, until he tastes her little honey as the first tasted."
"26123","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father informed me from Aisha: A woman of Banu Qurayza, her husband divorced her, then another man of them married her and divorced her, so she came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: He has only like this fringe of mine. He said: No, until you taste his little honey or he tastes your little honey. Hisham doubted."
"26124","Yahya narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us from Qatada from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah from Aisha: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say in his bowing and prostration: Glorified, Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit, three times. Then Yahya doubted about three."
"26125","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, he said: My father informed me from Aisha: Hamza ibn Amr al-Aslami said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to fast continuously, so shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"26126","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, he said: My father informed me from Aisha, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a single vessel; I and he would scoop from it."
"26127","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Aisha, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bathe from a single vessel, and I would say: Leave some for me, leave some for me. My father said likewise."
"26128","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Yahya from Amra: I heard Aisha saying: Had the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seen what women have innovated, he would have prevented them as the women of Banu Isra'il were prevented. He said: I said to Amra: And were the women of Banu Isra'il prevented from the mosque? He said: Yes."
"26129","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan, he said: Mansur narrated to me from Ibrahim from Umara from his aunt from Aisha from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The purest of what a man eats is from his earning, and his child is from his earning."
"26130","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from al-A'mash, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us from Hammam ibn al-Harith from Aisha, she said: I would see it, semen, upon the garment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I would scratch it off. And Yahya once said: And I would rub it off."
"26131","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, meaning al-Dastuwai, he said: Yahya narrated to us from Abu Salama from Urwa from Aisha: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would kiss while fasting."
"26132","Yahya narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us from al-Hakam from Ibrahim from Hammam ibn al-Harith from Aisha: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, similar to this, meaning about rubbing off semen."
"26133","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'ba, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to me from Talha, he said: Aisha said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I have two neighbors, to which of them shall I give a gift? He said: To the nearer of them to you by door."
"26134","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'ba, he said: al-Hakam narrated to me, he said: I said to Miqsam: I perform witr with three then go out to prayer fearing it will escape me. He said: No witr except with five or seven. He said: So I mentioned that to Yahya ibn al-Jazzar and Mujahid, and they said to me: Ask him from whom. So I said to him, and he said: From the trustworthy, from Aisha and Maymuna, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"26135","Yahya narrated to us from Husayn, he said: Budayl narrated to me from Abu al-Jawza' from Aisha: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to open the prayer with takbir and the recitation with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. When he bowed, he neither raised his head up nor lowered it, but between that. When he raised his head from bowing, he would not prostrate until he stood straight, and when he raised his head from prostration, he would not prostrate until he sat straight. He would say the greeting in every two rak'as, and he disliked spreading the forearms as the lion spreads, and he would spread his left foot and erect his right foot, and he forbade the عقب of Satan, and he would seal the prayer with taslim."
"26136","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwa, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Aisha informed me: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, people entered upon him in his illness visiting him, so he prayed with them sitting, and they began praying standing, so he signaled to them to sit. When he finished, he said: The imam is only appointed to be followed, so when he bows, bow, and when he rises, rise, and if he prays sitting, pray sitting."
"26137","Yahya ibn Sa'id and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said: Yahya narrated to us from Amra from Aisha, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeing it as nothing but hajj. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded whoever had the sacrificial animal with him to remain upon his ihram, and whoever did not have a sacrificial animal to exit ihram when he circumambulated. On the day of sacrifice, beef was brought to me, so I said: What is this? They said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slaughtered on behalf of his wives. Yahya said: Shu'ba said: So I mentioned that to al-Qasim, and he said: She brought you the hadith in its correct form. Ibn Numayr said: With five remaining of Dhu al-Qa'da, seeing it as nothing but hajj."
"26138","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Aisha, she said: My foster uncle came to me seeking permission after the hijab was imposed. I said: I will not permit until I seek permission from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Let your uncle enter upon you. I said: Only the woman suckled me, the man did not suckle me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He is your uncle, so let him enter upon you."
"26139","Waki' narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, Aisha informed me, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When supper is placed and prayer is established, begin with supper. And Waki' said: When prayer and supper are present. And Ibn Uyayna said: When supper is placed."
"26140","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, he said: My father informed me from Aisha, and Waki' said: Hisham narrated to us from his father from Aisha: Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I suffer istihada and do not become pure, shall I leave prayer? Waki' said, he said: No. Yahya said: That is not menstruation, that is only a vein. When menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it goes, wash the blood from yourself and pray. Yahya said: I said to Hisham: One washing, she bathes, and wudu at every prayer? He said: Yes."
"26141","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Urwa ibn al-Zubayr and Alqama ibn Waqqas and Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Mas'ud informed me of the hadith of Aisha, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the people of the slander said of her what they said, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, exonerated her. Each of them narrated to me a portion of her hadith, and some of them retained her hadith better than others and more firmly in narration, and I retained from each one of them the hadith he narrated to me, and part of their hadith confirms part. They mentioned that Aisha, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to go out on a journey, he cast lots among his wives, and whichever of them her lot came out, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out with her. Aisha said: So he cast lots among us in a battle he fought, and my lot came out in it, so I went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and that was after the hijab was revealed. I would be carried in my howdah and dismount in it during our march, until when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished his battle and turned back and we neared Madina, he announced one night to depart. So I stood when they announced departure and walked until I passed the army, and when I finished my need, I came to my camp and felt my chest, and a necklace of onyx of Zafar had broken, so I returned seeking my necklace, and seeking it detained me. The party who used to carry me came and carried my howdah and saddled it upon my camel which I rode, thinking I was in it. She said: Women in those days were light; flesh had not burdened them nor covered them, they ate only a mouthful of food, so the people did not notice the weight of the howdah when they saddled and lifted it. I was a young girl, so they sent the camel and went. I found my necklace after the army had gone on, and I came to their dwellings with no caller nor answerer in them, so I headed for my dwelling where I had been, thinking the people would miss me and return to me. While I sat in my dwelling, my eye overcame me and I slept. Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, had rested behind the army and traveled in the night, and in the morning reached my dwelling and saw the blackness of a sleeping human, so he came to me and recognized me when he saw me, for he had seen me before the hijab was imposed upon me. I woke at his retrieval phrase when he recognized me, and I covered my face with my jilbab. By Allah, he did not speak a word to me, nor did I hear a word from him other than his retrieval phrase, until he made his camel kneel and stepped upon its foreleg, so I rode it, and he set out leading the mount with me until we reached the army after they had halted at midday in the heat of noon. Those who perished perished concerning me, and the one who took upon himself the most of it was Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul. I arrived at Madina and fell ill when we arrived, a month, while people spread the saying of the people of the slander, and I sensed nothing of that. What made me doubt in my pain was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the kindness I used to see from him when I complained; he would only enter, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and greet, then say: How is that one? That made me doubt, and I did not sense the evil, until I went out after I recovered, and Umm Mistah went out with me toward al-Manasi', our place of relieving ourselves, and we would not go out except at night, and that was before privies were taken near our houses, and our affair was the affair of the first Arabs in keeping distant, and we were harmed by privies taken at our houses. I set out, I and Umm Mistah, she is the daughter of Abu Ruhm ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf, and her mother is the daughter of Sakhr ibn Amir, aunt of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and her son is Mistah ibn Uthatha ibn Abbad ibn al-Muttalib. I came, I and the daughter of Abu Ruhm, toward my house when we finished our affair, and Umm Mistah stumbled in her wrap and said: May Mistah perish. I said to her: Evil is what you said, you revile a man who witnessed Badr. She said: O dear, have you not heard what he said? I said: And what did he say? So she informed me of the saying of the people of the slander, and I increased in sickness upon my sickness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me and greeted, then said: How is that one? I said: Will you permit me to go to my parents? She said: I then wanted to verify the news from them, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted me, and I came to my parents and said to my mother: O mother, what are people saying? She said: O daughter, be easy upon yourself, for by Allah, seldom is there a beautiful woman with a man who loves her, having co-wives, except they multiply against her. She said: I said: Glory be to Allah, have people spoken of this? She said: So I wept that night until morning, no tear ceasing for me nor sleeping with sleep. Then I awoke weeping, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called Ali ibn Abi Talib and Usama ibn Zayd when revelation delayed, to consult them about parting his wife. She said: As for Usama ibn Zayd, he advised the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with what he knew of the innocence of his family and what he knew in himself of love for them, and said: O Messenger of Allah, they are your family, and we know only good. As for Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not constrained you, and women besides her are many, and if you ask the maid, she will tell you truth. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called Barira and said: O Barira, have you seen anything of Aisha that makes you doubt? Barira said to him: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have never seen upon her any matter that I blame her for, more than that she is a young girl who sleeps past her family's dough, so the domestic animal comes and eats it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and sought excuse from Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said while upon the minbar: O assembly of Muslims, who will excuse me regarding a man whose harm has reached me concerning my household? By Allah, I have known upon my family only good, and they mentioned a man upon whom I have known only good, and he would not enter upon my family except with me. Sa'd ibn Mu'adh al-Ansari stood and said: I excuse you from him, O Messenger of Allah; if he is of Aws, we strike his neck, and if he is of our brothers of Khazraj, you command us and we do your command. She said: Sa'd ibn Ubada stood, he is chief of Khazraj, and he was a righteous man, but zeal made him foolish, and said to Sa'd ibn Mu'adh: By Allah, you will not kill him nor be able to kill him. Usayd ibn Hudayr stood, he is cousin of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, and said to Sa'd ibn Ubada: You lie; by Allah, we shall surely kill him, for you are a hypocrite disputing for the hypocrites. The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, rose until they nearly fought, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood upon the minbar, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept calming them until they fell silent, and he fell silent. She said: I wept my day, no tear ceasing for me nor sleeping with sleep, then I wept my coming night, no tear ceasing for me nor sleeping with sleep, while my parents thought weeping would split my liver. She said: While they sat with me and I wept, a woman of the Ansar sought permission upon me, so I permitted her, and she sat weeping with me. While we were upon that, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon us and greeted, then sat. She said: He had not sat with me since what was said to me was said, and a month had passed with nothing revealed to him concerning my affair. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, testified when he sat, then said: Now, O Aisha, such and such has reached me about you, so if you are innocent, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will exonerate you, and if you have touched a sin, seek forgiveness of Allah then repent to Him, for when a servant confesses a sin then repents, Allah turns to him. She said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished his speech, my tear receded until I sensed not a drop of it. I said to my father: Answer for me the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in what he said. He said: By Allah, I do not know what I say to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said to my mother: Answer for me the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: By Allah, I do not know what I say to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: So I said, a young girl not reciting much of the Qur'an: By Allah, I have known that you heard this until it settled in yourselves and you believed it. If I say to you I am innocent, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knows I am innocent, you will not believe me in that, and if I confess to you an affair, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knows I am innocent, you will believe me. By Allah, I find no likeness for me and you except as the father of Yusuf said: So patience is beautiful, and Allah is the One sought for help against what you describe. She said: Then I turned and lay upon my bed. She said: By Allah, I then knew I was innocent and that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would exonerate me with my innocence, but by Allah, I did not think revelation would descend concerning my affair recited; my affair was more despicable in myself than that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, should speak concerning me a matter recited, but I hoped the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would see in sleep a vision by which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would exonerate me. She said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had not moved from his sitting, nor had anyone of the household gone out, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down upon His Prophet, and what used to seize him of heaviness at revelation seized him, until sweat like pearls poured from him on a wintry day, from the weight of the saying sent down upon him. She said: When it was lifted from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he laughed, the first word he spoke was to say: Rejoice, O Aisha; as for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He has exonerated you. My mother said to me: Stand to him. I said: By Allah, I will not stand to him, nor praise but Allah, Mighty and Majestic; He is who sent down my exoneration. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: Indeed those who brought the slander are a band among you, ten verses, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down these verses for my exoneration. She said: Abu Bakr said, and he used to spend upon Mistah for his kinship and poverty: By Allah, I shall never spend upon him anything ever after what he said of Aisha. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: Let not those of bounty among you and abundance swear, to His saying: Do you not love that Allah forgive you. Abu Bakr said: By Allah, I love that Allah forgive me, so he returned to Mistah the spending he used to spend upon him, and said: I shall never take it from him ever. Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had asked Zaynab bint Jahsh, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about my affair: What have you known or seen or reached you? She said: O Messenger of Allah, I guard my hearing and sight, and I have known only good. Aisha said: She is who used to rival me among the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, protected her with piety, while her sister Hamna bint Jahsh set out fighting for her, and perished among those who perished. He said: Ibn Shihab said: This is what reached us of the affair of these people."
"26142","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to me from Salih, Bahz said: I said to him: Ibn Kaysan? He said: Yes, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Alqama ibn Waqqas and Ubayd Allah ibn Utba narrated to me from Aisha, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the people of the slander said of her what they said, and Allah exonerated her. Each of them narrated to me a portion of her hadith, and some of them retained her hadith better than others and more firmly in narration, and I retained from each man of them the hadith he narrated to me from Aisha, and part of their hadith confirms part, though some of them retained it better than others. They said: Aisha said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted travel, he cast lots among his wives, and whichever her lot came out, he went out with her. Then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: He announced the night of departure, so I stood when they announced departure, and said: Of onyx of Zafar, and said: They are burdened with flesh, and said: So I headed for my dwelling, and said: Urwa said: I was informed that it was spread and narrated in his presence, and he affirmed it and listened to it and sought more of it. Urwa also said: None of the people of the slander was named except Hassan ibn Thabit and Mistah ibn Uthatha and Hamna bint Jahsh, among other people I have no knowledge of, except that they were a band as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said. The most of that was said to be with Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul. Urwa said: Aisha disliked Hassan being reviled in her presence, saying: He is who said: My father and his father and my honor are a shield for the honor of Muhammad against you. She said: Our affair was the affair of the first Arabs in keeping distant. He said: She had co-wives. He said: With what he knows of the innocence of his family. He said: So the domestic animal comes and eats it. He said: Though he was of our brothers of Khazraj. He said: A man of Khazraj stood, and the mother of Hassan was daughter of his uncle of his clan, he is Sa'd ibn Ubada, chief of Khazraj. She said: He was before that a righteous man, but zeal carried him. He said: My tear receded. He said: Her sister Hamna set out fighting for her. Urwa said: Aisha said: By Allah, the man of whom what was said was said says: Glory be to Allah, by Him in whose Hand is my soul, I have never uncovered the covering of any female ever. She said: Then he was killed after that in the path of Allah as a martyr."
"26143","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Salih ibn Kaysan, Ibn Shihab said: Urwa narrated to me, then he mentioned the hadith and its isnad, and said: Of onyx of Zafar, and said: They are burdened with flesh, and said: I headed, and said: In the open land, and said: She had co-wives, and said: So the domestic animal comes and eats it, and said: He was before that a righteous man, but zeal carried him, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept calming them until they fell silent, and said: My tear receded, and said: Fighting."
"26144","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us from Ma'mar, al-Zuhri said, and Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aisha said: I never comprehended my parents except while they professed the religion, and no day passed upon us but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us in it at the two ends of the day, morning and evening. When the Muslims were tried, Abu Bakr went out emigrating toward the land of Abyssinia, until when he reached Barka al-Ghimad, Ibn al-Daghina met him, he is chief of al-Qara, and Ibn al-Daghina said: Where do you intend, O Abu Bakr? Abu Bakr said: My people expelled me, then he mentioned the hadith. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to the Muslims: I have seen the abode of your emigration; I was shown a salty land with palms between two lava tracts, they are two harras. Whoever had emigrated went out toward Madina when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned that, and some who had emigrated to Abyssinia returned to Madina. Abu Bakr prepared to emigrate, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: At your leisure, for I hope permission will be given to me. Abu Bakr said: Do you hope that, may my father and mother be ransom for you? He said: Yes. So Abu Bakr held himself back for the companionship of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and fed two mounts he had with leaves of samur for four months. Al-Zuhri said: Urwa said: Aisha said: While we one day sat in our house at midday, two sayers said to Abu Bakr: This is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, coming veiled in an hour he did not used to come to us in. Abu Bakr said: Ransom for him be my father and mother; his coming at this hour is surely for an affair. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and sought permission, and permission was given him, and he entered. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he entered, said to Abu Bakr: Send out whoever is with you. Abu Bakr said: They are only your family, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Permission has been given me to go out. Abu Bakr said: Then companionship, may my father be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes. Abu Bakr said: Take, may my father be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, one of these two mounts of mine. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For a price. She said: We equipped them with the best equipment and made for them provisions in a bag, and Asma' bint Abi Bakr cut from her girdle and tied the bag, for that she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr joined a cave in a mountain called Thawr, and remained in it three nights."
"26145","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Abu Mulayh from Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Any woman who puts off her clothes in other than her house has torn what is between her and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, or the veil of what is between her and Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"26146","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Talha ibn Yahya from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Aisha: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray with a cloak of these striped ones upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray with part of it upon him and part of it upon me, and the cloak was of black garments."
"26147","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Mansur ibn Safiyya from his mother from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died while we had eaten our fill of the two black ones, dates and water."
"26148","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Urwa from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delayed the night prayer until Umar called him and said: The prayer; women and children have slept. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out and said: None of the people of the religions awaits it other than you."
"26149","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq informed me that Aisha informed him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her while she was screened with a curtain in which was an image of figures, so his face changed color, then he reached for the curtain and tore it with his hand, then said: Among the severest of people in punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who liken to the creation of Allah."
"26150","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from Hisham from his father from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me with a woman of good appearance with me, and said: Who is this? I said: This is so-and-so daughter of so-and-so, O Messenger of Allah; she does not sleep the night. He said: Hush, hush; take of deeds what you can bear, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not tire until you tire, and the most beloved deed to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is what its doer persists upon, though little."
"26151","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from Aisha, she said: A party of Jews entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Death upon you. Aisha said: I understood it, so I said: Upon you death and curse. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Gently, O Aisha; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves gentleness in all affairs. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear what they said? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have said: And upon you."
"26152","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, and Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri from Urwa from Aisha, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a single vessel in it the measure of a faraq."
"26153","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in a khamisa with marks, and when he finished his prayer, he said: Take this khamisa to Abu Jahm and bring me his anbijaniyya, for it distracted me just now from my prayer."
"26154","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray Asr before the sun left my chamber, rising."
"26155","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray while I lay across between him and the qibla like the lying of a bier."
"26156","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from Qatada from Mutarrif from Aisha: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say in his prostration or bowing: Glorified, Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"26157","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us from Ma'mar from Ibn Tawus from his father from Aisha: She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never left the two rak'as after Asr."
"26158","She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not seek the rising of the sun nor its setting to pray at that."
"26159","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Rabah narrated to us from Ma'mar from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Aisha: She said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when taken, leaned his back upon me. She said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr entered with a siwak in his hand, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked for it, and I took the siwak and sweetened it, then handed it to him, and he began cleaning his teeth with it, then his hand grew heavy, and he grew heavy upon me, saying: O Allah, in the Highest Company, O Allah, in the Highest Company, twice. She said: Then he was taken. Aisha says: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was taken while between my breast and throat."
"26160","Muhammad ibn Bakr and al-Ansari narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Urwa informed me that he heard Urwa and al-Qasim informing from Aisha, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with my hand with dharira in the Farewell Hajj, for exiting ihram and entering ihram. Al-Ansari said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Urwa."
"26161","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me that Urwa informed him that Aisha informed him, she said: I used to twist the necklaces of the sacrificial animal of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he sends with it and remains, avoiding nothing."
"26162","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Umayya informed me that Nafi', freedman of Ibn Umar, informed him that Aisha informed him: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Kill the gecko, for it blew upon Ibrahim, peace be upon him, the fire. He said: Aisha used to kill them."
"26163","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me from Urwa from Aisha, she said: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas and Abd ibn Zam'a disputed, then he mentioned the hadith, and said: He is yours, O Abd ibn Zam'a; the child is for the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"26164","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sa'd ibn Sa'id, brother of Yahya ibn Sa'id, informed me that Amra bint Abd al-Rahman informed him from Aisha: She heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Breaking the bone of the dead, dead, is like breaking it alive."
"26165","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me from Abu Salama from Aisha: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he wanted to sleep while junub, performed his wudu for prayer."
"26166","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata' informed me from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, he informed him that Aisha informed him, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray while I lay across upon the bed between him and the qibla. I said: Between them are the walls of the mosque? She said: No, in the house, toward its walls."
"26167","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us from Ibn Tawus from his father: He used to say after the tashahhud in the last Isha words he magnified greatly, saying: I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of Jahannam, and I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the False Messiah, and I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in Allah from the trial of life and death. He said: He magnified them and mentioned them from Aisha from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"26168","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Mulayka informed me that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad informed him that Aisha informed him: Sahla bint Suhayl ibn Amr came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim, Salim freedman of Abu Hudhayfa, is with us in our house, and he has reached what men reach. Abd al-Razzaq said: And he knew what men know. He said: Suckle him, you become unlawful to him. He said: I remained a year or near it not narrating it in fear, then I met al-Qasim and said: He narrated to me a hadith I have not narrated after. He said: What is it? So I informed him. He said: So he narrated it from me that Aisha informed me of it."
"26169","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed us: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me from Aisha: Abu Hudhayfa adopted Salim, he a freedman of a woman of the Ansar, as the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, adopted Zayd. Whoever adopted a man in Jahiliyya, people called him his son and he inherited from his inheritance, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: Call them by their fathers, it is more just with Allah; if you know not their fathers, then your brothers in religion and your freedmen. So they were returned to their fathers; whoever had no known father, then a freedman and brother in religion. Sahla came and said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to see Salim as a child dwelling with me and Abu Hudhayfa, seeing me in light dress, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has sent down concerning them what You know. He said: Suckle him five sucklings, so he was in the station of his child through suckling."
"26170","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Ata', he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me, and Rawh: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ata' informed me from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr that Aisha informed him, she said: My foster uncle, Abu al-Ja'd, sought permission upon me. Rawh said: Abu al-Ju'ayd. Abd al-Razzaq said, meaning Ibn Jurayj: Hisham ibn Urwa said to him, so I refused him. Hisham said to me: He is only Abu al-Qu'ays. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, I informed him of that. He said: Why did you not permit him, may your right hand be dusted."
"26171","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata' claimed that Aisha said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not die until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made lawful for him to marry what he wished. I said: From whom do you report this? He said: I do not know; I thought I heard Ubayd ibn Umayr saying that."
"26172","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqama from Aisha: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would kiss while fasting and embrace while fasting, and he was the most master of you of his desire."
"26173","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from Umara from an aunt of his from Aisha from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Your children are of the purest of your earning, so eat from the earning of your children."
"26174","Hammad ibn Usama narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah informed us from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayra from Aisha, she said: I missed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night from the bed, so I sought him, and my hand fell upon the soles of his feet while he was in the mosque, both erected, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; I cannot count praise upon You; You are as You praised Yourself."
"26175","Hammad ibn Usama narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us from his father from Aisha: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered in the year of the Conquest from Kada', and entered in an umra from Kuda."
"26176","Hammad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from his father from Aisha, she said: Revelation would descend upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a cold morning, and his forehead would pour sweat. Upon him be prayer and peace."
"26177","Hammad ibn Usama narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us from his father from Aisha, she said: I never envied a woman as I envied Khadija, and she died three years before he married me, for what I heard him mention her. His Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded him to give her glad tidings of a house of reed in Paradise, and he would slaughter the sheep then gift of it among her friends."
"26178","Hammad ibn Usama narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us from his father from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Duba'a bint al-Zubayr and said to her: Did you intend hajj? She said: By Allah, I find myself only ill. He said to her: Perform hajj and stipulate. He said: Say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is where You detain me. She was under al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad."
"26179","Hammad ibn Usama narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us from his father from Aisha, she said: I used to enter my house in which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and my father were buried, and I put off my garment, saying: He is only my husband and my father. When Umar was buried with them, by Allah, I never entered but with my clothes drawn tight upon me, from shyness of Umar."
"26180","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Waki' from Hisham, the meaning, he said: My father informed me from Aisha from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When one of you dozes while praying, let him sleep until sleep leaves him, for when he prays while drowsy, perhaps he goes to seek forgiveness and reviles himself."
"26181","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, he said: Aisha informed me: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned Safiyya. They said: She has menstruated. He said: Is she detaining us? They said: She has performed Ifada. He said: Then no."
"26182","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, he said: My father informed me from Aisha, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in his illness in which he died: Command Abu Bakr to pray with people. I said: Abu Bakr, when he stands in your place, will not make people hear from weeping. He said: Command Abu Bakr. I said to Hafsa: Say: Abu Bakr will not make people hear from weeping; would you command Umar? He said: O companions of Yusuf; command Abu Bakr to pray with people. Hafsa turned to me and said: I never gained good from you."
"26183","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'ba from Ash'ath from his father from Masruq from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, loved beginning with the right in his purification and his shoe and in his combing."
"26184","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us from Urwa, he said: My father informed me from Aisha, she said: Hamza ibn Amr al-Aslami came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I used to fast, meaning continuously, shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"26185","Yahya narrated to us from Isma'il, he said: Amir informed me from Masruq, he said: I asked Aisha about the choice, and she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave us choice; was it divorce?"
"26186","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, meaning al-Dastuwai, he said: Yahya narrated to us from Abu Salama, he said: I asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sleep while junub? She said: Yes, but he performed wudu like the wudu of prayer."
"26187","Yahya and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us from al-Hakam from Umara, Ibn Ja'far said: Ibn Umayr, from his mother from Aisha from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The child of a man is from his earning, of the purest of his earning, so eat of their wealth pleasantly."
"26188","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sufyan and Shu'ba narrated to us from Mansur, and Sulayman and Hammad from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade dubba' and muzaffat. Only Shu'ba said in the hadith of Mansur: So I said: The jar or the hantam? He said: I will not add for you beyond what I heard."
"26189","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, he said: My father narrated to me from Zaynab bint Abi Salama from Umm Salama: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You dispute to me, and perhaps some of you are more eloquent in his plea than others, and I only judge for him by what he says. Whomever I judge for him something of his brother's right by his saying, I only cut for him a piece of the Fire, so let him not take it."
"26190","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath narrated to me from his father from Masruq from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, liked the lasting of deeds. He said: I said: Which night did he stand? She said: When he heard the caller."
"26191","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulayka narrating from Dhakwan Abu Amr from Aisha from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Consult women in their private parts. He said: It was said: The virgin is shy and silent. He said: Her silence is her permission."
"26192","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me from his father that he heard Abu Hurayra saying: Whoever wakes junub, let him not fast. Abu Bakr and his father Abd al-Rahman set out until they entered upon Umm Salama and Aisha, and both said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would wake junub from other than a wet dream, then fast. Abu Bakr and his father Abd al-Rahman set out and came to Marwan and narrated to him. He said: I adjure you to go to Abu Hurayra and narrate to him. So they went to Abu Hurayra and informed him. He said: Did they both say it to you? They said: Yes. He said: They are more knowledgeable; only al-Fadl ibn Abbas informed me of it."
"26193","Yahya narrated to us from Abd al-Malik: Ata' narrated to us from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would be struck by janaba in the night while intending fasting, then bathe after dawn rises, then complete his fasting."
"26194","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Isma'il, he said: Amir narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman that he came to Aisha and said: Abu Hurayra gives us fatwa that whoever wakes junub has no fasting for him. What do you say concerning that? She said: I say nothing concerning that; the caller would call for prayer, and I would see water descending between his shoulders, then he would pray Fajr, then remain fasting."
"26195","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abi Mulayka from Aisha from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: No thorn befalls the believer, nor what is above it, meaning, except it is expiation for him."
"26196","Yahya narrated to us from Abu Hurra, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Hisham from Aisha: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he stood in the night, prayed two rak'as, shortening them."
"26197","Yahya and Ibn Ja'far narrated to us, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, Ibn Ja'far said: I heard Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Aisha from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Five the muhrim kills: the snake, the mouse, the pied crow, the kite, and the dog. Ibn Ja'far said: They are killed in the lawful and the sacred."
"26198","Hajjaj narrated to us with the like of the hadith of Ibn Ja'far exactly, he said: The vicious dog. And Ibn Ja'far said: The vicious."
"26199","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us from his father from Aisha, she said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was taken, he was shrouded in three white Yemeni garments of karsuf, meaning cotton. She said: In his shroud there was neither shirt nor turban."
"26200","Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Urwa from Aisha: Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman suffering istihada and do not become pure, shall I leave prayer? He said: No; avoid prayer the days of your menstruation, then bathe and perform wudu for every prayer, then pray, though blood drips upon the mat. Waki' said: Sit the days of your periods, then bathe."
"26201","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bring his head near to me while he was in seclusion, in i'tikaf, while I was in my room, so I would wash it and comb it while I was menstruating."
"26202","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Safiyyah, from his mother, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place his head in my lap while I was menstruating, and he would recite the Qur'an."
"26203","Waki' narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch me while I was menstruating; he was the most in control of you over his desire."
"26204","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr while the sun was still shining in my room."
"26205","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, he heard it from him, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night while I was beside him, menstruating, with a woolen cloak over me and part of it over him."
"26206","Waki' narrated to us: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I said to Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combine surahs in one rak'ah? She said: The Mufassal."
"26207","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Yazid, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray standing and sitting; when he began the prayer standing, he bowed standing, and when he began the prayer sitting, he bowed sitting."
"26208","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray sitting after he had grown old, until when thirty or forty verses of the surah remained for him, he would stand and recite them, then bow."
"26209","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of Ramadan."
"26210","Waki' narrated to us: Kahmas narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I said to Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha? She said: No, except when he came from a journey."
"26211","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lighten the two rak'ahs of Fajr."
"26212","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: Throughout the night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Witr, from its beginning, its middle, and its end, and his Witr ended at dawn; then he died while he prayed Witr at dawn."
"26213","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Abi Waththab, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: Throughout the night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Witr, from its beginning, its middle, and its end, and his Witr ended at dawn."
"26214","Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, and Sufyan from Abu Husayn, and he mentioned both of them together."
"26215","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night while I lay across between him and the qiblah, and when he wanted to pray Witr, he would wake me and I would pray Witr."
"26216","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Tamim, meaning Ibn Salamah, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: He woke me, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Get up and pray Witr."
"26217","Waki' narrated to us: Mis'ar and Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: I never met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the end of the night except that he was sleeping with me."
"26218","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you becomes drowsy in his prayer, let him sleep, for perhaps he intends to seek forgiveness but ends up cursing himself."
"26219","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan and Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Ghalib, he said: Ammar came, with al-Ashtar with him, seeking permission to see Aishah. He said: O mother. She said: I am not a mother to you. He said: Yes, even if you dislike it. She said: Who is this with you? He said: This is al-Ashtar. She said: Are you the one who wanted to kill my nephew? He said: I wanted to kill him, and he wanted to kill me. She said: Had you killed him, you would never have prospered; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except for one of three: a man who killed and so is killed, or a man who committed adultery after being married, or a man who apostatized after his Islam."
"26220","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: I used to hear that no prophet dies except that he is given the choice between this world and the Hereafter. She said: He developed hoarseness in his illness in which he died, and I heard him say: With those upon whom Allah has bestowed favor, of the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, and excellent are those as companions, so I thought that he had been given the choice."
"26221","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Witr with five rak'ahs, sitting only in the last of them."
"26222","Waki' narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice, so we chose him; was that a divorce?"
"26223","Waki' narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most hated of men to Allah, mighty and majestic, is the fiercely quarrelsome."
"26224","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id ibn Wahb al-Hamdani, from Aishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, those who give what they give while their hearts are fearful - is it the man who commits adultery and steals and drinks wine? He said: No, O daughter of Abu Bakr, or: No, O daughter of al-Siddiq, but it is the man who fasts and prays and gives charity while fearing that it will not be accepted from him."
"26225","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: A Jewish woman came to me and mentioned the torment of the grave, so I denied it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and I asked him, and he said: She spoke the truth; by the One in whose Hand is my soul, they are tormented in their graves until the animals hear their voices."
"26226","He said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Ward narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is reckoned will perish. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, does not Allah, mighty and majestic, say: He will be reckoned an easy reckoning? He said: O Aishah, that is the presentation; whoever has his reckoning debated will perish."
"26227","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Hudhayfah, from Aishah, that she mentioned a woman, and once she mimicked a woman, and said: She is short. So he said: You have backbitten her. I would not like to mimic anyone even if I had such and such."
"26228","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Isra'il and Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gentleness was never in anything except that it adorned it, nor was it removed from anything except that it disgraced it."
"26229","Waki' and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: I said to Aishah: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when he entered his house? She said: He would be in the service of his family, and when the prayer came, he would go out and pray."
"26230","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from his uncle al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and looked at the moon and said: O Aishah, seek refuge with Allah from the evil of the darkening night when it settles; this is the darkening night when it settles."
"26231","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed. Abd al-Rahman said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing. And Waki' said: She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed Uthman ibn Maz'un while he was dead. She said: I saw his tears flowing on his cheeks, meaning Uthman's. Abd al-Rahman said: And his eyes pouring forth, or he said: While he was weeping."
"26232","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Hind came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a miserly man, and he does not give me and my child what suffices me except what I take from his wealth without his knowledge. He said: Take what suffices you and your child in a reasonable manner."
"26233","Waki' narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch me while I was menstruating, and he was the most in control of you over his desire."
"26234","Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never struck a servant nor a woman, nor did he strike anything with his hand, except when striving in the cause of Allah."
"26235","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abdullah ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me in Shawwal and consummated the marriage with me in Shawwal, so which of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more favored with him than me? And Aishah used to like to marry off her women in Shawwal."
"26236","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any condition that is not in the Book of Allah is void, even if it is a hundred conditions."
"26237","Waki' narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from his mother Musaykah, from Aishah: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not build for you a house at Mina to shade you? He said: No; Mina is the resting place of whoever arrives first."
"26238","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Aishah and Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited the House at night."
"26239","Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Staying at al-Muhassab is not a Sunnah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only stayed there so that his departure would be easier."
"26240","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, and Aflah from al-Qasim, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about Safiyyah and said: Is she going to detain us? They said: O Messenger of Allah, she has already performed the Ifadah. He said: Then no, she may leave."
"26241","Waki' narrated to us: Aflah narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entering ihram for Hajj."
"26242","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: It is as if I am looking at the glistening of perfume in the partings of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was chanting the Talbiyah."
"26243","Waki' narrated to us: Aflah narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two hands of mine at ihram."
"26244","Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the best I could find."
"26245","Waki' narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim narrated to us, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity for her, meaning Barirah, and a gift for us."
"26246","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the Fire and the trial of the Fire, and the trial of the grave and the torment of the grave, and the evil of the trial of wealth and the evil of the trial of poverty, and the evil of the trial of the False Messiah. O Allah, wash away my sins with snow and hail water, and purify my heart of sins as the white garment is purified of filth, and distance me from my sins as You have distanced the east from the west. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, debt, and sin."
"26247","Waki' narrated to us: Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, from Shurayh ibn Hani', from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him; and death is before meeting Allah."
"26248","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The sleeping mat of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of leather stuffed with palm fiber."
"26249","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Hamzah al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling, and he was a man who fasted continuously, so he said: You have the choice; if you wish, fast, and if you wish, break the fast."
"26250","Waki' narrated to us: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his aunt Aishah bint Talhah, and Ibn Numayr from Talhah, he said: Aishah bint Talhah informed me with the same meaning, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me one day and said: Do you have anything? We said: No. He said: Then I am fasting. Then he came another day, and Ibn Numayr said after that: So we said: O Messenger of Allah, hays was gifted to us and we kept some for you. He said: Bring it, for I had begun the morning fasting, and he ate."
"26251","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed one of his wives while fasting, then she laughed."
"26252","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham, the companion of al-Dastuwai, narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from a woman called Umm Kulthum, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats food, let him say: In the name of Allah; if he forgets at its beginning, let him say: In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end."
"26253","Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a decorated woolen garment, and its markings would appear before him in prayer, so he gave it to Abu Jahm and took a woolen cloak of his without markings."
"26254","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she used to comb the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was menstruating."
"26255","Waki' narrated to us: Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would garland them, then send them."
"26256","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once sent garlanded sheep as sacrifice."
"26257","Waki' narrated to us: Ali ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."
"26258","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ruqyah for every poisonous bite."
"26259","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Wipe away the affliction, Lord of mankind; in Your hand is healing; none removes it but You."
"26260","Waki' narrated to us: Kahmas narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Aishah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I coincide with Laylat al-Qadr, with what should I supplicate? He said: You say: O Allah, You are Pardoning and love pardon, so pardon me."
"26261","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me, from his aunt Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was invited to the funeral of a boy of the Ansar, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, glad tidings to him, a sparrow of the sparrows of Paradise, who never knew evil nor did it. He said: Or other than that, O Aishah; Allah, mighty and majestic, created people for Paradise, He created it for them while they were in the loins of their fathers, and He created people for the Fire, He created it for them while they were in the loins of their fathers."
"26262","Waki' narrated to us, from Abu Aqil Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil, from Buhayyah, from Aishah, that she mentioned the children of the polytheists to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: If you wish, I will let you hear their wailing in the Fire."
"26263","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from a journey, and I had hung on my door a curtain with winged horses on it. She said: So he tore it down."
"26264","Waki' narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Makhlad ibn Khufaf ibn Ima' ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that the yield of the slave belongs to him by virtue of his guarantee. Ibn Abi Dhi'b said: And they had disputed over a slave a man bought and found a defect in, after having profited from him, so Urwah said, from Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that the yield of the slave belongs to him by virtue of his guarantee."
"26265","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya and Yazid narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her - Yazid said: She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Gabriel sends you greetings of peace. So she said: And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah."
"26266","Waki' narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Imran al-Hajabi narrated to me, he heard it from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My name is permitted but my kunyah is forbidden, or: My kunyah is forbidden but my name is permitted."
"26267","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: My soul has become wicked, but let him say: My soul has become heavy. Waki' said: Nausea."
"26268","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Dhakwan, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the khumrah."
"26269","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command me to wrap my lower garment while I was menstruating, then he would touch me."
"26270","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate their fill of wheat food for more than three days. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade sacrificial meats beyond three days because the people were in hardship, then he permitted them."
"26271","Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, and Aswad said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at ihram with the best I could find. Aswad said: Until I could see the glistening of the perfume on his head and beard."
"26272","Waki' narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The snake is harmful, the scorpion is harmful, the crow is harmful, and the mouse is harmful."
"26273","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The hadith of Ibn Umar, that the dead is tormented by the weeping of the living, was mentioned to her. She said: Abu Abd al-Rahman erred, just as he erred on the day of the well of Badr; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: He is being tormented while his family weep over him, meaning the disbeliever."
"26274","Waki' narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, that Barirah was under a contract of manumission, and her husband was a slave, so when she was freed, she was given the choice."
"26275","Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given the choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them, so long as there was no sin in it."
"26276","Waki' narrated to us, from Nafi', meaning Ibn Umar, from Salih ibn Sa'id, from Aishah, that she missed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his bed, so she touched him with her hand and found him while he was prostrating, saying: My Lord, grant my soul its piety, purify it, You are the best to purify it, You are its Protector and Master."
"26277","Waki' narrated to us, from Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: The family of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a wild animal, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, it would become excited and play in the house, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, it would be still and not move, lest it harm him."
"26278","Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform the supererogatory Duha prayer, yet I perform it."
"26279","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mubarak narrated to me, from Karimah bint Hammam, she said: I heard Aishah say: O assembly of women, beware of peeling the face. A woman asked her about dye, so she said: There is no harm in dye, but I dislike it because my beloved (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked its smell."
"26280","Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill with the illness in which he died, Bilal came to announce the prayer to him, so he said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. We said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man. Al-A'mash said: Gentle. And whenever he stands in your place, he weeps and cannot do it; if only you commanded Umar. He said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. We said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, and whenever he stands in your place, he weeps and cannot do it; if only you commanded Umar to lead the people in prayer. He said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, for you are the companions of Yusuf. So we sent to my father and he led the people in prayer, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt some relief, so he came out supported between two men, his feet dragging on the ground. When Abu Bakr sensed him, he went to step back, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him: Stay in your place. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he sat beside Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr followed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people followed Abu Bakr."
"26281","Waki' narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his seat three times."
"26282","Waki' narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha', from his father, from Masruq, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved beginning with the right in ablution, combing, and putting on shoes. And Waki' once said: Putting on shoes."
"26283","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel while we were both in major impurity."
"26284","Waki' narrated to us: Mis'ar and Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I would drink while menstruating, then hand it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would place his mouth on the place of my mouth. And I would gnaw meat from the bone while menstruating, then hand it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would place his mouth on the place of my mouth."
"26285","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed one of his wives, then went out to prayer without performing ablution. Urwah said: I said to her: Who is she but you? She said: So she laughed."
"26286","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Rawq al-Hamdani, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed, then prayed without performing ablution."
"26287","Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: A boy was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he urinated on him, so he poured water over it and did not wash it."
"26288","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah and Yahya narrated to us, they said: When Khadijah died, Khawlah bint Hakim, the wife of Uthman ibn Maz'un, came and said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry? He said: Whom? She said: If you wish, a virgin, and if you wish, a previously married woman. He said: Who is the virgin? She said: The daughter of the most beloved of Allah's creation, mighty and majestic, to you, Aishah bint Abi Bakr. He said: And who is the previously married woman? She said: Sawdah bint Zam'ah; she has believed in you and followed you in what you say. He said: Go and propose them for me. So she entered the house of Abu Bakr and said: O Umm Ruman, what good and blessing has Allah, mighty and majestic, brought upon you? She said: What is that? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to propose Aishah for him. She said: Wait for Abu Bakr until he comes. So Abu Bakr came, and she said: O Abu Bakr, what good and blessing has Allah brought upon you? He said: What is that? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to propose Aishah for him. He said: Is she suitable for him? She is the daughter of his brother. So she returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Return to him and say to him: I am your brother, and you are my brother in Islam, and your daughter is suitable for me. So she returned and mentioned that to him. He said: Wait, and he went out. Umm Ruman said: Mut'im ibn Adi had mentioned her for his son, and by Allah, he never made a promise and broke it to Abu Bakr. So Abu Bakr entered upon Mut'im ibn Adi, and with him was his wife, the mother of the boy, and she said: O son of Abu Quhafah, perhaps you will convert our companion and bring him into your religion which you follow, if he marries you. Abu Bakr said to Mut'im ibn Adi: Is this what she says? He said: She says that. So he left him, and Allah, mighty and majestic, removed what was in his heart about his promise which he had promised. So he returned and said to Khawlah: Call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me. So she called him, and he married her to him, while Aishah was then six years old. Then she went out and entered upon Sawdah bint Zam'ah and said: What good and blessing has Allah, mighty and majestic, brought upon you? She said: What is that? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to propose you for him. She said: I wish it; go to my father and mention that to him. He was a very old man, overtaken by age, who had stayed behind from Hajj. So she entered upon him and greeted him with the greeting of the Jahiliyyah. He said: Who is this? She said: Khawlah bint Hakim. He said: What is your matter? She said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah sent me to propose Sawdah for him. He said: A worthy, noble match; what does your companion say? She said: She desires that. He said: Call her to me. So she was called. He said: O my daughter, this woman claims that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib has sent to propose to you, and he is a worthy, noble match; do you love that I marry you to him? She said: Yes. He said: Call him for me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him, and he married her to him. Then her brother Abd ibn Zam'ah came from Hajj and began pouring dust on his head. He said after he became Muslim: By my life, I was foolish on the day I poured dust on my head because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sawdah bint Zam'ah. Aishah said: We came to Madinah and stayed with Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj in al-Sunh. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and entered our house, and men and women of the Ansar gathered to him. Then my mother came to me while I was on a swing between two palm stumps, swinging, so she took me down from the swing, and I had a small lock of hair, so she parted it and wiped my face with some water. Then she led me until she stopped me at the door, while I was panting, until I calmed down. Then she brought me in, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting on a bed in our house, with men and women of the Ansar with him. So she seated me in his lap, then said: These are your family, may Allah bless you in them and bless them in you. So the men and women jumped up and went out. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consummated the marriage with me in our house, with no camel slaughtered for me nor sheep slaughtered for me, until Sa'd ibn Ubadah sent us a bowl which he used to send to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he stayed with his wives. And I was then nine years old."
"26289","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Aishah, she said: When the verse of choice was revealed, he began with Aishah and said: O Aishah, I am presenting a matter to you, so do not decide anything about it until you present it to your parents, Abu Bakr and Umm Ruman. She said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it? He said: O Aishah, I am presenting a matter to you, so do not decide anything about it until you present it to your parents, Abu Bakr and Umm Ruman. She said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it? He said: O Aishah, I am presenting a matter to you, so do not decide anything about it until you present it to your parents, Abu Bakr and Umm Ruman. She said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it? He said: Allah said: O Prophet, say to your wives: If you desire the life of this world and its adornment, then come, I will provide for you and release you a gracious release. And if you desire Allah and His Messenger and the Home of the Hereafter, then Allah has prepared for the doers of good among you a great reward. She said: I desire Allah and His Messenger and the Home of the Hereafter, and I will not consult my parents about that, Abu Bakr and Umm Ruman. She said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, then he went around the rooms and said: Aishah said such and such. He said: So they said the same as what Aishah said."
"26290","Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Boys used to be brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would rub their palates and invoke blessing upon them. Then a boy urinated in his lap, so he called for water and poured water over the urine."
"26291","Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, and with me was a woman of Banu Asad ibn Khuzaymah. He said: Who is this? I said: This is so-and-so, and she stands the night in prayer, or does not sleep at night. He said: So he disliked that until I saw dislike on his face, and he said: Upon you is of deeds what you can bear, for Allah, mighty and majestic, does not tire until you tire."
"26292","Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The sleeping mat of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on which he and his family slept was of leather stuffed with palm fiber."
"26293","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Aban al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Urwah, that Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan wrote to him asking him about things, so Urwah wrote to him: Peace be upon you, and I praise to you Allah, besides whom there is no god. To proceed: You wrote to me asking me about things, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Aishah informed me that while they were at midday in their house, with none with Abu Bakr except his two daughters Aishah and Asma', the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them when the midday heat stood, and he never missed a day coming to the house of Abu Bakr at the beginning of the day and its end. When Abu Bakr saw him coming at midday, he said: Nothing has brought you, O Prophet of Allah, except some new matter. When he entered upon them in the house, he said to Abu Bakr: Send away those with you. He said: There is no watcher over you; they are only my two daughters. He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has permitted me to leave for Madinah. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, companionship. He said: Companionship. Abu Bakr said: Take one of the two mounts, and they were the two mounts Abu Bakr had been feeding, preparing them for leaving when permission was given to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Abu Bakr gave him one of the two mounts and said: Take it, O Messenger of Allah, and ride it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have taken it for a price."
"26294","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, and Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Aishah, she said: It is as if I am looking at the glistening of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after days while he was in ihram."
"26295","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, and Hisham ibn Urwah from his father, from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would send them and remain among us in a state of permissibility."
"26296","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, and Hisham ibn Urwah from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to depart, so it was said to him: Safiyyah bint Huyayy has menstruated. He said: She will surely detain us. They said: She performed the circumambulation of the House on the day of sacrifice. He said: Then let her depart."
"26297","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I used to rub semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would pray in it."
"26298","Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know you when you are angry and when you are pleased; when you are angry, you say: No, by the Lord of Ibrahim, and when you are pleased, you say: No, by the Lord of Muhammad."
"26299","Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from a man of the descendants of al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, all your women have a kunyah except me. He said: You are Umm Abdullah."
"26300","Waki' narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray thirteen rak'ahs at night."
"26301","Waki' narrated to us from Zakariyya from al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh from al-Sha'bi from Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not refrain from anything of my face while he was fasting."
"26302","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Salih al-Asadi from al-Sha'bi from Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. Abdullah said: Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath meaning Ibn Qays."
"26303","Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us from Abda ibn Abi Lubaba from Hilal, meaning Ibn Yasaf, from Farwah ibn Nawfal from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done and from the evil of what I have not done."
"26304","Waki' narrated to us from Harun from Budayl from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Fa-rawh and rayhan (So rest and bounty)."
"26305","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us from his father from Aishah that Barirah came to her while she was a mukatabah (a slave contracted for freedom); her people had contracted her for nine awaq (ounces of silver). So she said to her: If your people wish, I shall count it for them in one count, and the wala' (right of allegiance/inheritance) shall be for me. So she came to her people and mentioned that to them, and they refused except to stipulate the wala' for themselves. So Aishah mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: Do it. So she did it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and addressed the people; he praised Allah and extolled Him. He said: What is the matter with men who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah. He said: Every condition that is not in the Book of Allah is void; the Book of Allah is more deserving and His condition is more binding; and the wala' is for whoever frees."
"26306","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, the meaning, from Sufyan from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh from his father from Aishah, she said: Whoever narrates to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated standing after the Furqan (the Criterion, the Qur'an) was revealed to him, do not believe him; he did not urinate standing since the Furqan was revealed to him. Abd al-Rahman said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not urinate standing since the Furqan was revealed to him."
"26307","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to me, and Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah that Sawdah was a slow heavy woman; she asked permission from the Prophet to depart before his departure from Jam' (Muzdalifah), so he permitted her. Aishah said: I wished I had asked his permission."
"26308","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim said from his father from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from a journey, and I had screened with a namat (a figured curtain) in which there were images. She said: So he removed it. She said: And I took from it two cushions."
"26309","And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim said from his father from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah with these two hands of mine at his ihram (entering pilgrim sanctity) and when he stoned (the Jamarah) before he visited (the House)."
"26310","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan from Ash'ath from his father from Masruq from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Aishah while a man was with her. He said: So he said: Who is this? She said: My brother through suckling. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look at whom you suckle, for suckling is only from hunger (i.e. in infancy). Abd al-Rahman said: Look at who are your brothers; suckling is only from hunger."
"26311","Waki' narrated to us from Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Aswad, he said: I said to Aishah: Inform me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sleep the first of it and stand the last of it; when he stood he performed ablution and prayed what Allah Almighty had decreed for him. If he had a need for his wife he came to his wife, otherwise he inclined to his bed. If he had come to his wife he slept as he was, not touching water, until when it was at the first adhan he sprang up; by Allah she did not say: he stood. And if he was junub he poured water over himself; by Allah she did not say: he washed, nor did he perform his ablution for prayer. Then he prayed two rak'ahs then went out to the mosque."
"26312","Waki' and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan, the meaning, from al-Miqdam from his father from Aishah, she said: I would be menstruating, then I would take the bone with meat and gnaw it while menstruating, then hand it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would place his mouth upon the place of mine; and I would drink while menstruating, then hand it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would place his mouth upon the place of mine."
"26313","Ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh ibn Hani' from his father, he said: Aishah said: I would gnaw the bone while menstruating, and he mentioned the like of it."
"26314","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Amr ibn Ghalib from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except for a man who killed and so is killed, or a man who committed adultery after being married, or a man who apostatized after his Islam."
"26315","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Aishah that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died he was shrouded in three Yemeni white cotton garments, in which there was neither a shirt nor a turban."
"26316","He said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq and al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh from al-Bahiyy. Sharik said: al-Abbas said: from Aishah, and Abu Ishaq said: from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aishah: Hand me the khumrah (small prayer mat). So she said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand."
"26317","Waki' narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his illness in which he died: I wish some of my companions were with me. We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not call Abu Bakr for you? So he fell silent. We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not call Umar for you? So he fell silent. We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not call Ali for you? So he fell silent. We said: Shall we not call Uthman for you? He said: Yes. He said: So we sent to Uthman and he came, and he was alone with him and kept speaking to him while the face of Uthman kept changing."
"26318","Waki' narrated to us from Ali ibn Salih from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Ibrahim from Aishah, she said: My necklace was stolen, so I supplicated against its owner. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lighten (his load by your imprecation) upon him; leave him with his sin."
"26319","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Aishah and Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Tawaf on the Day of Sacrifice until the night."
"26320","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from Ali ibn Husayn from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"26321","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur ibn Safiyyah from his mother from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while we had eaten our fill of the two black ones: water and dates."
"26322","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman and al-Mundhir ibn Abi al-Mundhir from Abu Salamah from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the moon and said: O Aishah, seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this, for this is the darkener when it sets."
"26323","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, and he said: Ali, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah from Umm Bakr that she informed him from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the woman who sees what makes her doubt after purity: He said: It is only a vein, or he said: veins."
"26324","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, and he said: Ali narrated to us from Yahya, he said: Abu Qilabah narrated to me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah, the keeper of the House, informed him that Aishah informed him that a pain visited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he kept complaining and tossing upon his bed. So Aishah said to him: Had one of us done this you would have held it against him. So he said: It is intensified upon the believers; there is no believer whom a mishap befalls, a thorn or a pain, except Allah Almighty raises for him thereby a degree and removes thereby from him a sin, or like what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"26325","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah would pray, between his finishing the Isha prayer, which is what you call or name al-Atamah, until Fajr, eleven prostrations (rak'ahs); he would salute between every two, and perform witr with one; and he would prostrate in his voluntary prayer as long as one of you recites fifty verses before he raises his head. When the mu'adhdhin fell silent at the first (call) of the dawn prayer, he would bow two light rak'ahs, then lie down upon his right side; then the mu'adhdhin would come to him and he would go out with him."
"26326","Abd al-Malik ibn Umar narrated to us, and he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not perform the voluntary Duha prayer, yet I perform it."
"26327","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, and he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer one night. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, the women and children have slept. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and said: None among the people waits for this prayer except you. He said: And that was before Islam spread among the people."
"26328","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Urwah from Aishah; she informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed one night, and he mentioned its meaning."
"26329","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Hakim ibn Jubayr from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: I have not seen anyone hasten the Zuhr more than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"26330","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed from Diqrah, Umm Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhaynah, she said: We used to circumambulate with Aishah around the House, then one of her family came to her and said: You have sweated, so change your clothes. So she put down a garment that was upon her, and I offered her a cloak of mine with a cross embroidered. So she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it in a garment he removed it. She said: So she did not wear it."
"26331","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us from Ikrimah ibn Khalid from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, he said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about this hadith. He said: It reached Marwan that Abu Hurayrah narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that whoever is overtaken by dawn while junub, let him not fast that day. So he sent to Aishah asking her about that, and he (Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman) went with him and asked her. So she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub not from a wet dream, then he would fast. So he returned to Marwan and narrated to him. So he said: Meet Abu Hurayrah and narrate to him. So he said: He is my neighbor, and I dislike to confront him with what he dislikes. So he said: I adjure you to meet him. He said: So he met him and said: O Abu Hurayrah, by Allah I disliked to confront you with what you dislike, but the commander adjured me. He said: So he narrated to him. So he said: al-Fadl narrated it to me."
"26332","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suck nor two sucks prohibit (marriage)."
"26333","Isma'il narrated to us from Yunus from al-Hasan, he said: Aishah was asked about the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she said: His character was the Qur'an."
"26334","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from Abu Salamah, he said: I said to Aishah: O mother, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleep while junub? She said: Yes; he would not sleep until he washed his private part and performed his ablution for prayer."
"26335","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn informed us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad and Masruq, he said: We came to Aishah to ask her about touching (one's wife) for one fasting, but we were shy, so we stood before asking her. Then we walked I know not how long, then we said: We came to ask her about a need then return before asking her. So we returned and said: O Mother of the Believers, we came to ask you about something but were shy, so we stood. So she said: What is it? Ask whatever occurs to you. We said: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch (his wife) while fasting? She said: He used to do that, but he was the most controlling of his desire among you."
"26336","Isma'il narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us from al-Hasan, he said: A man said: I said to Aishah: What sufficed the washing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from major impurity? He said: So she called for a vessel, estimating it a sa' by this sa' of yours."
"26337","Isma'il narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Qasim saying: Aishah said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his entering halal (leaving ihram) and for his ihram."
"26338","Isma'il narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrating from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send the sacrificial animals, then I would twist their garlands with my hands, then he would not refrain from anything that one in halal (not in ihram) does not refrain from."
"26339","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I asked Aishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He would pray four before Zuhr and two after it, and two before Asr, and two after Maghrib, and two after Isha, then he would pray nine at night. I said: Standing or sitting? She said: He would pray a long night standing and a long night sitting. I said: How would he do when standing, and how would he do when sitting? She said: When he recited standing he bowed standing, and when he recited sitting he bowed sitting; and two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer."
"26340","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us from al-Sha'bi, he said: Aishah said to Ibn Abi al-Sa'ib, the storyteller of the people of Madinah: Three things: you shall surely pledge to me upon them or I shall contend with you. So he said: What are they? Rather I shall pledge to you, O Mother of the Believers. She said: Avoid rhymed prose in supplication, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions would not do that. And Isma'il once said: So she said: I knew the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions, and they would not do that. And narrate to the people every Friday once; if you refuse, then twice; if you refuse, then thrice. So do not bore the people of this Book; and let me not find you coming to a people while they are in some talk of theirs and cutting their talk upon them; but leave them, and if they press you upon it and command you with it, then narrate to them."
"26341","Isma'il narrated to us from Khalid, he said: A man narrated to me from Abu al-Aliyah from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in the prostration of the Qur'an at night, saying it in the prostration repeatedly: My face has prostrated to the One who created it and split its hearing and its sight by His power and His strength."
"26342","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Burd ibn Sinan narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Musa from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray in the garment in which he has intercourse."
"26343","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: I said to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad: The wife of my father suckled a girl from among the common people with the milk of my two brothers; do you see that I may marry her? So he said: No; your father is her father. He said: Then he narrated the hadith of Abu al-Qu'ays. So he said: Abu al-Qu'ays came to Aishah asking permission upon her, but she did not permit him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, she said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Qu'ays came asking permission upon me but I did not permit him. So he said: He is your uncle, so let him enter upon you. So I said: Only the woman suckled me, and the man did not suckle me. So he said: He is your uncle, so let him enter upon you."
"26344","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed us from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Aishah said: The standing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer was as long as one recites the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah)."
"26345","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: Aishah said: The family of Abu Bakr sent to us a leg of a sheep at night; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held and I cut, or I held and he cut. So the one to whom she narrates said: Upon other than a lamp? So she said: Had we a lamp we would have used it as condiment; a month would come upon the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which they would bake no bread nor cook a pot."
"26346","Isma'il narrated to us from al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Amrah from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite while sitting; when he intended to bow he would stand as long as a man recites forty verses."
"26347","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us from Nafi' that a woman entered upon Aishah, and there was a spear set up. So she said: What is this spear? So she said: We kill with it the geckos. Then she narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when Ibrahim was cast into the fire, all the beasts kept extinguishing from him except the gecko, for it kept blowing it upon him."
"26348","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us from al-Sha'bi, he said: Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me: when the earth is changed to other than the earth, and the heavens, and they emerge before Allah the One the Irresistible, where will the people be that day? He said: The people that day will be upon the Path (al-Sirat)."
"26349","Isma'il and Yazid narrated to us, the meaning, they said: al-Jurayri informed us from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I said to Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite the surahs? She said: Al-Mufassal (the short surahs from Qaf onward)."
"26350","I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray sitting? She said: Yes, after the people had broken him (aged him)."
"26351","I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha? She said: No, except that he come from his absence (a journey)."
"26352","I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast a month other than Ramadan? She said: No, by Allah; he did not fast a complete month other than Ramadan, nor did he leave it all without fasting something from it."
"26353","I said: Which of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was most beloved to him? She said: Abu Bakr. I said: Then who? She said: Then Umar. I said: Then who? She said: Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. Yazid said: I said: Then who? He said: So she fell silent."
"26354","Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, he said: They mentioned before Abu Qilabah the going out of women for the Eid. He said: Aishah said: The young virgin girls would come out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from her chamber."
"26355","Isma'il narrated to us from Yunus from al-Hasan from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the meeting of Allah, Allah loves his meeting; and whoever dislikes the meeting of Allah Almighty, Allah dislikes his meeting. So Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, is dislike of the meeting of Allah the dislike of death? For by Allah we dislike it. So he said: No, it is not that; but when Allah Almighty decrees the seizure (death) of the believer, He reveals to him what is before him of the reward of Allah Almighty and His honor, so he dies when he dies loving the meeting of Allah Almighty, and Allah loves his meeting. And when Allah Almighty decrees the seizure of the disbeliever and the hypocrite, He reveals to him what is before him of the punishment of Allah Almighty and His disgrace, so he dies when he dies hating the meeting of Allah, and Allah hates his meeting."
"26356","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would not leave off any need of his for his wife until the pilgrims returned."
"26357","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah and Yunus narrated to us. He said: Hammad narrated to us from Qatadah from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Safiyyah bint al-Harith from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of a menstruating woman (i.e. one who has reached puberty) is not accepted except with a khimar (head covering)."
"26358","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Safiyyah bint al-Harith from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept the prayer of a menstruating woman (one who has reached puberty) except with a khimar."
"26359","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Umayyah that she asked Aishah about this verse: Whether you reveal what is in yourselves or conceal it, Allah will reckon you for it, and about this verse: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it. So she said: No one has asked me about them since I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them. So he said: O Aishah, this is Allah's pursuing the servant for what befalls him of fever, mishap, and thorn, even the goods he places in his sleeve then misses then panics for it then finds it in his bosom, until the believer emerges from his sins as red gold emerges from the bellows."
"26360","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us from Mu'adhah from Safiyyah from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash with a sa' and perform ablution with a mudd."
"26361","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us from Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt, he said: They mentioned before Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, facing the qiblah with the private parts. So Irak ibn Malik said: Aishah said: They mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that some people dislike that. He said: So he said: They have done it; turn my seat toward the qiblah."
"26362","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah, she said: We called out the talbiyah for Hajj until when we were at Sarif I menstruated. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was weeping. So he said: What makes you weep, O Aishah? I said: I have menstruated; would that I had not performed Hajj. He said: Glory be to Allah; that is only something Allah Almighty has decreed for the daughters of Adam. Perform all the rites except that you do not circumambulate the House. She said: When we entered Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to make it an Umrah, let him make it an Umrah, except whoever has the sacrificial animal with him. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered cows for his wives on the Day of Sacrifice. When it was the night of al-Batha' I became pure. So she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), will my companions return with a Hajj and an Umrah while I return with a Hajj only? So he commanded Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and he took me to al-Tan'im, and I called out the talbiyah for an Umrah."
"26363","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The severest of people in punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allah Almighty."
"26364","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us from Mutarrif from Aishah that she made for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a black woolen cloak, so he wore it; when he sweated and found the smell of wool, he cast it off. He said: And I think he said: And the pleasant scent used to please him."
"26365","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni informed me from Yazid ibn Babnus, he said: I and a companion of mine went to Aishah and asked permission upon her. So she cast a cushion for us and drew the veil toward her. So my companion said: O Mother of the Believers, what do you say about al-irak? She said: And what is al-irak? And I struck the shoulder of my companion, so she said: Hush, you have harmed your brother. Then she said: What is al-irak? Al-mahid (menstruation). Say what Allah said: al-mahid. Then she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wrap himself around me and take from my head, with a garment between me and him, while I was menstruating. Then she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by my door, from what he would utter of the word by which Allah Almighty benefits, he passed one day and said nothing, then he passed again and said nothing, two or three times. I said: O slave girl, place a cushion for me at the door, and I bound my head. So he passed by me and said: O Aishah, what is the matter with you? So I said: I complain of my head. So he said: Rather I, O my head. So he went and did not remain but a little until he was brought carried in a cloak. So he entered upon me and sent to the women and said: I have complained and I cannot go around among you, so permit me to be with Aishah. And I had not nursed anyone before him. While his head was one day upon my shoulder, his head inclined toward my head, and I thought he wanted something from my head. Then a cool drop (?) came out of his mouth and fell upon the hollow of my throat, so my skin shuddered from it, and I thought he had fainted, so I covered him with a garment. Then Umar and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah came and asked permission, so I permitted them and drew the veil toward me. So Umar looked at him and said: O faint, how severe is the faint of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then they stood, and when they drew near the door, al-Mughirah said: O Umar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died. He said: You have lied; rather you are a man whom tribulation confuses. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will not die until Allah Almighty annihilates the hypocrites. Then Abu Bakr came, so I lifted the veil, and he looked at him and said: Indeed to Allah we belong and indeed to Him we return; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died. Then he came to him from the side of his head, lowered his mouth and kissed his forehead, then said: O prophet. Then he raised his head, then lowered his mouth and kissed his forehead, then said: O chosen one. Then he raised his head and lowered his mouth and kissed his forehead and said: O beloved friend; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died. So he went out to the mosque while Umar was addressing the people and saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will not die until Allah Almighty annihilates the hypocrites. So Abu Bakr spoke; he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Allah Almighty says: Indeed you will die and indeed they will die, until he finished the verse, and: Muhammad is only a messenger; messengers have passed before him; if he dies or is killed will you turn upon your heels, until he finished the verse. So whoever worshipped Allah Almighty, Allah is Living; and whoever worshipped Muhammad, Muhammad has died. So Umar said: And is it indeed in the Book of Allah? I did not feel that it was in the Book of Allah. Then Umar said: O people, this is Abu Bakr, and he is the elder of the Muslims, so pledge allegiance to him. So they pledged allegiance to him."
"26366","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us from Kathir from Abu Iyad from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with a woolen cloak over him, part of it upon him and part of it upon her."
"26367","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that Aishah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed, he would buy two huge fat horned white-and-black castrated rams. He said: So he would slaughter one of them for his ummah, for whoever affirmed tawhid (the Oneness of Allah) and bore witness to him of conveyance (of the message), and he would slaughter the other for Muhammad and the family of Muhammad."
"26368","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Hakim ibn Jubayr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Aishah that she said: I have not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hasten to anything more than his hastening to the two rak'ahs before Fajr, nor to booty."
"26369","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us from Sharik from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The purest of what a man eats is from his earning, and his child is from his earning."
"26370","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us from Sharik from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from Umarah from his paternal aunt from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"26371","Ishaq narrated to us: Sharik informed us from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah from Amr ibn Maymun from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"26372","Ishaq narrated to us from Sharik from Isma'il al-Suddi from al-Bahiyy, the freedman of al-Zubayr, from Aishah that she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"26373","And he said: Aswad ibn Amir (narrated) from Amr ibn Maymun from Aishah. Aswad said: And he once said: al-Suddi or Ziyad ibn Ilaqah; and that is because his son Abd al-Rahman said to him in the house: They mention it from you from al-Suddi. So he said: al-Suddi or Ziyad."
"26374","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us from Sharik from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Mujahid from al-Sa'ib from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The prayer of one sitting is upon half of the prayer of one standing."
"26375","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Mujahid from al-Sa'ib from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is upon half of the prayer of one standing."
"26376","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us from Sharik from Ibrahim and Layth from Mujahid from al-Sa'ib from Aishah, she raised it (to the Prophet). She said: He said: The prayer of one sitting is upon half of the prayer of one standing, except cross-legged."
"26377","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ata' claimed that he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr informing. He said: I heard Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informing that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stay with Zaynab bint Jahsh and drink honey with her. So I and Hafsah agreed together that whichever of us the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon, she should say: I smell from you the odor of maghafir (a foul-smelling gum); have you eaten maghafir? So he entered upon one of them, and she said that to him. So he said: Rather I drank honey with Zaynab bint Jahsh, and I will never return to it. So there was revealed: Why do you prohibit what Allah has allowed you; If you two repent, to Aishah and Hafsah; and: When the Prophet confided to some of his wives, for his saying: Rather I drank honey."
"26378","Hajjaj narrated to us from Sharik from Abu Ishaq from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out to the Fajr prayer with his head dripping from the washing of major impurity, then he would complete his fast that day."
"26379","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Aflah narrated to us from al-Qasim from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon some of his wives, then he slept while junub until morning, then he washed and fasted his day."
"26380","Hajjaj informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abdullah, a man from Quraysh, narrated to me that he heard Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Makhramah ibn al-Muttalib that he said one day: Shall I not narrate to you about me and about my mother? So we thought he meant his mother who bore him. Aishah said: Shall I not narrate to you about me and about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Yes. He said: She said: When it was my night in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with me, he turned, put down his cloak, removed his sandals and placed them by his feet, spread the edge of his izar upon his bed, and lay down. He remained only as long as he thought I had slept. Then he took his cloak gently, put on his sandals gently, opened the door and went out, then closed it gently. So I placed my shift upon my head, veiled myself, wrapped my izar, then set out after him until he came to al-Baqi'. So he stood and stood long, then raised his hands three times, then turned, hurried, so I hurried; he jogged, so I jogged; he ran, so I ran; so I outran him and entered. It was only that I lay down and he entered. So he said: What is the matter with you, O Aish, panting with your breath held? She said: I said: Nothing, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You shall surely inform me or the Subtle, the Aware will inform me. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be for you. So she informed him. He said: So you are the blackness I saw before me? I said: Yes. So he poked me in my back with a poke that pained me, and said: Did you think Allah and His Messenger would wrong you? She said: Whatever people conceal, Allah knows it. He said: Yes; Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me when you saw; he called me and hid it from you, so I answered him hiding it from you. He would not enter upon you while you had put down your clothes, and I thought you had slept, so I disliked to wake you and feared you would feel lonely. So he said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commands you to come to the people of al-Baqi' and ask forgiveness for them. She said: So how shall I say, O Messenger of Allah? So he said: Say: Peace upon the people of the abodes from the believers and the Muslims, and may Allah have mercy upon the predecessors among us and the successors, and we, if Allah wills, shall join you."
"26381","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar from Abdullah ibn Urwah from Urwah from Aishah that she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, his companions complained (of illness), and Abu Bakr, Amir ibn Fuhayrah the freedman of Abu Bakr, and Bilal complained. So Aishah asked permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to visit them, and he permitted her. So she said to Abu Bakr: How do you find yourself? So he said: Every man is greeted morning among his family while death is nearer than the strap of his sandal. And I asked Amir, so he said: I have found death before tasting it; the coward's death is from above him. And I asked Bilal, so he said: Would that I knew whether I shall spend a night in Fajj with idhkhir and jalil (fragrant plants) around me. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of their saying. So he looked to the sky then said: O Allah, make Madinah beloved to us as You made Makkah beloved to us, and more strongly; and bless for us in its sa' and its mudd; and transfer its fever to Mahya'ah, which is al-Juhfah, as they claimed."
"26382","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah from Abu Salamah that he heard Aishah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray every night thirteen rak'ahs: nine standing and two while sitting, then he would wait until the first call of the dawn is given, then he would bow two rak'ahs."
"26383","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from Irak ibn Malik from Urwah that Aishah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray thirteen rak'ahs at night with the two rak'ahs of Fajr."
"26384","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah from Irak from Urwah from Aishah, she said: Umm Habibah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about blood (prolonged bleeding). Aishah said: I had seen her tub full of blood. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Remain as long as your menstruation used to detain you, then wash and pray."
"26385","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us from Qays ibn Wahb from an elder from Banu Sarah. He said: I asked Aishah and said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was junub, would he wash his head with a washing that sufficed thereby, or would he pour water over his head? She said: Rather he would pour water over his head."
"26386","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us from al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh from al-Bahiyy from Aishah that Usamah ibn Zayd stumbled upon the threshold or the doorstep and was cut in his forehead. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Remove the harm from him. She said: So I found it filthy. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept sucking it then spitting it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If Usamah were a girl, I would have clothed him and adorned him until I spent him (in marriage)."
"26387","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh from his father, he said: I said to Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite poetry as example? She said: Sometimes he would recite as example the poetry of Ibn Rawahah, and he would say: And news will come to you from one whom you did not provision."
"26388","Hajjaj and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, Ibn Numayr said: al-Harithi, from his father, he said: I asked Aishah: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) go out to the desert? She said: Yes, to these watercourses. She said: He went out once, then he sent to me some of the charity camels and gave me an unridden she-camel. Hajjaj said: Not ridden. And he said: O Aishah, upon you is fear of Allah Almighty and gentleness, for gentleness is never in a thing except it adorns it, and gentleness is never removed from a thing except it mars it."
"26389","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh from his father from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a rising cloud in the sky, a cloud or wind, he would face it from wherever it was, and if he was in prayer he would seek refuge with Allah Almighty from its evil. When it rained he would say: O Allah, a wholesome beneficial downpour."
"26390","Hajjaj informed us: Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me. He said: And Muhammad ibn Muslim said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr saying: Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: So he returned to Khadijah with his heart trembling. So he entered and said: Wrap me, wrap me. So he was wrapped. When it was lifted from him, he said: O Khadijah, I have feared for myself a calamity; I have feared for myself a calamity. Khadijah said: Be glad, for by Allah Allah will never disgrace you; you speak truthfully, join kinship, bear the burden (of the weak), honor the guest, and help against the vicissitudes of truth. So Khadijah set out with me to Waraqah ibn Nawfal ibn Asad, and he was a man who had become Christian, an old blind man who would read the Gospel in Arabic. So Khadijah said to him: O uncle, listen to your nephew. So Waraqah said to him: O son of my brother, what do you see? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him of what he had seen of that. So Waraqah said to him: This is the Namus (the angel of revelation) who descended upon Musa. Would that I were in it a youth; would that I be alive when your people expel you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will they indeed expel me? He said: Yes; no man ever came with the like of what you have come with except he was opposed. If your day reaches me, I shall help you with a strong help."
"26391","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah that the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out at night when they relieved themselves to al-Manasi', which is an open ground. And Umar ibn al-Khattab would say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Veil your women. But the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not do it. So Sawdah bint Zam'ah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), went out one night of the nights at dinner time, and she was a tall woman. So Umar called her: We have indeed recognized you, O Sawdah, keen that the veil be revealed. Aishah said: So the veil was revealed."
"26392","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed her while he was fasting."
"26393","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Zuhri, and he mentioned it with its isnad and its meaning."
"26394","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to me from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The companions of these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Give life to what you have created."
"26395","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me from Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not perform the voluntary Duha prayer, and Aishah would perform it. And she used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left much of the deed fearing that the people would take it as a practice and it would be imposed upon them."
"26396","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given choice between two matters except he took the easier of them, so long as it was not a sin; if it was a sin he was the furthest of them from it. By Allah, he never avenged for himself in anything done to him ever, until the sanctities of Allah Almighty were violated, then he would avenge for Allah Almighty."
"26397","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: Sometimes I would twist the necklaces for the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would garland his sacrificial animal, then send it, then stay, not avoiding anything that a muhrim avoids."
"26398","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us from Hisham from his father from Aishah the like of it."
"26399","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: As if I look at the glistening of perfume in the partings of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he calls out the talbiyah."
"26400","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Safiyyah. She said: So we said: She has menstruated. She said: So he said: Aqra halqa (may she be barren and shaven); I see her only detaining us. She said: So we said: O Messenger of Allah, she has circumambulated on the Day of Sacrifice. He said: Then no (harm); order her to depart."
"26401","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said Al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, grew heavy with illness, Bilal came to inform him of the prayer, and he said: Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, and whenever he stands in your place he cannot make the people hear, so if only you ordered Umar. Then he said: Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She said: So I said to Hafsah: Tell him. So Hafsah said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, and whenever he stands in your place he cannot make the people hear, so if only you ordered Umar. Then he said: You are indeed the companions of Yusuf. Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She said: So they ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. When he had entered the prayer, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, felt some relief in himself. She said: So he stood supported between two men, with his feet dragging on the ground, until he entered the mosque. When Abu Bakr heard his movement, he went to step back, but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gestured to him to stay as you are. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came until he sat to the left of Abu Bakr. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would lead the people in prayer sitting, while Abu Bakr was standing, Abu Bakr following the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the people following the prayer of Abu Bakr."
"26402","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Abd al-Malik, from Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever vows to obey Allah, Mighty and Majestic, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Allah, Mighty and Majestic, let him not disobey Him."
"26403","Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard Ubaydullah ibn Umar, and Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Talhah ibn Abd al-Malik, from Al-Qasim, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: A strange hadith from the hadith of Yahya ibn Said; I heard it only from my father, from Ibn Numayr, and Talhah ibn Abd al-Malik was a man from the people of Aylah. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The companions of hadith said: This is not in Kufah; this is only from Ibn Numayr, from Ubaydullah, meaning Al-Umari. So I said to them: Go to Abu Khaythamah, for their hearing in Kufah is one, from Ibn Numayr. So they went and they found it so."
"26404","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would become junub during the night, then he would perform ablution, his ablution for prayer, until morning, and he would not touch water."
"26405","Yala narrated to us, he said Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Aishah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Jibril, peace be upon him, sends salam to you. She said: So I said: And upon him be salam and the mercy of Allah."
"26406","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Hassan, narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Diqrah, she said: I was walking with Aishah among some women between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, and I saw a woman wearing a khamisah in which there was a cross, so Aishah said to her: Remove this from your garment, for when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw it in a garment, he tore it off."
"26407","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Al-Thawri narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Hasan ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: Dried meat of a gazelle was gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in ihram, and he did not eat it."
"26408","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would raise his hands supplicating until I would grow weary for him from how high he raised them, supplicating: O Allah, I am only a human being, so do not punish me for insulting a man I insulted or harmed."
"26409","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Malik narrated to us, and Ishaq, meaning Ibn Isa Al-Tabba, said: Malik informed us, from Abu Al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: I would sleep in front of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with my legs in his qiblah, and when he wanted to prostrate he would nudge me, so I would draw in my legs, and when he stood I would stretch them. She said: And there were no lamps in the houses in those days."
"26410","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, he said Al-Zuhri said, and Urwah informed me, from Aishah, that she would not do that, and she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only alighted at Al-Abtah because it was a more convenient dwelling for his departure."
"26411","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Al-Thawri informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, or from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he wanted to sacrifice, would buy two huge fat white-black horned castrated rams, and would slaughter one of them for his ummah, from those who bore witness to tawhid and bore witness to him of conveyance, and he slaughtered the other for Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the family of Muhammad."
"26412","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: I would twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he would send them, and he would not avoid anything that the one in ihram avoids."
"26413","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: Hind came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, there was no tent on the face of the earth more beloved to me that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, should humble its people than the people of your tent, and today there is no people of a tent on the face of the earth more beloved to me that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, should honor them than the people of your tent. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And also, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul. Then she said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man, so is there any sin upon me if I spend upon his dependents from his wealth without his permission? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no sin upon you to spend upon them in a reasonable manner."
"26414","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Al-Thawri informed us, from Al-Amash, from Umarah, from Yahya ibn Al-Jazzar, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray nine rakahs of the night, and when he grew heavy and aged, he prayed seven."
"26415","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: He kept the recitation quiet, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the two rakahs of Fajr, and he recited in them: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"26416","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Mamar informed us, from Al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about bit, and he said: Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful, and bit is honey wine."
"26417","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Rifah Al-Qurazi divorced his wife and made her divorce final, then Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Zubayr married her after him, and she came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, she was with Rifah and he divorced her the last of three divorces, then she married Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Zubayr after him, and by Allah he has with him, O Messenger of Allah, only the like of this fringe. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled, then said to her: Perhaps you wish to return to Rifah. No, until you taste his little honey and he tastes your little honey. She said: And Abu Bakr was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Khalid ibn Said was sitting at the door of the chamber, not admitted, and Khalid began calling Abu Bakr, saying: O Abu Bakr, will you not rebuke this woman for what she speaks aloud before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"26418","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, he said: The wife of Uthman ibn Mazun entered upon Aishah, I think her name was Khawlah bint Hakim, while she was shabby in appearance, so she asked her: What is your affair? She said: My husband prays the night and fasts the day. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered, and Aishah mentioned that to him. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met Uthman and said: O Uthman, monasticism has not been prescribed upon us. Do you not have in me an example? For by Allah, I am the most fearful of Allah among you and the most observant of His limits."
"26419","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas said to his brother Sad: Do you know that the son of the slave-girl of Zamah is my son? Aishah said: When the day of the Conquest came, Sad saw the boy and recognized him by resemblance, and embraced him to himself, and said: The son of my brother, by the Lord of the Kabah. Then Abd ibn Zamah came and said: Rather he is my brother, and he was born on the bed of my father from his slave-girl. So they both went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Sad said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the son of my brother; look at his resemblance to Utbah. Aishah said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a resemblance the like of which people never saw clearer than it to Utbah. Then Abd ibn Zamah said: O Messenger of Allah, rather he is my brother; he was born on the bed of my father from his slave-girl. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The child belongs to the bed. And veil yourself from him, O Sawdah. Aishah said: So by Allah, he never saw her until she died."
"26420","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Aishah joyful and said: Did you not hear what Al-Mudliji said? He saw Usamah and Zayd sleeping in a garment, or in a blanket, with their feet exposed, and he said: These feet, some of them are from some."
"26421","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said Ibn Shihab informed me, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me while the lines of his face were gleaming."
"26422","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said Yahya narrated to us, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to observe itikaf, he would pray the morning prayer, then enter the place in which he wanted to observe itikaf. Then he wanted to observe itikaf in the last ten of Ramadan, so he ordered and a tent was pitched for him, and Aishah ordered and a tent was pitched for her, and Hafsah ordered and a tent was pitched for her. When Zaynab saw their tents, she ordered and a tent was pitched for her. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw that, he said: Is it righteousness you intend? So he did not observe itikaf in Ramadan, and he observed itikaf for ten days of Shawwal."
"26423","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said Wail ibn Dawud narrated to me, he said: I heard Al-Bahi narrating from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never sent Zayd ibn Harithah in an army except he put him in command over them, and had he remained after him, he would have appointed him as successor."
"26424","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said Hammad narrated to us, from Khalid Al-Hadhdha, from Khalid ibn Abi Al-Salt, that Irak ibn Malik narrated before Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz that Aishah said: It was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that some people dislike facing the qiblah with their private parts, so he said: Have they indeed done so? Turn my seat toward the qiblah."
"26425","Abu Kamil and Affan narrated to us, they said Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Al-Hasan, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would perform witr with nine rakahs, and when he grew bulky and fleshy, he prayed seven rakahs, then he prayed two rakahs while sitting. Affan said: When he grew fleshy and bulky."
"26426","Abu Kamil and Affan narrated to us, they said Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"26427","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit Al-Bunani, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Al-Numan, from Aishah, she said: When the two circumcised parts met, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would perform ghusl."
"26428","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhajir Al-Jabali narrated to us, from Mujahid, that Al-Saib asked Aishah and said: I cannot pray except sitting, so what do you think? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The prayer of a man sitting is like half his prayer standing."
"26429","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said Hammad narrated to us, Budayl ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited standing, he would bow standing, and when he recited sitting, he would bow sitting."
"26430","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Urwah, he said: I said to Aishah: What about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Indeed Al-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj of the House or Umrah, there is no sin upon him to go between them. By Allah, there is no sin upon anyone not to go between them. She said: Evil is what you said, O son of my sister. Had it been as you interpreted it, it would have been: There is no sin upon him not to go between them. It was only revealed because this clan of the Ansar, before they became Muslim, would enter ihram for Manat, the false goddess whom they worshipped at Al-Mushallal, and whoever entered ihram for her would scruple to go between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah. So they asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Indeed Al-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj of the House or Umrah, there is no sin upon him to go between them. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prescribed going between them, so no one should leave going between them."
"26431","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Aishah, Mother of the Believers, with what would the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform witr? She said: He would recite in the first rakah: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and in the second: Say, O disbelievers, and in the third: Say, He is Allah, One, and the two Muawwidhats."
"26432","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I asked Aishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: He would prolong the prayer standing and sitting, and when he prayed standing he would bow standing, and when he prayed sitting he would bow sitting. And I asked her about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would fast until we would say: He has fasted, he has fasted, he has fasted, and he would break fast until we would say: He has broken fast, he has broken fast, he has broken fast. And he did not fast a complete month since he came to Madinah except the month of Ramadan."
"26433","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yaqub ibn Utbah, from Al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned to me one day from a funeral at Al-Baqi, while I had a headache in my head and I was saying: O my head. He said: Rather I, O my head. He said: What harm would it do you if you died before me, so I washed you and shrouded you, then prayed over you and buried you? I said: Rather I, as if I see you, by Allah, had you done that, you would have returned to my house and consummated marriage in it with one of your wives. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled. Then began the pain in which he died."
"26434","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Aban ibn Salih, from Al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, she said: A woman came to her and said: A daughter of mine, her hair has fallen out, shall we put upon her head something to beautify her with? She said: I heard a woman ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the like of what you asked about, and he said: Allah has cursed the woman who connects hair and the woman who asks for it to be connected."
"26435","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn Al-Zubayr, he said: I entered upon Aishah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Umrah only in Dhu Al-Qadah, and he performed three Umrahs."
"26436","Mamar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us five things: wearing silk and gold, drinking in vessels of gold and silver, the red saddle-cloth, and wearing qassi. So Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, a thin thing of gold tied to musk, or tied to it? He said: No. Make it of silver and color it yellow with some saffron."
"26437","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Hisham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I asked Aishah about the prayer of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed standing, and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Muhammad ibn Salamah."
"26438","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: Sahlah bint Suhayl came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Salim was called the son of Abu Hudhayfah, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has revealed His Book: Call them by their fathers. And he would enter upon me while I am uncovered, and we are in a cramped house. So he said: Breastfeed Salim, you become unlawful to him."
"26439","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, he said Al-Zuhri said, and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah informed me that Aishah informed him, she said: The first illness of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began in the house of Maymunah, and he asked permission of his wives to be nursed in her house, and they permitted him. So he came out with one hand upon Al-Fadl ibn Abbas and one hand upon another man, while he dragged his feet on the ground. Ubaydullah said: So I narrated it to Ibn Abbas, and he said: Do you know who the other man is whom Aishah did not name? He is Ali, but Aishah feels no goodwill toward him."
"26440","Al-Zuhri said: So Urwah, or Amrah, informed me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in his illness in which he died: Pour upon me from seven waterskins whose ties have not been untied, perhaps I shall find relief and enjoin the people. Aishah said: So we seated him in a wash-basin of Hafsah made of copper, and we poured upon him the water from them, until he began gesturing to us that you have done. Then he went out."
"26441","Al-Zuhri said: And Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me, he said: Aishah and Ibn Abbas informed me that when death descended upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he would cast a khamisah over his face, and when he felt distress he would uncover it from his face, while saying: The curse of Allah upon the Jews and Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques. Aishah says: He warns against the like of what they did."
"26442","Al-Zuhri said: And Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed me, from Aishah: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered my house, he said: Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender man; when he recites the Quran he cannot hold back his tears, so if only you ordered other than Abu Bakr. She said: By Allah, nothing was in me except dislike that the people should take evil omen from the first who stands in the station of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: So I reviewed him two or three times, and he said: Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer, for you are the companions of Yusuf."
"26443","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu Atiyyah, from Aishah, she said: The talbiyah of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was three times; he would say: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing belong to You."
"26444","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said Al-Amash narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, from Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Hand me the prayer mat from the mosque. She said: So I said: I am menstruating. Then he said: Your menstruation is not in your hand."
"26445","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: A man divorced his wife, and she married another husband besides him, and he entered with her, and he had the like of a fringe, and he did not approach her except once without attaining anything from her. So she mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Shall I become lawful to my first husband? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You do not become lawful to your first husband until the other tastes your little honey and you taste his little honey."
"26446","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came from a journey. She said: So I hung upon my door a curtain in which were winged horses. She said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw it, he said: Remove it."
"26447","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would enter the morning junub, then he would wash and complete his fast."
"26448","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, strike a servant of his ever, nor a wife of his ever, nor strike with his hand anything ever, except to strive in the way of Allah. Nor was anything done to him ever so he took revenge for it from its doer, except it be for Allah, Mighty and Majestic; if it was for Allah, he took revenge for Him. Nor were two matters presented to him except he took the easier of them, unless it was a sin; if it was a sin, he was the farthest of people from it."
"26449","Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said Al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: Some people from the Jews came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Death be upon you, O Abu Al-Qasim. So he said: And upon you. Aishah said: So I said: And upon you death and disgrace. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Aishah, do not be obscene. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear what they said: Death be upon you? He said: Did I not reply to them what they said? I said: And upon you. Ibn Numayr said, meaning in the hadith of Aishah: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not love obscenity nor being obscene. And Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: Then this verse was revealed: And when they come to you, they greet you with what Allah has not greeted you with, until he finished."
"26450","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said Al-Amash narrated to us, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Urwah, from Aishah, and he said Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I would bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a single vessel."
"26451","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said Al-Amash narrated to us, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Urwah, from Aishah, and he said Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I would bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a single vessel."
"26452","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Alighting at Al-Abtah is not a sunnah; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only alighted at it because it was more convenient for his departure, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"26453","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, and Yala, Al-Amash informed us, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Urwah ibn Al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: I would wash the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in itikaf, and I was menstruating."
"26454","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Al-Amash, and Yala, Al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: When: When the aid of Allah and the conquest comes, to its end, was revealed, I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray a prayer except he said: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me."
"26455","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah, and he narrated to us from Al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Al-Aswad, from Aishah, he said: It reached her that some people say: The dog, the donkey, and the woman cut off the prayer. So Aishah said: You have likened us to dogs and donkeys. I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying facing the bed, while I was upon it between him and the qiblah, and when I had a need, I would slip away from the side of the foot of the bed, disliking to face him."
"26456","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Qutbah narrated to us, and he mentioned both together, and he said: The two feet of the bed."
"26457","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would be struck by janabah during the night while he intended fasting, so he would sleep and wake, and enter the morning junub, then he would pour water over himself, then perform ablution."
"26458","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would touch his wives while fasting, because he was the most in control of you of his desire."
"26459","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I saw the glisten of perfume in the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was uttering the talbiyah."
"26460","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Al-Amash, from Ibrahim, he said Al-Aswad narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pawned his armor to a Jew and took food from him."
"26461","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said Al-Amash informed us, from Umarah, from Abu Atiyyah, from Aishah, she said: I know how the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would utter the talbiyah. He said: So she would utter the talbiyah with these words: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing belong to You."
"26462","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The night prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was thirteen rakahs; he would make witr from that with five, not sitting in anything of them except in the last of them. Then when the caller to prayer called, he would stand and pray two light rakahs."
"26463","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, scraped mucus, or spit, or phlegm from the qiblah."
"26464","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said Hisham informed us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Kill the snake with two stripes, for it seeks the sight and causes miscarriage."
"26465","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you say: My soul has become wicked, but let him say: My soul has become heavy."
"26466","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in any of the night prayer sitting, until he entered age. Then he would sit and recite, until when thirty or forty verses of the surah remained, he would stand and recite them, then bow."
"26467","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would bathe, we would bathe from janabah from a single vessel, scooping from it together."
"26468","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray while I lay across between him and the qiblah, upon the bed upon which he and his family sleep. Then when he wanted to perform witr, he would wake me, and I would perform witr."
"26469","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer during his illness, and he would lead them."
"26470","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned Safiyyah, and it was said: She is menstruating. So he said: Perhaps she will detain us. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, she has already performed the ifadah. He said: Then no harm."
"26471","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah, she said: There was with her a woman from Banu Asad, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered and said: Who is this? She said: This is so-and-so; she does not sleep. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon you is what you can bear. For by Allah, Allah does not tire until you tire. The most beloved religion to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is that which its doer maintains."
"26472","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let the one in ihram kill the mouse, the crow, the kite, the vicious dog, and the scorpion."
"26473","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwah, informed us, from Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn Al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, Abu Usamah said in his hadith: I heard Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, before he died, while I supported him to my chest, say: O Allah, forgive me and have mercy upon me, and join me with the Highest Companion."
"26474","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she would comb the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in itikaf, he handing her his head, while she was in her chamber, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the mosque."
"26475","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was shrouded in three white Sahuli garments."
"26476","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, the foster-brother of Aishah, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: No man dies and a community of Muslims prays over him and they intercede for him, except their intercession is accepted."
"26477","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Asim Al-Ahwal, from Muadhah, she said: I asked Aishah and said: What is with the menstruating woman, that she makes up the fast and does not make up the prayer? So she said: Are you a Haruriyyah? She said: I said: I am not a Haruriyyah, but I ask. She said: That would befall us with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we would be ordered, and he would order making up the fast, and would not order making up the prayer."
"26478","Mamar said: And Ayyub informed me, from Abu Qilabah, from Muadhah, from Aishah, the like of it."
"26479","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would observe itikaf in the last ten of Ramadan until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took him."
"26480","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would kiss some of his wives while fasting."
"26481","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a night in the mosque in the month of Ramadan, with some people with him, then he prayed the second, and more gathered that night than the first. When it was the third or the fourth, the mosque filled until it was crowded with its people, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not come out to them. So the people began calling him: The prayer. But he did not come out. In the morning Umar ibn Al-Khattab said to him: The people kept waiting for you last night, O Messenger of Allah. He said: It was not hidden to me their affair, but I feared it would be made obligatory upon them."
"26482","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said Yunus informed us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, and he mentioned its meaning, meaning: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a night in the mosque in the month of Ramadan."
"26483","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never struck with his hand a servant of his ever, nor a wife, nor did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ever strike with his hand anything ever, except to strive in the way of Allah. Nor was he given choice between two matters ever except the more beloved of them to him was the easier of them, until it be a sin; if it was a sin, he was the farthest of people from sin. Nor did he take revenge for himself for anything brought to him, until the sanctities of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, were violated, then he would take revenge for Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"26484","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: Had the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seen the women today, he would have forbidden them going out, or prohibited them going out."
"26485","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfah as a collector, then a man disputed him about his charity, so Abu Jahm struck him and wounded his head. So they came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Retaliation, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: To you is such and such. But they were not satisfied. He said: Then to you is such and such. But they were not satisfied. He said: Then to you is such and such. Then they were satisfied. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I shall address the people and inform them of your satisfaction. They said: Yes. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed, and said: These Laythis came to me seeking retaliation, and I offered them such and such, and they were satisfied. Are you satisfied? They said: No. So the Muhajirun rushed at them, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered them to hold back, so they held back. Then he called them and increased them, and said: Are you satisfied? They said: Yes. He said: I shall address the people and inform them of your satisfaction. They said: Yes. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed, then he said: Are you satisfied? They said: Yes."
"26486","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, and he mentioned a hadith, then he said, Al-Zuhri said: So Urwah informed me, from Aishah, that she said: The first with which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was begun of revelation was the true dream in sleep, and he would not see a dream except it came like the brightness of morning. Then solitude was made beloved to him, so he would come to Hira and devote himself in it, and it is worship, for nights of set number, and he would provision for that, then return to Khadijah, and she would provision him for the like of them, until the truth came to him while he was in the cave of Hira. The angel came to him in it and said: Read. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am not a reader. He said: So he took me and pressed me until hardship reached me, then he released me and said: Read. So I said: I am not a reader. Then he took me and pressed me the second time until hardship reached me, then he released me and said: Read. So I said: I am not a reader. Then he took me and pressed me the third time until hardship reached me, then he released me and said: Read in the name of your Lord who created, until: what he did not know. He said: So he returned with them, his shoulders trembling, until he entered upon Khadijah and said: Wrap me, wrap me. So they wrapped him until the fear left him. Then he said: O Khadijah, what is with me? And he informed her the news. He said: And I feared for myself. So she said to him: No, be glad, for by Allah, Allah will never disgrace you ever. You join ties of kinship, and speak truthfully, and bear the burden of the weak, and honor the guest, and help in the calamities of truth. Then Khadijah set out with him until she brought him to Waraqah ibn Nawfal ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy, and he was the son of the uncle of Khadijah, the brother of her father, and he was a man who had become Christian in the pre-Islamic time, and he would write the Arabic script, and he wrote in Arabic from the Gospel what Allah willed him to write, and he was an old man who had become blind. So Khadijah said: O son of my uncle, listen from the son of your brother. So Waraqah said: Son of my brother, what do you see? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed him what he saw. So Waraqah said: This is the Namus that was sent down upon Musa, peace be upon him. Would that I were in it a youth; would that I be alive when your people expel you. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Are they indeed expelling me? So Waraqah said: Yes; no man ever came with the like of what you came with except he was treated with enmity. And if your day finds me, I shall aid you with strong aid. Then Waraqah did not remain but to die, and the revelation paused for a period, until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, grieved, in what reached us, with grief from which he went out repeatedly to throw himself down from the tops of mountain peaks. Whenever he reached the peak of a mountain to cast himself from it, Jibril, peace be upon him, appeared to him and said to him: O Muhammad, you are indeed the Messenger of Allah in truth. So that would calm his heart and his soul would settle, peace and blessings be upon him. Then he would return, and when revelation was long delayed, he went out for the like of that. Then when he reached the peak of a mountain, Jibril, peace be upon him, appeared to him and said to him the like of that."
"26487","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Abyssinians played for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he called me, and I looked from over his shoulder until I was satisfied."
"26488","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she would play with dolls, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would bring my companions to play with me."
"26489","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Abi Al-Zinad informed us, from Abu Al-Zinad, he said Urwah said to me: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that day: So the Jews know that in our religion there is latitude. I was sent with an upright tolerant Hanifiyyah."
"26490","Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, he said Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prayed a prayer, would persist in it, and the most beloved prayer to him was what is persisted in, though little. And he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not tire until you tire."
"26491","Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, he said Aban narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The most fasting of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a month of the year was Shaban, for he would fast all of it."
"26492","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: When it was the night of departure, I said: O Messenger of Allah, they return with an Umrah and a Hajj, and I return with a Hajj. So he sent my brother with me, and I performed Umrah. Then I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ascending, traveling by night toward the people of Madinah, while I was traveling by night toward the people of Makkah."
"26493","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, he said Muhammad ibn Dinar informed us, from Sad ibn Aws, from Misda ibn Yahya Al-Ansari, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would kiss her while fasting and suck her tongue."
"26494","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said Usamah ibn Zayd Al-Laythi narrated to us, from Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: Prayer was obligated as two rakahs, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, added in the resident prayer, and left the travel prayer as it was."
"26495","Yahya ibn Said Al-Umawi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I would play with dolls in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would bring my companions. When they saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they would shrink from him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would send them to me to play with me."
"26496","Zayd ibn Al-Hubab narrated to us, he said Ibrahim ibn Nafi informed me, he said Al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq informed me, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, that a woman from the Ansar married off a daughter of hers, and she complained and her hair fell out. So she came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Her husband wants her, shall I connect her hair? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah has cursed the women who connect hair."
"26497","Zayd ibn Al-Hubab narrated to us, he said Umar ibn Abi Wahb Al-Nasri informed me, he said Musa ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Kurayz Al-Khuzai narrated to me, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he performed ablution, would run his fingers through his beard with water."
"26498","Ali ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Mubarak, informed us, he said Umar ibn Abi Wahb Al-Khuzai informed us, he said Musa ibn Tharwan narrated to me, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Kurayz Al-Khuzai, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution, he would run his fingers through his beard with water."
"26499","He said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala Al-Sami narrated to us, Burd narrated to us, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: I went to open the door while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was standing praying. So he walked toward the qiblah, either to his right or to his left, until he opened for me, then he returned to his place of prayer."
"26500","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from Al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she would comb the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while menstruating, while he was in itikaf in the mosque, he handing her his head, while she was in her chamber."
"26501","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, and Yazid said: Sa'id informed us from Qatada from Safiyya bint Shayba from A'isha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ghusl with a sa' and perform wudu with about a mudd. Yazid said: with the measure of a mudd. Yazid said: from Safiyya bint Shayba or Mu'adha."
"26502","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammam informed us from Qatada from Safiyya bint Shayba, and he said: with the measure of a mudd and with the measure of a sa'."
"26503","Abd al-Wahhab narrated from Sa'id from Qatada from Safiyya bint Shayba from A'isha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ghusl with a sa' and perform wudu with the measure of a mudd or about it."
"26504","Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ali that A'isha used to take on debt, so it was said to her: What drives you to debt when you can do without it? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no servant who takes on debt with the intention in himself to repay it except that Allah's help is with him, so I seek that help."
"26505","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us from Shumaysa from A'isha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh made in earthen jars."
"26506","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal informed us from Abu al-Walid from A'isha, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sit after his prayer except for the time it takes to say: O Allah, You are al-Salam and from You is al-Salam, blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"26507","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from his father from A'isha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to touch one of us while she was menstruating, he ordered her to wrap her waist-cover, and when he wanted to sleep while junub, he performed wudu as his wudu for prayer."
"26508","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Asim informed us from Mu'adha bint Abd Allah, she said: A'isha informed me that she used to perform ghusl, she and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a single vessel."
"26509","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed us from Amra from A'isha, she said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had seen what women have introduced, he would have prevented them from the mosque just as the women of the Children of Israel were prevented."
"26510","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya informed us that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Akhi Amra informed him from Amra that she heard A'isha say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the two rak'as before Fajr and lighten them so much that I would say: Has he recited the Mother of the Qur'an in them?"
"26511","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in i'tikaf, and he would not enter the house except for a human need. She said: So I washed his head while between me and him was the threshold of the door."
"26512","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Maymun informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasar informed me, he said: A'isha informed me that when semen got onto the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would wash what had got onto his garment, then go out to prayer, and I would be looking at a spot on that garment of his from the trace of washing."
"26513","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us from al-Hasan from Sa'd ibn Hisham, he said: I came to Madina and entered upon A'isha, and she said to me: Who are you? I said: Sa'd ibn Hisham ibn Amir. She said: May Allah have mercy on your father. He said: I said: Inform me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite... I said: Yes, but inform me. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the last Isha with the people, then go to his bed, then when it was the middle of the night he would get up to his purification water and perform wudu, then enter the mosque and pray eight rak'as, equalizing the recitation, bowing, and prostration in them, then pray witr with one rak'a, then pray two rak'as sitting, then lay his head down; sometimes Bilal would come and notify him of the prayer before he dozed, and sometimes I doubted whether he dozed or not, until he notified him of the prayer. She said: That was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he grew old and put on flesh, then he would pray the last Isha with the people, then go to his bed, then when it was the middle of the night he would get up to his purification water and perform wudu, then enter the mosque and pray six rak'as, equalizing the bowing, prostration, and recitation among them, then pray witr with one rak'a, then pray two rak'as sitting; sometimes he would not doze until Bilal came and notified him of the prayer, and sometimes I doubted whether he dozed or not."
"26514","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Bahz ibn Hakim narrated to us, and once he said: he informed us, he said: I heard Zurara ibn Awfa say: A'isha was asked about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: He used to pray Isha, then pray two rak'as after it, then sleep; then when he woke up, with his wudu water covered and his siwak with him, he would use the siwak, then perform wudu, then stand and pray eight rak'as, reciting in them the Fatiha of the Book and whatever he wished of the Qur'an, and once he said: whatever Allah willed of the Qur'an, and he would not sit in any of them except in the eighth, in which he would sit and recite the tashahhud, then stand without giving salam and pray one rak'a, then sit and recite the tashahhud and supplicate, then give one taslima: al-salamu alaykum, raising his voice with it until it woke us, then say takbir while sitting and recite, then bow and prostrate while sitting, praying two rak'as sitting; these are eleven rak'as. Then when he put on much flesh and became heavy, he made the nine seven, not sitting except as he sat in the first, and praying the two rak'as sitting; this was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until Allah took his soul."
"26515","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us from Bahz ibn Hakim from Zurara ibn Awfa from Sa'd ibn Hisham, he said: I said to Umm al-Mu'minin A'isha: How was the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: He used to pray Isha, then he mentioned the hadith, and he would pray two rak'as standing, raising his voice as if waking us, rather waking us, then supplicate with a supplication letting us hear, then give one taslima, raising his voice with it."
"26516","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya informed us from Amir from Shurayh ibn Hani' from A'isha from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever loves the meeting with Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him, and death is before the meeting with Allah."
"26517","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya informed us from Abu Ishaq, he said: Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali narrated to me, he said: I said to A'isha: How was the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his family? She said: He was the best of people in character; he was not obscene, nor deliberately obscene, nor loud in the markets, nor did he repay evil with its like, but he pardoned and overlooked."
"26518","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya informed us from Abu Ishaq from al-Aswad from A'isha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to enter ihram, he would oil himself with the best oil he could find, so much that I would see the glisten of the oil in his hair."
"26519","And I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would send them with them, and he would not keep away from us from any woman."
"26520","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed us from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I said to A'isha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray sitting? She said: He would pray long at night sitting, and pray long at night standing; when he recited standing, he bowed standing, and when he recited sitting, he bowed sitting."
"26521","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us from Amir from Masruq, he said: I was reclining with A'isha, and she said: O Abu A'isha, I am the first who asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this. He said: That is Jibril; I have not seen him in the form in which he was created except twice: I saw him descending from heaven, the greatness of his creation filling what is between heaven and earth."
"26522","Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id informed us from Qatada from Mu'adha from A'isha, she said: Tell your husbands to wash from themselves the trace of stool and urine, for I am shy before them, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"26523","Yazid narrated to us, Urwa Abu Abd Allah al-Bazzaz informed us from al-Sha'bi from A'isha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ghusl from janaba, he began and performed wudu as his wudu for prayer, and washed his private part and his feet, and wiped his hand on the wall, then poured water over himself, and it is as if I see the trace of his hand on the wall."
"26524","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us from Yahya from Imran ibn Hittan that A'isha narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not leave in his house anything containing a cross-like figure except that he broke it."
"26525","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us from al-Miqdam from his father, he said: I said to A'isha: O mother, with what would the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) begin when he entered your house, and with what would he end? She said: He would begin with the siwak and end with the two rak'as of Fajr."
"26526","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while his armor was mortgaged for thirty sa's of barley."
"26527","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us from Makhlad ibn Khufaf from Urwa from A'isha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that return profit is by liability for loss."
"26528","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Salama from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand, then pointed to the moon and said: O A'isha, seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this, for this is the darkening night when it settles."
"26529","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from A'isha: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd ibn Zam'a: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sawda bint Zam'a to veil herself from him because of what he saw of his resemblance to Utba, and he did not see her until he met Allah."
"26530","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, informed us from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim that he heard Alqama ibn Waqqas al-Laythi say: I asked A'isha, I said: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray the two rak'as while sitting? She said: He would recite in them while sitting, then when he wanted to bow, he would stand and bow."
"26531","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed us from Abu Salama, he said: I asked A'isha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleep while junub? She said: Yes, but he would not sleep until he washed his private part and performed wudu as his wudu for prayer."
"26532","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed us from Abu Salama from A'isha, she said: A month would come upon the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with no smoke seen in any of his houses. He said: I said: O mother, what was their food? She said: The two black ones, water and dates, except that he had truthful neighbors from the Ansar who had milk animals, and they would send to him from their milk."
"26533","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, informed us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from A'isha that Zaynab bint Jahsh had prolonged bleeding in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to perform ghusl for every prayer; she would enter a tub full of water and immerse herself in it, then come out of it while the blood was overwhelming her, then go out and pray."
"26534","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from his father from his grandfather Alqama ibn Waqqas from A'isha that she said: I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he entered ihram and when he left it."
"26535","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, informed us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from A'isha, she said: A sheep was gifted to Hafsa while we were both fasting, so she broke my fast; and she was her father's daughter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us, and we mentioned that to him, and he said: Make up a day in its place."
"26536","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from A'isha, he said: A Jewish woman asked her, so she gave her, and she said to her: May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave. A'isha disapproved of that, then when she saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she told him, and he said: No. A'isha said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us after that: It has been revealed to me that you will be tried in your graves."
"26537","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya informed us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that he heard A'isha say: I twisted the garlands of the sacrificial animal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hands, and he sent them, and stayed, and did not leave anything he used to do."
"26538","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us from al-Qasim ibn Abbas from Abd Allah ibn Niyar from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a gazelle containing beads, and he divided it equally between the free woman and the slave woman."
"26539","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us from al-Zuhri from Urwa from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never performed the Duha supererogatory prayer at all, yet I perform it."
"26540","Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The snake is harmful, the scorpion is harmful, and the crow is harmful."
"26541","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad informed him from Amra bint Abd al-Rahman from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"26542","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr from A'isha, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The siwak is a purification for the mouth and pleasing to the Lord."
"26543","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us from Muhammad that A'isha was asked about the recitation in the two rak'as before the Fajr prayer, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite quietly in them, and she mentioned: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"26544","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us from Muhammad that A'isha stayed with Umm Talha al-Talhat, and saw her daughters praying without headcovers, and said: I see your daughters have menstruated, or some of them have menstruated. She said: Yes. She said: No slave-girl among them who has menstruated should pray except with a headcover on, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me with a girl with me, and he threw to me his waist-wrapper and said: Split it between this one and the girl with Umm Salama, for I do not see them except that they have menstruated, or: I do not see her except that she has menstruated."
"26545","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from A'isha, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hands for his ihram, and I perfumed him at Mina before he performed tawaf."
"26546","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Urwa from A'isha, she said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, so I went out, and there he was at al-Baqi', raising his head to the sky, and he said to me: Were you afraid that Allah and His Messenger would wrong you? She said: I said: I thought you had gone to one of your wives. He said: Allah, Exalted is He, descends on the night of the middle of Sha'ban to the lowest heaven and forgives more than the number of the hairs of the sheep of Kalb."
"26547","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammam informed us from Qatada from Safiyya bint Shayba from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform wudu with the measure of a mudd and perform ghusl with the measure of a sa'."
"26548","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us from Qatada from Safiyya bint Shayba from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every people has supporters, and the supporters of Quraysh are their freedmen."
"26549","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, make me among those who, when they do good, rejoice, and when they do wrong, seek forgiveness."
"26550","Yazid narrated to us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray four before Zuhr, and Yazid once said: two rak'as after it, and two rak'as before Fajr, and he used to say: What excellent two suras they are, which they recite in the two rak'as before Fajr: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"26551","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us from al-A'mash, meaning from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice, and we chose him, and we did not count it as divorce. Abu Bakr said: Abu al-Duha dropped from my book."
"26552","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us from Abu Ma'shar from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from A'isha, she said: I used to rub semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"26553","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us from Thabit al-Bunani from Abd Allah ibn Rabah from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Nu'man from A'isha from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory."
"26554","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba ibn al-Hajjaj informed us from Abu Imran al-Jawni from Talha, a man of Quraysh, from A'isha, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I have two neighbors, to which of them should I give a gift? He said: To the one nearer to you in door."
"26555","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us from Khalid al-Hadhdha' from Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt, he said: We were with Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and they mentioned a man sitting in the privy facing the qibla, and they disliked that, so he narrated from Irak ibn Malik from A'isha that that was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Have they done that? Turn my seat toward the qibla."
"26556","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us from Qatada from Zurara ibn Awfa from Sa'd ibn Hisham from A'isha from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The skilled one in the Qur'an is with the noble righteous scribes, and the one who recites it while it is hard for him has his reward twice."
"26557","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Ruman narrated to us from Urwa from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O A'isha, were it not that your people are recent in Jahiliyya, I would have ordered the House to be demolished, and I would have included in it what was excluded from it, and attached it to the ground, and made for it two doors, an eastern door and a western door, for they fell short in building it, so I would reach it to the foundation of Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
"26558","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salama informed us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'a from A'isha, she said: We came to Madina while it was thickets and tamarisk, and the family of Abu Bakr fell ill, so I sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to visit my father, and he permitted me. I came to him and said: O father, how do you find yourself? He said: Every man is greeted in the morning among his family, while death is nearer than the strap of his sandal. She said: I said: My father is delirious, by Allah. Then I came to Amir ibn Fuhayra and said: O Amir, how do you find yourself? He said: I have found death before tasting it; indeed the coward's death comes from above him. She said: Then I came to Bilal and said: O Bilal, how do you find yourself? He said: Would that I knew whether I will spend a night at Fakhkh with idhkhir and jalil around me. He said: Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: O Allah, bless for us our sa' and bless for us our mudd, and make Madina beloved to us as You made Makka beloved to us, and transfer its fever to Khumm and Mahyay'a."
"26559","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sadaqa ibn Musa informed us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us from Yazid ibn Babnus from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The registers with Allah, Exalted is He, are three: a register to which Allah pays no attention, a register from which Allah leaves nothing, and a register which Allah does not forgive. As for the register which Allah does not forgive, it is associating partners with Allah; Allah, Exalted is He, said: Whoever associates partners with Allah, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him. As for the register to which Allah pays no attention, it is the wrongdoing of the servant against himself between him and his Lord, from a day's fast he left or a prayer he left, for Allah, Exalted is He, forgives that and pardons if He wills. As for the register from which Allah leaves nothing, it is the wrongdoing of servants against one another: retribution, inevitably."
"26560","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, he said: My father narrated to me from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from A'isha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, he called his daughter Fatima and confided in her, and she wept, then he confided in her and she laughed. I asked her about that, and she said: When I wept, he informed me that he would die, so I wept; then he informed me that I am the first of his family to join him, so I laughed."
"26561","Yazid narrated from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, he said: My father informed me from al-Qasim from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever introduces into this matter of ours what is not of it, it is rejected."
"26562","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us from Qatada from Abu Hassan, he said: Two men of Banu Amir entered upon A'isha and informed her that Abu Hurayra narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Ill omen is in the house, the woman, and the horse. She became angry, and a part of her flew to the sky and a part to the earth, and she said: By the One who sent down the Furqan upon Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never said it at all; he only said: The people of Jahiliyya used to take omens from that."
"26563","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Burd informed us from Umm Salim al-Rasibiyya, she said: I heard A'isha say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the breath of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"26564","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us from al-Sha'bi from Masruq from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice, and we chose him; was it divorce?"
"26565","Mu'adh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Ata' from A'isha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a rain-laden cloud, meaning clouds, his face would change color and alter, and he would go in and out, come forward and turn back; then when it rained, he would be relieved of it. She said: A'isha mentioned to him some of what she saw of him, and he said: How do I know? Perhaps it is as the people of Ad said: Then when they saw it as a cloud coming toward their valleys, they said: This is a cloud bringing us rain; rather it is what you sought to hasten: a wind in which is a painful punishment."
"26566","Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from Abu Salama from A'isha, she said: We had a mat which we spread by day and curtained off by night; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on it one night, and the Muslims heard his recitation and prayed with his prayer. When the second night came, they increased, so he looked out at them and said: Burden yourselves with deeds you can bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire, and the most beloved deed to him was the most constant, even if little. She said: And when he prayed a prayer, he established it firmly."
"26567","Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli, he said: I asked A'isha about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: He would pray long at night standing, and long at night sitting; when he recited standing, he bowed standing, and when he recited sitting, he bowed sitting."
"26568","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Dawud from al-Sha'bi from Masruq, he said: I was with A'isha. He said: I said: Does not Allah say: And he saw him on the clear horizon, and: And he saw him another descent? She said: I am the first of this umma who asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them, and he said: That is only Jibril; I did not see him in the form in which he was created except twice: I saw him descending from heaven to earth, the greatness of his creation filling what is between heaven and earth."
"26569","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Dawud from Amir, he said: A'isha said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had concealed anything of what Allah sent down to him, he would have concealed these verses against himself: And when you say to the one upon whom Allah bestowed favor and you bestowed favor: Keep your wife and fear Allah, and you conceal in yourself what Allah will disclose, and you fear people while Allah is more worthy to be feared, up to His saying: And the command of Allah is accomplished."
"26570","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Dawud from al-Sha'bi that A'isha said: Prayer was obligated as two rak'as, two rak'as in Makka, then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina, he added with every two rak'as two rak'as, except Maghrib, for it is the witr of the day, and the Fajr prayer for the length of their recitation. He said: And when he traveled, he prayed the first prayer."
"26571","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Dawud from Azra from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Sa'd ibn Hisham, he said: A'isha said: We had a curtain with figures of birds, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O A'isha, move it away, for when I see it, I remember the world; and we had a velvet cloth he wore, she says its emblem was silk."
"26572","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us from Amr ibn Murra from Abu al-Duha from Masruq, he said: al-Siddiqa bint al-Siddiq, the beloved of the Beloved of Allah, the acquitted, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'as after Asr, and I did not disbelieve her."
"26573","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Dastuwai informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Urwa from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"26574","Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad narrated to us from Kahmas from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I said to A'isha: Which people were most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? A'isha said... I said: Then among men? She said: Her father."
"26575","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Dawud from Amir from A'isha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will not enter Makka nor Madina."
"26576","Abda narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us from a man, he said: I asked A'isha: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do in his house? She said: He would patch the garment and repair the sandal, or words to that effect."
"26577","Abda narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Fatima bint Muhammad from Amra from A'isha, she said: We did not know where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be buried until we heard the sound of spades at the end of the night, the night of Wednesday. Ibn Ishaq said: And al-masahi are shovels."
"26578","Rawh narrated to us, Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to us, he said: Fatima bint Abi Layth narrated to me from Umm Kulthum bint Amr ibn Abi Aqrab, she said: I heard A'isha say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Take the disliked beneficial talbina, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, it washes the belly of one of you as one of you washes his face with water from dirt. She said: When one of his family complained of illness, the pot would remain on the fire until one of its two ends came upon him. And he said, meaning Rawh in Baghdad: When one of his family complained of something, it would remain."
"26579","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said: Ata' informed me that he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr, and al-Dahhak said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Ata' from Ubayd ibn Umayr, saying: A'isha informed me that she said to the players: I wished I could see them. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the door, and I stood behind him looking between his ear and his shoulder while they played in the mosque. Ata' said: Persians or Abyssinians, and Ibn Umayr said: They are Abyssinians."
"26580","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Bunana, freedwoman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hayyan al-Ansari, from A'isha, Mother of the Believers, she said: While she was with her, a slave-girl wearing jingling bells that made sound was brought in upon her, and she said: Do not bring her in upon me unless you cut off her bells. Bunana asked her about that, and she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a bell, nor accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"26581","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us from Abu al-Nadr, freedman of Umar ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abu Salama from A'isha that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until we said: He will not break fast, and break fast until we said: He will not fast; and I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complete fasting a month at all except Ramadan, and I never saw him in any month fast more than in Sha'ban."
"26582","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Abu Bakr Asim, a freedman of Qurayba bint Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Qurayba from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting in fasting, so I said to him: You practice wisal. He said: I am not like any of you; I spend the night fed and given drink."
"26583","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us from Asim, freedman of Qurayba, from Qurayba from A'isha, and he mentioned its meaning."
"26584","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, Awfa ibn Dalham al-Adawi narrated to us from Mu'adha from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take something from our faces while fasting."
"26585","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Thumama ibn Kilab that Abu Salama narrated to him that A'isha narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make nabidh in gourds, nor in hantam, nor in naqir, nor in muzaffat; and do not make nabidh of raisins and dates together, nor make nabidh of unripe dates and ripe dates together."
"26586","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ziyad informed me that Abu Nuhayk informed him that Abu al-Darda' used to address the people that there is no witr for one who reaches dawn, so some believing men went to A'isha and informed her, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in the morning and pray witr."
"26587","Mu'adh narrated to us, Ikrima ibn Ammar narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would scrape semen from his garment with a stalk of idhkhir, then pray in it, and scrape it from his garment dry, then pray in it."
"26588","Rawh narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa said: from Ibn Shihab from Ibn Hazm from Urwa from A'isha, she said: A woman entered upon me with her two daughters, so I fed her a date, and she split it between them and did not eat anything of it; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: Whoever is tried with daughters by anything and treats them well, they will be a cover for him from the Fire."
"26589","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us from Sulayman, he said: I heard Khaythama narrate from Abu Atiyya from A'isha that she said: I know how the talbiya of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, then I heard her chant the talbiya: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, no partner have You; here I am, indeed praise and favor are Yours."
"26590","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Sulayman narrated to us from Khaythama from Abu Atiyya, he said: I heard A'isha say: I know how the talbiya of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was. He said: Then I heard her chant the talbiya after that: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, no partner have You; here I am, indeed praise and favor are Yours. My father said: Abu Atiyya's name is Malik ibn Hamza."
"26591","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, and he was an orphan in the care of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone."
"26592","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: I read to Malik ibn Anas from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone."
"26593","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed us that Urwa informed him that A'isha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram with Hajj and Umra in the Farewell Pilgrimage and drove the sacrificial animal with him; some people entered ihram with him with Umra and drove the sacrificial animal, and some entered ihram with Umra and did not drive a sacrificial animal. A'isha said: I was among those who entered ihram with Umra and did not drive a sacrificial animal. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, he said: Whoever among you entered ihram with Umra and drove the sacrificial animal with him, let him circumambulate the House and al-Safa and al-Marwa, and nothing forbidden to him becomes lawful until he completes his Hajj and sacrifices his animal on the Day of Sacrifice; and whoever among you entered ihram with Umra and did not drive a sacrificial animal with him, let him circumambulate the House and al-Safa and al-Marwa, then let him pour forth and become lawful, then enter ihram with Hajj and offer a sacrifice; whoever does not find, then fasting three days in Hajj and seven when he returns to his family. A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put forward the Hajj which he feared missing, and delayed the Umra."
"26594","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulayka from A'isha, she said: He entered upon me on the twenty-ninth, so I said: Not a night of them was hidden from me; only twenty-nine nights have passed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O A'isha, the month is twenty-nine."
"26595","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulayka informed me from a man of Banu Tamim whom we do not disbelieve, he said: I informed A'isha that Ibn Umar says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is twenty-nine. A'isha disapproved of that and said: May Allah forgive Abu Abd al-Rahman; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not say it so, but he said: The month is sometimes twenty-nine."
"26596","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us from Urwa from A'isha, she said: They used to fast the day of Ashura before Ramadan was obligated, and it was a day on which the Ka'ba was covered; then when Allah, Exalted is He, obligated Ramadan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever wishes to leave it, let him leave it."
"26597","Rawh narrated to us, Ata' informed me from Abu Salih al-Zayyat that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the fasting day of one of you, let him not be obscene that day nor shout; if someone insults him or fights him, let him say: I am a fasting man."
"26598","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada, he said: I heard Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah from A'isha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing: Glorified, Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"26599","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Qatada from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing: Glorified, Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"26600","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Urfuta narrated to us, my father said, but it is really Khalid ibn Alqama, he said: I heard Abd Khayr narrate from A'isha from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade gourds, hantam, and muzaffat. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father said: It is really Khalid ibn Alqama al-Hamdani; Shu'ba erred."
"26601","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Shumaysah, that she was with Aishah, then a person stood before her and said: O Mother of the Believers, what do you say about nabidh of the earthen jar? She said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the earthen jar."
"26602","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Hisham, from Shumaysah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the earthen jar."
"26603","Rawh narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge in his prayer from debt and sin. Then someone said: O Messenger of Allah, how often you seek refuge from debt! He said: When a man falls into debt, he speaks and lies, and promises and breaks his promise."
"26604","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abi Salamah, that Aishah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take of deeds what you can bear, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not tire until you tire. And the most beloved prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was what one persisted in, even if it was little, and when he prayed a prayer he persisted in it."
"26605","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: By Allah, a month would pass over the household of Muhammad during which we did not bake. He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat? She said: We had neighbors from the Ansar, may Allah reward them with good; they had some milk which they would gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"26606","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Umar ibn Abdillah ibn Urwah informed me that he heard Urwah and al-Qasim reporting from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my own hands with dharirah for the Farewell Hajj, for exiting ihram and entering ihram: when he entered ihram and when he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice before circumambulating the House."
"26607","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, that she said: I perfumed, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered ihram, with the best of my perfume that I could manage."
"26608","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam and Hammad and Mansur and Sulayman informed me, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that she said: It is as if I am looking at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram. Sulayman said: in his hair; Mansur said: in the roots of his hair; and al-Hakam and Hammad said: in his parting."
"26609","Rawh narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah al-Nakhai, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: It is as if I am looking at the glisten of musk on the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram."
"26610","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd Rabbihi, from Abi Iyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, that Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent him to Umm Salamah and Aishah. He said: I came to the boy of Umm Salamah, Nafi, and sent him to her, and he returned to me and informed me that Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub without a wet dream, then wake fasting. He said: Then he met the boy of Aishah, Dhakwan Abu Amr, and sent him to her, and asked her about that, and she informed him that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub without a wet dream, then wake fasting."
"26611","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to me, from Ubaydillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar al-Ansari, from Abi Yunus, the freedman of Aishah, from Aishah, that a man said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was standing at the door: O Messenger of Allah, I wake junub and I intend fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I wake junub and I intend fasting, then I wash and fast. The man said: You are not like us; what came before of your sin and what comes after has been forgiven you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said: By Allah, I hope I am the most God-fearing of you and the most knowledgeable of what I guard against."
"26612","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Bahiyy, from Ibn Umar, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to her: Hand me the prayer mat from the mosque. She said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand."
"26613","Rawh narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Aishah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was at Sarif and I was weeping. He said: What makes you weep, O Aishah? She said: I said: People return with two rites and I return with one rite. He said: Why is that? She said: I said: I have menstruated. He said: That is something Allah decreed for the daughters of Adam; do what the pilgrim does. She said: We reached Makkah, then we departed to Mina, then we departed to Arafah, then we stood with the people, then I stood at Jam, then I stoned the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice, then I stoned the Jimar with the people on those days. She said: Then he departed until he camped at al-Hasbah. She said: By Allah, he did not camp there except on my account, or Ibn Abi Mulaykah said on her authority: except on her account. Then he sent to Abd al-Rahman and said: Carry her behind you until you take her out of the Sanctuary. By Allah, he did not say: take her out to al-Jirranah nor to al-Tanim; so let her enter ihram for Umrah. She said: So we set out, and the nearest to the Sanctuary was al-Tanim, so I entered ihram from there for Umrah, then I came, then I came to the House and circumambulated it, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then I came to him and he departed. Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: And Aishah used to do that afterwards."
"26614","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj and camped at al-Shajarah. He said: Whoever wishes, let him enter ihram for Umrah, and whoever wishes, let him enter ihram for Hajj. Aishah said: So some of them entered ihram for Umrah and some of them entered ihram for Hajj. She said: And I was among those who entered ihram for Umrah, then the Day of Arafah caught me while I was menstruating. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Undo your hair and comb it, leave your Umrah and enter ihram for Hajj. Then when it was the night of al-Hasbah, he commanded me and I performed Umrah in place of my Umrah which I had left."
"26615","Rawh narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I asked Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast a whole month? She said: I did not know him to have fasted a whole month until he broke fast from it except Ramadan, nor to have broken fast for a whole month until he fasted from it, until he passed away (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"26616","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abi Hassan al-Araj, that two men entered upon Aishah and said: Abu Hurayrah narrates that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Omens are only in the woman, the mount, and the house. He said: Then a part of her flew to the sky and a part to the earth, and she said: By the One Who sent down the Quran upon Abi al-Qasim, he did not say it like that; rather the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The people of Jahiliyyah used to say: Omens are in the woman, the house, and the mount. Then Aishah recited: No calamity strikes on the earth nor in yourselves except in a Book, to the end of the verse."
"26617","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah narrated to us, from Budayl, from Abdillah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from a woman among them called Umm Kulthum, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eating with six of his Companions, then a hungry Bedouin came and ate it in two mouthfuls. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he mentioned the name of Allah it would have sufficed you. When one of you eats, let him mention the name of Allah; if he forgets to mention Allah at its beginning, let him say: In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end."
"26618","Rawh narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Nafi, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that she informed him that she bought a cushion with images on it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it, he stood at the door and did not enter. I recognized displeasure on his face, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I repent to Allah and to His Messenger; what have I done wrong? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with this cushion? I said: I bought it for you to sit on and recline on. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The makers of these images will be punished for them; it will be said to them: Give life to what you created. And he said: The house in which there is an image, the angels do not enter it."
"26619","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Aba Abdillah, meaning al-Jadali, saying: I asked the Mother of the Believers, Aishah, about the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He was not obscene, nor deliberately obscene, nor loud in the markets; rather he pardoned and overlooked."
"26620","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Ubayd narrated to me, from Nafi, he said, meaning Aba Asim; my father said: And I do not know who he is, meaning this Nafi. He said: I used to trade to al-Sham or to Egypt. He said: So I prepared for Iraq, and I entered upon Aishah, Mother of the Believers, and said: O Mother of the Believers, I have prepared for Iraq. She said: What is with you and your trade? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If one of you has provision in something, let him not leave it until it changes for him or becomes unfamiliar to him. So I went to Iraq, then I entered upon her and said: O Mother of the Believers, by Allah, I did not return the capital. So she repeated the hadith to him, or said: The hadith is as I narrated to you."
"26621","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"26622","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I known beforehand of my affair what I know now, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal, and I would have exited ihram with those who exited it for Umrah."
"26623","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that al-Hawla bint Tuwayt passed by Aishah while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with her. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is al-Hawla, and they claim she does not sleep at night. He said: She does not sleep at night? Take of deeds what you can bear, for by Allah, Allah does not tire until you tire."
"26624","My father said: Wahb narrated it to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Numan, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: al-Hawla bint Tuwayt ibn Habib ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza passed, and he mentioned it, and said: For Allah does not tire until you tire."
"26625","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri; Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said: Aishah informed me that al-Hawla bint Tuwayt ibn Habib ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza, and he mentioned the hadith."
"26626","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in disobedience to Allah, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"26627","He narrated to us."
"26628","Uthman narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling and two sucklings do not make unlawful."
"26629","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, Abdillah ibn Umar was informed, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Have you not seen that when your people built the Kabah they fell short of the foundations of Ibrahim? I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not return it upon the foundations of Ibrahim? He said: Were it not that your people are recent in disbelief. Ibn Umar said: If Aishah heard this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I do not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving touching the two corners adjacent to the Hijr except that the House was not completed upon the foundations of Ibrahim."
"26630","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing at the door of my room while the Abyssinians were playing with their spears, shielding me with his cloak so I could watch their play; then he kept standing until I was the one who turned away."
"26631","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would put his head into my room while he was in the mosque, and I would comb it; and he would not enter the house except for a need, except when he wanted ablution, while he was in itikaf."
"26632","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Usamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his mother Asma bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived from a journey, and I had bought a curtain with an image on it and hung it over a recess of my house. When he entered he disliked what I had done and said: Do you cover the walls, O Aishah? So I took it down and cut it into two cushions, and I saw him reclining upon one of them, and on it was an image."
"26633","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar informed me, he said: My father informed me, from Hamzah ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr; and Muhammad ibn Bakr said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar informed us, he said: My father informed me, from Hamzah ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No harm befalls the believer except that it brings him reward or expiation, even a stumble and a thorn."
"26634","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while a Jewish woman was with her, saying: Have you been told that you will be tried in the graves? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was startled and said: Only the Jews will be tried. Aishah said: We stayed some nights, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been told that it has been revealed to me that you will be tried in the graves. And Aishah said: Afterwards I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking refuge from the punishment of the grave."
"26635","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray eleven rakahs at night; that was his prayer: he would prostrate in one prostration of it the length of what one of you recites fifty verses before raising his head, and he would pray two rakahs before Fajr, then lie on his right side until the caller of prayer came to him."
"26636","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command fasting Ashura before Ramadan was revealed; then when Ramadan was made obligatory, whoever wished fasted and whoever wished broke fast."
"26637","Uthman narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salamah, that Aishah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to give his wives the choice, he began with me and said: O Aishah, I mention a matter to you, and it is no harm to you not to hasten until you consult your parents. She said: And he knew that my parents would not command me to separate from him. Then he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: O Prophet, say to your wives: If you desire the life of this world and its adornment, until he reached: has prepared for the doers of good among you a great reward. I said: In which of this should I consult my parents? For I have chosen Allah and His Messenger and the Abode of the Hereafter. She said: Then the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did what I did."
"26638","Uthman narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri; I found in one place from Urwah and in another place from Amrah, both of them Uthman said it, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives in the Farewell Hajj."
"26639","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that believing women would attend Fajr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return wrapped in their cloaks to their houses, unrecognized in the darkness."
"26640","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray upon a prayer mat, and said: O Aishah, remove this mat of yours from us, for I feared it would tempt people."
"26641","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Abu Shaddad narrated to us, from Mujahid, he said: Aishah said: We set out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we were at al-Hurr we turned, and I was upon a camel, and that was the last contact with them, and I was hearing the voice of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was among those acacia trees, saying: O my bride! She said: By Allah, I was in that state when a caller called: Drop the rein. So I dropped it, and Allah restrained it by His hand."
"26642","Sulayman ibn Dawud, meaning Aba Dawud al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, he said: I heard Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah narrating from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer in his illness in which he died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in front of Abu Bakr praying with the people sitting, while Abu Bakr prayed with the people and the people behind him."
"26643","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Musa; my father said: Rather it is Abdillah ibn Abi Qays, and that is correct, a freedman of Banu Nasr ibn Muawiyah. He said: Aishah said to me: Do not abandon night prayer, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not abandon it; and when he was ill or lazy he prayed sitting."
"26644","Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said: Ubaydillah ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah: Sahlah, daughter of Suhayl ibn Amr, came and said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim used to enter upon me while I was laying aside my garment, then now he enters upon me after he has grown and matured, and I find something in myself from that. He said: Then suckle him, for that will remove what you find in yourself."
"26645","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zurarah, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is not cut except for a quarter dinar."
"26646","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Aishah, that she made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a black wool cloak and he wore it; then when he sweated he smelled the wool and cast it off. He said: And I think he said: And he liked pleasant scent."
"26647","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Kathir, from Abi Iyad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed while upon him was a wool cloak, part of it upon him and part upon her."
"26648","Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Imran ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Ayli, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that an odor be found from him which would harm others."
"26649","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Aban, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: Safiyyah bint Shaybah narrated to me, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wash with a sa and perform ablution with a mudd."
"26650","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except over a husband."
"26651","Abd al-Samad and Abu Amir both said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abi Salamah, he said: I asked Aishah about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He would pray thirteen rakahs: he would pray eight rakahs, then perform witr, then pray two rakahs while sitting; when he intended to bow he stood and bowed; and he would pray two rakahs between the call and the iqamah of the Fajr prayer."
"26652","Abd al-Samad and Abu Amir, with the same meaning, both said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abi Salamah, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fast of the year more than his fasting of Shaban, for he would fast all of Shaban. And he would say: Take of deeds what you can bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire. And the most beloved deed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was what one persisted in, even if little; when he prayed a prayer he persisted in it."
"26653","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: We would garland sheep and send them, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a state of permissibility, nothing of it forbidden to him."
"26654","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Yazid, meaning al-Rishk, narrated to us, from Muadhah, she said: A woman asked Aishah, while I was present, about the continuous fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said to her: Do you act as he acts? For what came before of his sin and what comes after had been forgiven him, and his deed was supererogatory for him."
"26655","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Umm al-Hasan narrated to me; Abd al-Samad said: She is the grandmother of Abu Bakr al-Ataki; from Muadhah, she said: I asked Aishah about the menstruating woman whose garment is stained with blood. She said: I would menstruate in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for three cycles altogether without washing a garment of mine. And she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray with a garment upon me, part of it upon him and part upon me, while I was menstruating, sleeping near him."
"26656","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Qasim, meaning Ibn al-Fadl, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, from Aishah, that she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever borrows from people a debt, Allah knowing from him that he is keen to repay it, will have with him help and protection from Allah. And I seek that help."
"26657","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Umm Nahar bint Difa narrated to me, she said: Aminah bint Abdillah narrated to me that she witnessed Aishah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to curse the woman who peels the skin, the one whose skin is peeled, the tattooer, the one tattooed, the woman who joins hair, and the one whose hair is joined."
"26658","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, narrated to us, he said: I asked Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad about perfume for one in ihram. He said: My father al-Aswad informed me, from Aishah, that she said: It is as if I am looking at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram."
"26659","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Fatimah bint Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, she said: My mother narrated to me that she said: I asked Aishah, and her uncle sent her, saying: One of your sons sends you greetings of peace and asks you about Uthman ibn Affan, for people have reviled him. She said: May Allah curse whoever curses him. By Allah, he was sitting with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leaning his back upon me, while Jibril was revealing the Quran to him, and he was saying to him: Write, O Uthaym. Allah would not have given him that station except as one honored by Allah and His Messenger."
"26660","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: Most of the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting, except the prescribed prayer; and the most beloved deeds to him were what a person persisted in, even if little."
"26661","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Zayd, meaning Ibn Murrah Abu al-Mualla, narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted, of the harmful creatures, for a man in ihram to kill: the snake, the scorpion, the vicious dog, the spotted crow, the kite, and the mouse. And a scorpion stung the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he commanded killing it while he was in ihram."
"26662","Abd al-Samad and Affan both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umm Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion and Your obedience. It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Affan said: So Aishah said to him: You often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion and Your obedience. He said: What would make me feel secure? Hearts of servants are between the fingers of the Most Merciful; when He intends to turn the heart of a servant, He turns it. Affan said: Between two fingers of the fingers of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"26663","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hafsah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us regarding the fara: from every five sheep, a sheep; and commanded us to sacrifice for a girl a sheep and for a boy two sheep."
"26664","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah raises for one of you a date and a morsel as one of you raises his foal or his young camel, until it becomes like Uhud."
"26665","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abu Husayn narrated to us, from Abi Salih, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed while upon him was a garment, part of it upon me."
"26666","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah, he said: I entered upon Aishah and said: Will you not narrate to me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became heavy, and said: Have the people prayed? We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Put water for me in the washbasin. So we did, and he washed, then went to rise and fainted, then recovered and said: Have the people prayed? We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Put water for me in the washbasin. So we did, and he washed, then went to rise and fainted, then recovered and said: Have the people prayed? We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah. She said: And the people were gathered in the mosque waiting for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the Isha prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Abu Bakr that he lead the people in prayer; and Abu Bakr was a tender man, so he said: O Umar, lead the people in prayer. He said: You are more entitled to that. So Abu Bakr led them in prayer those days. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found some lightness, and came out between two men, one of them al-Abbas, for the Zhuhr prayer. When Abu Bakr saw him he went to step back, so he gestured to him not to step back, and commanded them, and they seated him beside him. Abu Bakr prayed standing while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed sitting. Then I entered upon Ibn Abbas and said: Shall I not present to you what Aishah narrated to me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Go ahead. So I narrated to him, and he did not deny anything of it, except that he said: Did she name for you the man who was with al-Abbas? I said: No. He said: He is Ali."
"26667","Abd al-Samad and Muawiyah ibn Amr both said: Zaidah narrated to us, Musa ibn Abi Aishah narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah, he said: I entered upon Aishah and said to her: Will you not narrate to me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became heavy, then he mentioned the hadith, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him not to step back; Muawiyah said: Step back; and said to them: Seat me beside him. So they seated him beside him. She said: Abu Bakr prayed while standing, following the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people prayed following the prayer of Abu Bakr, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting."
"26668","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi al-Furat, narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Aishah, that she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the plague. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that it was a punishment Allah sends upon whom He wills, then He made it a mercy for the believers. No man stricken by plague who stays in his house patiently, seeking reward, knowing that nothing befalls him except what Allah decreed for him, except that he will have the like of the reward of a martyr."
"26669","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended to wash from janabah, would perform ablution as his ablution for prayer, then pour upon his head three times, running his fingers through the roots of his hair."
"26670","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Harb narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari narrated to me that Amrah informed him that Aishah, Mother of the Believers, narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is cut for a quarter dinar."
"26671","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Harb narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Imran ibn Hittan, that Aishah, Mother of the Believers, informed him; my father said: And Abu Amir, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Imran ibn Hittan, that Aishah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not leave in his house a garment with a cross-like figure except that he removed it. Abd al-Samad said in his hadith, he said: And silk had mixed with our garments."
"26672","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Harb narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Imran ibn Hittan, that Aishah, Mother of the Believers, informed him; my father said: And Abu Amir, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Imran ibn Hittan, that Aishah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not leave in his house a garment with a cross-like figure except that he removed it. Abd al-Samad said in his hadith, he said: And silk had mixed with our garments."
"26673","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, that Abu Salamah narrated to him, and there was between him and his people a dispute over land, that he entered upon Aishah and mentioned that to her. She said: O Aba Salamah, avoid the land, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land will be encircled with it from seven earths."
"26674","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi, meaning Ibn Habib al-Hanafi, narrated to me, he said: I heard Aba Said al-Raqashi saying: I asked Aishah about nabidh of the earthen jar, and she brought out to me a jar from behind the curtain and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked what is made in this."
"26675","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abi Salamah, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss me while he was fasting."
"26676","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman and al-Mundhir ibn Abi al-Mundhir, from Abi Salamah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the moon and said: O Aishah, seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this, for this is the darkening night when it settles."
"26677","Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Abdillah, from the descendants of Zayd ibn Thabit, narrated to us, from Abi al-Rijal, from his mother Amrah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The surplus of water in a well is not to be withheld."
"26678","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out to al-Baqi and supplicate for them. Aishah asked him about that, and he said: I have been commanded to supplicate for them."
"26679","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse a people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"26680","Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, and Abdillah narrated to us, he said: al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ashath, from al-Hasan, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade celibacy. Abdillah said: Then my father narrated it to me, and said: I did not hear it from Yahya."
"26681","Abdillah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, Hatim ibn Abi Saghirah narrated to us, from Abi Qazaah, that Abd al-Malik, while circumambulating the House, said: May Allah destroy Ibn al-Zubayr for lying about the Mother of the Believers, saying: I heard her saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, were it not that your people are recent in disbelief, I would have opened the House; my father said: al-Ansari said: I would have demolished the House until I added to it from the Hijr, for your people fell short in building. Al-Harith ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Rabiah said: Do not say this, O Commander of the Believers, for I heard the Mother of the Believers narrating this. He said: Had I heard this before I demolished it, I would have left it upon the building of Ibn al-Zubayr."
"26682","Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Qays informed us, he said: Ata informed me, he said: Aishah informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), after the Asr prayer, did not enter upon her except that he prayed two rakahs with her."
"26683","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Ayyash narrated to us: Was it not mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he would wake junub, then wash and fast? Sufyan said: Hammad narrated it to me, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah."
"26684","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out with his Companions seeing it as nothing but Hajj. When he circumambulated the House and commanded his Companions and they circumambulated, he commanded them and they exited ihram. She said: And I had menstruated, so I observed all the stations except circumambulating the House. I said: They return with Umrah and Hajj while I return with Hajj. She said: So he sent my brother with me, and I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascending at dawn toward the people of Madinah while I was descending at dawn toward the people of Makkah."
"26685","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I used to twist the garlands for the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would remain; she said: And he would gift sheep."
"26686","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sleep at the beginning of the night and enliven its end."
"26687","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Hasan narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not perform ablution after the ritual bath."
"26688","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray at night until the last of his prayer was the witr."
"26689","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray nine rakahs at night."
"26690","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Mufaddal narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: We set out intending Hajj and I did not circumambulate. I said: They return, O Messenger of Allah, with Umrah and Hajj while I return with Hajj. She said: Safiyyah said: I do not see myself except detaining you. He said: May you be barren and shaven. He said: Did you circumambulate on the Day of Sacrifice? She said: Yes. She said: So he commanded her and she departed."
"26691","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Mufaddal narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), since there was revealed upon him: When the help of Allah and the victory comes, praying a prayer except that he supplicated and said: Glory be to You, my Lord, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me."
"26692","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I saw the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram."
"26693","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I would perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the best perfume I could find, until I would see the glisten of perfume on his head and his beard before he entered ihram."
"26694","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that Safiyyah menstruated before the departure, and she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Had you circumambulated the circumambulation of the Day of Sacrifice? She said: Yes. So he commanded her to depart, and she departed."
"26695","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not hasten to anything as he hastened to the two rakahs before Fajr."
"26696","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Khasif, he said: A man narrated to me thirty years ago, from Aishah, she said: I combed my hair with a severe combing, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Aishah, do you not know that upon every hair is janabah?"
"26697","Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, he said: I asked Aishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), how he used to pray. She said: He would pray the midday prayer, then pray two rakahs after it."
"26698","Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from al-Miqdam, from his father, that he asked Aishah what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would do before going out. She said: He would pray the two rakahs before Fajr, then go out to prayer; and when he entered he would use the siwak."
"26699","Abdillah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the two rakahs of Fajr, he would lie on his right side."
"26700","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend the night junub, then Bilal would come to him and announce the prayer to him, so he would rise and wash; I would look at the trickling of water in his hair and skin, then he would go out and I would hear his voice in the Fajr prayer, then he would remain fasting."
"26701","Asbat narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would remain fasting, not minding whatever of my face he kissed, until he broke his fast."
"26702","Asbat narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted ruqyah for every poisonous bite."
"26703","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Nubayh saying: I heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whatever is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire."
"26704","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Wail narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Bahiyy narrating that Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never sent Zayd ibn Harithah out with an army except that he put him in command over them, and if he remained after him he appointed him as his successor."
"26705","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: Some people argued and the tent rope struck the eye of one of them, so they laughed, so Aisha said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There is no believer pricked by a thorn or anything greater except that Allah removes a sin from him for it and raises him a degree by it."
"26706","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muti al-Ghazzal narrated to us, from Kardus, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away on his way and his family never ate their fill for three days of wheat food."
"26707","Rawh narrated to us, Aban ibn Samaa narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Aisha narrated to me that she used to perform ghusl with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a single vessel."
"26708","Arim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Abi Humayd, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in his illness from which he did not recover: May Allah curse the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques. He said: And Aisha said: Had it not been for that, his grave would have been made prominent, but it was feared that it would be taken as a mosque."
"26709","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded the wife of Abu Hudhayfah and she suckled Salim five breastfeedings, and he would enter upon her by that suckling."
"26710","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, that she heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only passed by a Jewish woman who was being wept over and said: You are weeping over her while she is being punished in her grave."
"26711","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray while my leg was in his qiblah; when he wanted to prostrate he nudged me and I drew it in, and when he stood I extended it."
"26712","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Kaysan informed me, he said: Muadhah narrated to me, she said: I heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The passing away of my ummah is by piercing and plague. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, this piercing we have known, so what is plague? He said: A swelling like the swelling of camels; the one who remains in it is like a martyr, and the one who flees from it is like the one who flees from battle."
"26713","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Kaysan informed me, he said: Amrah al-Adawiyyah narrated to me, she said: I heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The one who flees from plague is like the one who flees from battle."
"26714","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only forbade prayer that the rising of the sun and its setting be singled out for it."
"26715","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aisha, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he performed witr would pray two rakahs while sitting."
"26716","Abu Said, mawla of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Talhah ibn Shajjah narrated to us, he said: Warqa bint Hudham al-Hunaiyyah narrated to me, she said: I heard Aisha saying: I would sometimes see janabah on the garment of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I would rub it off."
"26717","Abu Said, mawla of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Talhah narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to me that Aisha said: I heard Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever has a debt and is concerned to repay it, or intends to repay it, there will remain with him a guard from Allah."
"26718","Abu Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would strive in the last ten nights what he would not strive in others."
"26719","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he was ill would recite over himself with the two Muawwidhatayn and blow. Aisha said: So when he became seriously ill I would blow over him with them and wipe with his right hand seeking its blessing."
"26720","Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali and Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr narrated to me, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Aisha, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would kiss while fasting. Abu al-Mundhir said: In Ramadan."
"26721","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad: He was asked about a man who bequeathed three dwellings of his, so al-Qasim said: That is taken out until it is put into one dwelling. And I heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does a deed upon which our command is not, it is rejected."
"26722","Hammad narrated to us, Aflah narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would enter the morning while junub then he would perform ghusl and fast his day."
"26723","Hammad and Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahid, mawla of Urwah, narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah Almighty said: Whoever humiliates a friend of Mine has made war with Me lawful, and My servant does not draw near to Me with anything like performing the obligations, and the servant continues to draw near to Me with supererogatory acts until I love him; if he asks Me I give him, and if he supplicates to Me I answer him. I have not hesitated over anything I do as I hesitate over his death, for he dislikes death and I dislike his distress. My father said: And Abu al-Mundhir said: Urwah narrated to me, he said: Aisha narrated to me. And Abu al-Mundhir said: harms Me."
"26724","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, she said: I was asked what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do in his house? She said: He was a human from humans; he would clean his garment and milk his sheep and serve himself."
"26725","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abdullah, from his brother Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a man who finds wetness and does not remember a wet dream; he said: He should perform ghusl. And about a man who sees that he had a wet dream but sees no wetness; he said: No ghusl upon him. So Umm Sulaym said: Is there anything upon the woman who sees that? He said: Yes; women are only the counterparts of men."
"26726","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Ibn Shihab and Salih ibn Abi Hassan, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would kiss while fasting."
"26727","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited this verse: He is the One who sent down upon you the Book; of it are verses precise, they are the foundation of the Book, and others ambiguous. As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is ambiguous of it, seeking discord and seeking its interpretation, and none knows its interpretation except Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you see those who follow what is ambiguous of it, those are the ones whom Allah named, or: then they are they, so beware of them."
"26728","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, she said: Al-Harith ibn Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, how does revelation come to you? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and it is the hardest upon me, then it leaves me and I have understood what he said, and sometimes the angel comes to me in the form of a man and speaks to me and I understand what he says. Aisha said: And I saw him with it descending upon him on a severely cold day, then it left him and his forehead was dripping with sweat."
"26729","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to me, from Harmalah al-Misri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, whoever is in charge of anything of my ummah and is gentle with them, be gentle with him, and whoever causes hardship upon them, cause hardship upon him."
"26730","Amir ibn Salih, of the descendants of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aisha, from al-Harith ibn Hisham, that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, how revelation comes to you? And he mentioned similar to the hadith of Malik."
"26731","Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Aflah informed me, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was with his wife then entered the morning and performed ghusl and prayed and fasted his day."
"26732","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak, meaning Ibn Uthman, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: Most of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he became heavy and bulky was while sitting."
"26733","Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One of you is approached by Satan and he says: Who created you? So he says: Allah. Then he says: Who created Allah? If one of you finds that, let him recite: I believe in Allah and His messengers, for that will remove it from him."
"26734","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Nubayh saying: I heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whatever is below the two ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire."
"26735","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, he said: I said to Aisha: Inform me of some of the supplication of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: He used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I did and from the evil of what I did not do."
"26736","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Samaa narrated to us, he said: My mother narrated to me, she said: I heard Aisha saying: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to forbid tattooing and hair joining and mutual hair joining and eyebrow plucking and mutual eyebrow plucking."
"26737","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It does not harm a woman that she stops between two houses of the Ansar or stops between her parents."
"26738","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that he informed him several times that Aisha informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: Whatever thorn or more befalls the Muslim is expiation for him."
"26739","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not speak rapidly like this speech of yours; he spoke with speech between which there was a pause, memorized by whoever heard it."
"26740","Arim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Malik, from Abu al-Jawza, from Aisha, that she was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey and she cursed a camel of hers, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered that it be sent back and said: Nothing cursed shall accompany me."
"26741","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Asim, mawla of Quraybah, from Quraybah bint Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wisal. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, but you perform wisal. He said: I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"26742","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Harmalah al-Misri narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah al-Mahri, he said: I entered upon Aisha and she said: Who are you? So I said: I am a man from the people of Egypt. Then he mentioned a story. So she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O Allah, whoever is in charge of the affair of my ummah and is gentle with them, be gentle with him, and whoever causes hardship upon them, cause hardship upon him."
"26743","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not perform wudu after ghusl."
"26744","Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Imran ibn Bashir, from Salim Sabalan, he said: We went out with Aisha to Makkah, and she would go out with Abu Yahya al-Taymi leading her in prayer. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr caught up with us and performed wudu poorly, so Aisha said to him: O Abd al-Rahman, perform wudu fully, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"26745","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from Aisha, she said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me: if I coincide with Laylat al-Qadr, what should I say in it? He said: Say: O Allah, You are Pardoning, You love pardon."
"26746","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Amr ibn Maymun, he said: I asked Aisha about a man who kisses while fasting. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would kiss while fasting."
"26747","Hashim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"26748","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Aisha - he claimed that he heard it from her - that she saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicating raising his hands, saying: O Allah, I am a human, so do not punish me: whichever man of the believers I harmed and reviled, do not punish me for it."
"26749","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, that Sad ibn Hisham narrated to him from Aisha - he heard it from her - she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, missed standing at night, his eyes overcome by sleep or pain, he would pray twelve rakahs during the day."
"26750","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ayyub, meaning Ibn Thabit, narrated to us, he said: Umm Dawud narrated to me, from Aisha, she said: I used to perfume the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his Hajj and his Umrah with the best I could find."
"26751","Yunus narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Mansur al-Hajabi, he said: My mother Safiyyah bint Shaybah narrated to me, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would recline in my lap while I was menstruating and recite the Quran."
"26752","Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray al-Subh and the believing women would leave wrapped in their murut, not recognized due to darkness, or he said: none of them recognizing the others."
"26753","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Five vicious creatures are killed in the Haram: the mouse, the scorpion, the crow, the kite, and the vicious dog."
"26754","He said: Yunus narrated to us, he said: Aban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he entered upon Aisha while disputing over a house, so Aisha said: O Abu Salamah, avoid the land, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wrongs a handspan of land will be encircled with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."
"26755","Hudbah narrated to us, he said: Aban al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"26756","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Safiyyah bint al-Harith, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The prayer of a menstruating woman is not accepted except with a khimar."
"26757","Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, that Umm Salamah said - Hasan said: from Umm Salamah, she said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was lying in my house, he suddenly sat up startled while saying istirja, so I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, what is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah, that you say istirja? He said: An army of my ummah coming from Sham heading to the House for a man whom Allah protects from them, until when they are at al-Bayda of Dhu al-Hulayfah they will be swallowed, and their sources are various. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, how will they all be swallowed while their sources are various? So he said: Among them is one who was coerced; among them is one who was coerced - three times."
"26758","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Yusuf ibn Sad, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"26759","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Yusuf ibn Sad, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha, with the like of it."
"26760","Yaqub narrated to us, and he said: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Aisha, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Five of the animals, all of them vicious, are killed in the Haram: the crow, the snake, the scorpion, the vicious dog, and the kite. And in the book of Yaqub in another place, in place of the snake, the mouse."
"26761","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If one of you feels sleep while praying, let him sleep until his sleep goes away; one of you may go to seek forgiveness from Allah and end up reviling himself."
"26762","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me in my house in an izar and a rida, faced the qiblah and extended his hand, then said: O Allah, I am only a human, so whichever servant of Your servants I reviled or harmed, do not punish me for it."
"26763","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Amr, from al-Muttalib, that Abdullah ibn Amir sent to Aisha maintenance and clothing, so she said to his messenger: O my son, I do not accept anything from anyone. When he left she said: Bring him back to me. So they brought him back, so she said: I remembered something the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me. He said: O Aisha, whoever gives you a gift without asking, accept it, for it is only provision Allah presented to you."
"26764","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray while I was lying across in front of him like a funeral bier, until when he wanted to perform witr he touched me with his foot and I knew he would perform witr, so I moved back somewhat from before him."
"26765","Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no marriage except with a wali, and the ruler is the wali of one who has no wali."
"26766","Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was junub and wanted to sleep, he would perform wudu."
"26767","Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Abdullah al-Madini and others, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, be gentle with whoever is gentle with my ummah and cause hardship upon whoever causes hardship upon it."
"26768","Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered in the year of the Conquest from Thaniyyat al-Idhkhir."
"26769","Yunus and Hasan narrated to us, they said: Mahdi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, that she was asked what the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do in his house? She said: He used to sew his garment and repair his sandal. She said: And he used to do what men do in their houses."
"26770","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived at Madinah while it was unhealthy; it was mentioned that fever struck them, so Abu Bakr fell ill, and when fever seized him he would say: Every man is greeted in the morning among his family while death is nearer than the strap of his sandal. She said: And Bilal, when fever seized him, would say: Would that I knew whether I will spend a night in a valley with idhkhir and jalil around me, and whether I will one day come to the waters of Majannah, and whether Shamah and Tafil will appear to me. O Allah, curse Utbah ibn Rabiah and Shaybah ibn Rabiah and Umayyah ibn Khalaf as they expelled us from Makkah. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw what befell them he said: O Allah, make Madinah beloved to us as our love for Makkah or more. O Allah, make it healthy and bless for us in its sa and its mudd, and transfer its fever to al-Juhfah. He said: So the newborn would be born at al-Juhfah and would not reach puberty until fever struck him."
"26771","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived at Madinah, Abu Bakr and Bilal fell ill, then he mentioned the hadith, meaning the hadith of Hammad, except that he did not mention the story of the newborn."
"26772","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, all my companions have a kunyah except me. He said: Take kunyah by your son Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. So she was called Umm Abdullah until she died."
"26773","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Amr, meaning Ibn Malik, from Abu al-Jawza, that Aisha said: I used to seek refuge for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a supplication when he was ill; Jibril used to seek refuge for him with it and supplicate for him with it when he was ill. She said: So I went to seek refuge for him with it: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, in Your hand is healing, there is no healer but You, heal with a healing that leaves no illness. She said: So I went to supplicate for him with it in his illness in which he died, so he said: Lift it from me. She said: It only used to benefit me in the period."
"26774","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Five vicious creatures are killed in the Haram: the scorpion, the mouse, the kite, the crow, and the vicious dog."
"26775","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not pray over Suhayl Ibn al-Bayda except in the mosque."
"26776","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Nothing befalls the Muslim, even the thorn he is pricked with, except that it reduces his sins."
"26777","Yunus narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Yashkuri narrated to us, he said: I heard my mother narrating that her mother went to the House for Hajj while the House at that time had two doors. She said: So when I finished my tawaf I entered upon Aisha. She said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, one of your sons sends you greetings of peace, and the people have spoken much about Uthman, so what do you say about him? She said: May Allah curse whoever curses him; I think she said it three times. I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with his thigh resting against Uthman, and I was wiping sweat from the forehead of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while revelation was descending upon him, and he married him two of his daughters, one after the other, and he would say: Write, Uthman. She said: Allah would not bring a servant of His close to His Prophet in such a position except a servant who is noble to Him."
"26778","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in itikaf in the mosque and would bring out his head and I would wash it with khitmi while I was menstruating."
"26779","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umm Muhammad, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was gifted a necklace of onyx and said: I shall give it to the most beloved of my family to me. So the women said: The daughter of Abu Quhafah has gone with it. So he hung it on the neck of Umamah bint Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"26780","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shumaysah, from Aisha, that a camel of Safiyyah became ill and with Zaynab was surplus of camels, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Zaynab: The camel of Safiyyah has become ill; if only you would give her a camel. She said: Should I give that Jewish woman? So he abandoned her and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became angry for two or three months until she raised her bed and thought that he would not be pleased with her. She said: Then one day at midday I saw his shadow, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered, so she put back her bed."
"26781","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: When these verses were revealed: You may defer whom you will of them and take to yourself whom you will, Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not see your Lord except hastening in your desire."
"26782","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha, she said: I raced the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I outran him."
"26783","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Budayl, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he recited standing would bow standing, and when he recited sitting would bow sitting."
"26784","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would go out to Fajr prayer with his head dripping from intercourse, not a wet dream."
"26785","Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us in the year one hundred and seventy-seven, from al-Amash, from Habib, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet and said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer prolonged bleeding. He said: Leave prayer the days of your menstruation, then perform ghusl and perform wudu for every prayer, even if it drips onto the mat."
"26786","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abu Yunus al-Qushayri narrated to us, he said: Abu Qazaah narrated to me that Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, while circumambulating the House, said: May Allah fight Ibn al-Zubayr, how he lies about the Mother of the Believers and claims that he heard her while she says: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Aisha, were it not that your people are recent in disbelief, I would have demolished the House until I added to it from al-Hijr; your people fell short in building. He said: So al-Harith ibn Abdullah said to him: Do not say this, O Commander of the Believers, for I heard Aisha saying it. He said: You heard it? He said: I heard it. He said: Had I heard this before I demolished it, I would have left it upon what Ibn al-Zubayr built."
"26787","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would often pray standing and sitting; when he prayed standing he would bow standing, and when he prayed sitting he would bow sitting."
"26788","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muti ibn Maymun al-Anbari, kunya Abu Said, narrated to us, he said: Safiyyah bint Ismah narrated to me, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, she said: A woman extended her hand from behind the curtain with a book to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, withdrew his hand and said: I do not know, is it the hand of a man or the hand of a woman? So she said: Rather a woman. So he said: If you were a woman you would have changed your nails with henna."
"26789","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, she said: As if I am looking at myself twisting the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of sheep, then he does not refrain from anything."
"26790","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, that the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died wanted to send Uthman to Abu Bakr asking him their inheritance from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So Aisha said to them: Has he not said - the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We are not inherited; what we left is charity."
"26791","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Amrah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would bring his head close to me and I would comb it while I was menstruating and he was in itikaf, and he would not enter the house except for human need."
"26792","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was never given choice between two matters except he took the easier of them, so long as it was not sin; if it was sin he was the farthest of people from it. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never took revenge for himself, except that the sanctity of Allah be violated, then he would take revenge for Allah Almighty."
"26793","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he complained would recite over himself with the Muawwidhat and blow; when his pain became severe I would recite over him and wipe from him with his hand hoping for its blessing."
"26794","Amr ibn Ayyub al-Mawsili narrated to us, from Jafar, from al-Zuhri - and Kathir said: Jafar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: He would see it on the mirt of one of us then rub it off - meaning semen - and their murut at that time were wool - meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"26795","Abu Qatan narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: I used to rub semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then I would not wash it. Abu Qatan said: She once said: its trace, and once said: its place."
"26796","Abu Qatan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Aisha, the like of its meaning."
"26797","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: Hafsah and I were fasting, and food we desired was presented to us and we ate from it. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, so Hafsah hastened to him before me - and she was her father's daughter - she said: O Messenger of Allah, we were fasting today and food we desired was presented to us and we ate from it. He said: Make up another day in its place."
"26798","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: Misar narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Hasan, from Ibn Maqil, from Aisha, that she owed a slave from the children of Ismail to free; captives came from Yemen from Khawlan and she wanted to free from them, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade me. Then captives came from Mudar from Banu al-Anbar, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded her to free from them."
"26799","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Said ibn Iyas al-Jurayri, from Abu Abdullah al-Jasri, he said: I entered upon Aisha and with her was Hafsah bint Umar, and she said to me: This is Hafsah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then she turned to her and said: I ask you by Allah to confirm me if I told a lie I said or belie me if I told a truth I said: Do you know that you and I were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he fainted, so I said to you: Do you think he has passed away? You said: I do not know. Then he recovered and said: Open the door for him. Then he fainted, so I said to you: Do you think he has passed away? You said: I do not know. Then he recovered and said: Open the door for him. So I said to you: Your father or my father? You said: I do not know. Then we opened the door and there was Uthman ibn Affan. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw him he said: Bring him near. So he leaned over him and told him secretly something - neither I nor you know what it is. Then he raised his head and said: Did you understand what I said to you? He said: Yes. He said: Bring him near. So he leaned over him another time like it and told him secretly something we do not know what it is. Then he raised his head and said: Did you understand what I said to you? He said: Yes. He said: Bring him near. So he leaned over him with a strong leaning and told him secretly something. Then he raised his head and said: Did you understand what I said to you? He said: Yes, my ears heard it and my heart retained it. So he said to him: Go out. He said: Hafsah said: O Allah, yes - or she said: O Allah, truth."
"26800","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif ibn Abi Tarif informed us, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would remain fasting and kiss whatever of my face he wished until he broke his fast."
"26801","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Ja'far narrated to us, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about a man who gives his wife a choice and she chooses him. He said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: I am going to present a matter to you, and you need not hasten until you consult your parents. I said: What is this matter? She said: Then he recited to me: O Prophet, say to your wives: If you desire the life of this world and its adornment, then come, I will provide for you and release you with a pleasant release. And if you desire Allah and His Messenger and the home of the Hereafter, then indeed Allah has prepared for the doers of good among you a great reward. She said: So I said: In which of this do you command me to consult my parents? Rather I desire Allah and His Messenger and the home of the Hereafter. She said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pleased with that and it delighted him, and he said: I will present to your companions what I presented to you. And he used to say to them as he said to Aishah, then he would say: Aishah has chosen Allah and His Messenger and the home of the Hereafter. Aishah said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us a choice, and we did not consider that a divorce."
"26802","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, she said: I saw the glistening of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after three days, while he was in ihram."
"26803","Ali narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: I saw the glistening of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram."
"26804","Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from Abu al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began the prayer standing he prayed standing, and when he began the prayer sitting he prayed sitting."
"26805","Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, the brother of Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Breaking the bone of the believer when dead is like breaking his bone when alive."
"26806","Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: Makhul narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three Yemeni garments of ribbed cloth."
"26807","Umar Abu Hafs al-Mu'ayti narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys while I was a young girl, I had not carried flesh nor become heavy. So he said to the people: Go ahead, and they went ahead. Then he said to me: Come, that I may race you. So I raced him and I outran him. Then he remained silent toward me until, when I had carried flesh and become heavy and had forgotten, I went out with him on one of his journeys, and he said to the people: Go ahead, and they went ahead. Then he said: Come, that I may race you. So I raced him and he outran me. And he began laughing while saying: This is for that."
"26808","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in retreat in the mosque he would not enter the house except for a need. She said: So I washed his head while between me and him was the threshold."
"26809","Muhammad ibn Yazid, meaning al-Wasiti, narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Aishah, if you have committed a sin, then seek Allah's forgiveness, for repentance from sin is remorse and seeking forgiveness."
"26810","Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'la al-Thaqafi, narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not sleep before the Isha prayer nor stay awake after it."
"26811","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while he was fasting."
"26812","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Aishah, she said: The prayer was obligated as two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, except Maghrib, it was obligated as three because it is witr. She said: And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled he prayed the first prayer except Maghrib, and when he resided he added with every two rak'ahs two rak'ahs, except Maghrib because it is witr, and Fajr because he lengthened the recitation in it."
"26813","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Ma'shar, from al-Nakha'i, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that she said: The right hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was for his purification and for his food, and his left was for his relieving himself and whatever was of harm."
"26814","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from a man, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Aishah, similar to it."
"26815","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Ma'shar, from al-Nakha'i, from Aishah, she said: The left hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was for his relieving himself and whatever was of harm, and his right was for his ablution and for his food."
"26816","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two rak'ahs of Fajr are better than the whole world."
"26817","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Mu'adhah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Duha four rak'ahs and add whatever Allah willed."
"26818","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Mu'adhah, from Aishah, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah, from a single vessel, and in his hadith was that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to begin before her."
"26819","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, that he entered upon Aishah and said: I wish to ask you about something, but I am shy before you. So she said: Ask whatever occurs to you, for I am only your mother. So I said: O Mother of the Believers, what makes ghusl obligatory? So she said: When the two circumcised parts meet, janabah becomes obligatory. And Qatadah used to follow this hadith with that Aishah said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that, then we bathed. So I do not know whether something is in this hadith or Qatadah used to say it."
"26820","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray frequently standing and sitting; when he prayed sitting he bowed sitting, and when he prayed standing he bowed standing."
"26821","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Aishah, and he said another time, al-Khaffaf, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to attain from the heads while fasting."
"26822","And Muhammad ibn Ja'far said, meaning in his hadith, from Sa'id, from Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Abbas, and thus al-Khaffaf said another time."
"26823","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Budayl informed us, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, that a woman among them called Umm Kulthum narrated to him, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eating food with six of his companions, then a hungry Bedouin came and ate it in two bites. So he said: Had he but mentioned the name of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, it would have sufficed you. So when one of you eats, let him mention the name of Allah; if he forgets to say In the name of Allah in its beginning, let him say: In the name of Allah in its beginning and its end."
"26824","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Sa'id was asked what a man says in his bowing, so he informed us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing and his prostration: Subbuh, Quddus, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."
"26825","Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us, he said: Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, narrated to us, from Alqamah, from his mother, in a story he mentioned, so Aishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever points with a piece of iron at any of the Muslims intending to kill him, then his blood has become due."
"26826","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Dawud, from Amir, from Aishah, she said: Had the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) been concealing anything, he would have concealed this verse: And when you say to the one upon whom Allah bestowed favor and you bestowed favor: Keep your wife to yourself and fear Allah, while you conceal within yourself what Allah will disclose."
"26827","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one skilled in the Qur'an is with the noble righteous scribes, and the one who reads it and stammers in it while it is hard upon him, then for him are two rewards, twofold."
"26828","Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay' narrated to me, from Ikrimah, he said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to the cooking pot and take the foreleg from it and eat it, then pray without performing ablution."
"26829","Abidah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: Whoever wakes up junub, then there is no fast for him. So Marwan sent Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman to Aishah to ask her. So he said to her: Abu Hurayrah says: Whoever wakes up junub, then there is no fast for him. So Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to become junub then complete his fast. So he sent to Abu Hurayrah and informed him that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to become junub then complete his fast. So Abu Hurayrah desisted."
"26830","Abidah narrated to us: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Aishah, he said: Some of us said: This one informed us from you that you said the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to embrace while fasting. She said: Yes, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most controlling of you over his desire."
"26831","Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeing it as nothing but Hajj. She said: When we arrived they performed tawaf, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him exit ihram. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a sacrificial animal with him. She said: And I was menstruating, so I could not perform tawaf. Then when it was the night of al-Hasbah I said: O Messenger of Allah, your women return with Hajj and Umrah while I return with Hajj. So he said to me: Go with your brother Abd al-Rahman to al-Tan'im, then the appointment between me and you is such-and-such. She said: So I met him at night while he was descending or ascending. She said: And the daughter of Huyayy said: I see myself as nothing but detaining you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Aqra, halqa, I see you as nothing but detaining you. Have you not performed tawaf on the Day of Sacrifice? She said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Then depart."
"26832","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, and he mentioned it with its isnad and its meaning."
"26833","Abidah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, he said: She said: You have equated us with the dog and the donkey. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take the middle of the bed and pray while I was in my blanket, so I would dislike facing him, and I would slip out from the direction of his feet."
"26834","Abidah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: As if I am looking at the glistening of perfume on the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he is in ihram."
"26835","Abidah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: Some women of the people of Hims came to Aishah, so Aishah said to them: Perhaps you are among the women who enter the bathhouses. So they said to her: We do so. So Aishah said to them: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any woman who puts off her clothes in other than her husband's house has torn what is between her and Allah."
"26836","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr Muhammad narrated to me, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah, died while he was eighteen months old, and he did not pray over him."
"26837","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When they intended to wash the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they differed about him. So they said: By Allah, we do not see how we should do: shall we strip the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as we strip our dead, or shall we wash him with his clothes on him? She said: So when they differed, Allah sent drowsiness upon them until, by Allah, there was not a man among the people but his chin was in his chest, asleep. She said: Then one spoke to them from the side of the house, they not knowing who he was, and he said: Wash the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his clothes on him. She said: So they hastened to him and washed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in his shirt; water and lote-tree leaves were poured over him, and the men rubbed him through the shirt. And she used to say: Had I faced from the matter what I have now seen, none would have washed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except his wives."
"26838","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The people used to pray in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan at night in scattered groups; a man would have something of the Qur'an with him, so with him would be five or six men, or fewer than that or more, and they would pray with his prayer. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me one night of that to set up for him a mat at the door of my chamber, so I did. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to it after he had prayed the last Isha. She said: So those in the mosque gathered to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them a long night. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left and entered, leaving the mat as it was. The next morning the people spoke of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with those who were with him in the mosque that night. She said: And the mosque was crowded with people in the evening. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them the last Isha, then entered his house, while the people remained. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What is the matter with the people, O Aishah? She said: So I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, the people heard of your prayer last night with those in the mosque, so they gathered for that, that you pray with them. She said: So he said: Fold up your mat from us, O Aishah. She said: So I did, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night not heedless, while the people remained in their place until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to Fajr. So she said: Then he said: O people, by Allah, I did not spend, and praise be to Allah, this night of mine heedless, nor was your place hidden from me, but I feared it would be obligated upon you. So undertake of deeds what you can bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire. He said: And Aishah used to say: The most beloved of deeds to Allah are the most constant of them, even if little."
"26839","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: Khuwaylah bint Hakim ibn Umayyah ibn Harithah ibn al-Awqas al-Sulamiyyah entered upon me, and she was with Uthman ibn Maz'un. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the shabbiness of her appearance and said to me: O Aishah, how shabby is the appearance of Khuwaylah. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman with no husband; he fasts the day and stands the night, so she is as one with no husband, thus she has neglected herself and wasted it. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Uthman ibn Maz'un, and he came to him. So he said: O Uthman, is it aversion from my sunnah? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, but it is your sunnah I seek. He said: For I sleep and pray, and fast and break fast, and marry women. So fear Allah, O Uthman, for your family has a right upon you, and your guest has a right upon you, and your self has a right upon you. So fast and break fast, and pray and sleep."
"26840","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: Al-Hawla bint Tuwayt passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, she prays much at night; when sleep overcomes her she ties herself with a rope and hangs onto it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her pray as long as she has strength for prayer; when she becomes drowsy, let her sleep."
"26841","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fast any month more than his fasting of Sha'ban; and he used to fast it, or most of it."
"26842","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abu al-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his mother Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid that the surplus water of the well be withheld."
"26843","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought from a man of the Bedouins a camel, or camels, for a wasq of stored dates, and the stored dates are ajwah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned with it to his house and sought the dates for him but did not find them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to him and said to him: O servant of Allah, we have bought from you a camel, or camels, for a wasq of stored dates, and we sought it but did not find it. He said: So the Bedouin said: O treachery! She said: So the people scolded him and said: May Allah fight you, would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commit treachery? She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for the holder of a right has a say. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to him and said: O servant of Allah, we bought your camels from you, thinking we had what we named to you, then we sought it but did not find it. So the Bedouin said: O treachery! So the people scolded him and said: May Allah fight you, would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commit treachery? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for the holder of a right has a say. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated that two or three times. Then when he saw he did not understand from him, he said to a man of his companions: Go to Khuwaylah bint Hakim ibn Umayyah and say to her: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says to you: If you have a wasq of stored dates, then lend it to us until we repay it to you, if Allah wills. So the man went to her, then the man returned and said: She said: Yes, it is with me, O Messenger of Allah, so send one to take it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: Go with it and pay him what is his. He said: So he went with it and paid him what was his. She said: Then the Bedouin passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting among his companions and said: May Allah reward you well, you have paid in full and excellently. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those are the best of Allah's servants to Allah on the Day of Resurrection: those who pay in full and excellently."
"26844","Ya'qub and Sa'd said: Our father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from Ishaq ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, from his father, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: There was in my care a young girl of the Ansar, so I married her off. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of her wedding and did not hear any amusement. So he said: O Aishah, this clan of the Ansar loves such-and-such."
"26845","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Qays al-Ansari narrated to me, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended a journey he cast lots among his wives; whichever of them her lot came out, he went out with her."
"26846","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: Sahlah bint Suhayl came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Salim was of us where you have known; we used to count him a son, and he used to enter upon me as he pleased, we not being veiled from him. Then when Allah sent down concerning him and his likes what He sent down, I noticed the face of Abu Hudhayfah when he saw him entering upon me. He said: So suckle him ten sucklings, then let him enter upon you as he pleases, for he is only your son. And Aishah used to view it as general for the Muslims, while others besides her of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) viewed that it was specific to Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, which Sahlah mentioned of his affair, as a concession for him."
"26847","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The verse of stoning and ten sucklings of the adult were sent down, and they were in a paper beneath a bed in my house. Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill we were occupied with his affair, and a small animal of ours entered and ate it."
"26848","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri and Hisham ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr both narrated to me, each narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: Barirah was with a slave, then she was freed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed her affair in her hand."
"26849","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, and Ibn Shihab narrated that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed him that Aishah, Mother of the Believers, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was covered when he died with a Yemeni hibarah garment."
"26850","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No prophet falls ill but is given a choice between this world and the Hereafter. She said: So when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill with the illness in which he was taken, he was seized by hoarseness, and I heard him saying: With those upon whom Allah has bestowed favor, of the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous. She said: So I knew that he had been given a choice."
"26851","Ya'qub and Sa'd said: Our father narrated to us, from his father, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Uthman, Sa'd said: al-Taymi, he said: I heard Aishah saying: She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to kiss me, so I said: I am fasting. So he said: And I am fasting. Then he kissed me."
"26852","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Ma'mar, he said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined toward me to kiss me. She said: So I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I am fasting. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: And I am fasting. Then he kissed me."
"26853","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Aishah, the like of it."
"26854","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from his father, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr saying: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his complaint: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, and if he stands in your place of prayer he will weep. So command Umar ibn al-Khattab to lead them in prayer. She said: So he said: Wait, command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She said: So I repeated to him, and he said: Wait, command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. She said: So I repeated to him, then she said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer; you are the companions of Yusuf."
"26855","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my lap when death came to him."
"26856","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The last sahar did not meet him with me except asleep, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"26857","Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, and he mentioned part of the hadith of al-Hudaybiyyah. He said: Muhammad ibn Muslim said: So Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to test whoever emigrated to him of the believing women with this verse, by the saying of Allah, the Exalted: O Prophet, when the believing women come to you pledging to you that they will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill their children, nor bring a slander they fabricate between their hands and their feet, nor disobey you in what is right, then accept their pledge and ask forgiveness for them from Allah; indeed Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said: Aishah said: So whoever affirmed this condition of the believing women, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: I have pledged to you, by speech. And by Allah, his hand never touched the hand of a woman at all in pledging; he pledged them only with his saying: I have pledged to you upon that."
"26858","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking refuge in his prayer from the trial of the Dajjal."
"26859","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah said: By Allah, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing at the door of my chamber while the Abyssinians were playing in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was screening me with his cloak that I might look at their play. Then he would stand for my sake until I was the one who turned away. So estimate the young girl, recent in age, eager for amusement."
"26860","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from his father, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever introduces into this affair of ours what is not of it, then it is rejected."
"26861","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Aishah, she said: Sahlah bint Suhayl ibn Amr, and she was under Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, enters upon us, while we are uncovered, and we used to view him as a son, and Abu Hudhayfah had adopted him as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had adopted Zayd. Then Allah sent down: Call them by their fathers; that is more just with Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her at that to suckle Salim. So she suckled him five sucklings, and he was in the position of her son through suckling. And by that Aishah used to command her sisters and the daughters of her sisters to suckle whoever Aishah loved to see her and enter upon her, even if grown, five sucklings, then he would enter upon her. And Umm Salamah and the rest of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused to admit upon them through that suckling anyone of the people until he suckled in the cradle. And they said to Aishah: By Allah, we do not know; perhaps it was a concession from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Salim apart from the people."
"26862","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah said: Umar ibn al-Khattab used to say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Veil your women. She said: But he did not do so. She said: And the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out at night, night after night, toward al-Manasi'. Then Sawdah bint Zam'ah went out, and she was a tall woman, so Umar saw her while he was in the mosque and said: I have recognized you, O Sawdah, out of eagerness that the veil be sent down. She said: Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, sent down the veil."
"26863","Ya'qub narrated to us: Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of the gecko: A little mischief-maker. She said: And I did not hear him command its killing."
"26864","Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Aishah saying: A Jewish woman entered upon me and said: Did you know you will be tried in the graves? She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that and was startled, then said: Only the Jews are tried. So Aishah said: Then I remained after that some nights, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you know it has been revealed to me that you will be tried in the graves?"
"26865","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that Aflah, the brother of Abu al-Qu'ays, came to her, and Abu al-Qu'ays had suckled Aishah through nursing, so he came to her seeking permission upon her, but she refused to permit him until she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she said: O Messenger of Allah, Aflah, the brother of Abu al-Qu'ays, came seeking permission upon me, but I did not permit him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What prevents you from permitting your uncle? I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Qu'ays is not the one who suckled me; only his wife suckled me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Permit him when he comes to you, for he is your uncle."
"26866","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that Barirah entered upon her seeking her help in her contract of manumission. So Aishah said to her, desiring her for herself: What if I count out to your people what is upon you in a single sum, would they do that, and I free you, so you would be my freed slave? So Barirah went to her people and presented that to them, and they said: No, except that your wala' be to us. Aishah said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and I mentioned that to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Buy and free, for wala' is only to the one who frees. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in the evening and said: What is the matter with men who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition not in the Book of Allah, then it is not his, even if he stipulates a hundred times. The condition of Allah is more rightful and more binding."
"26867","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab informed us, from his uncle, he said: Urwah informed me, from Aishah, that she said: She used to comb the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was menstruating, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in retreat in the mosque; so he would lean to the threshold of Aishah's door, and she would wash his head while she was in her chamber."
"26868","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed one night of nights with the Isha prayer, which is the one the people call the Atamah prayer. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not come out until Umar said: The prayer; the women and children have slept. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said to the people of the mosque when he came out to them: No one of the people of the earth awaits it other than you. And that was before Islam had spread among the people."
"26869","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: She said: The first of what was obligated upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of prayer was two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, except Maghrib, for it was three. Then Allah completed Dhuhr and Asr and the last Isha as four in residence, and affirmed prayer upon its first obligation while traveling."
"26870","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: Salma, the freed slave woman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or the wife of Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking permission against Abu Rafi'; he had beaten her. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Rafi': What is the matter with you and her, O Abu Rafi'? He said: She harms me, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did you harm him, O Salma? She said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not harm him with anything, but he broke wind while praying, so I said to him: O Abu Rafi', the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has commanded the Muslims that when wind comes out of one of them, he should perform ablution. So he stood and beat me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began laughing and saying: O Abu Rafi', she commanded you only to good."
"26871","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab al-Zuhri mentioned, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The excellence of prayer with siwak over prayer without siwak is seventyfold."
"26872","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Abbad, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of his journeys until, when we were at Turban, a town between it and Madinah a barid and miles, and it is a town with no water in it, and that was near dawn, a necklace of mine slipped from my neck and fell. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was detained seeking it until dawn rose, and the people had no water with them. She said: So I met from my father what Allah knows of scolding and blaming, and he said: In every journey for the Muslims there is from you trouble and affliction. She said: Then Allah sent down the concession of tayammum. She said: So the people performed tayammum and prayed. She said: My father says, when there came from Allah what came of concession for the Muslims: By Allah, I did not know, O my little daughter, that you are indeed blessed; what Allah has made for the Muslims, in your detaining them, of blessing and ease."
"26873","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I asked her: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when he was junub and wished to sleep before bathing? She said: He used to perform his ablution for prayer, then sleep."
"26874","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be straight and moderate, and know that none of you will be admitted to Paradise by his deed, and that the most beloved of deeds to Allah are the most constant, even if little."
"26875","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, he said: Aishah used to say: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning nothing but Hajj. Then when we arrived at Sarif I menstruated, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was weeping. So he said: What makes you weep? I said: I wish I had not gone out this year. He said: Perhaps you have menstruated, meaning: have you menstruated? She said: I said: Yes. He said: This is something Allah has written upon the daughters of Adam, so do what the pilgrim does, except that you do not circumambulate the House until you are pure. Then when we arrived at Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Make it an Umrah. So the people exited ihram except whoever had a sacrificial animal with him, and the sacrificial animal was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and the well-to-do. She said: Then they set out calling the talbiyah for Hajj. Then when it was the Day of Sacrifice I became pure, so the Messenger of Allah sent me and I performed ifadah, meaning I performed tawaf. She said: Then we were brought beef, so I said: What is this? They said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he slaughtered cattle on behalf of his wives. She said: Then when it was the night of al-Hasbah I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people return with Hajj and Umrah while I return with Hajj. So he commanded Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and he mounted me behind him on his camel. She said: I remember, while I was a young girl of recent age, that I would doze and the back of the saddle would strike my face, until he brought me to al-Tan'im, and I entered ihram for Umrah in recompense for the Umrah of the people which they performed."
"26876","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: So Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, from his father al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Hajj with five nights remaining of Dhu al-Qa'dah, and the people mentioned nothing but Hajj, until when he was at Sarif, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had driven the sacrificial animals with him, and nobles of the people, he commanded the people to exit ihram with an Umrah except whoever had driven the sacrificial animal. And I menstruated that day, so he entered upon me while I was weeping. So he said: What is the matter with you, O Aishah, perhaps you have menstruated. She said: I said: Yes, by Allah, I wish I had not gone out with you this year of mine on this journey. He said: Do not do so, do not say that, for you will fulfill all that the pilgrim fulfills except that you do not circumambulate the House. She said: So I continued upon my Hajj, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, and everyone who had no sacrificial animal with him exited ihram, and his wives exited ihram with an Umrah. Then when it was the Day of Sacrifice I was brought much beef, and it was placed in my house. So I said: What is this? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered cattle on behalf of his wives. Then when it was the night of al-Hasbah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me with my brother Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and he made me perform Umrah from al-Tan'im in place of my Umrah which I had missed. My father said: And Ya'qub narrated to us in another place, in Hajj: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his wives, and they exited ihram with an Umrah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the people that whoever had no sacrificial animal with him should exit ihram, and commanded whoever had a sacrificial animal with him, of the nobles of the people, to remain upon his ihram."
"26877","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Aishah narrated to him that he said, when they said: We feared it is pleurisy, it is from Satan, and Allah would not give him power over me."
"26878","Ibn Ishaq said: Ibn Shihab said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was often heard by me saying: Allah has not taken a prophet until He gives him a choice. She said: So when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was attended, the last word I heard from him while he was saying: Rather the Highest Companion, of Paradise. She said: I said: Then, by Allah, he will not choose us, and I knew it was what he used to say to us: A prophet is not taken until he is given a choice."
"26879","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Ya'qub ibn Utbah narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned on that day when he entered from the mosque, and reclined in my lap. Then a man of the family of Abu Bakr entered upon me, and in his hand was a green siwak. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at it in his hand with a look by which I knew he wanted it. She said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, would you like me to give you this siwak? He said: Yes. She said: So I took it and chewed it for him until I softened it, and gave it to him. She said: So he cleaned his teeth with it as vigorously as I ever saw him cleaning his teeth with a siwak before it. Then he put it down, and I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) growing heavy in my lap. She said: So I went to look at his face, and behold his sight had become fixed, while he was saying: Rather the Highest Companion, of Paradise. So I said: You have been given a choice and you have chosen, by the One who sent you with the truth. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken."
"26880","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Abbad, he said: I heard Aishah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died between my chest and my throat, in my turn; I wronged no one in it. So from my foolishness and youthfulness is that the Messenger of Allah was taken while he was in my lap, then I placed his head upon a pillow and stood lamenting with the women and striking my face."
"26881","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from his wife Fatimah bint Muhammad ibn Imarah, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Zurarah, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: We did not know of the burial of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we heard the sound of shovels in the depth of the night, the night of Wednesday. Muhammad said: And Fatimah narrated to me this hadith."
"26882","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, that Aishah said: Upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a black khamisah when his pain became severe. She said: So he would place it once upon his face and once uncover it from him, while saying: May Allah fight a people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques, forbidding that to his ummah."
"26883","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Rabah narrated to us, he said: I said to Ma'mar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken while he was sitting? He said: Yes."
"26884","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: So Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Aishah, she said: The last of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined was that he said: Two religions shall not remain in the Arabian Peninsula."
"26885","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah informed me that Aishah and Abdullah ibn Abbas said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached by death, he began casting a khamisah upon his face; when it distressed him he uncovered it. He said, and he was thus: The curse of Allah upon the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques, warning them against the like of what they did."
"26886","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people the fear prayer at Dhat al-Riqa' of Nakhl. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) split the people in two parts; one party lined up behind him and one party stood facing the enemy. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir and the party who had lined up behind him said takbir. Then he bowed and they bowed, then he prostrated and they prostrated. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head and they raised with him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained sitting while they prostrated for themselves the second prostration. Then they stood and stepped back upon their heels walking backward until they stood behind them. She said: Then the other party came forward and lined up behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they said takbir, then bowed for themselves, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated his second prostration and they prostrated with him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in his rak'ah and they prostrated for themselves the second prostration. Then both parties stood together and lined up behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed with them and they bowed together, then he prostrated and they prostrated together. Then he raised his head and they raised with him, all that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) very swiftly, not sparing to lighten as much as he could. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam and they gave salam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, while the people had shared with him in the whole prayer."
"26887","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When I parted the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him, I made a parting from his crown and let his forelock fall between his temples."
"26888","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Qur'an, then it is deficient."
"26889","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, while he was governor over Madinah, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray toward her while she was lying across before him. He said: So Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, and he was with Umar, said: Perhaps, O Abu Abdullah, she said: While I was at his side. He said: So Urwah said: I inform you with certainty and you answer me with conjecture; rather lying across before him like the lying of a funeral bier."
"26890","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr both narrated to me, each narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray of the night thirteen rak'ahs, with his two rak'ahs after Fajr, before dawn: eleven rak'ahs of the night, six of them two by two, and he would perform witr with five, not sitting in them."
"26891","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, that Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that Aishah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was sitting in the shade of Fari' Ujum Hassan, a man came to him and said: I am burnt, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What is your affair? He said: I fell upon my wife while I was fasting. She said: And that was in Ramadan. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Sit down. So he sat in the side of the people. Then a man came with a donkey upon it a sack in which were dates. He said: This is my charity, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is the burnt one a while ago? So he said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Take this and give it in charity. He said: And where is charity, O Messenger of Allah, except upon me and mine? By the One who sent you with the truth, I find nothing, I and my dependents. He said: So take it. So he took it."
"26892","Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Thawr ibn Yazid al-Kala'i narrated to me, and he was trustworthy, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Salih al-Makki, he said: I performed Hajj with Adi ibn Adi al-Kindi, so he sent me to Safiyyah bint Shaybah, daughter of Uthman, keeper of the Ka'bah, to ask her about things she had heard from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So among what she narrated to me was that she heard Aishah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no divorce nor emancipation in compulsion."
"26893","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yazid ibn Ruman narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded concerning the slain that they be cast into the well, so they were cast into it, except what was of Umayyah ibn Khalaf, for he swelled in his armor and filled it. So they went to move him and he came apart, so they left him and cast upon him what concealed him of dust and stones. Then when he had cast them into the well, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over them and said: O people of the well, have you found what your Lord promised true? For I have found what my Lord promised me true. So his companions said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you speak to dead people? He said: So he said to them: They have known that what I promised them is true. Aishah said: And the people say: They heard what you said to them, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They have known."
"26894","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Abbad, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the people of Makkah sent concerning the ransom of their captives, Zaynab bint Rasul Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent concerning the ransom of Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi' with wealth, and sent with it a necklace of hers that had belonged to Khadijah, with which she had entered upon Abu al-As when he built with her. She said: So when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it, he was moved by intense tenderness for her, and said: If you see fit to release her captive to her and return to her what is hers, then do so. So they said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So they released him and returned to her what was hers."
"26895","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the killing of Ja'far came, we recognized grief in the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Then a man entered upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the women have overcome us and tempted us. He said: So return to them and silence them. He said: So he went, then returned and said to him the like of that. He says: And perhaps affectation harms its people. He said: So go and silence them; if they refuse, then throw dust in their mouths. She said: I said to myself: May Allah keep you away, for by Allah you neither spared yourself nor are you obeying the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I knew he would not be able to throw dust in their mouths."
"26896","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: None of their women was killed except a single woman. She said: By Allah, she is with me, talking with me, laughing heartily, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was killing their men in the market, when a caller called her name: Where is so-and-so? She said: I, by Allah. She said: I said: Woe to you, what is the matter with you? She said: I am to be killed. She said: I said: And why? She said: An offense I committed. She said: So she was taken away and her neck was struck. And Aishah used to say: By Allah, I do not forget my amazement at her cheerfulness and much laughter, though she knew she would be killed."
"26897","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq, Juwayriyah bint al-Harith fell in the share of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, or a cousin of his, and she contracted with him for her freedom. And she was a sweet comely woman; none saw her but she captivated him. So she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his help in her contract. She said: By Allah, it was only that I saw her at the door of my chamber and I disliked her, and I knew he would see of her what I saw. So she entered upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am Juwayriyah bint al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, chief of his people, and there has befallen me of affliction what is not hidden from you. So I fell in the share of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, or a cousin of his, and I contracted with him for myself, so I have come to you seeking your help upon my contract. He said: So is there for you something better than that? She said: And what is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I fulfill your contract and marry you. She said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I have done so. She said: And the news went out to the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Juwayriyah bint al-Harith. So the people said: The in-laws of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they released what was in their hands. She said: So by his marrying her he freed a hundred households of Banu al-Mustaliq. And I know no woman who was of greater blessing upon her people than she."
"26898","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Aflat ibn Khalifah, he said: My father Sufyan says Fulayt, from Jasrah bint Dajajah, from Aishah, she said: Safiyyah sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) food she had made for him while he was with me. Then when I saw the servant girl, trembling seized me until shivering overcame me. So I struck the bowl and threw it. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at me and I recognized anger in his face. So I said: I seek refuge with the Messenger of Allah that he curse me today. She said: He said: Rather. She said: I said: And what is its expiation, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Food like her food and a vessel like her vessel."
"26899","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, and Abu Sa'id said: Za'idah narrated to us: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The family of Muhammad did not satiate, since they came to Madinah, three days in succession with food until he died. Abu Sa'id said: Three nights in succession with wheat bread until he died."
"26900","Husayn narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, that he said: I asked Aishah, I said: Inform me of something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with, that I might supplicate Allah with it and Allah benefit me with it. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say much: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done and from the evil of what I have not done."
"26901","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Aishah, that she said: When a sick person was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer, there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness."
"26902","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Masruq, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman spends from the food of her house without causing ruin, she has her reward for what she spent, and her husband has his reward for what he earned, and the storekeeper has the like of that, none of their rewards decreasing from the reward of the others in anything."
"26903","Ziyad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Tufayl al-Bakkai narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, he said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, tell me something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate often: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done and from the evil of what I have not done."
"26904","Ziyad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Whoever is overtaken by the prayer while junub does not fast. He said: So I mentioned that to Aishah, and she said: He says nothing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake up among us junub, then he would stand and bathe, then Bilal would come to him and announce the prayer to him, then he would go out and pray with the people while water dripped on his skin, then he would remain fasting that day of his."
"26905","Ziyad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: I asked Aishah what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade to make nabidh in. She said: He forbade al-dubba and al-muzaffat. He said: I said: And ships. She said: I only tell you what I heard, and I do not tell you what I did not hear."
"26906","Ziyad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I asked Aishah how the deed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, did he single out anything of the days. She said: No, and which of you can bear what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do."
"26907","Ziyad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, he said: Aishah said: When the verse in al-Baqarah about wine came down, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it in the mosque, then he forbade trade in wine."
"26908","Al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Bahiyy, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to remember Allah in all his states."
"26909","Al-Walid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim is pricked by a thorn or more except Allah raises him a degree by it and removes a sin from him by it."
"26910","Amir ibn Salih ibn Abdillah ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam Abu al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr while the sun had not left her chamber, and the wall was an expanse, and Amir gestured with his hand."
"26911","Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, she said: We would slaughter a sheep, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send portions of it to the friends of Khadijah."
"26912","Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seclude himself in worship in the last ten of Ramadan."
"26913","Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord commanded me to give Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl."
"26914","Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gecko is a little wicked one."
"26915","Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to sleep while junub, would perform ablution as his ablution for prayer, and when he wanted to eat or drink, he would wash his hand then eat and drink."
"26916","Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woman is like a rib, if you straighten her you break her, and she is enjoyed with the crookedness in her."
"26917","Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believer is struck by a thorn or more except Allah cuts away a sin from him by it."
"26918","Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded building mosques in the quarters and commanded that they be cleaned and perfumed."
"26919","Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I was not jealous of any wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as I was jealous of Khadijah, and that was because of what I used to hear of his mentioning her."
"26920","Hasan ibn Musa and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Bakr, that she informed him that Aishah said about a woman who sees something of blood that makes her doubt after purity: She said: It is only a vein or veins."
"26921","Hasan ibn Musa and Hashim and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah informed me, and Hashim said: from Abu Salamah, that Aishah, and Hashim said: from Aishah, informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the two rakahs between the call and the iqamah of the dawn prayer."
"26922","Hasan ibn Musa and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Shayban narrated to us, from al-Ashath, from his father, from Masruq, he said: I said to Aishah: Which deed was most pleasing to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He loved the lasting one. He said: I said: At what time did he pray. She said: When he heard the caller he stood and prayed."
"26923","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Fudayl, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, he said: Khuthaym ibn Irak narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake up junub from intercourse, then bathe, then wake up fasting."
"26924","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz informed him that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him that Aishah, Mother of the Believers, informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her while fasting."
"26925","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe with a sa and perform ablution with a mudd."
"26926","Hasan narrated to us, he said: I heard Shayban, from Layth, from Mujahid, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The black dog is a devil."
"26927","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Abu Hashim narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, from al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Aishah, she said: I used to rub janabah off the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"26928","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: As if I look at the gleam of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he is in ihram."
"26929","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me after Khadijah died, before his departure to Madinah by two or three years, while I was a girl of seven years. When we came to Madinah, women came to me while I was playing on a swing, my hair in locks, and they took me and prepared me and adorned me, then they brought me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he consummated with me while I was a girl of nine years."
"26930","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Aishah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raced me and I beat him."
"26931","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that when the Messenger of Allah finished with al-Ahzab, he entered the washroom to bathe, and Jibril came, and I saw him through the crack of the door with dust bound on his head, and he said: O Muhammad, have you laid down your weapons. He said: We have not laid down our weapons yet. Rise against Banu Qurayzah."
"26932","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I used to recite ruqyah over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the evil eye: Wipe away the harm, Lord of mankind, healing is in Your hand, none removes it but You."
"26933","Abu Nuh Qurad narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad informed us, from Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from some of their shaykhs that Ziyad, freedman of Abdillah ibn Abbad ibn Abi Rabiah, narrated to them, from one who narrated to him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat before him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have slaves who lie to me and betray me and disobey me, and I beat them and insult them, so how am I with them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: According to their betrayal of you and disobedience of you and lying to you, and your punishment of them: if it is less than their sins, it is a merit for you over them, and if your punishment of them is equal to their sins, it is even, neither for you nor against you, and if your punishment of them is above their sins, the remaining merit before you will be taken from you for them. So the man began to weep before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and cry out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with him, does he not read the Book of Allah: And We shall set up the balances of justice for the Day of Resurrection, so no soul will be wronged in anything, and if it be the weight of a mustard seed We shall bring it, and sufficient are We as reckoners. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, I find nothing better than parting with these, meaning his slaves. I call you to witness that they are all free."
"26934","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Budayl, from Abu al-Jawza, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to open the prayer with takbir and open the recitation with: Praise be to Allah."
"26935","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Subayi, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdillah, he said: I said to Aishah: What is al-Kawthar. She said: A river given to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the belly of Paradise. He said: I said: And what is the belly of Paradise. She said: Its middle, its banks hollowed pearl."
"26936","These hadiths are additions of Abdullah. Abdullah said: I found these hadiths from here to the end of them in my father's book in his handwriting. He said: Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never struck with his hand any of his wives nor a servant, nor did he ever strike anything with his hand except to strive in the way of Allah. She said: Nothing was taken from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he avenged it except that the sanctities of Allah be violated, then he would avenge for Allah. She said: No two matters were ever offered to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one easier than the other, but he took the easier one unless it was a sin, and if it was a sin he was the farthest of people from it."
"26937","I found in my father's book: Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, that she informed him that she and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe from one vessel, each scooping from it."
"26938","I found in my father's book: Amir ibn Salih narrated to me, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: My soul is wicked, but let him say: My soul is heavy."
"26939","I found in my father's book: Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, that she screened her door with a figured curtain in which were winged horses, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from a journey and commanded her, so she took it down."
"26940","I found in my father's book: Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Amrah, from Aishah, that she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) secluded himself, he did not leave the mosque except for human need."
"26941","I found in my father's book: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Aishah, that it reached her that Ibn Umar narrates from his father Umar ibn al-Khattab that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished by the weeping of his family over him. She said: May Allah have mercy on Umar and Ibn Umar, for by Allah they are neither liars nor belied nor adding. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said that about a man of the Jews, and he passed by his family while they wept over him, and he said: They weep over him while Allah Almighty punishes him in his grave."
"26942","I found in my father's book: Said ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Wail ibn Dawud narrated to us, from al-Bahiyy, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never sent Zayd ibn Harithah in an army except he put him in command over them, and had he remained after him he would have appointed him successor."
"26943","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn more than three days except for a husband."
"26944","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He used to kiss while fasting. This is the end of the Musnad of Lady Aishah."
